<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>PROJECT ANGLERFISH — locations</name><description><![CDATA[1174 locations from the report at <a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report">b0b.dev/report</a>. 817 carry a date parsed from their own context text and drive the time slider; 357 do not and are shown at every slider position.]]></description><Style id="t-financial"><IconStyle><color>ff00ccff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff00ccff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-military"><IconStyle><color>ff4444ff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff4444ff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-underground"><IconStyle><color>ff0066ff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff0066ff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-surveillance"><IconStyle><color>ffffcc00</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ffffcc00</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-enclave"><IconStyle><color>ffff88cc</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ffff88cc</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-archaeological"><IconStyle><color>ff41ff00</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff41ff00</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-conflict"><IconStyle><color>ff6600ff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff6600ff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-governance"><IconStyle><color>ffffffff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ffffffff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-blacksite"><IconStyle><color>ff0088ff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff0088ff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-obelisk"><IconStyle><color>ff00c2e6</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff00c2e6</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-organized-crime"><IconStyle><color>ffff00ff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ffff00ff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-submarine-cable"><IconStyle><color>ffffe500</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ffffe500</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-satellite"><IconStyle><color>ff03ff76</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff03ff76</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-mining"><IconStyle><color>ff0091ff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff0091ff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-airport"><IconStyle><color>ff6633ff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff6633ff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-corporate"><IconStyle><color>ff4370ff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff4370ff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-museum"><IconStyle><color>ffff88b3</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ffff88b3</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-crypto-tech"><IconStyle><color>ff76e600</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff76e600</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-technology"><IconStyle><color>ffdaff64</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ffdaff64</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-sports-gambling"><IconStyle><color>ff40d7ff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff40d7ff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-animal-research"><IconStyle><color>fff900d5</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>fff900d5</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-capital"><IconStyle><color>ffff4d7c</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ffff4d7c</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-datacenter"><IconStyle><color>ffff6229</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ffff6229</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-epstein-network"><IconStyle><color>ff4417ff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ff4417ff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Style id="t-mass-shooting"><IconStyle><color>ffffffff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><color>ffffffff</color><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style><Folder><name>Section II (22)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>MCC New York (closed 2021) - Epstein death site</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Metropolitan Correctional Center, 150 Park Row. Jeffrey Epstein died here 10 Aug 2019 - ruled suicide by hanging (OCME); fracture pattern read as homicide-consistent by family pathologist Michael Baden (attributed, contested). DOJ OIG documented the failure stack: 75+ falsified guard rounds, cellmate never replaced against written directive, DVR failed 29 Jul leaving one recording camera that could not see the cell door. The 2025 DOJ &#x27;raw&#x27; video was shown by metadata analysis to be assembled in Premiere with ~2m53s absent; later House releases contained the &#x27;missing minute,&#x27; contradicting the official explanation. Facility closed 2021. See report Section II - the death record. Sources: OIG 23-085; WIRED; CBS (2025); House Oversight (Sep 2025).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2019-08-10</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-74.001,40.7133,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>FPC Bryan, Texas - Ghislaine Maxwell custody</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Federal Prison Camp Bryan: minimum-security, dormitory-style women&#x27;s camp. Ghislaine Maxwell - the network&#x27;s only living convicted principal - was moved here 1 Aug 2025, one week after nine hours of immunized DOJ interviews, despite BOP policy ordinarily excluding sex offenders from camps; officials called the transfer &#x27;highly unusual.&#x27; She invoked the Fifth to Congress (Feb 2026) while a pardon stays publicly un-ruled-out; the Senate opposed clemency by unanimous resolution (Jul 2026). Projected release 2037. The documented leverage structure around the surviving node - see report Section V. Sources: BOP; CNN (Aug 2025); Axios (Feb/Jul 2026).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2025-08-01</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-96.3661,30.6602,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mount of Olives Cemetery, Jerusalem (Robert Maxwell grave)</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Robert Maxwell - Ghislaine&#x27;s father - buried here 10 Nov 1991 with near-state honors: PM Shamir and President Herzog (eulogy) attended, days after he went overboard from the yacht Lady Ghislaine. The widely repeated &#x27;six intelligence chiefs in attendance&#x27; claim traces to secondary literature; the Shamir quote cannot be verified verbatim. The scene itself is the documented signal: a foreign publisher buried on the Mount of Olives with a head of state eulogizing. See report Section V - The Maxwell Template. Sources: JTA (Nov 1991); Times of Israel (2020).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1991-11-10</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>35.2454,31.778,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Headington Hill Hall, Oxford (Pergamon Press HQ)</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Robert Maxwell&#x27;s Pergamon Press headquarters and residence. Scientific publishing was a near-perfect Cold War access vehicle: legitimate East-West passage, standing contact with scientists on both sides. Built from contacts made in his 1945-47 press-control posting in British-occupied Berlin. UK DTI verdict (1971): &#x27;not a person who can be relied on to exercise proper stewardship of a publicly quoted company.&#x27; Sources: DTI report (1971); Wikipedia (sourced).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1945-01-01</begin><end>1945-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-1.2214,51.7593,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lady Ghislaine last position, off Gran Canaria (approx.)</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Robert Maxwell went overboard from his yacht Lady Ghislaine near here, 5 Nov 1991 (position approximate). Spanish inquest: heart attack followed by accidental drowning - no official finding of suicide or murder; both persist as commentary only. Two weeks earlier he had sued Seymour Hersh over The Samson Option&#x27;s Mossad allegations. The £460M Mirror pension fraud surfaced within weeks of his death. A death honestly readable three ways is the deniability signature. Sources: Spanish inquest reporting (Dec 1991); Washington Post (Oct 1991).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1991-11-05</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-15.85,27.74,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Axon Enterprise HQ, Scottsdale AZ</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Axon Enterprise (Taser) HQ. Acquired Carbyne for $625M; deal closed ~Feb 2026 (Axon took the remaining ~89% stake). Carbyne&#x27;s NG911 caller-geolocation and live-video capability - the Epstein-funded, Barak-chaired firm - now operates inside a publicly-traded US police-technology company serving ~300 emergency centers across 23 states. BLOWBACK NODE: the surveillance capability consolidated, it did not dissolve. Sources: Axon press release (Nov 2025); GovTech; Forbes (Feb 2026).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2026-02-01</begin><end>2026-02-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-111.8879,33.5312,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>9 East 71st Street Townhouse, NYC</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Former Herbert N. Straus mansion, one of the largest private residences in Manhattan. Its use passed to Epstein via Leslie Wexner / L Brands in the 1990s. Named in victim testimony; sold 2021. Appears throughout the House Oversight EFTA email release as Epstein&#x27;s operational base. Sources: NYT; USVI filings; House Oversight EFTA release. CURRENT OWNER: sold 2021 (~$51M) to a former Goldman Sachs executive (Michael Daffey); no connection to the current owner.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2021-01-01</begin><end>2021-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9663,40.7716,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Zorro Ranch, Stanley, New Mexico</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>~10,000 acres held through Epstein entities (Cypress Inc. / NES LLC). Named in victim testimony and New Mexico AG inquiries. Sources: NYT; NM AG. CURRENT OWNER: sold 2023 to the Huffines family (renamed San Rafael Ranch).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-105.98,35.1466,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Little St. James, USVI (LSJ)</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Epstein&#x27;s private island, central to the trafficking allegations. USVI v. Epstein estate settled for ~$105M (2022). Source: USVI Dept. of Justice. CURRENT OWNER: Little &amp; Great St. James sold ~2023 (~$60M) to Stephen Deckoff (Black Diamond Capital) for a planned resort; proceeds part-fund the victims settlement.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-01-01</begin><end>2022-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-64.825,18.301,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Great St. James, USVI</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Adjacent island Epstein acquired in 2016. Source: USVI filings.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2016-01-01</begin><end>2016-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-64.813,18.306,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>358 El Brillo Way, Palm Beach</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Site of the 2005-06 Palm Beach Police investigation whose federal handling became the 2008 non-prosecution agreement (see Acosta). Sources: Palm Beach PD; DOJ OPR report (2020). STATUS: mansion demolished 2021; the lot was resold — nothing of the original structure remains.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2005-01-01</begin><end>2005-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-80.0388,26.6853,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>22 Avenue Foch, Paris</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Epstein&#x27;s Paris apartment, referenced in the French judicial investigation connected to Jean-Luc Brunel. Source: Paris Prosecutor (OCRVP).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>2.283,48.8719,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Carbyne (Reporty) HQ, Tel Aviv</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Israeli emergency-call-routing / caller-geolocation surveillance-tech firm. Epstein was an investor; former Israeli PM Ehud Barak chaired it. A documented Epstein-Barak-surveillance-tech tie and a key node of the HYPOTHESIS layer. Sources: Bloomberg; Haaretz; MintPress. UPDATE (2026): Carbyne was acquired by Axon Enterprise (Taser) for $625M, deal closed ~Feb 2026; Barak exited the board in 2020; later backers include Founders Fund (Peter Thiel) and a 2025 AT&amp;T-led $100M round. Sources: Axon (Nov 2025); GovTech; Forbes (Feb 2026).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>34.792,32.0743,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Apollo Global Management (Leon Black), 9 W 57th St</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Apollo founder Leon Black paid Epstein ~$158M (2012-2017) for tax/estate structuring, per the independent Dechert LLP review (2021); Black later stepped down as Apollo CEO. In-corpus: Epstein family-office threads reference Apollo stock and ~$190M cash. This is established public record (a payment), not an adjudicated crime. Sources: Dechert review (2021); SEC; NYT. UPDATE (2026): a federal securities class action (SDNY, Mar 2026) alleges Apollo/Black concealed Epstein business ties after Feb-2026 file releases; a Delaware derivative suit over exit payments is also ongoing. Litigation unresolved.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9772,40.7638,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>MIT Media Lab, Cambridge</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Accepted Epstein-linked donations; director Joi Ito resigned in 2019 after reporting (Ronan Farrow, The New Yorker) that the Lab concealed Epstein&#x27;s gifts. Source: The New Yorker; MIT / Goodwin Procter report (2020).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.0872,42.3608,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>MC2 Model Management (Jean-Luc Brunel), Paris</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Modeling agency seeded with ~$1M from Epstein. Brunel was charged in France with rape of minors and died in La Sante prison in Feb 2022. jmail topic tag: &#x27;Conspiring w/ Brunel&#x27;. Sources: Paris Prosecutor; AFP.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-02-01</begin><end>2022-02-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>2.3075,48.8698,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Deutsche Bank (US HQ, 60 Wall St), NYC</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Epstein&#x27;s principal bank after JPMorgan exited the relationship (~2013-2018). July 2020: New York Dept. of Financial Services imposed a $150M consent-order penalty for significant compliance failures, expressly including the bank&#x27;s handling of the Epstein account - a documented, penalty-paid finding, not merely alleged. This is the institutional record; no individual banker is pinned. Sources: NYDFS consent order &amp; press release (7 Jul 2020). UPDATE: an Aug 4 2026 Senate Finance (Wyden) report alleges DB was late filing SARs on &gt;$250M in suspicious Epstein-linked wires - Wyden&#x27;s finding; DB settled without admission.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2020-07-01</begin><end>2020-07-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-74.0089,40.7053,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bank of America Tower (One Bryant Park), NYC</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Third bank to settle with Epstein survivors: agreed Mar 2026 to pay ~$72.5M in Doe v. Bank of America (1:25-cv-08520, SDNY; &gt;=60 survivors, period June 2008-July 2019); final-approval hearing set 27 Aug 2026. Settlement carries NO admission of liability. Completes the bank cluster after JPMorgan (~$290M, 2023) and Deutsche Bank ($75M victims settlement, 2023). Institutional record; no individual pinned. Sources: American Banker; NBC; court docket 1:25-cv-08520; Barchart.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2026-08-27</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-73.9846,40.7556,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>La Sante Prison, Paris (Brunel custody death)</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Jean-Luc Brunel - MC2 modeling agent, charged in France with rape of minors and suspected of procuring for Epstein - was found dead in his cell here, 19 Feb 2022; ruled suicide by hanging. A second charged principal dead in custody before trial, echoing the MCC record two nodes over. (Brunel deceased.) Sources: Paris Prosecutor; AFP; Reuters (Feb 2022).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2022-02-19</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>2.3417,48.8342,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>USVI Superior Court, Charlotte Amalie, St. Thomas</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>Venue of the Epstein estate probate, docket ST-19-PB-80 (~$577M estate). The court appointed Special Master Rosalie Ballentine to account for the estate&#x27;s assets, liabilities, income and expenditures. Seven reports exist: the first (Sept 2020) is public; reports 3-6 are SEALED. Motions to unseal by the New York Times and McClatchy (Miami Herald) were DENIED three times - 23 Sep 2025, 3 Oct 2025, and reconsideration denied 29 Jan 2026 - on grounds that third-party privacy outweighs access, that the reports are not judicial documents, and that the Epstein Files Transparency Act reaches only DOJ-held material, not the estate&#x27;s. A court-ordered reconstruction of where the money went exists, and access to it has been litigated and refused. NOTE: online &#x27;forensic&#x27; reconstructions claiming $2.1B across shell entities are amateur analyses, not this court&#x27;s work. Sources: St. Thomas Source (Aug 2025); Virgin Islands Daily News.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2025-09-23</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-64.9321,18.3396,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Edge Foundation / Brockman Inc., NYC (approx.)</name><styleUrl>#t-epstein-network</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; epstein-network</p><p>John Brockman&#x27;s literary agency and the Edge Foundation - the intellectual gatekeeper of Epstein&#x27;s science network (report Section VI). Epstein-linked foundations supplied roughly 74% of Edge&#x27;s income 2001-2017 ($638K of $857K), funding the &#x27;billionaires&#x27; dinners&#x27; that introduced him to Minsky, Pinker, Dawkins, Dennett and others; Edge ended the dinner after his final 2015 donation. Institutional node: attendance at a salon is not misconduct, and no attendee is accused here. Position approximate. Sources: BuzzFeed News (Aldhous, 2019); Slate (Aug 2019).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2001-01-01</begin><end>2001-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.972,40.7642,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NYPD International Liaison post - Israel National Police Sharon District HQ, Kfar Saba</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section II</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>ADDED 31 Aug 2026 from the sub-national liaison research. The NYPD — a MUNICIPAL police force — has run permanent overseas liaison posts for two decades, currently 14 overseas and 3 domestic, with detectives embedded inside foreign national police services. The Israel post opened around September 2012 NOT at the US Embassy but inside the Israel National Police Sharon District headquarters at Kfar Saba. Officers&#x27; salaries are public money; travel, housing and office costs are paid by the private New York City Police Foundation. No statute, local law, council resolution or published MOU creating the programme has been found and the NYPD has never cited one. The City Comptroller has never audited the Intelligence Division; the NYPD Inspector General, whose mandate expressly covers partnerships with other law-enforcement agencies, has published nothing on it in twelve years. STRUCTURE ONLY — no person here is characterised, and nothing implies any individual is a criminal or an intelligence asset. COORDINATES APPROXIMATE (Kfar Saba).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#II">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-09-01</begin><end>2012-09-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>34.907,32.175,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section VII (182)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Bank for International Settlements (BIS)</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Founded May 17, 1930. 63 member central banks. Sovereign immunity on Swiss soil. Transferred 23 tons Czech gold to Nazi Germany (March 1939). Bretton Woods voted to dissolve it - it survived.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1930-05-17</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>7.5886,47.5476,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Basel, Switzerland</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>BIS headquarters. The central bank of central banks operates from Swiss soil with diplomatic immunity.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>7.5886,47.5596,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Jekyll Island, Georgia</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>November 1910: Six men met secretly at JP Morgan&#x27;s exclusive club. Their plan became the Federal Reserve Act (1913). They denied the meeting for 20+ years.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1910-11-01</begin><end>1910-11-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-81.4201,31.0654,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Federal Reserve, Washington D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Created by Federal Reserve Act, Dec 23, 1913 - signed during Congressional recess. Network of private member banks with government-appointed board.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1913-12-23</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-77.0455,38.8927,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>JP Morgan HQ, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>JP Morgan likely arranged Jekyll Island Club access. 77 years later, Greenspan (Morgan board member) became Fed Chair.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.9753,40.7566,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kuhn, Loeb &amp; Co., New York</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Paul Warburg&#x27;s firm. Warburg designed the Federal Reserve, became first Board member (1914). CFR director 1921-1932.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1914-01-01</begin><end>1914-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-74.0113,40.7074,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chase Manhattan / Rockefeller, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>David Rockefeller&#x27;s bank. Volcker alternated between Chase and U.S. government. Chase → Treasury → Chase → Treasury → NY Fed → Fed Chair.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-74.0088,40.7057,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Council on Foreign Relations (CFR), New York</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Founded 1921. 500+ members served in U.S. government. 21+ Secretaries of Defense/War, 22+ Secretaries of State, 16+ CIA Directors. Harold Pratt House, 58 E 68th St.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1921-01-01</begin><end>1921-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9679,40.7686,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bilderberg Hotel, Oosterbeek, Netherlands</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>First Bilderberg Meeting: May 29-31, 1954. Annual meetings of 120-150 heads of state, bankers, media editors. Chatham House Rule - content is secret.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1954-01-01</begin><end>1954-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>5.8403,51.9867,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Trilateral Commission, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Founded July 1973 by David Rockefeller. Published &#x27;Crisis of Democracy&#x27; (1975) arguing too much participation is the problem.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1973-07-01</begin><end>1973-07-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9723,40.754,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vatican City - St. Peter&#x27;s Square</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Spiritual control hub. Independent city-state since 1929. Egyptian obelisk from Heliopolis brought by Caligula 37 AD. Absolute monarchy. 1.3B Catholic adherents.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1929-01-01</begin><end>1929-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.4539,41.9022,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>City of London Corporation (Square Mile)</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Governing body of the Square Mile since 1067. Own police, own Lord Mayor. Businesses outvote residents 24,000 to 9,000. Processes $2.7T forex daily.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.0922,51.5155,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cleopatra&#x27;s Needle, Victoria Embankment, London</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Egyptian obelisk from Heliopolis (1450 BC, Pharaoh Thutmose III). Brought to London 1878. Same origin as Vatican obelisk.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1878-01-01</begin><end>1878-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.1166,51.5085,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Washington Monument, Washington D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>555 ft 5.125 in. Egyptian obelisk design - NPS: &#x27;evoking timelessness of ancient civilizations&#x27;. Aluminum cap inscribed &#x27;Laus Deo&#x27;. Masonic cornerstone July 4, 1848.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1848-07-04</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-77.0353,38.8895,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Place de la Concorde Obelisk, Paris</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Egyptian obelisk from Luxor. Companion to London and New York obelisks. Four Egyptian obelisks across four Western capitals.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>2.3212,48.8656,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cleopatra&#x27;s Needle, Central Park, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Egyptian obelisk from Heliopolis. Third of three obelisks distributed across three Western capitals (London, Paris, New York).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.9654,40.7796,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>East India Company, London</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Founded 1600. Own military (260,000 troops), own courts, own currency. Operated 274 years. Prototype for modern corporate sovereignty.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1600-01-01</begin><end>1600-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.083,51.5128,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hamburg, Germany - M.M. Warburg</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Warburg family banking dynasty HQ. Paul and Max Warburg operated banks on both sides of the Atlantic through both World Wars.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.9937,53.5511,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Citadel HQ, Chicago</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Ken Griffin&#x27;s hedge fund. Bernanke (Fed Chair 2006-14) became senior advisor after bailing out Wall Street with public money.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2006-01-01</begin><end>2006-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-87.627,41.8884,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Carlyle Group, Washington D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Fed Chair Jerome Powell was Carlyle partner. Co-founder David Rubenstein simultaneously chairs CFR and sits on Trilateral Commission.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.0423,38.905,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>General Dynamics HQ, Reston, VA</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Crown Family acquired 1959. Sole manufacturer of MK-80 series bombs used in Gaza. Sold electronics division to Carlyle Group (1992).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1959-01-01</begin><end>1959-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.3478,38.9526,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Aspen Institute, Washington D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Henry Crown Fellowship connects Crown Family (GD) → Jonathan Greenblatt (ADL CEO). Think tank bridging defense industry to advocacy.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.0388,38.9078,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>ADL Headquarters, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Anti-Defamation League. CEO Jonathan Greenblatt is a Henry Crown Fellow (Aspen Institute) - connected to the Crown Family that owns General Dynamics.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.9772,40.7527,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Svalbard Global Seed Vault, Arctic Norway</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Opened 26 February 2008. Built, owned and fully funded by the Government of Norway; run by NordGen with the Crop Trust part-funding operations. Seeds are held under &#x27;black box&#x27; terms: boxes are never opened and only the depositing genebank can withdraw them. First withdrawal: ICARDA, 2015-2019, to rebuild a collection lost to the Syrian war. 1.4 million+ samples from 134 institutions (2026).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2008-02-26</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>15.4942,78.2355,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fort Moore (formerly Fort Benning) - School of the Americas / WHINSEC</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>School of the Americas (renamed WHINSEC 2001). Trained officers who became Latin American dictators: Noriega, Galtieri, D&#x27;Aubuisson, Rios Montt (convicted genocide), Banzer. The rebranding pattern - the training continued, the name changed.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2001-01-01</begin><end>2001-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-84.9649,32.3537,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Carlisle Barracks, PA - U.S. Army War College</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Sisi attended International Fellows Program (2006). Became head of Egyptian Military Intelligence (2010), led 2013 coup, now constructing NAC - 700 km² AI-surveilled city. Carlisle produced the architect of Memphis.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2006-01-01</begin><end>2006-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.1886,40.2026,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>National Defense University, Washington D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>International officers program trains foreign military leaders in U.S. doctrine. Graduates return carrying the architecture in their training.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.016,38.864,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fort Leavenworth, KS - Command and General Staff College</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>International Military Student program. Foreign officers trained in U.S. command philosophy and strategic doctrine.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-94.9217,39.3553,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Royal Military Academy Sandhurst, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Trained King Abdullah II (Jordan), King Hamad (Bahrain), Sultan Qaboos (Oman), Crown Prince Hussein (Jordan), Gulf state royals. British Empire ended. The officer pipeline did not.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.7693,51.3484,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tehran, Iran - 1953 Operation Ajax</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>CIA-MI6 joint operation. Democratically elected Mossadegh removed, Shah installed. SAVAK trained by CIA and Mossad. Blowback: 1979 Islamic Revolution.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1953-01-01</begin><end>1953-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>51.389,35.6892,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Guatemala City - 1954 Operation PBSUCCESS</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Democratically elected Arbenz removed. Dulles brothers (CIA Director + Secretary of State) both had United Fruit Company financial ties. The brothers who ordered the coup profited from it.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1954-01-01</begin><end>1954-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-90.5069,14.6349,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kinshasa, Congo - 1961 Lumumba Assassination</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Patrice Lumumba - first democratically elected leader - assassinated. CIA documented involvement. Mobutu installed, ruled 32 years, looted est. $5 billion.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1961-01-01</begin><end>1961-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>15.3222,-4.325,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Jakarta, Indonesia - 1965 CIA Kill Lists</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Sukarno removed, Suharto installed. CIA provided kill lists. U.S. Embassy supplied names. 500,000–1,000,000 killed. Suharto ruled 31 years.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1965-01-01</begin><end>1965-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>106.865,-6.1751,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Santiago, Chile - 1973 Allende Coup</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Democratically elected Allende died in palace during Sept 11, 1973 coup. CIA documented (Church Committee), $8M+ covert funding. Pinochet disappeared 3,000+ people.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1973-09-11</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-70.6693,-33.4489,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Congress for Cultural Freedom HQ, Paris</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Established 1950 as CIA front, operated in 35 countries. Funded literary magazines, art exhibitions, conferences. Exposed 1967 by Ramparts. The Western cultural apparatus as intelligence operation. Kosinski was embedded in this network.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1950-01-01</begin><end>1950-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>2.3376,48.8606,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fort Belvoir, VA - ISA / Task Force Orange HQ</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Intelligence Support Activity (ISA) headquarters. The most classified U.S. military intelligence unit - JSOC&#x27;s field intelligence arm. Known by 12+ codenames (CENTRA SPIKE, GRAY FOX, CEMETERY WIND, etc.), changed every ~2 years. Nicknamed &#x27;The Activity&#x27; and &#x27;Army of Northern Virginia.&#x27; Created 1980 after Operation Eagle Claw failure. Provides SIGINT/HUMINT to Delta Force and DEVGRU. The unit that finds the targets.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1980-01-01</begin><end>1980-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.1454,38.7119,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Arlington, VA - ISA First Secret HQ</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>ISA&#x27;s original secret headquarters (1981). Arlington sits on land confiscated from Robert E. Lee&#x27;s estate. The unit nicknamed &#x27;Army of Northern Virginia&#x27; was first headquartered on the Confederate general&#x27;s seized ground. SAP codename: OPTIMIZE TALENT. Budget: $7M classified.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1981-01-01</begin><end>1981-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.106,38.8799,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tegucigalpa, Honduras - SEASPRAY/ISA Operations Base</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>ISA SIGINT specialists operated from Honduras (1982-85+) during Operation Queens Hunter. SEASPRAY clandestine aviation flew Beechcraft King Airs. Monitored Salvadoran guerrilla communications while School of the Americas graduates ran counter-guerrilla death squads in the same theater. Same government funded both the intelligence and the killing.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1982-01-01</begin><end>1982-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-87.1921,14.0723,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Medellín, Colombia - CENTRA SPIKE / Pablo Escobar Hunt</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>ISA&#x27;s SIGINT team (codename CENTRA SPIKE) tracked Pablo Escobar&#x27;s communications (1989-93), providing geolocation intelligence leading to his death December 1993. Documented in Mark Bowden&#x27;s Killing Pablo. The classified targeting capability deployed against a drug lord for a foreign government.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1993-12-01</begin><end>1993-12-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-75.5658,6.2476,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ramstein Air Base, Germany</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>USAFE-AFAFRICA headquarters. Key drone operations relay station - kill commands for Africa/Middle East routed through Ramstein. Largest U.S. military community outside the U.S. (~57,000 personnel + dependents). If the drone strikes a target in Yemen, the signal passes through Ramstein.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>7.6003,49.4369,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Aviano Air Base, Italy</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>31st Fighter Wing. NATO forward deployment for Mediterranean and Middle East operations. Used in Kosovo, Libya, Afghanistan campaigns. Southern European power projection.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>12.5965,46.0319,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Naval Support Activity Naples, Italy</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>U.S. Naval Forces Europe / Naval Forces Africa / Sixth Fleet headquarters. Commands naval operations across Europe and Africa from Italian soil.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>14.2815,40.815,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NAS Sigonella, Sicily, Italy</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>&#x27;Hub of the Med.&#x27; Primary logistics and ISR hub for Mediterranean, North Africa, and Middle East. Drone operations base. The surveillance eye in the center of the Mediterranean.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>14.9222,37.4017,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>RAF Lakenheath, Suffolk, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>48th Fighter Wing - only U.S. F-35A unit in Europe. Nuclear weapons storage capability. American nuclear weapons on British soil.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>0.5608,52.4093,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Naval Station Rota, Spain</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Four Aegis BMD destroyers forward-deployed. Supports Sixth Fleet Mediterranean operations. Gateway between Atlantic and Mediterranean.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-6.35,36.6375,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Souda Bay, Crete, Greece</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>NATO naval facility. Deepest natural harbor in the Mediterranean. U.S. munitions storage and logistics for eastern Mediterranean operations. Ancient Minoan territory now hosts missile storage.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>24.1194,35.4875,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Camp Bondsteel, Kosovo</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Largest U.S. military base in the Balkans. Built 1999 by Halliburton/KBR (Dick Cheney was Halliburton CEO 1995-2000). The VP&#x27;s company built the base the U.S. operates. 955 acres.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1999-01-01</begin><end>1999-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>21.2467,42.3592,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Thule Air Base, Greenland</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Northernmost U.S. base. Ballistic missile early warning (BMEWS). Space surveillance. Project Iceworm (1960s): secret nuclear missile tunnels under Greenland ice - Camp Century. Danish government was not informed.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1960-01-01</begin><end>1960-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-68.7031,76.5312,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Aegis Ashore, Deveselu, Romania</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>U.S. missile defense site on Romanian soil. Mk 41 launch system can also fire Tomahawk cruise missiles. The &#x27;defensive&#x27; system with offensive capability. Russia cites this as justification for its own deployments.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>24.3389,44.0342,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Aegis Ashore, Redzikowo, Poland</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Second European Aegis Ashore site. Operational 2023, 200 km from Russian Kaliningrad exclave. Same dual-use Mk 41 launchers as Deveselu.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-01-01</begin><end>2023-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>17.1003,54.4781,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>U.S. AFRICOM / EUCOM, Stuttgart, Germany</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Kelley Barracks - headquarters for both U.S. Africa Command and U.S. European Command. AFRICOM commands operations across 53 African nations from European soil - the command structure never left the continent.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.1178,48.6914,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Landstuhl Regional Medical Center, Germany</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Largest U.S. military hospital outside the U.S. All combat casualties from Middle East/Africa theaters transit through Landstuhl. The hospital that receives the bodies from the wars commanded by Stuttgart.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>7.5422,49.3914,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Grafenwöhr Training Area, Germany</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Largest U.S. military training area in Europe. 232 sq km. Used continuously since 1910 - through both World Wars, Cold War, and present. American soldiers train on the same Bavarian ground the Imperial German Army used.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1910-01-01</begin><end>1910-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>11.9322,49.6903,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Al Udeid Air Base, Qatar</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Combined Air Operations Center (CAOC) - commands all U.S. air operations across Middle East. 10,000+ U.S. personnel. Qatar hosts both Al Udeid AND Al Jazeera - the base that commands the bombing and the network that broadcasts it in the same 4,468 sq mi country.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>51.315,25.1174,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Camp Arifjan, Kuwait</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>U.S. Army Central (ARCENT) forward headquarters. Third Army. Largest ground force concentration in the Middle East. Pre-positioned equipment for rapid regional deployment.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>48.0822,29.1819,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NSA Bahrain - U.S. Fifth Fleet HQ</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Commander, Naval Forces Central Command / U.S. Fifth Fleet. Controls naval operations from the Suez Canal to the Strait of Hormuz. Based in a Sunni-ruled kingdom with a Shia majority population.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>50.565,26.2361,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Incirlik Air Base, Turkey</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>NATO nuclear weapons storage - estimated 50 B61 nuclear bombs. U.S. has stored nuclear weapons in Turkey since 1959. Turkey threatened to deny access during 2003 Iraq invasion and 2019 Syria operation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2003-01-01</begin><end>2003-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>35.4258,37.0017,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Al Dhafra Air Base, UAE</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>U.S., French, and UAE Air Forces co-located. RQ-4 Global Hawk and U-2 reconnaissance aircraft. Spy planes from three countries share one runway.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>54.5475,24.2481,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Air Base 201, Agadez, Niger</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>$110M U.S. drone base. MQ-9 Reaper operations. Niger&#x27;s 2023 coup expelled U.S. forces - base handed over. Russia/Wagner Group moved in. The $110M drone base evacuated in months, now occupied by the competitor.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-01-01</begin><end>2023-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>7.9869,16.9667,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Camp Humphreys, South Korea</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Largest overseas U.S. military base. $11B construction. USFK headquarters. 3,500 acres, 42,000 personnel. The largest U.S. foreign base on the planet, 35 miles from the DMZ.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.0314,36.9628,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Osan Air Base, South Korea</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>51st Fighter Wing. Closest U.S. air base to North Korea. Nuclear-capable aircraft. 48 miles from Seoul, 64 miles from DMZ.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.03,37.0908,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fleet Activities Yokosuka, Japan</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Home port of the U.S. Seventh Fleet. Forward-deployed carrier strike group. The only forward-deployed U.S. carrier is based in Japan. Commands the Pacific from another nation&#x27;s harbor.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.6536,35.2833,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kadena Air Base, Okinawa, Japan</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Largest U.S. air base in the Pacific. 18th Wing. Okinawa hosts 70% of U.S. military facilities in Japan on 0.6% of Japan&#x27;s land. The island is 0.6% of territory hosting 70% of the bases.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.7681,26.3517,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>MCAS Futenma, Okinawa, Japan</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Marine Corps Air Station in the center of Ginowan city (pop. 100,000). &#x27;Most dangerous base in the world.&#x27; Agreed to relocate in 1996. Still there in 2026. 30 years of promising to move.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1996-01-01</begin><end>1996-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>127.7553,26.2742,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Yokota Air Base, Tokyo, Japan</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>USFJ headquarters and Fifth Air Force. Located in western Tokyo - the capital of a sovereign nation hosts foreign military command. Yokota controls the airspace over greater Tokyo. Japanese commercial aircraft route around U.S. military airspace over their own capital.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.3487,35.7485,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Andersen AFB + Naval Base Guam</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Pacific power projection hub. B-52, B-1, B-2 bomber rotations. $8.7B military buildup underway. Nuclear submarine port. Guam has no vote in Congress but hosts bombers projecting power across the Pacific.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>144.9244,13.5839,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Guantanamo Bay Naval Base, Cuba</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>45 sq mi on Cuban soil. Lease since 1903 - $4,085/year (Cuba refuses to cash checks since 1959). Detention facility since 2002 - outside U.S. legal jurisdiction. 780 detainees total; 9 ever convicted.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1903-01-01</begin><end>1903-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-75.0961,19.9023,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Soto Cano Air Base, Honduras</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Joint Task Force-Bravo. U.S. military presence in Central America since Cold War. Same Honduras where ISA ran Operation Queens Hunter. Proximity to School of Americas graduates who governed the region.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.6212,14.3822,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CFS Leitrim, Ottawa, Canada</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Canadian Forces Station Leitrim. CSE (Communications Security Establishment) SIGINT facility. Five Eyes Canadian signals intelligence node. Canada&#x27;s primary electronic surveillance station.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-75.63,45.3414,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chinese Naval Support Base, Djibouti</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>China&#x27;s first overseas military base, operational 2017. 2 km from Camp Lemonnier (U.S.). The two largest economies have military bases within 2 km of each other on African soil.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-01-01</begin><end>2017-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>43.0581,11.5925,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fiery Cross Reef, South China Sea (China)</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Artificial island on submerged reef. 3,000m runway, hangars, radar, missile systems. The Hague ruled China&#x27;s claims have &#x27;no legal basis&#x27; (2016). China rejected the ruling.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2016-01-01</begin><end>2016-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>112.89,9.55,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Naval Facility Tartus, Syria (Russia)</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Russia&#x27;s only Mediterranean naval base. Russia&#x27;s entire Mediterranean naval presence depends on this Syrian port since 1971.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1971-01-01</begin><end>1971-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>35.8867,34.89,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Khmeimim Air Base, Syria (Russia)</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Russian air operations base since September 2015. Su-35, Su-34, Su-24 combat aircraft. Latakia province - the Assad family&#x27;s home territory hosts Russia&#x27;s air force.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2015-09-01</begin><end>2015-09-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>35.9456,35.4131,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Khyber Pass, Pakistan-Afghanistan Border</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>2,400-year-old logistics corridor. Alexander the Great, Timur, Mughal Empire, British Empire, Soviet supply interdiction, NATO supply route. 1,670m elevation, 53 km long. The same pass used for 2,400 years of military logistics - the geography doesn&#x27;t change, only the uniforms.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>71.0956,34.0583,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CFB Esquimalt, British Columbia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Royal Canadian Navy Pacific fleet headquarters. Maritime Forces Pacific. Nanoose Bay torpedo testing range. Canadian Pacific naval projection - the other Five Eyes navy on the Pacific Rim.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-123.4139,48.4322,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Murmansk - Northern Fleet HQ, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Russian Northern Fleet: nuclear submarine force, aircraft carriers. Ice-free Arctic port (Gulf Stream). Polyarny, Gadzhiyevo, and Vidyayevo submarine bases nearby. Largest concentration of nuclear weapons in the world per square kilometer.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>33.0827,68.9585,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kaliningrad, Russia - Baltic Exclave</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Russian exclave between Poland and Lithuania. Iskander nuclear-capable missiles. Baltic Fleet headquarters. Formerly Königsberg (German) until 1945. The territory Russia kept after WWII, wedged into NATO&#x27;s eastern flank. Suwalki Gap - 65 km border between Kaliningrad and Belarus - NATO&#x27;s most vulnerable corridor.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1945-01-01</begin><end>1945-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>20.4522,54.7104,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sevastopol, Crimea - Black Sea Fleet</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Russian Black Sea Fleet headquarters since 1783. Underground submarine base at Balaklava (Cold War, carved into mountain, designed to survive nuclear strike). Crimea annexed 2014. The port that caused the Crimean War (1853), influenced the Cold War, and triggered the current war.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2014-01-01</begin><end>2014-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>33.5254,44.6167,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vladivostok - Pacific Fleet Submarine Bases</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Pacific Fleet nuclear submarine bases: Rybachiy (SSBN base, Kamchatka) and Pavlovskoye. Borei-class SSBNs carrying Bulava SLBMs (10 MIRV warheads each). Russia&#x27;s Pacific nuclear deterrent hides in these ports.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>132.73,42.9,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Plesetsk Cosmodrome, Arkhangelsk Oblast, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>World&#x27;s most active launch site by total launches (~1,600+). Originally SS-7 ICBM base (1957). Now launches military satellites, GLONASS navigation constellation, and Angara rockets. Northernmost orbital launch facility. Existence denied until 1983 despite Western intelligence tracking launches since 1966.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1957-01-01</begin><end>1957-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>40.5777,62.9271,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kronstadt Naval Fortress, St. Petersburg, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Baltic Fleet base since 1704 (Peter the Great). Island fortress guarding St. Petersburg. 1921 Kronstadt Rebellion - sailors who made the Revolution revolted against it; crushed by Trotsky. Forts across the Gulf of Finland created kill zones for any naval approach. The fortress that guards the city that guards the Baltic.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1921-01-01</begin><end>1921-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>29.7714,59.9961,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Severodvinsk / Sevmash, Arkhangelsk Oblast, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Sevmash shipyard - Russia&#x27;s sole nuclear submarine construction facility. Every Russian nuclear submarine ever built was constructed here. Borei-class (SSBN), Yasen-class (SSGN), Belgorod (special missions submarine carrying Poseidon nuclear torpedo). Closed city. One shipyard builds the entire undersea nuclear deterrent.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>39.8302,64.5635,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nizhny Tagil - Uralvagonzavod, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>World&#x27;s largest tank factory. T-72, T-90, T-14 Armata production. 30,000+ employees. Built during WWII industrial evacuation east of Urals. Also manufactures rail cars (civilian cover for military production line). The factory floor that has produced more main battle tanks than any facility in history.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>60.0544,56.9225,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Jianggezhuang Submarine Base, Qingdao, China</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>PLA Navy North Sea Fleet nuclear submarine base. Underground pens visible in satellite imagery. China&#x27;s nuclear submarine deterrent - the underwater component of the second-strike capability.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>120.67,36.04,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Yulin Naval Base, Hainan, China</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Underground submarine base with tunnel entrance. Type 094 Jin-class SSBNs (JL-2 nuclear missiles). South China Sea access to deep water - submarines can dive to operating depth immediately upon exiting the tunnel. The mountain opens and nuclear submarines emerge.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>109.55,18.22,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>London City Airport</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; airport</p><p>Opened 1987 in Docklands redevelopment zone. Short runway (1,508m) - steep approach angle. Surrounded by financial district. Canary Wharf, HSBC, Barclays, Citigroup all within 2 miles. The private airport for the banking sector - built on former Royal Docks.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1987-01-01</begin><end>1987-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>0.0553,51.5053,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Diego Garcia Air Base, British Indian Ocean Territory</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; airport</p><p>Secret U.S./UK military base. 12,000-ft runway. B-52, B-2 stealth bomber operations. Entire Chagossian population forcibly removed (1968-73) - 2,000 people deported to make way for the base. ICJ advisory opinion (2019): UK sovereignty illegal. Population still exiled.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1968-01-01</begin><end>1968-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>72.4111,-7.3133,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>RAF Ascension Island, South Atlantic</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; airport</p><p>Wideawake Airfield - 10,000-ft runway on volcanic island. Critical relay for Falklands War logistics. NASA tracking station. GCHQ/NSA signals intelligence. Shared between military, intelligence, and space agencies on a volcanic rock in the mid-Atlantic.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-14.3517,-7.9467,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Masirah Island Air Base, Oman</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; airport</p><p>Remote island airbase, Arabian Sea. Former RAF, now Royal Air Force of Oman with U.S. access agreements. Staging point for Iraq/Afghanistan operations. Desert One (1980 Iran hostage rescue attempt) staged from here. Remote basing for regional force projection.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1980-01-01</begin><end>1980-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>58.8904,20.6754,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lajes Field, Terceira, Azores</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; airport</p><p>Mid-Atlantic staging base. Used for Iraq War rendition flights. Cold War: nuclear weapons storage (confirmed by declassified documents). Portuguese sovereignty, American operations. The mid-ocean refueling stop for everything that shouldn&#x27;t land on the mainland.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-27.091,38.7618,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>London City Island, Leamouth Peninsula</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>New-build luxury residential island in London Docklands. English National Ballet, London Film School. Built on former industrial land at Leamouth where the River Lea meets the Thames. Named &#x27;City Island&#x27; - a manufactured island identity for real estate marketing. Part of the Canning Town/Canary Wharf financial corridor redevelopment.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.0044,51.5078,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Isle of Dogs, London</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Canary Wharf sits on the Isle of Dogs - former West India Docks built on slave trade profits (1802). East India Company warehouses. Now: HSBC, Barclays, Morgan Stanley, Citigroup, JPMorgan towers. The slave trade docks became the banking district. The geography changed uses, not function.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1802-01-01</begin><end>1802-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.0178,51.4933,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>BlackRock HQ, New York City</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>$10 trillion AUM (2024) - largest asset manager on Earth. Aladdin platform: AI risk management system monitoring $21.6T in assets. Larry Fink: former First Boston mortgage trader. BlackRock advises the Federal Reserve on bond purchases - the asset manager advising the central bank on buying the assets it manages.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2024-01-01</begin><end>2024-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-74.0021,40.7539,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vanguard HQ, Malvern, Pennsylvania</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>$8.1 trillion AUM. Largest mutual fund provider. Vanguard is BlackRock&#x27;s largest shareholder. BlackRock is Vanguard&#x27;s largest shareholder. Circular ownership - the two largest pools of capital on Earth own each other by design.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-75.5146,40.043,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>State Street HQ, Boston</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>$4.1 trillion AUM. Third member of the &#x27;Big Three&#x27; - BlackRock, Vanguard, State Street together hold 20%+ of most S&amp;P 500 companies. Three firms, one vote. Custodial bank for the world&#x27;s institutional money. The Big Three collectively are the largest shareholder in 88% of S&amp;P 500 companies.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-71.0565,42.3555,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Booz Allen Hamilton, McLean, Virginia</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>3 miles from CIA headquarters. Edward Snowden was a Booz Allen contractor when he leaked NSA documents. 99% of revenue from government contracts. The consulting firm whose employees have security clearances - the privatization of intelligence work.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.1772,38.9236,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Halliburton, Houston, Texas</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Dick Cheney: CEO (1995-2000), then Vice President (2001-2009). No-bid Iraq War contracts: $39.5 billion. KBR subsidiary: military logistics, base construction, food services. The CEO of the defense contractor became Vice President, then gave contracts to his former company.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1995-01-01</begin><end>1995-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-95.4345,29.7532,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lausanne, Switzerland - IOC Headquarters</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>International Olympic Committee HQ since 1915. Tax-exempt. IOC members: diplomatic immunity. $7.6B revenue per Olympic cycle. Thomas Bach (current president): former fencer, Adidas board member. The organization that sells amateur athletics for billions while paying zero tax in Switzerland.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1915-01-01</begin><end>1915-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>6.6323,46.5197,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CIA Headquarters, Langley, Virginia - Art Collection</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>CIA Fine Arts Commission: over 100 works decorating Langley. CIA funded Abstract Expressionism during Cold War via Congress for Cultural Freedom. Jackson Pollock, Mark Rothko, Robert Motherwell - exhibited globally as proof of American &#x27;freedom&#x27; vs Soviet realism. Tom Braden (CIA): &#x27;I&#x27;m glad the CIA funded abstract art.&#x27; The agency that weaponized modern art.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.1464,38.951,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Museum of Modern Art (MoMA), New York - CIA Cultural Front</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Nelson Rockefeller: MoMA president, also CIA-connected. International Council of MoMA organized touring exhibitions of Abstract Expressionism - funded secretly by CIA. Frances Stonor Saunders documented this in &#x27;The Cultural Cold War.&#x27; MoMA as intelligence asset. The museum as soft power projection.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.9776,40.7614,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Broken Obelisk - Barnett Newman, Rothko Chapel, Houston</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Barnett Newman&#x27;s &#x27;Broken Obelisk&#x27; (1963-69). Inverted obelisk balanced on pyramid apex - the obelisk broken, power inverted. Dedicated to Martin Luther King Jr. Sits in reflecting pool outside Rothko Chapel. The obelisk of power, snapped and turned upside down. Newman: &#x27;The self, terrible and constant, is for me the subject of painting.&#x27; The anti-monument.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1963-01-01</begin><end>1963-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-95.3961,29.7374,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vigeland Sculpture Park (Frognerparken), Oslo</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Gustav Vigeland: 212 bronze and granite sculptures. The Monolith: 14.12m granite column of 121 intertwined human figures - carved from single block over 14 years. Wheel of Life, Fountain of cosmic cycles. Entire human lifecycle depicted: birth, struggle, death, transcendence. The largest sculpture park by a single artist in the world. Vigeland&#x27;s obsession: the human body as architecture of existence.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>10.7013,59.9271,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>The Alamo (Astor Place Cube), New York City</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Tony Rosenthal&#x27;s &#x27;Alamo&#x27; (1967). 8-foot cor-ten steel cube balanced on vertex - rotates when pushed. The spinning cube at the intersection. Cube geometry: Kaaba (Mecca), Black Cube of Saturn symbolism, Borg (Star Trek), 2001: A Space Odyssey monolith. The cube that invites you to spin it. Public art as participatory occult geometry.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1967-01-01</begin><end>1967-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9912,40.7296,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>The Sphere (Koenig), Originally WTC Plaza, Now Liberty Park</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Fritz Koenig&#x27;s &#x27;The Sphere&#x27; (1971). Originally centered in WTC Austin J. Tobin Plaza - between the Twin Towers. Survived 9/11 damaged but intact. Moved to Battery Park, then Liberty Park (2017). The sculpture that stood between two towers and survived their fall. Originally symbolized &#x27;world peace through world trade.&#x27; Now a memorial. The sphere between the towers.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1971-01-01</begin><end>1971-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-74.0134,40.7115,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cloud Gate (The Bean), Chicago</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Anish Kapoor, 2006. 110-ton polished stainless steel. Reflects and distorts the Chicago skyline - the viewer sees themselves warped. Kapoor: exclusive license to Vantablack (blackest substance on Earth) - no other artist may use it. The artist who owns a color. The sculpture that shows you a distorted version of yourself. The mirror that lies.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2006-01-01</begin><end>2006-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-87.6233,41.8827,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vessel (Hudson Yards), New York City</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Thomas Heatherwick, 2019. $200M, 154 flights of stairs going nowhere. Nicknamed &#x27;The Shawarma.&#x27; Three suicides in 18 months - closed. Stephen Ross (developer): Trump fundraiser, Equinox/SoulCycle owner. Hudson Yards: $25B luxury development on railyard - largest private real estate development in U.S. history. The monument to going nowhere, built on nothing, funded by everything.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-74.0013,40.7532,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Charging Bull, Bowling Green, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Arturo Di Modica, 1989. Installed guerrilla-style after 1987 stock market crash. 3.5-ton bronze bull - symbol of aggressive financial optimism. Tourists rub its testicles for luck. &#x27;Fearless Girl&#x27; (State Street Global Advisors marketing campaign) placed opposite 2017. The bull that represents Wall Street&#x27;s self-image: unstoppable, virile, charging forward. The sculpture the financial industry adopted as its totem.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1989-01-01</begin><end>1989-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-74.0134,40.7056,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kapoor&#x27;s Sky Mirror, Rockefeller Center, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Anish Kapoor, 2006. 35-foot polished steel concave mirror tilted at angle - reflects sky into ground, ground into sky. Installed at Rockefeller Center - the Rockefeller family compound. The sky inverted in front of the building of the family that shaped the 20th century. Kapoor: &#x27;I&#x27;m interested in a notion of art that engages the mythical.&#x27; The portal in front of the power center.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2006-01-01</begin><end>2006-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9787,40.7587,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kaaba, Masjid al-Haram, Mecca</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>The Black Cube. 13.1m x 11.03m x 12.86m. Black silk cloth (kiswah) replaced annually. Believed built by Ibrahim (Abraham). Black Stone (al-Hajar al-Aswad) set in eastern corner - pre-Islamic, possibly meteoritic. 2M+ circumambulate during Hajj. The cube that 1.8 billion people face five times daily. The original cube. Every other cube sculpture references this, whether it knows it or not.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>39.8262,21.4225,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nevelson Chapel / Chapel of the Good Shepherd - Louise Nevelson, NYC</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Louise Nevelson: white-painted wood assemblages creating monolithic wall sculptures - essentially cubes and boxes nested within boxes. Chapel of the Good Shepherd at St. Peter&#x27;s Church, NYC: entire environment as sculpture. The church inside the sculpture inside the box. Nevelson&#x27;s work: the cube repeated, stacked, nested, until the wall becomes architecture.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.971,40.7527,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lateran Obelisk, Piazza San Giovanni, Rome</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Tallest standing ancient Egyptian obelisk: 32.18m (105.6 ft). Originally erected at Karnak by Thutmose III (1425 BC). Moved to Alexandria by Constantine II, then to Rome 357 AD. Fell, buried, re-erected 1588 by Pope Sixtus V. The oldest, tallest obelisk - moved by three empires across 3,000 years.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1588-01-01</begin><end>1588-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.5063,41.8859,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Flaminio Obelisk, Piazza del Popolo, Rome</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>From Heliopolis, Egypt. Erected by Pharaoh Ramesses II (1213 BC). Augustus brought it to Rome in 10 BC after conquering Egypt. The conqueror&#x27;s trophy: take the enemy&#x27;s religious monument and put it in your plaza. Every obelisk in Rome is a stolen sacred object.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>12.4764,41.9106,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Montecitorio Obelisk, Rome - Sundial</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>From Heliopolis. Erected by Psamtik II (590 BC). Augustus used it as gnomon of the Horologium Augusti - a solar meridian line (sundial) in the Campus Martius. The obelisk that tells time. Power measured by the shadow it casts.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>12.4794,41.9009,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Obelisk of Theodosius, Istanbul (Hippodrome)</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Lower portion of obelisk of Thutmose III (originally 30m, now 18.54m). Brought from Karnak to Alexandria by Constantine, then to Constantinople by Theodosius I (390 AD). Marble base depicts Theodosius with captives. The obelisk that traveled through three empires: Egyptian → Roman → Byzantine → Ottoman (standing in its same spot as the Ottoman empire rose and fell around it).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>28.9752,41.0063,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Axum Obelisk (Stele), Axum, Ethiopia</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>24m tall, 1,700 years old. Aksumite Kingdom funerary marker. Looted by Mussolini&#x27;s troops (1937) - shipped to Rome. Ethiopia demanded return for 60 years. Finally returned 2005 - re-erected 2008. The obelisk stolen by a fascist dictator and returned only after decades of diplomacy. Italy kept it in Rome near the Circus Maximus. Colonialism as interior decorating.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1937-01-01</begin><end>1937-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>38.7176,14.1307,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Obelisk of Buenos Aires, Plaza de la República</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Built 1936. 67.5m tall. Commemorates 400th anniversary of first founding of Buenos Aires. Not ancient Egyptian - purpose-built. But the form is the message: Argentina declaring itself heir to the power lineage. Every modern city that builds an obelisk is making a claim about what kind of power it wields.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1936-01-01</begin><end>1936-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-58.3816,-34.6037,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Obelisco de São Paulo, Brazil</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Built 1947. 72m tall - taller than Washington Monument. Commemorates Constitutionalist Revolution (1932). In the Ibirapuera Park complex. South America&#x27;s largest obelisk. The obelisk as assertion: we too are an imperial power.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1947-01-01</begin><end>1947-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-46.655,-23.5875,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bunker Hill Monument, Charlestown, Boston</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>67m granite obelisk (1827-43). Commemorates Battle of Bunker Hill (1775). One of the earliest American obelisks - pre-dates Washington Monument. Masonic cornerstone laid by Marquis de Lafayette (1825). The American obelisk tradition begins here: military victory inscribed in Egyptian form. Why Egyptian? The founders&#x27; obsession with ancient architecture as legitimacy.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1827-01-01</begin><end>1827-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.0609,42.3763,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cleopatra&#x27;s Needle, Istanbul (Walled Obelisk)</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>The &#x27;Walled Obelisk&#x27; or Obelisk of Constantine VII: built 10th century AD as replacement for a collapsed bronze-plated obelisk. Stone core remains. Adjacent to the genuine Egyptian Obelisk of Theodosius. The empire that couldn&#x27;t steal an obelisk, so it built a copy. The copy next to the original. Istanbul has both.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>28.9758,41.0058,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Foro Italico Obelisk (Mussolini&#x27;s Obelisk), Rome</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>36m Carrara marble monolith inscribed &#x27;MVSSOLINI DVX.&#x27; Erected 1932 for the Fascist sports complex. Allied forces considered demolishing it after WWII but left it standing - too structurally integrated. The fascist obelisk they couldn&#x27;t tear down. Mussolini: inscribed his own name on an obelisk, in the city of stolen obelisks. The dictator as pharaoh.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1932-01-01</begin><end>1932-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.4561,41.9294,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Place Vendôme Column, Paris</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Not a traditional obelisk but a column - built by Napoleon (1810) from melted-down captured cannons (1,200 Austrian and Russian guns from Austerlitz). 44m tall, spiral reliefs modeled on Trajan&#x27;s Column. Destroyed by Paris Commune (1871), rebuilt. Gustave Courbet charged for reconstruction costs - fled to Switzerland, died in exile. The column made of enemy weapons, destroyed by revolutionaries, rebuilt by the state.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1810-01-01</begin><end>1810-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>2.3294,48.8675,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Piazza Navona Obelisk (Fountain of Four Rivers), Rome</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Bernini&#x27;s Fountain of Four Rivers (1651). Roman-made obelisk (not Egyptian import) - cut in Aswan granite imitating pharaonic style. Bernini: four river gods representing the four known continents. The Nile god&#x27;s head covered - because the Nile&#x27;s source was unknown. The obelisk sitting on a void: the power symbol whose origin even its makers didn&#x27;t fully understand.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1651-01-01</begin><end>1651-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.4729,41.899,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Psychiatrisch Ziekenhuis Wolfheze (Pro Persona), Netherlands</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Founded 1906 as psychiatric hospital. 86-hectare campus in Wolfheze woods. WWII: British 1st Airborne gliders landed on hospital grounds during Operation Market Garden (Sept 17, 1944). German bombing killed 81 patients and staff. Entire institutional chain - Psychiatrisch Ziekenhuis Wolfheze → De Gelderse Roos → Pro Persona - is absent from Wikipedia (all three are REDLINKS). 5 buildings are listed municipal monuments: Hoofdgebouw, Sonneheerdt, kerkgebouw, de Vlinder, watertoren (1907, architect E. Knevel). 1.3km from Bilderberg Hotel through connected woodland. A 100+ year institution with 86 hectares and WWII bombing casualties has zero encyclopedia presence.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1944-09-17</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>5.7864,52.0042,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Deelen Air Base (Fliegerhorst Deelen), Netherlands</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>WWII Luftwaffe Nachtjagd (night fighter) central command - Gefechtsstand Diogenes bunker controlled all German night fighter operations over Northwestern Europe. Dedicated military railway connected Wolfheze station to Deelen. Post-war: Royal Netherlands Air Force base. 4km north of Bilderberg Hotel. The command bunker that directed aerial defense of the Reich had its supply line running through the same woods where Bilderberg meets.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>5.8731,52.0606,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hotel Hartenstein / Airborne Museum, Oosterbeek</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>British 1st Airborne Division headquarters during Battle of Arnhem, Operation Market Garden (Sept 17-25, 1944). General Roy Urquhart commanded from this hotel. Of 10,000 British airborne troops, only 2,398 escaped across the Rhine. Now the Airborne Museum Hartenstein. 600m west of Bilderberg Hotel on the same Utrechtseweg. The hotel where a battle was lost became a museum; the hotel 600m east where power meets became the Bilderberg.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1944-01-01</begin><end>1944-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>5.8325,51.9881,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Laag Wolfheze Estate, Oosterbeek</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Rijksmonument 523653/523654/523655. Manor house at Utrechtseweg 321, built 1919 by architect ir. Samuel de Clercq. Gardens designed by Samuel Voorhoeve (1920). A nationally protected heritage estate on the same Utrechtseweg corridor as the Bilderberg Hotel - yet has NO Wikipedia article in any language. The Wikipedia article for a Rijksmonument returns 404.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1919-01-01</begin><end>1919-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>5.8003,51.9883,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bilderberg Estate Boundary Post, Oosterbeek</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Municipal monument: &#x27;grenspaal v.m. landgoed de Bilderberg&#x27; - boundary post of the former Bilderberg estate at intersection of Utrechtseweg and Wolfhezerweg. The estate (Landgoed de Bilderberg) that the hotel sits on has NO Wikipedia article. The hotel itself has no Dutch Wikipedia article. The boundary post marking where the estate begins is a listed monument - but the estate it marks is undocumented.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>5.8136,51.9881,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>De Witte Poort (The White Gate), Oosterbeek</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Villa &#x27;De Witte Poort&#x27; - The White Gate - Utrechtseweg, Oosterbeek. Built circa 1850. Municipal monument. Part of the 19th-century villa corridor along Utrechtseweg where wealthy Dutch families built estates. White-painted gate/entrance structure. White paint = wealth signal (expensive lead white/titanium dioxide vs. cheap red iron oxide barnpaint). The white gate on the road to the Bilderberg.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1850-01-01</begin><end>1850-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>5.828,51.9875,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kasteel Doorwerth, Renkum</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Medieval castle dating to approximately 1260. Rijksmonument. On the Rhine river in Renkum municipality - same municipality as Bilderberg Hotel, Wolfheze, and the entire Utrechtseweg corridor. One of the oldest intact castles in Gelderland province. The corridor from Kasteel Doorwerth to Bilderberg Hotel spans 800 years of Dutch power architecture.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>5.7944,51.9631,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Howard Lutnick / Cantor Fitzgerald, NYC</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Born July 14, 1961. CEO and Chairman of Cantor Fitzgerald - 658 of 960 employees killed on 9/11 (floors 101-105 of One WTC). Lutnick survived because he was taking his son to first day of kindergarten. Rebuilt the firm. Became 41st U.S. Secretary of Commerce (Feb 2025). Co-chaired Trump transition team. Tether cryptocurrency: Cantor Fitzgerald holds $80B+ in U.S. Treasury securities backing USDT stablecoin. Visited Jeffrey Epstein&#x27;s Little Saint James island December 2012. Owned property at 11 East 71st Street - adjacent to Epstein&#x27;s Manhattan residence. $806M+ in assets. Board: WTC Memorial Foundation, Partnership for NYC, Weill Cornell Medicine.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1961-07-14</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-74.0134,40.7127,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hunneschans (Early Medieval Fortification), Heveadorp</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Early medieval fortification (circa 1000 AD) in Heveadorp, Renkum municipality. Part of the deep historical layering of the Bilderberg corridor - from Neolithic burial mounds (4000+ years old) through medieval fortifications through 19th-century estates to the 1954 Bilderberg Meeting. The same woodland has been a site of power and strategic significance for millennia.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1954-01-01</begin><end>1954-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>5.785,51.9722,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>New York Stock Exchange, 11 Wall Street</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>The NYSE is the world&#x27;s largest stock exchange by market capitalization of listed companies, exceeding US$28 trillion, operating from its 1903 Beaux-Arts building at 11 Wall Street. Trading is now electronic but the floor remains the symbolic center of American equity capital. Source: Wikipedia, New York Stock Exchange; NYSE (nyse.com).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1903-01-01</begin><end>1903-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-74.0112,40.7071,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>London Stock Exchange, Paternoster Square</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>The London Stock Exchange, founded in 1801 and now headquartered at 10 Paternoster Square beside St Paul&#x27;s Cathedral, is one of the world&#x27;s oldest exchanges and the primary listing venue for the City of London. Its parent LSEG is a global markets-infrastructure and data firm. Source: Wikipedia, London Stock Exchange; LSEG (lseg.com).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1801-01-01</begin><end>1801-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.0991,51.515,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Federal Reserve Bank of New York Gold Vault, 33 Liberty St</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>The vault 80 feet below 33 Liberty Street held roughly 507,000 gold bars weighing about 6,331 metric tons as of 2024 — the world&#x27;s largest known gold depository, larger than Fort Knox. Nearly all of it is stored on behalf of foreign central banks and international organizations such as the IMF. Source: Federal Reserve Bank of New York (newyorkfed.org/aboutthefed/goldvault.html).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-74.0085,40.7082,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>European Central Bank, Frankfurt</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>The ECB, in its twin-tower headquarters completed in 2014 around the historic Grossmarkthalle, sets monetary policy for the euro area (20 member states) and is the primary supervisor of the eurozone&#x27;s largest banks. It is the central pillar of European monetary power. Source: Wikipedia, European Central Bank; ECB (ecb.europa.eu).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2014-01-01</begin><end>2014-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>8.7029,50.1096,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bank of England, Threadneedle Street</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Founded in 1694 and nicknamed &#x27;The Old Lady of Threadneedle Street,&#x27; the Bank of England is the UK&#x27;s central bank and holds one of the world&#x27;s largest gold reserves in its vaults — around 400,000 bars for the UK and other nations&#x27; central banks. It sets UK monetary policy and underpins the City of London. Source: Bank of England (bankofengland.co.uk); Wikipedia, Bank of England.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1694-01-01</begin><end>1694-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.0889,51.5142,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>International Monetary Fund HQ, Washington D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>The IMF, established at Bretton Woods in 1944 and headquartered two blocks from the White House, has 190 member countries and provides balance-of-payments loans whose conditions shape the economic policy of borrowing nations. Its lending capacity runs to roughly US$1 trillion. Source: International Monetary Fund (imf.org); Wikipedia, International Monetary Fund.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1944-01-01</begin><end>1944-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.0442,38.8989,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Île Longue SSBN Base - Brest, France</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Selected by Charles de Gaulle in 1965 and operational since 1972, Île Longue in the Brest roadstead is the main base for France&#x27;s Force Océanique Stratégique — its four Triomphant-class ballistic-missile submarines — and stores the warheads and missile fuel. Around 2,400 military and civilian personnel staff one of France&#x27;s most sensitive sites. Source: GlobalSecurity.org, &#x27;l&#x27;Ile Longue&#x27;; Naval Technology.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1965-01-01</begin><end>1965-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-4.5081,48.3043,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nevatim Airbase - F-35I Hub, Negev, Israel</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Nevatim, 15 km east-southeast of Beersheba in the Negev, is one of Israel&#x27;s largest air bases and the primary hub for its F-35I &#x27;Adir&#x27; stealth fighters, hosting three squadrons (140, 116 and 117). Built 1980–1983 with joint Israeli-US funding after the Sinai withdrawal, it was struck by Iranian ballistic missiles in 2024. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Nevatim Airbase&#x27;; GlobalSecurity.org.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1980-01-01</begin><end>1980-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>35.0302,31.205,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Berbera Airbase - UAE Military Foothold, Somaliland</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Under a 2017 agreement, the UAE established a military base at the Gulf of Aden port of Berbera, roughly 250 km from Yemen; its Soviet-built 2.6-mile runway can host fighters, heavy transports and drones. Satellite imagery from late 2025 shows renewed expansion including ammunition depots and around a dozen underground bunkers overlooking the Bab el-Mandeb. Source: BBC News; Middle East Eye; Sri Lanka Guardian (satellite analysis).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-01-01</begin><end>2017-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>44.9415,10.3872,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Offutt AFB - U.S. Strategic Command (STRATCOM) HQ, Nebraska</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Offutt AFB near Omaha — home of Strategic Air Command from 1948 — is headquarters of U.S. Strategic Command, responsible for the nation&#x27;s nuclear deterrent, global strike and nuclear command-and-control. A new $1.3 billion command-and-control facility, the Gen. Curtis E. LeMay Building, was dedicated there in 2019. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;United States Strategic Command&#x27;; Military Times; GlobalSecurity.org.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1948-01-01</begin><end>1948-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-95.9082,41.1172,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>INS Kadamba (Project Seabird) - Karwar, India</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>INS Kadamba near Karwar on the Arabian Sea is the anchor of Project Seabird, India&#x27;s largest naval-infrastructure program; commissioned in 2005 and spread across 45 sq km with 23 km of coastline, its phased expansion is planned to make it the largest Indian naval base east of the Suez Canal, sited out of easy strike range of neighbours. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;INS Kadamba&#x27;; Byju&#x27;s / Testbook Project Seabird briefings.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2005-01-01</begin><end>2005-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>74.1223,14.7769,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Naval Base Simon&#x27;s Town - South Atlantic, South Africa</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Naval Base Simon&#x27;s Town near Cape Town is the South African Navy&#x27;s largest base and home to its frigate and submarine flotillas. A dockyard since 1743 and a Royal Navy station until handed to South Africa in 1957, it guards the strategic Cape sea route and the backdoor to the South Atlantic. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Naval Base Simon&#x27;s Town&#x27;; Simonstown Agreement.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1957-01-01</begin><end>1957-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>18.438,-34.1896,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bohemian Grove - Monte Rio, California</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>A 2,700-acre private redwood encampment owned by San Francisco&#x27;s all-male Bohemian Club, where each July roughly 2,000 elite members — including U.S. presidents, executives and officials — gather for the &#x27;Cremation of Care&#x27; ritual. Early Manhattan Project planning was discussed at the Grove in September 1942. Source: Bohemian Grove — Wikipedia / The Press Democrat.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1942-09-01</begin><end>1942-09-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-122.9991,38.4667,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>OECD Headquarters (Château de la Muette) - Paris</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>The 38-member Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development is headquartered at the Château de la Muette in the 16th arrondissement. The building was bought in 1948 by the OEEC, the body created to administer U.S. Marshall Plan aid, before it became the OECD in 1961. Source: OECD (oecd.org) / Wikipedia.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1948-01-01</begin><end>1948-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>2.2692,48.8617,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Atlantic Council - Washington, D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>The NATO-aligned foreign-policy think tank opened a new 80,000-square-foot global headquarters at 1400 L Street NW in November 2024, nearly double its previous size. Its funders have included Western governments, Gulf states and defense contractors, drawing scrutiny over donor influence on its research. Source: Atlantic Council press release (atlanticcouncil.org).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2024-11-01</begin><end>2024-11-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.0324,38.9035,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>National Endowment for Democracy (NED) - Washington, D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Created in 1983 as a congressionally funded grantmaking foundation, NED channels an annual congressional appropriation into more than 2,000 grants across roughly 100 countries. Co-founder Allen Weinstein famously said &#x27;a lot of what we do today was done covertly 25 years ago by the CIA.&#x27; Source: National Endowment for Democracy (ned.org) / Wikipedia.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1983-01-01</begin><end>1983-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.0285,38.8959,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Wilton Park (Wiston House) - Wiston, West Sussex</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>An executive agency of the UK Foreign, Commonwealth &amp; Development Office based since 1951 at the 16th-century Wiston House, Wilton Park convenes around 80 strategic policy dialogues a year, drawing roughly 3,500 officials and opinion-formers from over 120 countries in support of UK foreign policy. Source: Wilton Park (wiltonpark.org.uk) / Wikipedia.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1951-01-01</begin><end>1951-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.359,50.8998,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Freemasons&#x27; Hall (United Grand Lodge of England) - London</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Headquarters of the United Grand Lodge of England, the world&#x27;s oldest Grand Lodge, on a site used for Masonic meetings since 1775. The Art Deco building, erected 1927-1933 as a memorial to Freemasons killed in WWI, contains 22 lodge rooms and administers thousands of lodges across England and Wales. Source: Freemasons&#x27; Hall, London — Wikipedia / UGLE (ugle.org.uk).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1927-01-01</begin><end>1927-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.1208,51.5153,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Open Society Foundations HQ - New York</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>George Soros&#x27;s grantmaking network, founded in 1993, is headquartered at 224 West 57th Street in Manhattan. With an endowment of roughly $23 billion, it funds civil-society, human-rights and media groups worldwide and is a recurring target of political campaigns internationally. Source: Open Society Foundations — Wikipedia / GuideStar.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1993-01-01</begin><end>1993-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9815,40.7659,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Luxor Temple Standing Obelisk (Twin of the Concorde Obelisk)</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>The ~25 m red-granite obelisk of Ramesses II still stands at the entrance pylon of Luxor Temple; its twin was gifted to France in the 1830s and now stands in Paris&#x27;s Place de la Concorde. France formally renounced any claim to the remaining Luxor obelisk in 1981. Source: UNESCO World Heritage &#x27;Ancient Thebes with its Necropolis&#x27; / obelisks.org.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1830-01-01</begin><end>1830-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>32.6391,25.6995,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Wellington Testimonial (Wellington Monument), Phoenix Park, Dublin</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>At 62 m (203 ft), the granite obelisk to the Duke of Wellington, begun 1817 and completed only in 1861 due to funding shortfalls, is the tallest obelisk in Europe; its bronze relief plaques were cast from cannon captured at Waterloo. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Wellington Monument, Dublin&#x27; / Buildings of Ireland.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1817-01-01</begin><end>1817-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-6.3031,53.349,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Elephant and Obelisk (Pulcino della Minerva), Piazza della Minerva, Rome</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>A 6th-century BC Egyptian obelisk mounted on Bernini&#x27;s marble elephant, unveiled 1667 outside Santa Maria sopra Minerva beside the former seat of the Roman Inquisition and Dominican order; the Latin inscription frames the elephant as a symbol that a robust mind is needed to sustain solid wisdom. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Elephant and Obelisk&#x27; / Bernini catalogue.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1667-01-01</begin><end>1667-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.4775,41.8979,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Quirinal Obelisk, Piazza del Quirinale, Rome</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>A ~14.6 m ancient Roman obelisk moved from the Mausoleum of Augustus and re-erected in 1786 by Pope Pius VI between the colossal Dioscuri statues, directly before the Quirinal Palace - former papal residence and now the official residence of the President of the Italian Republic. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Obelisks of Rome&#x27; (Quirinal obelisk).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1786-01-01</begin><end>1786-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.4865,41.8993,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>San Jacinto Monument, La Porte, Texas</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>At 172.92 m (567.31 ft) and topped by a 220-ton Lone Star, this 1936-39 obelisk on the Houston Ship Channel is the world&#x27;s tallest masonry column, taller than the Washington Monument, commemorating the 1836 Battle of San Jacinto that secured Texan independence. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;San Jacinto Monument&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1936-01-01</begin><end>1936-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-95.09,29.732,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shaheed Minar (Ochterlony Monument), Kolkata</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>A 48 m column-obelisk built in 1828 to honor East India Company general David Ochterlony, fusing Egyptian, Syrian and Turkish motifs; independent India renamed it Shaheed Minar (&#x27;Martyrs&#x27; Tower&#x27;) in 1969, converting a colonial monument into a memorial to freedom fighters. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Shaheed Minar, Kolkata&#x27; / Maps of India.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1828-01-01</begin><end>1828-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>88.3493,22.5629,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Obelisk of Montevideo (a los Constituyentes de 1830), Uruguay</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>A 40 m three-sided pink-granite obelisk by sculptor Jose Luis Zorrilla de San Martin, inaugurated 1938 at the entrance to Parque Batlle, bearing three bronze figures for &#x27;Law&#x27;, &#x27;Liberty&#x27; and &#x27;Force&#x27; to honor the framers of Uruguay&#x27;s first 1830 constitution. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Obelisk of Montevideo&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1830-01-01</begin><end>1830-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-56.1644,-34.8974,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>SWIFT Headquarters, La Hulpe, Belgium</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>SWIFT, the cooperative that runs the dominant global interbank financial-messaging network, links more than 11,000 institutions across over 200 countries and carries tens of millions of messages daily. Control over SWIFT access has become a key instrument of financial sanctions, as when Russian banks were cut off in 2022. Source: Wikipedia, SWIFT (Society for Worldwide Interbank Financial Telecommunication).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-01-01</begin><end>2022-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>4.479,50.7346,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>DTCC, Jersey City</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>The Depository Trust &amp; Clearing Corporation clears and settles the vast majority of US securities transactions; in 2025 its subsidiaries processed transactions valued at roughly US$4.7 quadrillion. As the central securities depository, DTCC holds custody of most US stocks and bonds through its nominee, Cede &amp; Co. Source: Wikipedia, Depository Trust &amp; Clearing Corporation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2025-01-01</begin><end>2025-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-74.0346,40.7309,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ugland House, George Town, Cayman Islands</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>This five-story building, home to the law firm Maples and Calder, is the registered office for roughly 40,000 companies — a density that prompted President Obama to call it &#x27;either the biggest building or the biggest tax scam on record.&#x27; It is an icon of offshore corporate structuring. Source: Wikipedia, Ugland House; Foreign Policy, &#x27;House of 19,000 Corporations&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-81.3024,19.2886,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Corporation Trust Center, 1209 North Orange St, Delaware</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>This single Wilmington address is the registered-agent home to hundreds of thousands of entities — reported at over 285,000 in 2012 — including subsidiaries of Apple, Google, Coca-Cola and Walmart, exploiting Delaware&#x27;s corporate-secrecy and tax regime. Run by CT Corporation (Wolters Kluwer). Source: Wikipedia, Corporation Trust Center; Washington Free Beacon.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-75.5477,39.7485,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>People&#x27;s Bank of China, Beijing</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>The PBOC is the central bank of China, managing the world&#x27;s largest foreign-exchange reserves (over US$3 trillion) and issuing the renminbi. It pioneered a state-controlled central bank digital currency (the digital yuan / e-CNY) and is a central instrument of China&#x27;s financial statecraft. Source: Wikipedia, People&#x27;s Bank of China.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>116.3545,39.9072,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rothschild &amp; Co, New Court, London</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>New Court on St Swithin&#x27;s Lane has been the London seat of the Rothschild banking house since 1809; it hosted the twice-daily London gold &#x27;fixing&#x27; from 1919 until N M Rothschild withdrew in 2004. The firm remains a leading independent M&amp;A advisory house. Source: Wikipedia, Rothschild &amp; Co / N M Rothschild &amp; Sons.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1919-01-01</begin><end>1919-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.089,51.5123,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>HMNB Clyde (Faslane) - Trident Submarine Base, Scotland</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>HMNB Clyde at Faslane on the Gare Loch is the home port of the Royal Navy&#x27;s four Vanguard-class SSBNs carrying Trident II D5 missiles, providing the UK&#x27;s sole continuous-at-sea nuclear deterrent; the associated RNAD Coulport, 8 miles away, stores and processes the warheads. It is among the most heavily protected sites in Britain. Source: Nuclear Information Service, &#x27;Faslane and Coulport Nuclear Submarine Bases: A Briefing&#x27; (nuclearinfo.org); GlobalSecurity.org.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-5.8618,56.4603,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pokhran Test Range - Operation Shakti, Rajasthan, India</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>At the Pokhran Test Range in the Thar Desert, India conducted the Pokhran-II (Operation Shakti) series of five underground nuclear detonations on 11–13 May 1998, including a claimed 45-kiloton thermonuclear device, moving India to declared nuclear-weapons status and triggering international sanctions. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Pokhran-II&#x27;; Nuclear Weapon Archive, &#x27;Operation Shakti: 1998&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1998-05-13</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>71.9198,26.9199,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ream Naval Base - China-Backed Expansion, Cambodia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>China financed a major upgrade of Cambodia&#x27;s Ream Naval Base from 2022, adding a 300-metre deepwater pier, a 5,000-ton dry dock and a slipway; two Chinese Type-056A corvettes have been stationed there near-continuously since December 2023, prompting US concern it could become a PLA Navy foothold on the Gulf of Thailand. Source: CSIS Asia Maritime Transparency Initiative; Nikkei Asia; NPR (2025).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-12-01</begin><end>2023-12-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>103.6133,10.5058,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sohae Satellite Launching Station - Tongchang-ri, North Korea</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Sohae (Tongchang-ri) on North Korea&#x27;s northwest coast is the DPRK&#x27;s primary long-range rocket facility and the site of all seven of its satellite launch attempts since 2012, doubling as a testbed for ICBM development. Following Kim Jong Un&#x27;s March 2022 visit, satellite imagery has shown near-constant expansion of pads, an assembly building and a new sea port. Source: CSIS Beyond Parallel; 38 North; NTI Facilities Profile.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-03-01</begin><end>2022-03-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>124.3891,40.0985,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Natanz Nuclear Enrichment Complex - Iran</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Iran&#x27;s main uranium-enrichment site near Natanz houses underground halls designed for tens of thousands of gas centrifuges; around 2009–2010 the Stuxnet cyberweapon sabotaged its controllers, forcing Iran to decommission and replace roughly 1,000 centrifuges — the first known state-on-state destructive cyberattack on physical infrastructure. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Natanz nuclear facility&#x27;; Institute for Science and International Security (ISIS); IEEE Spectrum.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2009-01-01</begin><end>2009-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>51.9136,33.5071,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>HMAS Stirling (Fleet Base West) - AUKUS SRF-West, Australia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>HMAS Stirling on Garden Island off Rockingham is the Royal Australian Navy&#x27;s submarine home port and the designated site for AUKUS &#x27;Submarine Rotational Force – West&#x27;: from 2027 up to four US and one UK nuclear-powered submarines will rotate through, backed by an Australian investment of up to A$8 billion. Source: Australian Submarine Agency (asa.gov.au); Australian Dept of Defence.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>115.7264,-32.2972,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Khan Research Laboratories - Kahuta, Pakistan</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>The Khan Research Laboratories at Kahuta, founded in 1976 by A.Q. Khan using centrifuge blueprints taken from URENCO in the Netherlands, is Pakistan&#x27;s main gas-centrifuge uranium-enrichment and nuclear-weapons lab; it began producing highly enriched uranium in 1986 and is not subject to IAEA safeguards. Source: Federation of American Scientists; GlobalSecurity.org; Atomic Heritage Foundation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1976-01-01</begin><end>1976-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>73.3882,33.5913,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>World Economic Forum HQ - Cologny, Geneva</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>The WEF, founded by Klaus Schwab in 1971, runs from its lakeside headquarters at 91-93 Route de la Capite in Cologny, Geneva. It maintains a top &#x27;Strategic Partner&#x27; tier of roughly 100 of the world&#x27;s largest corporations that pay premium membership fees and shape its agenda. Source: World Economic Forum / Geneva Environment Network (genevaenvironmentnetwork.org).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1971-01-01</begin><end>1971-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>6.1922,46.2247,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Davos Congress Centre - WEF Annual Meeting, Davos</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>The 12,000-square-metre Congress Centre has hosted the World Economic Forum&#x27;s flagship annual meeting since 1971, drawing around 3,000 heads of state, CEOs and financiers each January under heavy security. The venue can accommodate up to 5,000 participants across a plenum and 34 rooms. Source: Davos Congress Centre — Wikipedia / davos.ch.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1971-01-01</begin><end>1971-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>9.827,46.7978,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chatham House (Royal Institute of International Affairs) - London</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Founded in 1920, Chatham House occupies a Grade I-listed former residence of three British prime ministers at 10 St James&#x27;s Square, donated to the institute in 1923. It originated the globally used &#x27;Chatham House Rule&#x27; of source non-attribution and is consistently ranked among the world&#x27;s most influential think tanks. Source: Chatham House (chathamhouse.org) / Wikipedia.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1920-01-01</begin><end>1920-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.1278,51.5074,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Munich Security Conference - Hotel Bayerischer Hof, Munich</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Held annually since 1963 at the Hotel Bayerischer Hof, the Munich Security Conference is the world&#x27;s leading forum on international security policy, gathering heads of state, defense ministers and NATO leadership. Landmark speeches there, including Vladimir Putin&#x27;s 2007 address, have marked shifts in global geopolitics. Source: Munich Security Conference (securityconference.org) / Wikipedia.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2007-01-01</begin><end>2007-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>11.5727,48.1406,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ditchley Foundation - Enstone, Oxfordshire</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>The Ditchley Foundation, an Anglo-American educational trust established in 1958 at a 1722 James Gibbs mansion, hosts around twelve private conferences a year of roughly 40 senior figures from politics, business, the military, media and academia. All discussions are held under the Chatham House Rule. Source: Ditchley Foundation (ditchley.com) / Wikipedia.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1958-01-01</begin><end>1958-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-1.4544,51.9155,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Obelisk of Senusret I (Al-Masalla), Heliopolis, Cairo</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>The 20.7 m, roughly 120-ton red-granite obelisk raised by Pharaoh Senusret I around 1940 BC is the oldest standing obelisk in Egypt and the sole surviving element of the great Temple of Ra-Atum at ancient Heliopolis, now swallowed by Cairo&#x27;s Matariya district. It marks the ancient priestly-solar power center that gave the West its obelisk form. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Al-Masalla&#x27; / EgyptToday, &#x27;Meet the Obelisk of Senusret I&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1940-01-01</begin><end>1940-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>31.2357,30.0444,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pantheon Obelisk (Macuteo Obelisk), Piazza della Rotonda, Rome</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>A 6.34 m Egyptian obelisk carved under Ramesses II (c. 1279-1213 BC) for Heliopolis, later moved to Domitian&#x27;s sanctuary of Isis, then re-erected over Barigioni&#x27;s fountain before the Pantheon by Pope Clement XI in 1711 - one of thirteen ancient obelisks the papacy re-raised across Rome as emblems of Church authority. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Pantheon obelisk&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1711-01-01</begin><end>1711-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.4769,41.8993,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tower of the Juche Idea (Juche Tower), Pyongyang</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Completed 1982 for Kim Il Sung&#x27;s 70th birthday, this 170 m granite spire is the tallest granite structure in the world, built from 25,550 blocks (one per day of the leader&#x27;s first 70 years) and capped by a 20 m illuminated metal torch - a state monument to the ruling Juche ideology. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Juche Tower&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1982-01-01</begin><end>1982-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>125.7474,39.0168,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Monument to the People&#x27;s Heroes, Tiananmen Square, Beijing</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>A 37.94 m granite obelisk built 1952-58 at the exact center of Tiananmen Square to honor revolutionary martyrs; designed by architect Liang Sicheng, it later became a focal gathering point during the 1989 pro-democracy protests. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Monument to the People&#x27;s Heroes&#x27; / TravelChinaGuide.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1952-01-01</begin><end>1952-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>116.3914,39.9027,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Woody Island (Yongxing) - PLA Outpost, Paracel Islands</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Woody Island (Yongxing), the largest of the disputed Paracels and seat of China&#x27;s Sansha city, hosts an ~8,900-foot military-civil runway able to handle nuclear-capable H-6 bombers, plus reinforced hangars, radar sites and HQ-9 surface-to-air missile batteries, functioning as the administrative and military center of China&#x27;s South China Sea presence. Source: CSIS (Gregory Poling); Newsweek; Radio Free Asia; CNBC.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>112.343,16.834,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>L3Harris Communications &amp; Spectrum Dominance - 1680 University Ave, Rochester NY</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>The segment headquarters for L3Harris tactical communications, and the largest manufacturer in the Rochester region - roughly 3,800 employees across aerospace and defense programs (Rochester Business Journal, Aug 2026). ORIGIN: founded as RF Communications by four engineers - Bill Stolze, Elmer Schwittek, Roger Bettin and Herbert VandenBrul - who developed their first long-range two-way radios for government customers in a Park Avenue basement in 1960, opened in a vacant beauty parlor on Merchants Road, and moved to 1680 University Avenue two years later, where the site remains. Acquired by Harris Corporation in early 1969; Harris merged with L3 Technologies in 2019 to form L3Harris. PRODUCT: the Falcon tactical radio line (Falcon III, Falcon IV) - manpack and handheld radios that are a standard for US and allied tactical communications; the USMC selected Falcon IV manpack and handheld sets, and in July 2026 the site took an $84M US Army order for next-generation Falcon manpacks. The segment&#x27;s name is the plainest statement of what it sells: not &#x27;communications&#x27; but SPECTRUM DOMINANCE - the electromagnetic spectrum treated as terrain to be held. LEADERSHIP, 17 Aug 2026: Christopher Aebli - Rochester-based, with the company since 1991 - was named segment president. The same-day context matters and is documented: L3Harris&#x27;s board removed chairman and CEO Christopher Kubasik after a code-of-conduct investigation (SEC Form 8-K), named Sam Mehta CEO, and Mehta&#x27;s promotion out of the Space &amp; Mission Systems / Communications &amp; Spectrum Dominance role is what vacated the seat Aebli filled. A local appointment with a corporate-governance cause, not a local one. Sources: RBJ (17 Aug 2026; 9 Jul 2026); L3Harris/Harris press material on RF Communications&#x27; 50th anniversary; L3Harris 8-K (17 Aug 2026); Naval Technology (USMC Falcon IV).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2026-08-17</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-77.55891,43.14796,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>L3Harris Technologies HQ - Melbourne, Florida</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VII</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Corporate headquarters of L3Harris Technologies, formed by the 2019 merger of Harris Corporation and L3 Technologies. Roughly 45,000 employees and about $22.5 billion in trailing-twelve-month revenue as of 31 March 2026. Four reporting segments: Space &amp; Airborne Systems, Integrated Mission Systems, Communication Systems, and Aerojet Rocketdyne - the solid-rocket-motor manufacturer, whose acquisition consolidated a large share of US missile propulsion inside a single prime. On 17 August 2026 the board removed chairman and CEO Christopher Kubasik following a board-directed code-of-conduct investigation, filed an 8-K, and appointed Sam Mehta president and CEO effective immediately, with lead independent director Lewis Hay III as independent chairman; the company stated the conduct finding was not connected to financial reporting, controls, customer relationships or operational performance, and Kubasik received no severance or accelerated vesting. Sources: L3Harris Form 8-K (17 Aug 2026); Reuters; Breaking Defense; Aviation Week; SpaceNews.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2026-08-17</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-80.63437,28.0929,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section VIII (17)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>New Jersey Turnpike - Nash Crash Site</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>May 23, 2015: John Nash and wife Alicia killed in taxi crash returning from Norway (Abel Prize). Nash proposed &#x27;Ideal Money&#x27; - a currency indexed to an industrial consumption price index, functionally describing Bitcoin&#x27;s design. Both ejected - not wearing seatbelts.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2015-05-23</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-74.5169,40.3032,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Temple City, California - Hal Finney</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Hal Finney lived here. 10 blocks from Dorian Satoshi Nakamoto. Received first Bitcoin transaction from Satoshi (2009). Created first reusable proof-of-work system (RPOW). Both dead within 9 months of Nash.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2009-01-01</begin><end>2009-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-118.0579,34.1073,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Alcor, Scottsdale, Arizona</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Alcor Life Extension Foundation. Finney&#x27;s body cryopreserved at -196°C. The operational builder of Bitcoin is frozen in a desert facility. Peter Thiel also reportedly signed up for cryopreservation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-111.9269,33.459,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Zug, Switzerland - Crypto Valley</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Self-proclaimed &#x27;Crypto Valley.&#x27; Ethereum Foundation HQ. Bitcoin Suisse. Xapo. Cardano/IOHK. Swiss canton with lowest tax rates. The offshore finance model applied to cryptocurrency - same geography, updated product.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>8.5155,47.166,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>El Zonte, El Salvador - Bitcoin Beach</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Origin of El Salvador&#x27;s Bitcoin adoption. Anonymous donor seeded BTC in fishing village (2019). President Bukele made BTC legal tender (2021). Chivo wallet - government-run Bitcoin wallet. Village experiment scaled to national monetary policy.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-89.3864,13.4975,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Volcano Bond Site, Conchagua, El Salvador</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Proposed &#x27;Bitcoin City&#x27; at base of Conchagua volcano. Geothermal-powered Bitcoin mining. $1B &#x27;Volcano Bond&#x27; - tokenized sovereign debt. The volcano as power source for a digital currency city that hasn&#x27;t been built.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.8469,13.2756,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Genesis Block Café, Hong Kong</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Named after Bitcoin&#x27;s first block (Jan 3, 2009). Hong Kong: global crypto trading hub before 2023 regulatory shifts. Proximity to mainland China - where 65%+ of Bitcoin mining once concentrated before the ban.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2009-01-03</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>114.1545,22.2816,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>FTX / Albany Resort, Nassau, Bahamas</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>FTX moved its headquarters to Nassau in 2021 and collapsed in November 2022 in one of history&#x27;s largest financial frauds; founder Sam Bankman-Fried ran the empire from a roughly $40 million penthouse at the gated Albany resort and was later convicted on seven counts and sentenced to 25 years. FTX left an $8 billion customer shortfall. Source: Rolling Stone / Forbes / Time (2022); U.S. v. Bankman-Fried.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-11-01</begin><end>2022-11-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.3067,25.0608,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Glen Park Branch Library, San Francisco (Silk Road Arrest)</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>In October 2013 the FBI arrested Ross Ulbricht, the &#x27;Dread Pirate Roberts&#x27; behind the Bitcoin-powered darknet market Silk Road, at this branch library while he was logged into the site&#x27;s admin panel. He was sentenced to life before receiving a full presidential pardon in January 2025. Source: KQED (2013 SF sting); NBC News; Glen Park Association.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2013-10-01</begin><end>2013-10-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-122.4336,37.734,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ledger HQ, Paris, France</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Paris-based Ledger is the leading maker of hardware wallets for securing crypto private keys offline, having sold more than 7.5 million devices across 200 countries with over 20% of the world&#x27;s crypto assets reportedly secured on its hardware. A 2020 data breach exposed roughly a million customers&#x27; contact details. Source: Decrypt (&#x27;Ledger Unveils New Global Headquarters in Paris&#x27;); Ledger careers.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2020-01-01</begin><end>2020-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>2.3414,48.8664,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chainalysis HQ, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Chainalysis is the leading blockchain-forensics firm, tracing crypto transactions for law enforcement and governments in over 70 countries; its clients include the FBI, DEA, IRS Criminal Investigation and the UK National Crime Agency, making it a central node in state surveillance of cryptocurrency flows. Source: Wikipedia: Chainalysis; Chainalysis Government Solutions.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.8088,40.9126,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ekibastuz Bitcoin Mining Hub, Kazakhstan</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>After China banned crypto mining in May 2021, coal-rich Ekibastuz became a magnet for relocating miners, briefly helping push Kazakhstan to the world&#x27;s second-largest Bitcoin hash rate; the local Enegix facility alone was built to power over 50,000 ASICs at 150 MW, roughly five times the town&#x27;s own peak demand, straining the national grid. Source: MIT Technology Review (2023); Rest of World; Bitcoin Magazine.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2021-05-01</begin><end>2021-05-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>75.3289,51.7276,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mt. Gox Office, Cerulean Tower, Shibuya, Tokyo</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>The Shibuya-based Mt. Gox exchange handled over 70% of all global Bitcoin transactions before it collapsed in February 2014, having lost roughly 850,000 BTC (worth hundreds of millions then, tens of billions later) to theft and mismanagement. Protesters gathered outside its Tokyo office as it filed for bankruptcy. Source: Wikipedia: Mt. Gox; Japan Times (Mt. Gox coverage).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2014-02-01</begin><end>2014-02-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>139.7009,35.6556,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bitmain HQ, Beijing, China</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Beijing-based Bitmain is the world&#x27;s largest maker of Bitcoin-mining ASICs, at times commanding roughly 90% of the market for mining rigs through its Antminer brand, and it operates Antpool, one of the largest mining pools. Its dominance means even &#x27;Made in USA&#x27; Bitcoin largely runs on Chinese-designed hardware. Source: Bloomberg (2024); Wikipedia: Bitmain.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>116.2924,39.9581,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Riot Platforms Rockdale Facility (Whinstone), Texas</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Built on an abandoned aluminum smelter, Riot Platforms&#x27; Rockdale site is the largest single Bitcoin-mining facility by developed capacity in North America at about 700 MW, and Greenpeace calls it the most energy- and carbon-intensive Bitcoin mine in the US. Riot acquired builder Whinstone for $651 million in 2021. Source: Greenpeace USA; Global Energy Monitor (Whinstone Bitcoin mining facility).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2021-01-01</begin><end>2021-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-97.0058,30.6549,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Strategy (MicroStrategy) HQ, Tysons Corner, Virginia</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Founded by Michael Saylor, the software firm rebranded from MicroStrategy to &#x27;Strategy&#x27; in 2025 and is the world&#x27;s largest corporate Bitcoin holder, having amassed roughly 597,000 BTC (worth over $70 billion in mid-2025) funded largely through equity and debt issuance. It pioneered the Bitcoin corporate-treasury model. Source: Virginia Business; Bitcoin Treasuries; Wikipedia: MicroStrategy.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2025-01-01</begin><end>2025-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.223,38.9191,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bletchley Park, Milton Keynes, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section VIII</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Bletchley Park was Britain&#x27;s WWII codebreaking center, where Alan Turing and colleagues broke the German Enigma and Lorenz ciphers and built Colossus, the world&#x27;s first programmable electronic digital computer. It is a foundational site of modern cryptography and computing, kept secret for decades after the war. Source: UK National Museum of Computing / Bletchley Park Trust.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#VIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.7465,52.0349,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section IX (154)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Harvard Law School, Cambridge, MA</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Dershowitz: youngest full professor in Harvard Law history (age 28). Felix Frankfurter Professor of Law, 1964-2013. 49 years at the institution. Same Harvard whose scientists Epstein surrounded himself with.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1964-01-01</begin><end>1964-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.1167,42.377,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Palm Beach County, FL - Epstein NPA</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; governance</p><p>2008: Dershowitz helped negotiate Epstein&#x27;s non-prosecution agreement with U.S. Attorney Alexander Acosta. Deal shielded unnamed co-conspirators. Victims not notified. Federal judge later ruled it violated victims&#x27; rights (2019).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2008-01-01</begin><end>2008-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-80.0534,26.7153,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cheyenne Mountain, Colorado</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>NORAD/USNORTHCOM. 2,000 ft below granite. 5.1 acres floor space. Operational 1966. Military moved BACK IN and hardened against EMP.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1966-01-01</begin><end>1966-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-104.8467,38.7446,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Raven Rock (Site R), Pennsylvania</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Alternate National Military Command Center. Built 1951-53. 6 miles from Camp David with underground corridor connection.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1951-01-01</begin><end>1951-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.4247,39.7365,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Camp David, Maryland</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Presidential retreat. Connected to Site R via underground corridor. 6 miles from the alternate Pentagon.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.465,39.6484,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mount Weather, Bluemont, Virginia</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Emergency Operations Center. FEMA High Point Special Facility. Classified continuity-of-government facility.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.8872,39.0938,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>The Greenbrier, White Sulphur Springs, WV</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Project Greek Island - secret Congressional bunker built 1958-61 beneath luxury resort. Decommissioned 1992 after media exposure.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1992-12-01</begin><end>1992-12-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-80.3016,37.788,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mount Yamantau, Urals, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>~400 sq mi underground facility. Construction began 1960s, expanded 1990s. Closed city of Mezhgorye (~17,000 pop) services it.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1960-01-01</begin><end>1960-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>58.1,54.25,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kosvinsky Kamen, Urals, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Russian nuclear command facility inside granite mountain. &#x27;Dead Hand&#x27; Perimeter system - designed to launch without human authorization.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>58.9667,59.4833,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Moscow - Metro-2 / D-6</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Secret parallel metro system connecting Kremlin, Ministry of Defense, FSB HQ, Vnukovo-2 airport. Underground command facilities at Sharapovo &amp; Chekhov (30,000 capacity each).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>37.6173,55.7558,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Project 131, Hubei Province, China</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Underground command HQ built for Mao Zedong, 1969-71. Chinese government D.U.M.B. program.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1969-01-01</begin><end>1969-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>114.3055,30.5928,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Beijing Underground City</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Built 1969-79. Capacity 300,000 people. Beneath the capital of the world&#x27;s most populous country.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1969-01-01</begin><end>1969-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>116.4074,39.9042,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>816 Nuclear Military Plant, Chongqing, China</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>18 years construction by 60,000 soldiers. Nuclear weapons production facility carved into mountain.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>107.9511,29.4316,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Burlington / Corsham, Wiltshire, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Central Government War HQ in former quarry. 35 acres, capacity 4,000 officials. British deep state continuity facility.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-2.1878,51.4327,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Jerusalem Underground Command, Israel</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Crisis command center beneath the Judaean Mountains. Israeli continuity-of-government facility.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.2137,31.7683,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Klara Bunker, Stockholm, Sweden</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Capacity 8,000-12,000 people. Sweden has 65,000+ fallout shelters for 10 million population.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>18.0686,59.3293,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Diefenbunker, Ottawa, Canada</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>CFS Carp. Primary Canadian nuclear bunker, 1958-63. Now a Cold War museum. The bunker was built; the question is what replaced it.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1958-01-01</begin><end>1958-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-76.0457,45.351,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>COFAS, Taverny, France</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>French Air Force nuclear command center inside mountain. French force de frappe command facility.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>2.2028,49.0175,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mont Verdun, near Lyon, France</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Combined air defense and nuclear command facility. French deep state continuity infrastructure.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>4.778,45.8735,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Regierungsbunker, Ahrweiler, Germany</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Federal government bunker built 1960-72. 17.3 km of tunnels. 203m section now a museum. The rest was demolished - allegedly.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1960-01-01</begin><end>1960-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>7.1093,50.5457,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>K-116, Zlíchov, Prague, Czech Republic</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Cold War-era underground command bunker beneath Zlíchov hill. Eastern Bloc continuity infrastructure.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>14.4025,50.0624,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>REGAN Vest, Jutland, Denmark</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Government nuclear bunker, western Denmark. Scandinavian D.U.M.B. network.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.5018,56.2639,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Salt Pit / &#x27;The Dark Prison&#x27;, North Kabul, Afghanistan</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>CIA facility. Detainee Gul Rahman froze to death November 2002. &#x27;Enhanced interrogation&#x27; - the U.S. government&#x27;s euphemism for torture.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2002-11-01</begin><end>2002-11-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>69.1618,34.5964,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Stare Kiejkuty, Poland</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Former intelligence facility converted to CIA black site. Confirmed by European Court of Human Rights 2014.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2014-01-01</begin><end>2014-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>21.2753,53.8098,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mihail Kogălniceanu, Romania</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>CIA detention at military airbase. Confirmed ECHR 2018. European NATO ally hosting secret U.S. torture facility.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2018-01-01</begin><end>2018-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>28.4865,44.3622,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Antaviliai, Lithuania</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Former riding school converted to CIA detention facility. Confirmed ECHR 2018. Another EU/NATO state hosting black sites.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2018-01-01</begin><end>2018-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>25.3163,54.7484,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ramasun Station / &#x27;Detention Site Green&#x27;, Thailand</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>CIA&#x27;s first black site (2002). Former Five Eyes SIGINT facility converted to detention. Surveillance infrastructure repurposed for torture.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2002-01-01</begin><end>2002-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>102.7708,17.4069,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Camp Lemonnier, Djibouti</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>U.S. military base serving as rendition transit hub. 1,245 documented CIA flights in the rendition network.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>43.1464,11.5469,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Diego Garcia, British Indian Ocean Territory</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>UK-administered, leased to U.S. Rendition flights confirmed. Chagossian population forcibly removed 1960s to make room for the base.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1960-01-01</begin><end>1960-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>72.4229,-7.3195,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Negev Nuclear Research Center, Dimona, Israel</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>31.0013°N, 35.1445°E. 13 km SE of Dimona. Israel installed false walls before U.S. inspections (1965-69). Inspectors called inspections &#x27;useless&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1965-01-01</begin><end>1965-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>35.1445,31.0013,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Little Saint James Island, U.S. Virgin Islands</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>OWNERSHIP UPDATED 31 Aug 2026 — this marker still described the island as Epstein&#x27;s, which has not been true since 2023. 70–78 acres. Sally-port doors. Dedicated fibre-optic cable to St Thomas. SOLD MAY 2023, together with Great Saint James, to STEPHEN DECKOFF for US$60M; he has said publicly that he never met Epstein and never set foot on the islands until they were marketed after the 2019 death. Announced plan: a 25-room luxury resort, originally targeted about two years out; no construction has been reported as of 2026. Deckoff is named here solely as the documented purchaser — nothing in this marker implies any connection to Epstein&#x27;s conduct, and his own statement is recorded alongside the fact.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-05-01</begin><end>2023-05-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-64.8253,18.3,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kola Superdeep Borehole, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Deepest artificial point on Earth: 12,262m (40,230 ft). Soviet drilling program 1970–1992. Reached 1/3 through continental crust. Found microscopic fossils at 6km, super-heated water at extreme depth, temperatures 80°C higher than predicted. Abandoned because rock became plastic and hole kept closing. If D.U.M.B. networks operate at hundreds of meters, the drilling technology to reach kilometers exists.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1970-01-01</begin><end>1970-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>33.3441,69.3963,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Dulce, New Mexico - Archuleta Mesa</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Alleged underground facility beneath Archuleta Mesa, on Jicarilla Apache Nation reservation. 95 miles north of Los Alamos National Lab (Manhattan Project). 120 miles from Sandia National Labs. Jurisdictional gap: federal vs. tribal sovereignty. Pattern: alleged underground facilities consistently located on indigenous land near nuclear infrastructure - Pine Ridge, Dulce, Nevada Test Site (Shoshone land), Area 51.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-106.9989,36.9336,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Camp Hero / Montauk AFS, Long Island</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Montauk Air Force Station. SAGE radar (AN/FPS-35, 126-ft antenna). Operational 1942–1981. Underground facilities in military construction records. Alleged Project Montauk: mind control/electromagnetic research extending MK-Ultra. Adjacent to Plum Island (bioweapons) and Brookhaven National Lab (particle physics). Three federal research facilities at Long Island&#x27;s eastern tip.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1942-01-01</begin><end>1942-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.8573,41.0711,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Plum Island Animal Disease Center</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>USDA/DHS biological research facility. Foot-and-mouth disease, foreign animal diseases. Originally Army Chemical Corps (biological weapons, 1954). Proximity to Montauk and Brookhaven. Scheduled relocation to NBAF (Manhattan, Kansas). The bioweapons lab near the mind control lab near the particle physics lab - all on one island chain.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1954-01-01</begin><end>1954-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-72.1893,41.1854,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>HAARP, Gakona, Alaska</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>High-frequency Active Auroral Research Program. 3.6 MW, 180 antenna array. Originally DARPA/Air Force/Navy. Transferred to University of Alaska Fairbanks (2015). Ionospheric heater: communications disruption, over-the-horizon radar, ELF submarine communication. Transfer to university changed FOIA jurisdiction, not capability.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2015-01-01</begin><end>2015-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-145.15,62.3907,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Clear Space Force Station, Alaska</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>AN/FPS-132 UEWR missile warning radar. NORAD ballistic missile detection. Ground-based midcourse defense architecture. Northern early warning line.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-149.195,64.295,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Joint Base Elmendorf-Richardson, Alaska</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>NORAD Alaska Region. Pacific Air Forces (11th Air Force). U.S. Army Alaska. Primary Arctic airpower projection. Joint base combining Air Force and Army at Alaska&#x27;s population center.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-149.807,61.253,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fort Greely, Alaska - Missile Defense</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>Ground-based Midcourse Defense (GMD) operational interceptors. Anti-ballistic missile shield&#x27;s northern component. The missiles that defend against missiles, stationed in permafrost.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-145.737,63.995,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>McMurdo Station, Antarctica (US)</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>Ross Island. Largest Antarctic station - 1,000+ personnel in summer. NSF operated, U.S. military logistics (Operation Deep Freeze). Runway, harbor. Nuclear history: PM-3A reactor 1962–1972, removed after radioactive leaks. Military-supported &#x27;peaceful research&#x27; on a continent that bans military operations.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1962-01-01</begin><end>1962-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>166.668,-77.846,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Amundsen-Scott South Pole Station (US)</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>Geographic South Pole. IceCube Neutrino Observatory - detecting particles that pass through the entire Earth. NSF station, military logistics. The most remote permanently occupied facility on Earth.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>0.0,-89.983,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vostok Station, Antarctica (Russia)</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Lowest temperature ever recorded: −89.2°C (1983). Drilled into subglacial Lake Vostok - freshwater lake sealed beneath 4km of ice for 15–25 million years. What lives in a sealed lake for 15 million years? Samples restricted. Russian deep-drilling expertise connects to Kola Superdeep Borehole program.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1983-01-01</begin><end>1983-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>106.837,-78.464,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Concordia Station, Antarctica (France/Italy)</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>Dome C, East Antarctic Plateau. ESA Mars conditions analog - testing Mars habitation protocols in Antarctica. The space agency rehearses planetary colonization at the bottom of this planet.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>123.35,-75.1,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rothera Station, Antarctica (UK)</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>Adelaide Island. British Antarctic Survey. Blue-ice runway for intercontinental flights. A military-grade runway on a continent that bans military operations. The research station with more capability than its treaty allows.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-68.13,-67.57,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Palmer Station, Antarctica (US)</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>Anvers Island, Antarctic Peninsula. Marine and terrestrial biology. The northernmost U.S. Antarctic station - closest to South America, easiest access, least controlled.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-64.054,-64.774,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pine Island Glacier, Antarctica</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Fastest-melting glacier on Earth. If Pine Island + Thwaites (&#x27;Doomsday Glacier&#x27;) collapse: +3m sea level rise. The glacier named &#x27;Doomsday&#x27; is monitored by the nations whose emissions are melting it. Extensive satellite and sensor networks monitor from orbit - the surveillance state watches ice.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-100.0,-75.167,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Denver International Airport (DIA)</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>Opened 1995, $4.8B over budget. 33,531 acres (53 sq mi - twice Manhattan). Masonic capstone dated March 19, 1994 (&#x27;New World Airport Commission&#x27;). &#x27;Blue Mustang&#x27; (&#x27;Blucifer&#x27;) - 32-ft blue horse with glowing red eyes, killed its sculptor. Underground baggage system abandoned. Murals depicting gas-masked soldiers, burning cities, dead children. Fuel system: 5 underground storage buildings with subterranean pipes to 28 hydrant pits. Underground tunnels extend far beyond operational need. Sits directly between Buckley SFB (NRO satellite ops) and Cheyenne Mountain (NORAD).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1994-03-19</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-104.6737,39.8561,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Dulles International Airport (IAD), Virginia</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>27 miles from CIA headquarters at Langley. Named after John Foster Dulles (Secretary of State, brother of CIA Director Allen Dulles - who orchestrated coups in Guatemala, Iran, Congo). CIA shuttle bus ran between Langley and Dulles. Documented CIA rendition flights.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.4565,38.9531,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shannon Airport, Ireland - Rendition Transit</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>Documented CIA rendition flight transit point. Irish neutrality did not prevent use as refueling stop for extraordinary rendition flights. Over 1,000 CIA-linked flights transited Shannon (2001-2008). The neutral country&#x27;s airport as logistics node in the torture pipeline.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2001-01-01</begin><end>2001-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-8.9247,52.702,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Palma de Mallorca Airport, Spain - Rendition Transit</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>Documented CIA rendition flight hub. Jeppesen Dataplan (Boeing subsidiary, Denver-based) provided flight planning for rendition aircraft. European Parliament investigation confirmed rendition flights through Spanish territory.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>2.7389,39.5517,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Johnston Atoll, Pacific - Chemical/Military</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>Remote Pacific atoll, 1,328 km from Honolulu. Chemical weapons storage/destruction (VX, sarin, mustard gas) until 2000. Nuclear weapons testing (1962). Biological weapons open-air testing. Now &#x27;wildlife refuge&#x27; on contaminated soil.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1962-01-01</begin><end>1962-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-169.5339,16.7295,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Groom Lake / Area 51 Airstrip, Nevada</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>CIA/USAF classified flight test facility. 12,000-ft runway. U-2, SR-71, F-117 all tested here. JANET airlines flies workers daily from Las Vegas. Government denied existence until 2013 CIA declassification. On Western Shoshone land (Treaty of Ruby Valley, 1863 - never ceded).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1863-01-01</begin><end>1863-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-115.8111,37.235,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tora Bora, Nangarhar Province, Afghanistan</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>White Mountains (Safed Koh), ~14,000 ft elevation. CIA-funded mujahideen tunnel complex built 1980s with Pakistani ISI assistance against Soviet occupation. Multi-level cave system: ventilation shafts, hydroelectric power, arms depots, medical facilities. Bin Laden compound December 2001 - U.S. relied on Afghan militias (not U.S. ground forces) to assault. He escaped to Pakistan. The CIA built the tunnels, then couldn&#x27;t take them back.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2001-12-01</begin><end>2001-12-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>70.5744,34.0972,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Zhawar Kili, Paktia Province, Afghanistan</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Major mujahideen base complex near Pakistan border. CIA/ISI funded during Soviet-Afghan War. Multiple tunnel systems with garages, arms depots, training facilities. Bombed by U.S. in 1998 cruise missile strikes (Operation Infinite Reach) and again in 2001. The tunnels survived the missiles designed to destroy them.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1998-01-01</begin><end>1998-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>69.7,33.3,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Khost-Gardez Pass (K-G Pass), Afghanistan</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Major logistics corridor between Khost and Gardez. Tunnel complexes throughout the mountain passes. Soviet forces, mujahideen, Taliban, and U.S. forces all fought over the same tunnel-laced corridors. Chapman Forward Operating Base (CIA) was 15 km from Khost - December 2009 base attack killed 7 CIA officers.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2009-12-01</begin><end>2009-12-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>69.5,33.5,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shamsi Airfield (CIA Drone Base), Balochistan, Pakistan</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>Secret CIA drone base. Predator/Reaper operations into Afghanistan. Pakistan publicly denied its existence while receiving $1B+/year in U.S. military aid. Evicted after NATO Salala incident (2011) killed 24 Pakistani soldiers. The drone base the host country pretended didn&#x27;t exist.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2011-01-01</begin><end>2011-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>65.841,27.851,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Củ Chi Tunnels, Vietnam</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>~250 km tunnel network. Three levels deep. Hospitals, command centers, weapons factories, living quarters - all underground. Defeated the most technologically advanced military on Earth. U.S. created &#x27;Tunnel Rats&#x27; units to combat them. Agent Orange, B-52 carpet bombing, chemical gas - the tunnels survived it all.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>106.4635,11.1415,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vịnh Mốc Tunnels, Quảng Trị, Vietnam</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Entire village moved underground to survive U.S. bombing. Three levels, 30m deep. 17 babies born underground. 2,000+ days of continuous habitation. The village that burrowed into the earth and survived.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>107.1106,17.0803,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Gotthard Base Tunnel, Switzerland</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>World&#x27;s longest railway tunnel: 57.09 km, up to 2,300m below the Alps. Opened 2016, cost CHF 12.2B. Opening ceremony widely discussed for its theatrical production. Connects northern and southern Europe&#x27;s rail logistics through the mountain the Swiss built their National Redoubt inside.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2016-01-01</begin><end>2016-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>8.65,46.83,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Channel Tunnel (Chunnel), UK-France</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>50.45 km, 75m below seabed. Three tunnels: two rail, one service. Longest undersea portion of any tunnel on Earth. Connects two nuclear powers under a body of water that has stopped invasions for 1,000 years. Opened 1994.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1994-01-01</begin><end>1994-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>1.4861,51.0125,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CFB North Bay - NORAD Underground, Ontario</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>NORAD Region headquarters 60 stories underground inside granite. Built 1959-63, hardened against nuclear strike. Canadian NORAD Sector - the underground half of the continent&#x27;s air defense. Blast doors, self-contained atmosphere. Still operational.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1959-01-01</begin><end>1959-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-79.42,46.36,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CFB Suffield / DRDC Suffield, Alberta</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>2,690 km² - largest military base in the Commonwealth. British Army Training Unit Suffield (BATUS). Defence Research and Development Canada: chemical/biological weapons testing. Ralston experimental range. The chemical weapons testing ground the size of a small country.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-111.0,50.27,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>HMCS Trinity, Debert, Nova Scotia</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Underground naval command center, Cold War era. NATO SOSUS (Sound Surveillance System) - tracking Soviet submarines from underground bunker in Nova Scotia. The ear beneath the Atlantic.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-63.45,45.4147,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rideau Canal / Parliamentary Precinct Tunnels, Ottawa</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Tunnel network beneath Parliament Hill - connects major government buildings. Rideau Canal (UNESCO World Heritage) - originally military logistics canal built 1826-32 as alternate supply route in case of U.S. invasion. 202 km. The canal built to survive an American invasion, now a skating rink.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1826-01-01</begin><end>1826-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-75.6972,45.4215,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chelyabinsk-40 / Ozersk, Russia (Mayak)</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Mayak nuclear complex - Soviet plutonium production. Kyshtym disaster (1957): third-worst nuclear disaster in history (after Chernobyl and Fukushima). Entire population of Chelyabinsk-40 and surrounding villages irradiated. Techa River and Lake Karachay - most radioactively contaminated lake on Earth. Standing at the shore for 1 hour = lethal dose. Closed city - population still there.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1957-01-01</begin><end>1957-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>60.705,55.713,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Krasnoyarsk-26 / Zheleznogorsk, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Underground plutonium production complex inside a mountain. Mining and Chemical Combine - now stores spent nuclear fuel. Also houses Reshetnev ISS - satellite manufacturing. The underground nuclear facility that became an underground satellite factory. Closed city.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>93.5333,56.25,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kapustin Yar, Astrakhan Oblast, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>Soviet rocket testing range since 1946. First Soviet missile launches. Underground test facilities. Russia&#x27;s original Cape Canaveral. The site where captured V-2 rocket scientists (paralleling U.S. Operation Paperclip) launched the Soviet space and missile program.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1946-01-01</begin><end>1946-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>45.755,48.57,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sarov / Arzamas-16, Russia (VNIIEF)</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Russia&#x27;s primary nuclear weapons design facility - VNIIEF (All-Russian Scientific Research Institute of Experimental Physics). Soviet &#x27;Los Alamos.&#x27; First Soviet atomic bomb (RDS-1, 1949) and hydrogen bomb (RDS-6, 1953) designed here. Closed city - 92,000 residents behind barbed wire. No road signs, no maps, no entry without FSB clearance. The city that does not officially exist built the weapon that changed everything.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1949-01-01</begin><end>1949-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>43.3235,54.9353,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Novaya Zemlya, Arctic Russia - Nuclear Test Site</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>Arctic nuclear weapons testing range. 224 nuclear detonations (1955-1990). Site of the Tsar Bomba (October 30, 1961): 50-megaton thermonuclear weapon - largest man-made explosion in history. Shockwave circled the Earth three times. Mushroom cloud rose 64 km. Windows shattered 900 km away. Seismic wave measurable on third pass. Indigenous Nenets people forcibly relocated 1955.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1961-10-30</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>54.9833,73.35,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Semipalatinsk Test Site (The Polygon), Kazakhstan</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; military</p><p>Soviet nuclear weapons test site. 456 nuclear tests (1949-1989) including the first Soviet atomic bomb. 18,500 km² - larger than some countries. 1.5 million people exposed to fallout. Birth defects, cancers, and genetic damage persist through generations. &#x27;The Polygon&#x27; - the geometry of contamination. Closed 1991 by Kazakhstan&#x27;s first act of independence. The land that absorbed 456 nuclear explosions and the people who absorbed them too.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1949-01-01</begin><end>1949-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>78.43,50.07,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Gaza Tunnel Network, Rafah Crossing</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Estimated 1,300+ tunnels under Rafah border with Egypt. Smuggling corridor for food, medicine, weapons, fuel. Israel&#x27;s 2023-24 ground operation specifically targeted tunnel infrastructure. Miles of underground passages beneath a 25-mile strip. The underground city beneath the surface city.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-01-01</begin><end>2023-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>34.2522,31.2475,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hezbollah Tunnel Network, Southern Lebanon</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Cross-border attack tunnels into Israel discovered 2018-19 (Operation Northern Shield). Multi-year construction with concrete reinforcement. Strategic depth - the border is not the surface, it extends underground.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2018-01-01</begin><end>2018-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>35.2037,33.2774,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>DMZ Tunnels, Korean Peninsula</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Four infiltration tunnels discovered (1974-1990). Third tunnel: 1,635m long, 73m deep, capable of moving 30,000 troops per hour. North Korea denied building them - claimed they were coal mines (no coal found). How many remain undiscovered?</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1974-01-01</begin><end>1974-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>126.95,37.95,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Balaklava Submarine Base, Crimea</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Object 825 GTS - Soviet underground submarine base carved into a mountain. Canal system allows submarines to enter through camouflaged sea entrance, traverse through the mountain, and exit the other side. Designed to survive a direct nuclear strike. Now a museum. The mountain that swallows submarines.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>33.597,44.4986,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cassidy International Airport, Kiritimati (Christmas Island)</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>Remote Pacific atoll. British nuclear tests: Operation Grapple (1957-58), 3 hydrogen bomb detonations. U.S. nuclear tests: Operation Dominic (1962), 24 atmospheric detonations. 300+ service personnel exposed to radiation. Now a &#x27;wildlife sanctuary&#x27; on irradiated coral.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1957-01-01</begin><end>1957-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-157.35,1.9862,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Esrange Space Center, Kiruna, Sweden</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Sounding rocket launch facility above Arctic Circle. Satellite ground station. European Space Agency operations. Military and civilian dual-use. The northernmost launch facility in Europe - accessible only to those who know it exists.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>21.1042,67.8933,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Woomera Range Complex, Australia</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>Largest weapons testing range in the Western world (122,000 km²). British nuclear tests at Maralinga (1956-63) - Aboriginal Anangu people irradiated and displaced. Joint U.S.-Australian defense facility. Drone testing, missile testing. Indigenous land as weapons laboratory.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1956-01-01</begin><end>1956-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>136.834,-31.1556,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kwajalein Atoll / Reagan Test Site, Marshall Islands</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>U.S. Army missile testing facility. Space Fence radar installation. 67 nuclear tests on Bikini and Enewetak atolls (1946-58) - Marshallese people permanently displaced. Compact of Free Association gives U.S. military access in exchange for aid. Nuclear testing victims still seeking compensation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1946-01-01</begin><end>1946-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>167.73,8.72,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cayenne, French Guiana - EU Space Launch</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Guiana Space Centre - EU&#x27;s primary orbital launch facility. Equatorial position gives +17% payload advantage. Arianespace, ESA, French military launches. European space operations launched from South American jungle on indigenous Kali&#x27;na land.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-52.7681,5.2394,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Derinkuyu Underground City, Cappadocia, Turkey</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>18 stories deep. Capacity: 20,000 people with livestock and provisions. Connected to Kaymakli by 8km tunnel. Carved from volcanic tuite. Who built a city for 20,000 people underground, complete with ventilation, water wells, and rolling stone doors - and why?</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>34.7344,38.3736,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>MIT - Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Cambridge, MA</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>MIT Radiation Laboratory (WWII): radar development. MIT Lincoln Laboratory: SAGE air defense, missile defense, space surveillance - DOD funded since 1951. MIT Instrumentation Lab (now Draper): Apollo guidance, ICBM guidance, Trident submarine navigation. MKUltra Subproject 48 at MIT. Noam Chomsky&#x27;s entire career at a DOD-funded institution - the most famous critic of the military-industrial complex employed by its R&amp;D arm. MIT Media Lab accepted $800K from Jeffrey Epstein AFTER his first conviction. Annual DOD research funding: $1B+. The university that builds the weapons and critiques the weapons with the same campus ID.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1951-01-01</begin><end>1951-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.0942,42.3601,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Stanford University, Palo Alto, CA</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Stanford Research Institute (SRI) - separated 1970 after Vietnam War protests, but contracts continued. SRI ran Project Stargate (remote viewing) for CIA/DIA. Stanford AI Lab (SAIL): foundational AI research, DARPA funded. MKUltra experiments at Stanford: Dr. Leo Hollister administered LSD to volunteers including Ken Kesey - Kesey&#x27;s acid experiences at Stanford VA hospital directly produced the Merry Pranksters and the 1960s counterculture. The CIA&#x27;s drug experiment accidentally invented the counterculture. Google, Hewlett-Packard, Cisco, Yahoo - all Stanford. The university as Silicon Valley seed bank. CIA seed → counterculture flower → tech harvest.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1970-09-01</begin><end>1970-09-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-122.1697,37.4275,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Yale University, New Haven, CT</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Skull and Bones (founded 1832): Bush 41, Bush 43, John Kerry, William F. Buckley Jr., James Jesus Angleton (CIA counterintelligence chief). The secret society that produced CIA directors, presidents, and the man who ran CIA&#x27;s mole hunt for 20 years. Yale recruited for OSS/CIA since WWII - &#x27;Yale was practically the CIA&#x27;s farm team&#x27; (Evan Thomas). MKUltra Subproject 66 at Yale under Dr. José Delgado - brain electrode stimulation, remote-controlled bull experiment (1963). The university that builds the intelligence community from its graduating class.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1832-01-01</begin><end>1832-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-72.9223,41.3163,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Harvard University, Cambridge, MA</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>MKUltra at Harvard: Dr. Henry Murray&#x27;s personality assessment experiments on undergraduate Ted Kaczynski (1959-1962) - 200 hours of deliberately humiliating psychological abuse. Murray was OSS assessment chief during WWII. Harvard also: Dr. Timothy Leary&#x27;s Psilocybin Project (1960-63), fired after LSD advocacy. Henry Kissinger: Harvard professor → National Security Advisor → Secretary of State → architect of Operation Condor (40,000+ killed). Harvard Kennedy School: the factory that produces the foreign policy establishment. The university that psychologically tortured the Unabomber and trained the war criminals.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1959-01-01</begin><end>1959-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.1167,42.377,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Johns Hopkins University / APL, Laurel, MD</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Johns Hopkins Applied Physics Laboratory: DOD&#x27;s largest university-affiliated research center. $2.8B annual revenue. Missile defense, submarine warfare, space systems, cybersecurity. APL invented the proximity fuze (WWII) - the fuse that detonates near the target, not on impact. Also: Johns Hopkins School of Medicine Psilocybin Research (Roland Griffiths, 2006-2023) - the same university system that builds missile guidance researches mystical experiences through psychedelics. The proximity fuze AND the psychedelic - both are about reaching the target without direct contact.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2006-01-01</begin><end>2006-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-76.8978,39.1667,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>University of Chicago, IL</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Manhattan Project: Enrico Fermi achieved first self-sustaining nuclear chain reaction under Stagg Field bleachers (December 2, 1942). Chicago Pile-1 - the experiment that proved the bomb was possible, conducted beneath a football stadium. Also: &#x27;Chicago School&#x27; economics (Milton Friedman) - free-market ideology deployed through CIA-backed coups (Chile 1973, Argentina). Friedman&#x27;s &#x27;Chicago Boys&#x27; trained economists who restructured Latin American economies under military juntas. The university that split the atom and then split the economies.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1942-12-02</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-87.5987,41.7886,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Columbia University, New York, NY</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Manhattan Project administration headquarters (1942-1946). New York State Psychiatric Institute is a Columbia affiliate - MKUltra experiments (Hoch, Cattell, Harold Blauer&#x27;s death). Columbia&#x27;s School of International and Public Affairs (SIPA) - intelligence community recruiting pipeline. Zbigniew Brzezinski: Columbia professor → National Security Advisor → architect of Operation Cyclone (Afghan mujahideen → Taliban). The university that administered the bomb project and killed Harold Blauer in its psychiatric ward.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1942-01-01</begin><end>1942-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9626,40.8075,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Georgetown University, Washington D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Georgetown School of Foreign Service: CIA recruiting ground since the 1950s. Georgetown&#x27;s Center for Security and Emerging Technology (CSET) - AI policy for DOD. Bill Clinton (Georgetown &#x27;68 → Rhodes Scholar → Governor → President). Georgetown&#x27;s Jesuit tradition: the university sits at the intersection of Catholic intelligence networks and American foreign policy. The diplomatic corps&#x27; alma mater. The school where you learn to serve the state and call it public service.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1950-01-01</begin><end>1950-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.0723,38.9076,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>University of California, Berkeley</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Berkeley Radiation Laboratory (Ernest Lawrence): cyclotron, plutonium isolation, Manhattan Project. UC Berkeley managed Los Alamos and Lawrence Livermore (nuclear weapons labs) for decades through the UC system. COINTELPRO: FBI heavily surveilled Berkeley campus (1960s-70s), infiltrated Free Speech Movement, anti-war organizations. The university that built the bomb and then protested the bomb while the FBI surveilled both activities. UC system still manages Lawrence Livermore and Los Alamos through NNSA contract.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1960-01-01</begin><end>1960-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-122.2585,37.8719,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Caltech - California Institute of Technology, Pasadena</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>JPL (Jet Propulsion Laboratory) is a Caltech-managed NASA center. Jack Parsons - JPL co-founder - conducted Thelema rituals with L. Ron Hubbard (Babalon Working, 1946) and was Aleister Crowley&#x27;s Agape Lodge leader in Pasadena. The rocket scientist who was also an occultist. Parsons held SECRET clearance while performing sex magick rituals. Died in 1952 explosion (ruled accidental). Caltech/JPL: the rocket that reached the Moon was born in an occultist&#x27;s garage. Annual NASA/DOD funding: $2.5B+.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1946-01-01</begin><end>1946-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-118.1253,34.1377,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Princeton University / IDA, Princeton, NJ</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Institute for Defense Analyses (IDA): Princeton-affiliated DOD think tank. JASON advisory group administered through IDA (1960-2002). Einstein, Oppenheimer, von Neumann - all Princeton Institute for Advanced Study. The JASON scientists who advised on Vietnam War electronic barrier (McNamara Line), nuclear weapons effects, climate change (1979 Charney Report), and directed energy weapons - recruited from Princeton&#x27;s orbit. The university that hosts the think tank that advises on everything classified.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1960-01-01</begin><end>1960-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-74.6514,40.3431,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>University of Pennsylvania, Philadelphia</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Penn&#x27;s Holmesburg Prison experiments (1951-1974): Dr. Albert Kligman - UPenn dermatology professor - used prisoners for dioxin exposure, radioactive isotopes, psychoactive drugs. Army/CIA/Dow Chemical funded. Kligman said when he first saw Holmesburg: &#x27;All I saw before me were acres of skin.&#x27; The dermatologist who saw prisoners as square footage. Also: ENIAC (first general-purpose computer, 1945) built at Penn - WWII Army contract. The university that built the first computer and rented prisoner skin to the Army.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1951-01-01</begin><end>1951-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-75.1932,39.9522,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>RAND Corporation, Santa Monica, CA</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Research ANd Development - originally Douglas Aircraft Company project, spun off 1948. Air Force → nuclear strategy → game theory → Herman Kahn&#x27;s &#x27;On Thermonuclear War&#x27; (thinking the unthinkable). Daniel Ellsberg worked at RAND before leaking the Pentagon Papers. RAND&#x27;s nuclear war modeling → MAD (Mutually Assured Destruction) doctrine. Also: RAND Internet (Paul Baran&#x27;s packet switching, 1964 - the distributed network designed to survive nuclear attack became the internet). The think tank that designed nuclear apocalypse strategy and the internet. Both were designed to survive the other.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1948-01-01</begin><end>1948-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-118.4953,34.0195,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tavistock Institute, London, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Founded 1947 from the Tavistock Clinic (1920). British Army psychological warfare research (WWII): selection of officers, morale operations, mass psychology. John Rawlings Rees - Tavistock director - proposed &#x27;psychological shock troops&#x27; to reshape society. Connected to Kurt Lewin (group dynamics), Wilfred Bion (group therapy), Eric Trist (sociotechnical systems). CIA and Tavistock shared research on mass persuasion. The institute whose WWII research on breaking enemy morale was redirected toward domestic populations. Not a conspiracy theory - a documented institutional history of applied social control research.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1947-01-01</begin><end>1947-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.128,51.525,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>École Polytechnique, Paris, France</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Founded 1794 by Napoleon. France&#x27;s premier military-scientific école - under Ministry of Defense until 2009. Graduates run French nuclear weapons program (CEA), aerospace (Airbus, Dassault), intelligence (DGSE). The grande école system: France&#x27;s elite selected at 18 by exam, channeled into state service. The school that Napoleon built to produce the officer-engineers who would run his empire. The empire changed. The school didn&#x27;t.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1794-01-01</begin><end>1794-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>2.2117,48.7147,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Technion - Israel Institute of Technology, Haifa</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Israel&#x27;s premier STEM university. Unit 8200 (SIGINT) recruits heavily from Technion and produces founders: Check Point Software, NSO Group (Pegasus spyware), Cellebrite (phone forensics). The Technion→8200→startup pipeline: military surveillance training → commercial surveillance products. Pegasus zero-click spyware sold to governments that used it on journalists (Jamal Khashoggi&#x27;s associates, Mexican reporters, Indian activists). The university that trains the coders who build the spyware that surveils the journalists.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.0235,32.7775,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Moscow State University (MSU), Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Soviet Union&#x27;s flagship university. GRU and SVR recruitment pipeline. Nuclear weapons research, space program personnel, cyber warfare units. Kaspersky Lab founders: MSU graduates. The building itself - MGU Main Building - is one of Stalin&#x27;s &#x27;Seven Sisters&#x27; (1953), 240m tall, designed as an architectural statement: education as state monument. The university that trained the scientists and the spies in the same building, because they were the same program.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1953-01-01</begin><end>1953-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>37.5314,55.7033,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tsinghua University, Beijing, China</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>China&#x27;s premier STEM university. Xi Jinping (Tsinghua Chemical Engineering, class of 1979). Hu Jintao (Tsinghua Hydraulic Engineering). China&#x27;s top leadership is Tsinghua alumni - the &#x27;Tsinghua clique.&#x27; PLA Unit 61398 (cyber warfare) recruits from Tsinghua and Shanghai Jiao Tong. Tsinghua&#x27;s AI research: surveillance state R&amp;D. The university that produces the presidents, the generals, and the coders who build the Great Firewall.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1979-01-01</begin><end>1979-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>116.3267,39.9987,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>JASON - IDA / MITRE, McLean, VA</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>JASON: elite scientific advisory group (founded 1960). ~60 scientists, mostly physicists, recruited from top universities. Named after Greek mythology (or &#x27;July-August-September-October-November&#x27; - summer study origin). Administered by IDA (1960-2002), then MITRE Corporation. Members include 11 Nobel laureates, 50+ NAS members. JASON studies are classified. Known work: Vietnam electronic barrier (McNamara Line), nuclear weapons effects, submarine detection, directed energy weapons, climate change (the 1979 &#x27;JASON Report&#x27; / Charney Report was one of the first authoritative climate assessments). The 60 scientists who advise on everything the government doesn&#x27;t want peer-reviewed.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1960-01-01</begin><end>1960-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.1773,38.9339,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>JASON Summer Study - La Jolla, CA</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>JASON&#x27;s summer study sessions historically held at UC San Diego / La Jolla campus. 6-week intensive classified sessions where 30-60 elite scientists review DOD/IC problems. The format: compartmented briefings → analysis → classified report. JASON members maintain university positions - they are embed academics with clearances. The summer camp where physics professors become defense consultants. La Jolla: 15 miles from Camp Pendleton USMC, 95 miles from Edwards AFB, same coast as Vandenberg SFB. The beach where classified science happens.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-117.2713,32.8328,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>MITRE Corporation, Bedford, MA</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Federally Funded Research and Development Center (FFRDC). Spun off from MIT Lincoln Laboratory (1958). Operates NORAD&#x27;s Cheyenne Mountain systems, FAA air traffic control systems, IRS tax systems, VA health records, DHS cybersecurity frameworks, NSA&#x27;s intelligence systems. MITRE administered JASON (2002-2019). Annual revenue: $2.5B - 100% government funded. Zero commercial clients. The company that is technically &#x27;not government&#x27; but runs every government system. The private-sector entity with no private sector.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1958-01-01</begin><end>1958-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.2756,42.4862,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory, Livermore, CA</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Nuclear weapons design laboratory (founded 1952 by Edward Teller and Ernest Lawrence). JASON members consult here regularly. Designed the W87 warhead (Minuteman III), W80 (cruise missile). Also: National Ignition Facility (NIF) - achieved fusion ignition December 5, 2022 (2.05 MJ out from 1.3 MJ laser input). The laboratory that designs nuclear weapons achieved fusion in the same building complex. Multiple JASON members hold appointments here. UC Berkeley/UC system managed until 2007.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2022-12-05</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-121.768,37.6819,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Los Alamos National Laboratory, NM</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Manhattan Project headquarters (1943). Oppenheimer&#x27;s laboratory. Trinity test site is 200 miles south. Los Alamos designed Fat Man (Nagasaki) and Little Boy (Hiroshima, with Oak Ridge enrichment). JASON scientists maintain relationships with LANL weapons physicists - the advisory group and the weapons lab share personnel across the classification boundary. Still designs every new U.S. nuclear warhead. Population of Los Alamos town: 13,000. All of them live because of the bomb.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1943-01-01</begin><end>1943-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-106.306,35.88,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mt. Shasta, Siskiyou County, California</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>14,179 ft stratovolcano. Reported inner-earth entrance since 1930s (Frederick Spencer Oliver, &#x27;A Dweller on Two Planets&#x27;). Lava tube systems extend beneath the mountain. Native Wintu and Shasta peoples consider it sacred - axis mundi. Marked as primary entrance on 1978 U.S.A. Inner-Earth Access Map. Persistent reports of anomalous lights, subterranean sounds, and electromagnetic disturbances. The mountain the indigenous peoples said was inhabited from within - centuries before the government maps marked the same location.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1978-01-01</begin><end>1978-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-122.3106,41.3099,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mt. Rainier, Washington</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>14,411 ft - tallest peak in Cascades. Extensive lava tube and cave systems. 1947 Kenneth Arnold UFO sighting occurred near this mountain - the event that coined &#x27;flying saucers.&#x27; Marked as reported entrance on 1978 Inner-Earth map. Steam caves at summit created by volcanic heat. Paradise Ice Caves (discovered 1908). The volcano with internal warmth, internal caves, and the sighting that started modern UFO history.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1947-01-01</begin><end>1947-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-121.7603,46.8523,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Carlsbad Caverns, New Mexico</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>119 known caves carved from Permian-age reef (250-280 million years old). Big Room: 8.2 acres, 255 ft ceiling - largest natural chamber in North America. Lechuguilla Cave reaches 1,604 ft depth. The deepest caves in the Western Hemisphere sitting 170 miles from Dulce and 100 miles from White Sands. Marked as known cavern on 1978 Inner-Earth map. What is deeper than Lechuguilla? The caves that haven&#x27;t been found yet.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1978-01-01</begin><end>1978-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-104.5567,32.1479,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mammoth Cave, Kentucky</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>World&#x27;s longest known cave system: 426+ miles explored, estimated 600+ miles total. Five levels deep. Underground rivers. Pre-Columbian indigenous mining (4,000+ years of human use). Saltpeter mining for gunpowder (War of 1812). Tuberculosis hospital underground (1840s). Marked as major cavern system on 1978 Inner-Earth map. 426 miles of mapped passages and they are still mapping. The longest known system on Earth - &#x27;known&#x27; being the operative word.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1812-01-01</begin><end>1812-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-86.1004,37.1862,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lava Beds National Monument, California</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Over 800 lava tube caves. Modoc War (1872-73): Captain Jack&#x27;s Modoc band held off U.S. Army for months using lava tube fortress. Medicine Lake Volcano shield. 55 miles SE of Mt. Shasta. Marked as primary lava tube system on 1978 Inner-Earth map. The indigenous people who used the lava tubes as military infrastructure against the U.S. Army - and won for months. The tubes go deeper than the military could follow.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1872-01-01</begin><end>1872-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-121.5076,41.7142,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Yucca Mountain, Nevada</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Proposed high-level nuclear waste repository. 5 miles of tunnels bored through volcanic tuff at 1,000 ft depth. $15B spent before Obama halted it (2011). 70,000 metric tons of nuclear waste currently stored at 80+ sites across the U.S. with nowhere to go. 65 miles NW of Area 51. On Western Shoshone land (Treaty of Ruby Valley, 1863). The tunnel complex they built, then abandoned - but the tunnels are still there. What are they used for now?</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2011-01-01</begin><end>2011-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-116.4282,36.8382,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>China Lake NAWS, Ridgecrest, California</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>1.1 million acres - largest single land holding in the U.S. Navy. Weapons development since 1943. July 2019 Ridgecrest earthquakes (M6.4 + M7.1) centered directly beneath the base - the largest California earthquakes in 20 years occurred under a weapons testing facility. Underground weapons magazine complexes. Marked on 1978 Inner-Earth map and 1996 DUMB World Bases map. The earthquakes that hit the underground weapons base - not the city.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-07-01</begin><end>2019-07-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-117.6924,35.6856,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tonopah Test Range, Nevada</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>DOE/NNSA nuclear weapons testing facility within the Nevada Test and Training Range. F-117 Nighthawk stealth fighter was secretly based here 1981-1988 before public reveal. Underground test chambers. 70 miles NW of Area 51. Marked on 1996 DUMB World Bases map. The range where they hid the stealth fighter for seven years - if they hid an aircraft program, what else is underground?</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1981-01-01</begin><end>1981-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-116.7808,37.7988,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Dugway Proving Ground, Utah</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>798,855 acres of restricted desert. Chemical/biological weapons testing since 1942. 2011 lockdown: a vial of VX nerve agent went missing. Open-air biological testing (Project SHAD, 1960s). Underground bunkers and test chambers. Marked on 1996 DUMB World Bases map. The facility that lost a vial of VX nerve agent - the most lethal substance on Earth - and locked down 800,000 acres to find it. What else is stored beneath that desert?</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2011-01-01</begin><end>2011-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-112.9336,40.1756,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chaco Canyon, New Mexico</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>UNESCO World Heritage. Ancestral Puebloan ceremonial center (850-1250 CE). Great houses with subterranean kivas - circular underground chambers aligned to solstice events. 400+ miles of engineered roads radiating outward to outlier sites. Marked as suspected ancient tunnel site on Four Corners Event Characteristics map. The underground chambers and 400-mile road network predate European contact by centuries. The Puebloans built underground first.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-107.9613,36.0604,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mt. Taylor, New Mexico</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>11,301 ft - sacred to Navajo (Tsoodził, &#x27;Turquoise Mountain&#x27;), Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni peoples. Major uranium mining district surrounding the mountain (Grants Uranium Belt - largest uranium deposits in U.S.). Jackpile Mine (Laguna Pueblo): largest open-pit uranium mine in the world, on indigenous land. Marked on Four Corners Event Characteristics map. The sacred mountain surrounded by uranium extraction - the mineral that powers the bombs and the reactors, mined from land the people consider holy.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-107.6323,35.2733,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Socorro, New Mexico</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>New Mexico Institute of Mining and Technology. Energetic Materials Research and Testing Center (EMRTC) - underground explosive testing. 40 miles from Trinity Site (first atomic bomb, July 16, 1945). Very Large Array radio telescope 50 miles west. Seismological Observatory monitors earthquakes across the state. Marked on Four Corners Event Characteristics map. The town with underground explosives testing, nuclear ground zero down the road, and a listening array pointed at the sky.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1945-07-16</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-106.9013,34.0584,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Paris Catacombs, France</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>300+ km of tunnels beneath Paris. Former limestone quarries (13th century onward). Ossuary holds remains of 6+ million people (transferred 1786-1860). WWII: French Resistance headquarters in the catacombs; German bunker in adjacent tunnels. Only 1.7 km open to public. Cataphiles (illegal urban explorers) access the remaining 298+ km. The city beneath the city - older than the sewers, deeper than the metro, and largely unmapped. What connects to what is still unknown.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1786-01-01</begin><end>1786-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>2.3322,48.8338,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Edinburgh Vaults, Scotland</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>South Bridge Vaults (1788): 120 rooms beneath the bridges of Edinburgh&#x27;s Old Town. Used as taverns, workshops, and residences - then abandoned and sealed. Underground streets and multi-room complexes. Mary King&#x27;s Close: 17th-century street buried beneath the Royal Exchange. Edinburgh is built on layers - the surface city is the newest version. The underground city came first.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1788-01-01</begin><end>1788-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-3.1883,55.949,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kaymakli Underground City, Cappadocia, Turkey</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>8 levels deep (only 4 open to public). Capacity: ~3,500 people. Connected to Derinkuyu by 8 km tunnel. One of 36+ underground cities in Cappadocia - the most in any single region on Earth. Storage rooms, churches, wineries, stables all underground. First used by Hittites (~2000 BCE). 36 underground cities in one region. The question is not who built them - it is what they were hiding from.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2000-01-01</begin><end>2000-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>34.7525,38.4575,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Wieliczka Salt Mine, Poland</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>UNESCO World Heritage. Operating since 13th century - 700+ years of continuous mining. 287 km of tunnels on 9 levels, reaching 327m depth. Underground chapels (St. Kinga&#x27;s Chapel: chandeliers carved from rock salt), lakes, sanitariums. 2,000+ chambers. The underground city carved from salt over seven centuries. Now a spa, a chapel, and a museum - but still 287 km of tunnels that took 700 years to dig.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>20.0553,49.9833,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Coober Pedy, South Australia</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>&#x27;Opal Capital of the World.&#x27; 60% of residents live underground (&#x27;dugouts&#x27;) due to extreme surface temperatures (40°C+). Underground homes, churches, hotels, shops. Population ~1,700. Established 1915. The town that moved underground voluntarily. No government mandate, no military purpose - just humans who decided the surface was uninhabitable and built downward. Marked on Eastern Hemisphere underground city map.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1915-01-01</begin><end>1915-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>134.7544,-29.0135,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Naica Mine, Chihuahua, Mexico</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Cave of the Crystals (Cueva de los Cristales): selenite crystals up to 12m long and 55 tonnes - the largest natural crystals ever found. 300m below surface. Temperature 58°C, humidity 90-99%. Lethal without protective equipment. Discovered 2000 during mining operations. Flooded again 2015 when pumps were turned off. The crystal cave that kills you in 10 minutes without a suit - found by accident inside a lead and silver mine. What else is 300m down that hasn&#x27;t been pumped dry?</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2000-01-01</begin><end>2000-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-105.4967,27.8514,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lalibela Rock-Hewn Churches, Ethiopia</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>11 monolithic churches carved downward from bedrock (12th-13th century). Bet Giyorgis (Church of St. George): cruciform, carved 40 ft into a pit. Connected by underground passages and tunnels. UNESCO World Heritage. The churches were not built - they were excavated. Each one carved from a single piece of living rock, connected by subterranean corridors. The engineering required predates the tools that should have made it possible.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>39.0472,12.0319,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Wuhan Institute of Virology (BSL-4) - Wuhan, China</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>China&#x27;s first BSL-4 laboratory opened at the WIV (Chinese Academy of Sciences) in 2015, built under a Sino-French initiative at an eventual cost of ~US$42 million with 3,000 m² of BSL-4 space plus BSL-2/BSL-3 labs. It became a central subject of COVID-19 origin investigations. Source: Wikipedia / Emerging Infectious Diseases (CDC) (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wuhan_Institute_of_Virology).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2015-01-01</begin><end>2015-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>114.2611,30.3769,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>TSMC / Hsinchu Science Park - Hsinchu, Taiwan</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Roughly 90% of the world&#x27;s most advanced semiconductors are produced in the Hsinchu cluster anchored by TSMC, and by 2025 essentially all top-tier AI training chips are fabricated in TSMC&#x27;s Taiwan fabs — the concentration underpinning the &#x27;Silicon Shield&#x27; theory of Taiwan&#x27;s deterrence. Source: Foreign Policy / Newsweek (foreignpolicy.com/2025/11/03/taiwan-silicon-shield-tsmc-semiconductor-chips).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>120.993,24.7773,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>ITER Fusion Reactor - Saint-Paul-lès-Durance, France</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>The 35-nation ITER tokamak at Cadarache aims to produce ~500 MW of fusion power from 50 MW of input (gain of 10). Originally budgeted near €5 billion, official estimates have risen to roughly €18–20 billion, with some outside observers citing program costs as high as ~$65 billion. Source: Physics World / Wikipedia (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ITER).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>5.7776,43.7071,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Oak Ridge National Laboratory - Oak Ridge, Tennessee, USA</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Established in 1943 as the Manhattan Project&#x27;s plutonium-piloting &#x27;Secret City&#x27; (population eventually ~75,000), ORNL is now the DOE&#x27;s largest science and energy lab and hosts Frontier, the world&#x27;s first exascale supercomputer, built with HPE Cray and AMD for about US$600 million. Source: Wikipedia / Undark / HPE (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frontier_(supercomputer)).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1943-01-01</begin><end>1943-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-84.3119,35.9301,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>RIKEN Center for Computational Science (Fugaku) - Kobe, Japan</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>RIKEN R-CCS on Kobe&#x27;s Port Island houses Fugaku, an ARM-based supercomputer with 158,976 nodes and ~442 PFLOPS peak that topped the TOP500 list in June 2020 — Japan&#x27;s flagship high-performance computing facility, successor to the K computer. Source: RIKEN R-CCS / Wikipedia (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fugaku_(supercomputer)).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2020-06-01</begin><end>2020-06-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>135.2207,34.6529,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Huawei Ox Horn Campus - Dongguan, China</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Huawei&#x27;s ~300-acre R&amp;D campus on Songshan Lake, opened June 2018 at a cost of ~US$1.5 billion, is built as 12 villages replicating European cities (Paris, Verona, Freiburg) linked by an imported Swiss red train, and houses tens of thousands of researchers at a company central to US–China tech-sanctions disputes. Source: Wikipedia / Yahoo Finance (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huawei_Ox_Horn_Campus).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2018-06-01</begin><end>2018-06-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>113.8819,22.8804,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Olsztyn-Mazury Airport (Szymany), Poland</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>A remote airfield where a Council of Europe inquiry found at least seven CIA-linked flights landed in 2002-2003, delivering high-value detainees to the nearby Stare Kiejkuty intelligence base ~12 miles away; Gulfstream jets reportedly bypassed customs. Khalid Sheikh Mohammed is said to have been held and waterboarded near here. Source: Worldcrunch, &#x27;Inside a Secret CIA Prison in the Polish Countryside&#x27;; CBS News, &#x27;Polish Logs Confirm CIA Rendition Flights&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2002-01-01</begin><end>2002-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>20.9473,53.4875,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Wenchang Space Launch Site, Hainan, China</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>China&#x27;s southernmost and only coastal spaceport, operational since 2016 at 19 N latitude to maximize payload; its seaside location lets oversized Long March 5/7/8 rocket stages built in Tianjin be shipped by sea barge, bypassing rail size limits, and it supports China&#x27;s space-station and lunar heavy-lift missions. Source: Wikipedia / Wenchang Space Launch Site; China Space Report, chinaspacereport.wordpress.com.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2016-01-01</begin><end>2016-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>110.9598,19.6286,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Jiuquan Satellite Launch Center, Inner Mongolia, China</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>China&#x27;s oldest and largest launch complex, located in the Gobi Desert (despite its Gansu-derived name it lies in Inner Mongolia&#x27;s Ejin Banner), and the sole site for the country&#x27;s crewed Shenzhou spaceflights; it is operated under the People&#x27;s Liberation Army. Source: China Space Report, chinaspacereport.wordpress.com; Wikipedia / Jiuquan Satellite Launch Center.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>100.2838,40.965,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Satish Dhawan Space Centre, Sriharikota, India</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>India&#x27;s primary spaceport, on a barrier island off the Bay of Bengal, from which ISRO launches its PSLV and GSLV/LVM3 rockets including the Chandrayaan and Mangalyaan interplanetary missions; the near-equatorial coastal site allows spent stages to drop safely over the sea. Source: ISRO, isro.gov.in; Wikipedia / Satish Dhawan Space Centre.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>80.2256,13.6281,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mittelwerk / Mittelbau-Dora Underground V-2 Factory, Nordhausen</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Nazi Germany converted a gypsum mine inside the Kohnstein hill into the underground Mittelwerk plant to mass-produce V-2 ballistic missiles and V-1 flying bombs using concentration-camp labor. Over 60,000 prisoners passed through the associated Mittelbau-Dora camp from 1943-1945 and at least a third died, making the missile program deadlier for its builders than its targets. Source: US Holocaust Memorial Museum (ushmm.org); Wikipedia, &#x27;Mittelwerk&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1943-01-01</begin><end>1943-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>10.7507,51.5345,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Gran Sasso National Laboratory (LNGS), Assergi</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>The largest underground physics laboratory in Europe, carved off a highway tunnel beneath 1,400 m of dolomite rock that cuts the cosmic-ray flux a million-fold, comprising three experimental halls (~100 m each) totaling about 180,000 cubic metres. It hosts dark-matter and neutrino experiments and was the endpoint of the 2011 CERN neutrino-speed measurement. Source: INFN / LNGS (lngs.infn.it).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2011-01-01</begin><end>2011-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>13.5162,42.4211,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>ASML Headquarters - Veldhoven, Netherlands</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>ASML is the only firm on Earth able to build extreme-ultraviolet (EUV) lithography machines — bus-sized systems priced around €150 million each — and holds effectively 100% of the EUV market; the Netherlands has barred EUV exports to China since 2019 under US pressure, making Veldhoven a linchpin of the global chip war. Source: Silicon Canals / Wikipedia (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ASML).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>5.417,51.4044,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NSO Group Headquarters - Herzliya, Israel</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>The Israeli cyber-intelligence firm NSO Group, founded 2010, develops Pegasus — a zero-click smartphone spyware classified as a military export and licensed sale-by-sale by the Israeli government. Investigations documented its use against journalists, activists and Palestinian NGO staff, and the US blacklisted the company in 2021. Source: Wikipedia / Amnesty International / OCCRP Pegasus Project (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NSO_Group).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2010-01-01</begin><end>2010-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>34.8469,32.1656,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>VECTOR State Research Center of Virology - Koltsovo, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Founded 1974 within the Soviet Biopreparat network, VECTOR is one of only two WHO-authorized repositories on Earth for the live variola (smallpox) virus, with BSL-1 to BSL-4 capability and ~1,614 staff. A 2019 explosion at the facility drew global attention to its pathogen stocks. Source: Wikipedia / Slate (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_Research_Center_of_Virology_and_Biotechnology_VECTOR).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1974-01-01</begin><end>1974-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>83.1871,54.9368,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>DARPA Headquarters - Arlington, Virginia, USA</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; technology</p><p>The Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency, created February 7, 1958 in response to Sputnik, funds the Pentagon&#x27;s emerging-technology research (its ARPANET work seeded the internet). Its 13-story, 353,000 sq ft Ballston headquarters at 675 North Randolph Street meets DoD anti-terrorism standards with an 82-foot secured perimeter. Source: Wikipedia / CoStar (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DARPA).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1958-02-07</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-77.1086,38.8787,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Long Tieng (Lima Site 20A), Laos</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>A CIA-run airbase and &#x27;secret city&#x27; that was the unofficial headquarters of the Secret War in Laos; at its peak the single airstrip handled around 900 daily takeoffs and landings, making it one of the busiest airfields in the world, while the surrounding town of 40,000 never appeared on maps. Source: CNN Travel, &#x27;Long Tieng, Laos: Once the most secret place on Earth&#x27;; Wikipedia / Long Tieng.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>103.0345,18.8632,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pinal Airpark (Marana), Arizona, USA</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>During the Vietnam era, Marana was the headquarters of all CIA air operations and the main U.S. maintenance base for Intermountain Airlines, a CIA front supporting Air America; later acquired by Evergreen, it is today the world&#x27;s largest commercial-aircraft storage and heavy-maintenance boneyard. Source: Center for Land Use Interpretation, clui.org; Wikipedia / Pinal Airpark.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-111.3325,32.5111,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Udorn Royal Thai Air Force Base, Udon Thani, Thailand</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>The Asian headquarters of Air America, the CIA&#x27;s covertly owned airline, and one of five Thai bases used covertly by the U.S. from 1961; it also hosted &#x27;Headquarters 333,&#x27; the Thai command directing forces in Laos. Air America ran operations into Laos from Udorn until June 1974. Source: Wikipedia / Udorn Royal Thai Air Force Base; Grey Dynamics, &#x27;Project 404&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1974-06-01</begin><end>1974-06-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>102.668,17.5212,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Transit Center at Manas, Bishkek, Kyrgyzstan</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>A key U.S. logistics hub for the Afghanistan war until 2014, at the center of a fuel-contracting scandal: a 2010 congressional probe found offshore suppliers Mina Corp and Red Star Enterprises had won over $1 billion in Pentagon contracts and imported jet fuel via opaque structures allegedly deceiving Russia. Source: Eurasianet, &#x27;Deconstructing Manas Fuel Suppliers&#x27; Corporate Structures&#x27;; U.S. House Oversight subcommittee report (Dec. 2010).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2010-01-01</begin><end>2010-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>74.6037,42.8761,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Eloy Alfaro Air Base (FOL Manta), Ecuador</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; airport</p><p>From 1999 to 2009 the U.S. ran this coastal base as a Forward Operating Location, flying E-3 Sentry and P-3 Orion surveillance missions across a 6,400 km swath feeding intelligence to Joint Interagency Task Force South; Manta flights accounted for about 60% of eastern-Pacific drug interdictions before Ecuador declined to renew the lease. Source: GlobalSecurity.org, &#x27;Eloy Alfaro Air Base / FOL Manta&#x27;; Air &amp; Space Forces Magazine.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1999-01-01</begin><end>1999-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-80.8169,-1.032,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sohae Satellite Launching Station (Tongchang-ri), North Korea</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>North Korea&#x27;s principal rocket-launch and engine-test facility near the Chinese border, used for satellite launches widely assessed as covers for long-range ballistic-missile development; commercial-satellite analysts (38 North, CSIS) closely track its gantry and engine-stand expansions. Source: 38 North (Stimson Center), 38north.org; CSIS Beyond Parallel, beyondparallel.csis.org.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>124.3891,40.0985,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sonnenberg Tunnel Civil Defense Shelter, Lucerne, Switzerland</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Built 1971-1976, this twin-bore motorway tunnel doubled as the world&#x27;s largest civilian nuclear fallout shelter, engineered to hold 20,000 people behind 350-tonne blast doors, with a seven-storey central cavern housing a command post, hospital, radio studio and prison cells. Switzerland cut its rated capacity to 2,000 in 2002 after concluding the dual-use design was unworkable. Source: Swiss Review (swisscommunity.org); Wikipedia, &#x27;Sonnenberg Tunnel&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1971-01-01</begin><end>1971-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>8.2808,47.0341,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Olavsvern Naval Base, Ramfjord, Tromsø</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>A Cold War Royal Norwegian Navy submarine base blasted into a mountain 15 km south of Tromsø near the Soviet border, protected by 270 m of gabbro rock and holding a 340 m submarine dock, dry dock and ammunition stores; NATO spent about USD 500 million building it. Decommissioned and sold to private investors in 2013, it later hosted Russian-chartered research vessels, prompting a security controversy. Source: The War Zone (twz.com); Newsweek; Wikipedia, &#x27;Olavsvern&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2013-01-01</begin><end>2013-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>19.1845,69.5625,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Onkalo Spent Nuclear Fuel Repository, Olkiluoto</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>The world&#x27;s first deep geological repository for permanent disposal of spent nuclear fuel, excavated by Posiva about 430 m into 1.9-billion-year-old bedrock on the Finnish west coast, with capacity for 6,500 tonnes of uranium sealed to isolate waste for 100,000 years. The IAEA&#x27;s director general called it a &#x27;game changer&#x27; for the nuclear industry. Source: IAEA (iaea.org); Wikipedia, &#x27;Onkalo spent nuclear fuel repository&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>21.4908,61.2341,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>China Jinping Underground Laboratory (CJPL), Sichuan</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Now the world&#x27;s deepest and largest underground laboratory, sited beside a hydropower traffic tunnel under 2,400 m of rock beneath Jinping Mountain; its CJPL-II expansion, operational December 2023, spans about 330,000 cubic metres and overtook Italy&#x27;s Gran Sasso in both depth and volume. It houses the PandaX and CDEX dark-matter searches. Source: Scientific American; Wikipedia, &#x27;China Jinping Underground Laboratory&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-12-01</begin><end>2023-12-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>102.2668,27.8953,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Waste Isolation Pilot Plant (WIPP), Carlsbad</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>The only U.S. deep geologic repository for defense transuranic (mostly plutonium-contaminated) waste, with disposal rooms mined 2,150 feet down into a 2,000-foot-thick, 250-million-year-old salt bed that slowly creeps shut to encapsulate the waste. Operating since 1999, it suffered a 2014 radiological release from a chemically reactive waste drum that shut the facility for years. Source: U.S. Department of Energy (energy.gov); EPA (epa.gov).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2014-01-01</begin><end>2014-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-105.996,34.5802,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kelvedon Hatch Secret Nuclear Bunker, Essex</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>A three-storey Cold War bunker sunk about 125 feet under an ordinary-looking Essex bungalow, walls of 10 feet of reinforced concrete inside a Faraday cage, designed as a Regional Government Headquarters for up to 600 personnel (potentially including the Prime Minister) to administer survivors after a nuclear strike. Decommissioned in 1992 and now a museum. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Kelvedon Hatch Secret Nuclear Bunker&#x27;; Nuclear Essex (nuclearessex.com).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1992-01-01</begin><end>1992-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>0.2547,51.6743,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bunker-42 (Tagansky Protected Command Point), Moscow</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>A 7,000-square-metre command complex, &#x27;Facility-02,&#x27; built from 1950 on Stalin&#x27;s orders 65 metres beneath Moscow near Taganskaya metro, intended as a bomb-proof refuge and command post for Soviet strategic nuclear-armed bombers. Staff were reportedly bused in windowless vehicles and kept unaware of its location; it now operates as a Cold War museum. Source: Rusmania (rusmania.com); Wikipedia, &#x27;Tagansky Protected Command Point&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1950-01-01</begin><end>1950-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>37.6671,55.7416,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mount Pony Federal Reserve Bunker (Culpeper Switch), Virginia</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>A radiation-hardened 140,000-square-foot bunker excavated into Mount Pony in 1969 as the Federal Reserve&#x27;s continuity-of-government center; it stored roughly USD 4 billion in shrink-wrapped currency to restart the economy after nuclear war and ran the &#x27;Culpeper Switch&#x27; handling the Fed&#x27;s national wire transfers from 1970-1988. Now the Library of Congress Packard Campus audio-visual archive. Source: Gizmodo/Paleofuture; FAS Nuclear Forces (nuke.fas.org); Wikipedia, &#x27;National Audio-Visual Conservation Center&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1969-01-01</begin><end>1969-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.9731,38.442,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Projekt Riese Underground Complex, Owl Mountains</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>An unfinished Nazi network code-named &#x27;Riese&#x27; (Giant) begun 1943-45 across seven sites in the Owl Mountains and Książ Castle, with about 90,000 cubic metres of tunnels excavated (only ~11% concrete-lined) and its true purpose - Führer headquarters or weapons plant - still undocumented. Built by forced laborers who died in large numbers from disease, starvation and cave-ins. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Project Riese&#x27;; Atlas Obscura.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1943-01-01</begin><end>1943-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>16.3256,50.8071,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Željava Underground Air Base (Objekt Klek 505), near Bihać</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section IX</b> &middot; underground</p><p>Yugoslavia&#x27;s largest underground air base, built 1957-1965 beneath Mount Plješevica on the Croatia-Bosnia border, with roughly 3.5 km of tunnels sized to shelter up to 60 warplanes and five runways (the longest 3,630 m). The withdrawing Yugoslav People&#x27;s Army dynamited the tunnels and runways in 1992 to deny its use. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Željava Air Base&#x27;; forgottenairfields.com.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#IX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1957-01-01</begin><end>1957-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>15.756,44.753,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section X (148)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>The Octagon (State Strategic Command Center) - New Capital, Egypt</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; military</p><p>Egypt&#x27;s Ministry of Defence headquarters, inaugurated July 2026. Official name: State Strategic Command Center. 22,000 acres (89 km²) across 13 zones, ~1,160 acres of floor area, eight buildings set around a ring; the Pentagon is one building of about 29 acres. Sits inside the New Capital, 45 km east of Cairo, whose governing vehicle ACUD is 51% Ministry of Defence, alongside 6,000+ AI cameras and the Iconic Tower (393.8m). Who financed the complex is not in the public record: US FMF ($1.3bn/yr since 1987) is disbursed to US contractors from a Federal Reserve Bank of New York account and cannot buy Egyptian construction; CSCEC financing is documented for the CBD, not for this; no Israeli funding is documented at any tier — Israeli coverage of the Octagon is the worried kind.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2026-07-01</begin><end>2026-07-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>31.653917,29.937917,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tura–Masara limestone quarries, Egypt</name><styleUrl>#t-underground</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; underground</p><p>About 6 km of underground limestone galleries on the Nile&#x27;s east bank, ~12 km south of Cairo and west of the Octagon. Cut as tunnels, not open pits, with limestone pillars left standing to carry the roofs. Source of the Great Pyramid&#x27;s outer casing (~67,390 m³ of fine Tura limestone for Khufu alone). Mapped for the British military in WWII for use as bomb-proof storage. Now the Tura cement works — Portland and oil-well cement — under Heidelberg Materials. Three tenancies in one hole in the ground; continuity of use is not continuity of purpose.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>31.2833,29.9333,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NEOM / THE LINE, Saudi Arabia</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>170km linear city, 200m wide, 500m tall mirrored glass walls. AI-managed population. OXAGON floating industrial city. TROJENA ski resort. Huwaitat tribe killed for resisting.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.3,27.95,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Songdo International Business District, South Korea</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Built on 1,500 acres reclaimed from Yellow Sea. &#x27;Ubiquitous city&#x27; with ubiquitous sensing. Population ~180,000 (below 300,000 target).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>126.6593,37.3818,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Masdar City, Abu Dhabi, UAE</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Zero-carbon planned city by Foster + Partners. Population ~5,000 vs 50,000 target. The smart city that couldn&#x27;t attract residents.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>54.6154,24.4265,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Quayside / Sidewalk Toronto, Canada</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Proposed 12-acre smart district by Google/Sidewalk Labs. Cancelled 2020 after public backlash over data harvesting. Toronto said no.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2020-01-01</begin><end>2020-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-79.3602,43.6426,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Amaravati, Andhra Pradesh, India</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>New state capital - 217 sq km by Foster + Partners. Stalled after 2019 elections. 33+ villages displaced. The displaced don&#x27;t get the smart city.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>80.518,16.515,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nusantara, Borneo, Indonesia</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>New national capital replacing Jakarta. 256,000 hectares. Government relocation began 2024. Moving the capital to the jungle.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2024-01-01</begin><end>2024-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>116.8312,-1.2834,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Forest City, Johor, Malaysia</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>$100B development by Country Garden. Largely empty ghost city. The smart city that no one moved to.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>103.631,1.3487,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Microsoft HQ, Redmond, Washington</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Windows 72% desktops, Azure cloud, GitHub (100M+ developers), LinkedIn (1B users), VS Code, PowerShell. The operating system layer.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-122.1267,47.6405,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Amazon / AWS HQ, Seattle</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Jeff Bezos. AWS hosts ~33% global cloud. Ring doorbell surveillance. Whole Foods. Washington Post. The infrastructure layer.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-122.3364,47.6223,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Google / Alphabet HQ, Mountain View, CA</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>92% search, Chrome 65%, Android 72%, YouTube 2B users. Project Maven (military AI). Project Nimbus ($1.2B Israeli AI targeting).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-122.0841,37.422,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Meta HQ, Menlo Park, CA</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Zuckerberg: 57.7% voting control. Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp: 3.07B monthly users. One person controls the social graph of half of humanity.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-122.1817,37.453,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Menwith Hill, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; military</p><p>Largest NSA facility outside USA. ECHELON station. 33 satellite tracking radomes; taps both fibre cables and satellite communications. Operated by Lockheed Martin. The arms manufacturer runs the listening post.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-1.6874,54.0016,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pine Gap, Northern Territory, Australia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; military</p><p>Joint CIA/ASD facility. ECHELON intercept station and satellite ground station processing signals from geostationary SIGINT satellites. Five Eyes southern hemisphere signals intelligence hub.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>133.737,-23.7981,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Waihopai Station, New Zealand</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; military</p><p>ECHELON intercept station. New Zealand node of the Five Eyes surveillance network.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>173.6167,-41.8,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Misawa Air Base, Japan</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; military</p><p>ECHELON intercept station. Five Eyes Asian Pacific signals intelligence node.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>141.3686,40.7031,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sugar Grove, West Virginia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; military</p><p>NSA intercept station. Domestic SIGINT collection facility.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-79.283,38.512,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Yakima Research Station, Washington</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; military</p><p>NSA intercept station. Pacific Northwest signals intelligence facility.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-120.5286,46.6818,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Gaza - Gaza Marine Gas Field</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Natural gas reserves discovered 2000 beneath Gaza territory. Mass civilian casualties. General Dynamics MK-80 bombs. Nimbus AI targeting.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2000-01-01</begin><end>2000-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>34.4667,31.5,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Porthcurno, Cornwall, UK - Cable Landing Station</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Historic submarine cable station since 1870. First transatlantic telegraph cables. GCHQ/NSA tap point - Operation Tempora (Snowden documents, 2013). Over 200 fiber optic cables pass through British waters. The UK&#x27;s geographic position makes it a mandatory chokepoint for transatlantic data.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2013-01-01</begin><end>2013-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-5.654,50.042,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bude, Cornwall, UK - GCHQ Cable Tap</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>GCHQ Bude - Tempora program intercept station. Snowden documents confirmed GCHQ taps submarine cables with 200+ probes, buffering 3 days of internet traffic and 30 days of metadata. Shared with NSA. The Five Eyes cables tap.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-4.5432,50.8307,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Marseille, France - Cable Landing Hub</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Major Mediterranean cable landing hub. 13+ submarine cable systems terminate here. Connects Europe to Africa, Middle East, and Asia. French DGSE intelligence maintains intercept capabilities at cable landing points.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>5.3698,43.2965,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fujairah, UAE - Cable Landing Station</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Strategic Gulf cable landing point. 10+ cables terminate here including Asia-Africa-Europe 1 (AAE-1) and FLAG. Connects Middle East to global internet backbone. UAE signals intelligence monitors traffic.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>56.3264,25.1288,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mumbai, India - TATA Landing Station</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Major submarine cable hub for South Asia. Multiple cable systems including TGN-Eurasia, i2i, and SEACOM. India&#x27;s RAW intelligence maintains monitoring at cable landing stations.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>72.8777,19.076,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Singapore - Cable Landing Hub</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Southeast Asia&#x27;s primary cable hub. 30+ submarine cable systems. Changi North cable landing station. Singapore&#x27;s geographic position makes it a mandatory transit point for Asia-Pacific data - the digital Strait of Malacca.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>103.8303,1.2494,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tuas, Singapore - Equinix Cable Station</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Major cable landing for trans-Pacific and intra-Asian cables. Equinix data center colocation. Where submarine cables meet cloud infrastructure.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>103.64,1.31,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Manasquan, New Jersey - TAT-14 Landing</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Transatlantic cable landing station. TAT-14 and other major cables connect here. NSA&#x27;s proximity to cable landing stations in the northeastern U.S. documented in Snowden disclosures.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-74.0486,40.1262,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tuckerton, New Jersey - Cable Landing</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Historic and active submarine cable landing. Multiple transatlantic cables terminate here. NSA intercept point. New Jersey coast is a primary transatlantic cable corridor.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-74.3402,39.6037,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Long Island, New York - Cable Landing</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Multiple submarine cables terminate on Long Island&#x27;s shores. Connects to Manhattan data centers. Dense concentration of transatlantic cable landings along the northeastern U.S. coast.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.135,40.7891,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Miami, Florida - AMPATH Cable Landing</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Americas cable hub. ARCOS, Bahamas Internet Cable System, and multiple Latin American cables terminate here. Connects North America to Caribbean, Central and South America. NAP of the Americas data center.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-80.1918,25.7617,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fortaleza, Brazil - Cable Landing</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>South American cable hub. SACS (South Atlantic Cable System) connects directly to Angola. EllaLink connects to Europe. Brazil&#x27;s northeastern coast is the landing point for South Atlantic cables.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-38.5433,-3.7172,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Luzon, Philippines - Cable Landing</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Major Asia-Pacific cable landing. Multiple cables including Asia-America Gateway (AAG) and Southeast Asia-Japan Cable (SJC). Strategic Pacific data hub.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>120.9842,14.5995,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lantau Island, Hong Kong - Cable Landing</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>China&#x27;s primary international cable hub. Asia-Pacific Gateway (APG), Asia Submarine-cable Express (ASE), and multiple cable systems. Chinese government maintains monitoring at all cable landing stations.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>113.944,22.2588,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Busan, South Korea - Cable Landing</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>East Asian cable hub. Korea-Japan Cable Network, Flag Pacific-1, and Unity cables terminate here. Connects Korean peninsula to trans-Pacific backbone.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>129.0756,35.1796,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sydney, Australia - Cable Landing Hub</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Australia&#x27;s primary cable landing. Southern Cross Cable, Australia-Japan Cable, and multiple systems terminate here. ASD (Australian Signals Directorate) intercept capabilities. Five Eyes southern node.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>151.2093,-33.8688,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Djibouti - Cable Chokepoint</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Critical submarine cable chokepoint - 10+ cables transit the narrow strait between Africa and Arabia. Same location as Camp Lemonnier (U.S. military / rendition hub). Military base and cable chokepoint share coordinates.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>43.1456,11.5721,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Egypt - Suez Canal Cable Corridor</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>15+ submarine cables transit Egyptian territory through the Suez Canal zone. Cable cuts in 2008 and 2013 disrupted internet for millions in the Middle East and South Asia. Single geographic chokepoint for Europe-Asia data.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2008-01-01</begin><end>2008-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>32.1746,30.0444,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Strait of Malacca - Cable Transit</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Critical strait transited by multiple Asia-Pacific submarine cables. One of the world&#x27;s busiest shipping lanes is also a critical data transit corridor. 40% of global trade and significant cable infrastructure share the same chokepoint.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>101.5,2.5,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vladivostok, Russia - ROTACS Landing</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Russia&#x27;s Pacific cable landing. ROTACS (Russia Optical Trans-Arctic Cable System) will connect to Russian Arctic infrastructure. Russia building alternative cable routes independent of Five Eyes chokepoints.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>131.9113,43.1332,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cape Canaveral / Kennedy Space Center, FL</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Primary U.S. satellite launch facility. SpaceX (Musk) launches Starlink constellation here - 6,000+ satellites providing global internet coverage. NRO reconnaissance satellites also launch from here. The surveillance constellation and the commercial constellation share the same launchpad.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-80.6077,28.3922,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vandenberg Space Force Base, CA</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>West coast satellite launch facility. NRO, Space Force, and SpaceX launches. Starlink polar orbit launches. Military and commercial satellite infrastructure co-located.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-120.5724,34.742,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Buckley Space Force Base / ADF-C, Aurora, CO</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Aerospace Data Facility-Colorado (ADF-C) - NRO&#x27;s primary CONUS ground station. Home of Space Delta 20 (satellite reconnaissance operations). Processes imagery from NRO spy satellites worldwide. &#x27;Sentient&#x27; AI system ingests ADF-C data - classified NRO program that uses AI to autonomously retask satellites at machine speed (&#x27;tipping and queueing&#x27;). NSA Colorado co-located on same installation - signals intelligence and imagery intelligence fused at same coordinates. Space-Based Infrared System (SBIRS) missile warning. The ground station that sees everything, now with an AI deciding what to look at next.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-104.752,39.717,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Schriever Space Force Base, Colorado Springs, CO</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>GPS Master Control Station - controls the entire Global Positioning System constellation (24+ satellites). AFSPC (Air Force Space Command). The facility that controls global positioning for military and civilian use.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-104.5286,38.8058,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Weilheim Ground Station, Bavaria, Germany</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>DLR (German Aerospace Center) satellite ground station. Controls European satellite programs including Copernicus Earth observation and Galileo navigation. EU&#x27;s independent satellite control.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>11.0806,47.8808,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fucino Space Centre, Abruzzo, Italy</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Telespazio ground station. Controls Galileo (EU GPS alternative), COSMO-SkyMed (Italian military radar satellites), and commercial communications satellites. Europe&#x27;s largest commercial satellite ground station.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>13.6008,41.9774,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Svalbard Satellite Station (SvalSat), Arctic Norway</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Northernmost satellite ground station on Earth. Only station that can contact polar-orbiting satellites on every pass. Used by NASA, NOAA, ESA, and NRO. Same Svalbard that houses the seed vault - data and genetics preserved at the same coordinates.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>15.3894,78.2306,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>GCHQ Bude, Cornwall, UK - Satellite Intercept</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>GCHQ satellite communications intercept station. Linked to Echelon. Taps Intelsat and other commercial satellite traffic. Dual-function: cable tap and satellite intercept at same facility.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-4.5432,50.8307,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Starlink Gateway, Merrillan, WI</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>SpaceX Starlink ground gateway station. Routes internet traffic between Starlink satellites and the terrestrial internet backbone. Musk&#x27;s satellite network requires terrestrial ground stations - each one is a potential intercept point.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-90.833,44.45,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Starlink Gateway, Conrad, MT</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>SpaceX Starlink ground station. Northern U.S. gateway. Starlink operates 6,000+ satellites - the largest satellite constellation in history, owned by a single individual (Musk, Tier 5).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-111.946,48.17,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>OneWeb Ground Station, Fairbanks, AK</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>OneWeb satellite ground station. Bharti Global (India) and UK government joint venture. Competitor to Starlink with 630+ satellites. Arctic ground station for polar orbit coverage.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-147.72,64.84,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Beijing Satellite Control Center, China</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Controls China&#x27;s BeiDou navigation constellation (55 satellites - alternative to GPS), Tiangong space station, Chang&#x27;e lunar missions, and military reconnaissance satellites. China&#x27;s sovereign satellite control infrastructure.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>116.3333,39.9667,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Baikonur Cosmodrome, Kazakhstan</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Russia&#x27;s primary satellite launch facility. GLONASS navigation constellation, military reconnaissance satellites, and ISS crew launches. Soviet-era facility on sovereign Kazakh soil, leased to Russia. The satellite launch site is in another country.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>63.305,45.965,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NRO Headquarters, Chantilly, VA</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>National Reconnaissance Office - builds and operates U.S. spy satellites. Manages 200+ satellites (2025). Advanced Systems &amp; Technology (AS&amp;T) Directorate houses &#x27;Sentient&#x27; - classified AI system that autonomously retasks satellites at machine speed. &#x27;Tipping and queueing&#x27;: Sentient detects anomaly in one data source, instantly redirects satellite constellation to investigate. Ingests EVERYTHING - imagery, SIGINT, financial records, weather, mobile device data, shipping traffic, social networks. NRO proliferated constellation: 150+ new satellites by April 2025 in addition to legacy birds. The satellites are deliberately &#x27;dumb&#x27; - passive sensor platforms with software-defined payloads updated from ground. Intelligence lives in the ground architecture, not in orbit. The AI that watches the world.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2025-04-01</begin><end>2025-04-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.4508,38.8819,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Aerospace Data Facility-East (ADF-E) / Area 58, Fort Belvoir, VA</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>ADF-E - NRO ground station code-named &#x27;Area 58.&#x27; Manages KH-11 KENNEN electro-optical imagery satellites and Lacrosse/Onyx synthetic aperture radar satellites. NGA (National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency) co-located - imagery processing and geospatial intelligence fused at same facility. Sits on Fort Belvoir alongside ISA/Task Force Orange (documented separately). The ground station that processes what the spy satellites photograph, located 15 miles from NRO headquarters.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.1583,38.7361,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Aerospace Data Facility-Southwest (ADF-SW), White Sands, NM</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>ADF-SW - NRO ground station at White Sands Missile Range, New Mexico. Third node of ADF ground station triad (Colorado, East, Southwest). Redundant satellite processing facility - if ADF-C or ADF-E are destroyed, ADF-SW maintains continuity. White Sands: first atomic bomb test (Trinity, 1945), first captured V-2 rocket launches, and now NRO satellite ground processing. Nuclear birth site repurposed as the backup brain for the satellite surveillance constellation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1945-01-01</begin><end>1945-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-106.6108,32.5019,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>BlackSky Technology, Herndon, VA</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>BlackSky - commercial geospatial intelligence company. Constellation of high-revisit-rate Earth observation satellites. NRO commercial imagery provider. &#x27;Hoovering up&#x27; data from dozens of satellites, 100M+ mobile devices, ships, aircraft, social networks, and environmental sensors. Spectra AI platform fuses satellite imagery with alternative data sources for real-time global monitoring. Herndon HQ - 10 miles from NRO headquarters in Chantilly. A commercial company vacuuming up 100 million mobile device signals and selling the analysis to the spy satellite agency down the road.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.4055,38.9556,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Maxar Technologies (Vantor), Westminster, CO</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Maxar Technologies - rebranded to Vantor (2025). Builds and operates WorldView satellite constellation. Provides &#x27;90% of the foundational GEOINT&#x27; to U.S. intelligence community. NRO&#x27;s primary commercial imagery supplier. Builds satellite buses for NRO classified missions. Westminster CO headquarters - 30 miles from Buckley SFB/ADF-C. The company that builds the satellites, operates the commercial constellation, and provides the baseline imagery that Sentient AI processes. 90% of the pictures the intelligence community looks at come from one company.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2025-01-01</begin><end>2025-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-105.0275,39.9147,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Planet Labs, San Francisco, CA</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Planet Labs - operates largest Earth observation constellation in history (~200 Dove satellites). Daily imaging of Earth&#x27;s entire landmass. NRO commercial imagery provider. &#x27;Daily scan&#x27; model - every point on Earth photographed every day, archived forever. Change detection at planetary scale. Unlike traditional spy satellites that photograph on command, Planet photographs everything every day whether anyone asked or not. The haystack is pre-built. Sentient just searches it.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-122.3963,37.7815,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>SpaceX Starshield / MILNET, Hawthorne, CA</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>SpaceX headquarters - operates MILNET/Starshield military satellite constellation. 480+ classified satellites in low Earth orbit as of June 2025. &#x27;Hybrid mesh network&#x27; combining commercial Starlink and dedicated military payloads. Space Force Delta 8 oversees operations. The same company (SpaceX/Musk, Tier 5) that operates 6,000+ commercial Starlink satellites also operates 480+ dedicated military satellites forming a mesh network for the Pentagon. NRO reconnaissance data can route through this mesh. The commercial internet constellation and the military spy constellation share the same operator, same factories, same launch vehicles.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-118.328,33.9207,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Brookhaven National Laboratory, Long Island</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; technology</p><p>DOE national laboratory. Relativistic Heavy Ion Collider (RHIC). Particle physics, nuclear physics, nanotechnology. Same Long Island corridor as Camp Hero/Montauk and Plum Island. Federal research concentration at the geographic terminus.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-72.8865,40.8715,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hollywood, Los Angeles</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Entertainment industry as cultural manufacturing. Operation Mockingbird: CIA infiltration of 400+ journalists. Laurel Canyon: military/intelligence families became counterculture musicians - Jim Morrison (father: Admiral, Gulf of Tonkin), Frank Zappa (father: chemical warfare, Edgewood Arsenal). The counterculture manufactured by intelligence children.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-118.3287,34.0928,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Burbank - Lockheed Skunk Works / Studios</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Lockheed operated in Burbank 1928-1994; the Skunk Works (from 1943) designed the U-2, SR-71 and F-117 here. ALSO: Warner Bros, Walt Disney Studios, NBC/Universal. The city that built stealth aircraft builds entertainment content - same zip code, different product lines. THE EXIT, DATED: Skunk Works headquarters moved to Palmdale in 1992; the Burbank shutdown completed in 1994. Burbank kept the visible image industry and lost the invisible one. WHAT STAYED: the site sits inside the San Fernando Valley Superfund site, listed 1986 (Burbank Operable Unit) - TCE, PCE, hexavalent chromium and 1,4-dioxane in groundwater, with roughly 3.3 billion gallons treated and returned to municipal supply annually. THE OTHER HALF OF THE SENTENCE: Burbank built the airframe; Rochester, NY made and processed the film it carried (see Kodak Hawkeye Works). Sources: EPA San Fernando Valley Superfund record; Lockheed Burbank plant histories.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1928-01-01</begin><end>1928-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-118.309,34.1808,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Glendale, California</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>DreamWorks Animation HQ. Nestlé USA HQ. Forest Lawn Memorial Park - entertainment industry burial ground. Part of the 20-mile Hollywood/Burbank/Pasadena entertainment-military corridor.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-118.2551,34.1425,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Laurel Canyon, Los Angeles</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Lookout Mountain Air Force Station - classified film studio operated by U.S. Air Force (1947–1969). Produced classified films of nuclear tests, military operations. Same canyon where military/intelligence families&#x27; children became the 1960s counterculture: Jim Morrison, Frank Zappa, David Crosby, Jackson Browne. The military film studio sat above the neighborhood that manufactured the counterculture. The base produced classified content. The canyon produced cultural content. Same geography, same families, different product lines.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1947-01-01</begin><end>1947-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-118.369,34.1078,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vivex Biologics, Marietta, Georgia</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Timothy Taylor - CEO/founder connected to Vivex Biologics. Multiple medical/pharmaceutical patents. Identified as &#x27;Tyler D.&#x27; in Dr. Diana Walsh Pasulka&#x27;s &#x27;American Cosmic&#x27; (2019). Top-level DoD clearances. Involved in NASA rocket launches at Cape Canaveral. Reports receiving &#x27;downloads&#x27; of patentable information during meditation - monastic lifestyle protocol (hydration, sleep discipline, no substances, 1-3 hrs daily meditation). The biotech executive with defense clearances who reverse-engineers anomalous materials and patents the results.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-84.5499,33.9526,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fayetteville, North Carolina - Bledsoe Encounters</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Chris Bledsoe - UAP/NHI contactee documented by NASA, CIA, DIA, and multiple intelligence community figures. Timothy Taylor (&#x27;Tyler D.&#x27;) connected to Bledsoe through intelligence community channels. Bledsoe&#x27;s encounters investigated by NASA Chief Scientist (Jim Green era). Fayetteville adjacent to Fort Liberty (formerly Bragg) - JSOC, Delta Force, Special Operations Command. The contactee lives next to the special operations headquarters. The intelligence community investigates the phenomenon while the military community surrounds it.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-78.8784,35.0527,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Esalen Institute, Big Sur, California</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Human potential movement headquarters. John C. Lilly conducted consciousness research here - sensory deprivation tanks, dolphin communication, ketamine protocols. Lilly coined &#x27;Earth Coincidence Control Office&#x27; (ECCO) - the concept that coincidences are orchestrated by a higher control system. CIA funding through Lilly&#x27;s earlier dolphin communication research. MKUltra → sensory deprivation → isolation tanks → Lilly → ECCO → Timothy Taylor pipeline. The counterculture research center funded by the intelligence community it claims to transcend.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.6303,36.1307,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fullerton, CA - Philip K. Dick / VALIS</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Philip K. Dick (1928–1982). Science fiction author whose work maps the architecture: Blade Runner (surveillance state), Minority Report (pre-crime policing), A Scanner Darkly (mass surveillance), Total Recall (memory erasure), Man in the High Castle (alternate totalitarianism), Adjustment Bureau (reality manipulation by hidden controllers). Films generated $1B+ revenue. FBI visited Dick and wife (1955); Dick wrote TO the FBI accusing others of subversion (1972, 1974). Home burglary (1971): safe blown, papers stolen, never solved - classic intelligence operation pattern. Feb–March 1974 (&#x27;2-3-74&#x27;): after sodium pentothal (MKUltra truth serum), experienced VALIS - &#x27;Vast Active Living Intelligence System&#x27; - an external intelligence transmitting information directly into his mind. Parallel to ECCO (Lilly) and Timothy Taylor&#x27;s &#x27;downloads.&#x27; Wrote 8,000-page Exegesis (1 million words) documenting the experience. Core thesis: &#x27;The Empire never ended&#x27; - Rome never fell, it changed costumes. Donated papers to Cal State Fullerton. Died in Santa Ana, 1982. The architecture&#x27;s most prolific scribe: he documented the system from inside, and the system turned his documentation into entertainment product.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1974-03-01</begin><end>1974-03-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-117.9242,33.8703,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Eareckson AFS, Shemya Island, Alaska</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Aleutian Islands signals intelligence. Cobra Dane phased-array radar. Remote Pacific monitoring at the western terminus of the Aleutian chain. The listening post at the edge of the hemisphere.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>174.112,52.7115,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CERN Large Hadron Collider, Geneva</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; technology</p><p>27 km circumference particle accelerator, 100m underground. Crosses French-Swiss border four times. Cost: $13.25B. Confirmed Higgs boson (2012). The largest machine ever built, invisible from the surface. Controls the border between particle physics and theoretical physics.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>6.1432,46.2044,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CFS Alert, Nunavut, Canada</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Northernmost permanently inhabited place on Earth. 817 km from North Pole. Signals intelligence station - Five Eyes Arctic SIGINT. Closer to Moscow than to Ottawa. The listening post at the top of the world.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-62.3481,82.5018,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Canadian Forces Station St. John&#x27;s, Newfoundland</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Transatlantic cable landing zone. Submarine cable infrastructure crossing the Atlantic terminates here. Five Eyes cable intelligence node. The eastern edge of North America where the cables come ashore.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-52.7126,47.5615,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Novosibirsk - Akademgorodok, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; technology</p><p>&#x27;Science City&#x27; - built 1957 as purpose-built Soviet research center in Siberian forest. 35 research institutes, 65,000 scientists. Nuclear physics, genetics, particle physics. The Soviet model: build the research city from scratch in the forest, far from prying eyes.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1957-01-01</begin><end>1957-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>83.0941,54.8529,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lubyanka Building, Moscow - FSB/KGB HQ</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Federal Security Service (FSB) headquarters. Previously KGB, NKVD, OGPU, Cheka - the address changed occupants but kept the function since 1919. Internal prison in basement. Stalin&#x27;s purge orders originated here. Every Russian intelligence directorate traces lineage to this building. The yellow building on the square that has watched Moscow for a century.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1919-01-01</begin><end>1919-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>37.6276,55.76,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cambridge, UK - ARM Holdings / Silicon Fen</name><styleUrl>#t-crypto-tech</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; crypto-tech</p><p>Silicon Fen - Europe&#x27;s largest technology cluster. ARM Holdings (SoftBank-owned): chips in 95% of smartphones. Every mobile device, every transaction, every location ping passes through ARM architecture designed here. The village that designed the world&#x27;s nervous system.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>0.1218,52.2053,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tsukuba Science City, Japan</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Purpose-built science city (1960s). JAXA headquarters. KEK particle accelerator. Over 300 research institutions. 20,000+ researchers. The Japanese model: build the entire research city from scratch, 60 km from Tokyo. Government-planned knowledge concentration.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1960-01-01</begin><end>1960-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>140.0766,36.0835,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shenzhen, China - Hardware Capital</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; technology</p><p>From fishing village (1979) to 17.5M people. Huawei, Tencent, DJI, ZTE, BYD. Manufactures 90% of world&#x27;s consumer electronics. SEZ model - Special Economic Zone as controlled economic experiment. The factory floor of the surveillance state.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1979-01-01</begin><end>1979-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>114.0579,22.5431,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Palantir HQ, Denver, Colorado</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Co-founded by Peter Thiel (PayPal, CIA-funded). CIA was first customer (In-Q-Tel investment). Gotham platform: military/intelligence. Foundry: corporate. Used by ICE for immigrant tracking. Denver HQ - same city as DIA. The surveillance company named after a seeing-stone from Tolkien.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-104.9994,39.7506,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Black Cube HQ, Vienna / Berlin</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Black Cube: private intelligence firm founded by former Israeli Mossad and Aman operatives (2010). Hired by Harvey Weinstein to surveil accusers. Hired by Hungarian government against NGOs. The private spy firm named after the most sacred geometric form. The cube that watches.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2010-01-01</begin><end>2010-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>16.3738,48.2082,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Paramount Pictures, Hollywood</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Founded 1912. Oldest surviving Hollywood studio. CIA Office of Public Affairs maintains entertainment liaison office - provides script notes, military equipment access, and base locations to studios that portray the agency favorably. Paramount: Top Gun (1986, Navy recruitment spiked 500%), Mission: Impossible franchise. The studio that launders military recruitment through entertainment product.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1912-01-01</begin><end>1912-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-118.3195,34.0833,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Universal Studios, Universal City</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>NBCUniversal - owned by Comcast. The Bourne franchise: CIA assassins, mass surveillance, rogue programs. Jurassic World: DARPA/InGen genetic weapons. Universal Studios theme park: the entertainment that makes you walk through the intelligence architecture for fun. Parent company Comcast is the nation&#x27;s largest internet provider - the studio AND the surveillance pipe.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-118.3534,34.1381,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sony Pictures / Columbia, Culver City</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Sony Pictures Entertainment - formerly Columbia Pictures (founded 1918). Zero Dark Thirty (2012): CIA collaborated directly with filmmakers, provided classified briefings. Scandal: CIA director Leon Panetta disclosed classified info to screenwriter Mark Boal at CIA ceremony. The agency shaped the film about the agency. Sony hack (2014, attributed to North Korea/Lazarus Group) - state-level cyberattack on a movie studio over &#x27;The Interview.&#x27; The studio as geopolitical target.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1918-01-01</begin><end>1918-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-118.4014,34.0201,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Walt Disney Studios, Burbank</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Walt Disney&#x27;s FBI informant file: SAC Contact/Special Agent in Charge (1940-1966). Disney testified before HUAC (1947), named union organizers as communists. CIA-Disney cooperation: &#x27;Man in Space&#x27; (1955) series with Wernher von Braun (Operation Paperclip). Disneyland opened same year. Disney now owns: Marvel, Lucasfilm (Star Wars), Pixar, ABC, ESPN, National Geographic, 21st Century Fox entertainment. The company that went from FBI informant to controlling 40% of U.S. box office.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1940-01-01</begin><end>1940-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-118.3254,34.1565,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Warner Bros. Studios, Burbank</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Warner Bros. Discovery - merged with Discovery (2022). The Matrix franchise: simulated reality, machine control, human batteries. Eyes Wide Shut (1999): Kubrick&#x27;s film about elite ritual societies - he showed the final cut to Warner Bros. executives and died 4 days later, March 7, 1999. Warner reportedly cut 24 minutes before release. The studio that received Kubrick&#x27;s last film and edited it after he died.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1999-03-07</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-118.3381,34.1483,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pinewood Studios, Buckinghamshire, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>UK&#x27;s premier film studio since 1936. James Bond franchise home. Ian Fleming - Bond creator - was Naval Intelligence Division officer (Section 17). Bond is not fiction about intelligence. Bond is intelligence officer fiction BY an intelligence officer. MI5/MI6 entertainment liaison mirrors CIA&#x27;s. Pinewood also: Star Wars, Marvel UK productions. 30 miles from GCHQ Bude (submarine cable tap). The studio that makes spy films for the spy agency.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1936-01-01</begin><end>1936-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.534,51.548,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Elstree Studios, Hertfordshire, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Original Star Wars trilogy (1977-1983), Indiana Jones, The Shining. Adjacent to Elstree film history - Borehamwood was &#x27;British Hollywood.&#x27; Also home to Big Brother UK. From Kubrick to reality TV surveillance entertainment - the arc of the panopticon as content.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1977-01-01</begin><end>1977-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.294,51.656,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shepperton Studios, Surrey, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Established 1931. Ridley Scott&#x27;s Alien, Blade Runner. In 2023 the studio capacity expansion was funded as part of UK&#x27;s creative industries strategy - state investment in cultural production infrastructure. 25 miles from central London, 40 miles from GCHQ Cheltenham.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1931-01-01</begin><end>1931-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.459,51.386,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cinecittà Studios, Rome, Italy</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Founded 1937 by Mussolini - literally &#x27;Cinema City.&#x27; Built as fascist propaganda infrastructure. Fellini transformed it postwar. Ben-Hur (1959), Cleopatra (1963), Gangs of New York (2002). NATO&#x27;s Allied Joint Force Command Naples is 140 miles south. The propaganda studio that became art cinema. The fascist infrastructure repurposed but never demolished.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1937-01-01</begin><end>1937-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.575,41.852,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Studio Babelsberg, Potsdam, Germany</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>World&#x27;s oldest large-scale film studio (1912). Metropolis (1927, Fritz Lang) - the film that depicted class stratification as architectural fact. UFA under Goebbels: Nazi propaganda machine. Postwar: DEFA (East German state film). Post-reunification: Hollywood productions (Inglourious Basterds, Grand Budapest Hotel). The studio that served Weimar, Nazi, Communist, and capitalist masters. Every regime needs a camera.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1912-01-01</begin><end>1912-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>13.058,52.388,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mosfilm Studios, Moscow, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Soviet Union&#x27;s primary film studio (founded 1920). Eisenstein&#x27;s &#x27;Battleship Potemkin&#x27; (1925) - the film that taught the world montage was a weapon. Soviet cinema as state function: every film approved by Goskino (State Committee for Cinematography). Tarkovsky&#x27;s &#x27;Stalker&#x27; (1979): the Zone as forbidden knowledge territory. Mosfilm still operates. Russia&#x27;s RT (state media) is the modern continuation - same state, different medium.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1920-01-01</begin><end>1920-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>37.5285,55.7155,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mumbai Film City (Goregaon), India</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Bollywood - world&#x27;s largest film industry by output: 1,500-2,000 films/year (vs. Hollywood&#x27;s ~700). Dadasaheb Phalke Studios, Yash Raj Films, Film City complex. Indian cinema as soft power: RAW (Research and Analysis Wing) documented Bollywood&#x27;s role in cultural influence across South Asia, Middle East, Africa. India&#x27;s Information and Broadcasting Ministry reviews/censors content. The world&#x27;s largest dream factory, state-supervised.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>72.8384,19.1631,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ramoji Film City, Hyderabad, India</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Guinness World Record: largest film studio complex (1,666 acres). Telugu, Tamil, Hindi, and international productions. Owned by Ramoji Group (Eenadu media conglomerate). India produces films in 20+ languages - the most linguistically diverse film industry on Earth. Cultural manufacturing at continental scale.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>78.6808,17.2543,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Toho Studios, Setagaya, Tokyo, Japan</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Godzilla (1954) - the first film was not entertainment. It was Hiroshima processed through metaphor. The monster created by nuclear radiation, destroying Tokyo - 9 years after the actual nuclear destruction of Hiroshima and Nagasaki. Toho produced it. Akira Kurosawa&#x27;s films also Toho. Japanese cinema&#x27;s postwar output is atomic trauma rendered as genre. The bomb became a monster. The monster became a franchise.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1954-01-01</begin><end>1954-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>139.6101,35.6321,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CJ ENM / Korean Film Studios, Seoul</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>South Korean cultural export machine - &#x27;Hallyu&#x27; (Korean Wave). Parasite (2019, Bong Joon-ho): class architecture as thriller - first non-English Best Picture Oscar. K-pop, K-drama: South Korean government&#x27;s Ministry of Culture invests directly in cultural export as soft power strategy. CJ Group (Samsung family offshoot). The chaebols that manufacture electronics also manufacture culture. Same conglomerate structure, different product lines.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>127.104,37.514,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hengdian World Studios, Zhejiang, China</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>World&#x27;s largest outdoor film studio - 7,930 acres. Built replicas of Beijing&#x27;s Forbidden City, entire historical Chinese cities. 200+ productions simultaneously. China&#x27;s film market: $7.3B+ annual box office (second largest globally). Every film released in China requires CCP Central Propaganda Department approval. 34 foreign films allowed per year (import quota). The world&#x27;s second largest entertainment market, fully state-curated.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>120.247,29.131,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>China Film Group / Beijing Studios</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>State-owned enterprise under CCP Central Propaganda Department. Monopoly on foreign film imports (34/year quota). Co-production agreements require script approval, PLA cooperation, positive portrayal of China. Hollywood studios (Disney, Universal, Paramount) self-censor for Chinese market access - removing Taiwan flags, altering plotlines, cutting scenes. The market that censors the content before the content is made. $7B+ leverage.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>116.466,39.981,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nollywood - Lagos Film District, Nigeria</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>World&#x27;s second largest film industry by volume (~2,500 films/year). $6.4B industry. Nollywood emerged from video parlor culture in the 1990s - no state funding, no studio system, pure market-driven production. Films distributed via VCD/DVD/streaming across Africa. Cultural influence: 300M+ viewers across the continent. The film industry that was never designed, never funded, and outproduces Hollywood. Organic cultural manufacturing.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1990-01-01</begin><end>1990-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>3.3792,6.5244,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fox Studios Australia, Sydney</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>20th Century Fox (now Disney) Australian hub. The Matrix trilogy filmed here. Star Wars prequels. Marvel productions. Five Eyes intelligence partner (Pine Gap, ASD) producing Five Eyes entertainment content. Sydney: AUKUS submarine deal partner producing films about military technology for the military alliance that funds the submarine deal.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>151.219,-33.892,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Weta Workshop / Stone Street Studios, Wellington, NZ</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Peter Jackson&#x27;s production complex. Lord of the Rings, Avatar, King Kong. New Zealand - Five Eyes member. GCSB (Government Communications Security Bureau) operates signals intelligence. The country with 5 million people and a signals intelligence agency also built Middle-earth. Wellington: Five Eyes node disguised as Hobbiton.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>174.772,-41.301,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sines Cable Landing Station - Sines, Portugal</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Sines is Portugal&#x27;s emerging Atlantic subsea hub: EllaLink lands here after crossing ~5,900 km from Fortaleza, Brazil, and the 8,760 km Medusa Mediterranean cable and the US-bound Nuvem system also terminate at the Sines Tech / Start Campus Sines 4.0 landing platform. It concentrates Europe–Americas–Africa traffic in one neutral facility. Source: Submarine Networks / EllaLink (submarinenetworks.com/en/stations/europe/portugal).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-8.869,37.9565,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Telxius Virginia Beach Cable Landing Station - Virginia Beach, USA</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>This single station at 1900 Corporate Landing Parkway lands three transatlantic systems: Microsoft/Meta&#x27;s MAREA (200 Tbps to Sopelana, Spain), Google&#x27;s 250 Tbps Dunant (to Saint-Hilaire-de-Riez, France), and Telxius&#x27;s ~11,000 km BRUSA (to Brazil and Puerto Rico), making it a primary US East Coast internet gateway. Source: Telxius / Submarine Networks (submarinenetworks.com/en/stations/north-america/usa-east/virginia-beach-cls).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1900-01-01</begin><end>1900-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-76.0085,36.7775,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Melkbosstrand Cable Landing Station - Cape Town, South Africa</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Telkom&#x27;s Melkbosstrand station north of Cape Town lands the legacy SAT-3/WASC and SAFE systems and, since 2022, Google&#x27;s 144 Tbps, 12-fibre-pair Equiano cable running down Africa&#x27;s west coast from Lisbon, a chokepoint for southern African connectivity. Source: News24 / Submarine Networks (submarinenetworks.com/en/stations/africa/south-africa).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-01-01</begin><end>2022-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>18.4453,-33.7322,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nangan / Matsu Islands Cable Landing - Lienchiang County, Taiwan</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>In February 2023 both undersea cables linking Taiwan&#x27;s Matsu Islands to the main island were severed six days apart — Taiwan attributed the No. 2 break to a Chinese fishing vessel and No. 3 to a Chinese freighter — leaving ~13,000 residents largely offline for nearly two months, a flashpoint case in cable-sabotage concerns. Source: New Bloom Magazine / PBS NewsHour (newbloommag.net/2023/02/17/matsu-submarine-cable-cut).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-02-01</begin><end>2023-02-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>119.9388,26.1529,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Piti Cable Landing Station - Piti, Guam</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Guam is a Pacific &#x27;highway exchange&#x27; where trans-Pacific systems interconnect; GTA&#x27;s typhoon-hardened GU1/GU2 stations at Piti land SEA-US, JGA North and JGA South. The steel-reinforced concrete facility is engineered to withstand 170-mph wind gusts, reflecting the cables&#x27; strategic value as the nearest US territory to Asia. Source: GTA / Popular Science / Submarine Networks (submarinenetworks.com/en/stations/north-america/usa-guam/piti).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>144.6964,13.4647,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mombasa Cable Landing Station - Mombasa, Kenya</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Mombasa is East Africa&#x27;s principal cable gateway, landing SEACOM (a 17,000 km system), the 10,000 km EASSy along Africa&#x27;s east coast, TEAMS, PEACE, and a planned 2Africa branch, funneling the region&#x27;s international bandwidth through one coastal node. Source: Submarine Networks / WIOCC SEACOM (submarinenetworks.com/en/stations/africa/kenya).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>39.6672,-4.0505,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chikura Cable Landing Station - Minamiboso, Japan</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>KDDI&#x27;s Chikura station in Chiba lands the 11,629 km FASTER trans-Pacific cable (a Google/KDDI/SingTel/China Mobile/China Telecom consortium, 60 Tbps design) plus Unity and other systems, making it a key eastern terminus for US–Japan internet traffic. Source: Submarine Networks / FASTER (submarinenetworks.com/en/stations/asia/japan/faster-ckikura-cls).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.9547,34.9767,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Catania / Sicily Cable Landing Hub - Catania, Italy</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>More than 20 subsea cables land on Sicily; the Catania landing station is a carrier-neutral node for SEA-ME-WE 5, and Sparkle&#x27;s Sicily Hub interconnects most Mediterranean cables, positioning the island as a primary Europe–Asia–Africa transit point. Source: Telecom Italia Sparkle / Submarine Networks (submarinenetworks.com/en/stations/europe/italy/sicily).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>15.0874,37.5024,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Jeddah Cable Landing - Red Sea Chokepoint, Saudi Arabia</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Jeddah anchors the Red Sea corridor, one of the world&#x27;s densest cable chokepoints, where ~18 cables carrying Europe–Asia traffic run close together. In Feb 2024 the anchor of the Houthi-struck bulk carrier Rubymar severed four cables (AAE-1, Seacom, EIG, TGN) between Jeddah and Djibouti, degrading service for parts of Asia and Africa. Source: ORF / Foreign Policy (orfonline.org — &#x27;Undersea chokepoints: The Red Sea cable disruptions&#x27;).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2024-02-01</begin><end>2024-02-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>39.1742,21.5504,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bandon Cable Landing Station - Bandon, Oregon, USA</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>The small Oregon coastal town of Bandon is the US landing point of Google&#x27;s FASTER trans-Pacific cable to Chikura/Shima, Japan and Tanshui, Taiwan — one of several trans-Pacific systems that make the Oregon coast a major gateway between North America and Asia. Source: Submarine Networks / FASTER (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FASTER_(cable_system)).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-124.4094,43.1196,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sopelana Cable Landing Station - Biscay, Spain</name><styleUrl>#t-submarine-cable</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; submarine-cable</p><p>Sopelana, near Bilbao, is the European terminus of the Microsoft/Meta MAREA cable, which runs ~4,000 miles (6,600 km) from Virginia Beach and can carry 200 Tbps, one of the highest-capacity transatlantic routes into southern Europe. Source: Telxius / Data Centre Magazine (telxius.com/en/marea-2).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-2.9838,43.3803,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Integrated Joint Operations Platform (IJOP) - Xinjiang Public Security, Ürümqi</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>The IJOP is a predictive-policing system rolled out across Xinjiang after a 2016 directive, aggregating data from Wi-Fi sniffers, ID cards, cameras and checkpoints to flag Uyghurs for questioning and detention. Human Rights Watch and Cure53 reverse-engineered its mobile app in 2019, documenting it in &#x27;China&#x27;s Algorithms of Repression.&#x27; Source: Human Rights Watch, &#x27;China&#x27;s Algorithms of Repression&#x27; (2019); ASPI Xinjiang Data Project.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2016-01-01</begin><end>2016-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>87.6139,43.8244,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NYPD Lower Manhattan Security Coordination Center (Domain Awareness System)</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Opened in 2008 at 55 Broadway, this NYPD/Microsoft-built center aggregates the Domain Awareness System — as of 2014 pulling feeds from about 6,500 CCTV cameras and reading roughly 2 million license plates per day across Lower Manhattan. Source: Wikipedia (Lower Manhattan Security Initiative / Domain Awareness System); NYC.gov.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2008-01-01</begin><end>2008-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-74.013,40.7068,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>GCHQ &#x27;The Doughnut&#x27; - Cheltenham, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>The 200-metre-diameter ring building completed in 2003 houses Britain&#x27;s signals-intelligence agency GCHQ and its roughly 5,500 staff; documents leaked by Edward Snowden in 2013 revealed its Tempora bulk-interception programme tapping transatlantic fibre cables. Source: Wikipedia (The Doughnut / GCHQ); The Guardian (Snowden disclosures).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2003-01-01</begin><end>2003-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-2.1214,51.8978,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Clearview AI Headquarters - New York</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Clearview AI operates a facial-recognition engine matching faces against a database it says exceeds 20-30 billion images scraped from the web and social media, sold to law enforcement; regulators in the UK, France, Italy, Australia and elsewhere have fined the firm for unlawful data collection. Source: Wikipedia (Clearview AI); ICO/CNIL enforcement actions.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.9939,40.7481,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>BND Headquarters - Berlin, Germany</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Germany&#x27;s foreign-intelligence service (BND) occupies the world&#x27;s largest intelligence headquarters — 260,000 m2, completed 2017 at a cost of about EUR 1.09 billion — housing roughly 4,000 of its staff on Chausseestraße in central Berlin. Source: Wikipedia (Headquarters of the Federal Intelligence Service); Daily Sabah.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-01-01</begin><end>2017-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>13.3781,52.5323,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Moscow &#x27;Safe City&#x27; Facial-Recognition Network - Moscow, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Moscow&#x27;s Department of Information Technology runs a live facial-recognition network — powered by NtechLab&#x27;s FindFace — across roughly 175,000+ street and metro cameras, launched at scale on 1 January 2020; it has been used to identify and detain protesters and draft evaders. Source: Biometric Update; TASS; VSquare (Kremlin Leaks).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2020-01-01</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>37.6064,55.6256,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Goldstone Deep Space Communications Complex - Fort Irwin, California</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Operated by NASA&#x27;s JPL on the U.S. Army&#x27;s Fort Irwin reservation, Goldstone is the U.S. node of the three-station Deep Space Network; its 70-metre &#x27;Mars&#x27; antenna received the first images of Neil Armstrong&#x27;s moonwalk and tracks interplanetary spacecraft. Source: Wikipedia (Goldstone Deep Space Communications Complex); NASA/JPL.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-116.8726,35.331,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Madrid Deep Space Communications Complex - Robledo de Chavela, Spain</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>One of three NASA Deep Space Network complexes spaced ~120 degrees apart in longitude, this site ~65 km west of Madrid has operated since 1965 and hosts a 70-metre antenna; it is run by JPL with Spain&#x27;s INTA. Source: Wikipedia (Madrid Deep Space Communications Complex); NASA.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1965-01-01</begin><end>1965-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-4.2525,40.4271,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Guiana Space Centre - Kourou, French Guiana</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Europe&#x27;s primary spaceport, operated by France&#x27;s CNES and ESA near the equator at Kourou, launches Ariane and Vega rockets; its near-equatorial location gives a fuel-saving boost for placing satellites into geostationary orbit. Source: Wikipedia (Guiana Space Centre); ESA/CNES.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-52.7739,5.2124,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Satish Dhawan Space Centre (SHAR) - Sriharikota, India</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>ISRO&#x27;s sole orbital launch site, on Sriharikota island on India&#x27;s east coast, launches the PSLV and GSLV/LVM3 rockets; it was the departure point for the Chandrayaan and Mangalyaan planetary missions. Source: Wikipedia (Satish Dhawan Space Centre); ISRO.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>80.2256,13.6281,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cavalier Space Force Station (PARCS) - North Dakota</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Home to the AN/FPQ-16 PARCS UHF phased-array radar (~6,144 elements) run by the 10th Space Warning Squadron, this isolated North Dakota site provides ICBM/SLBM missile warning and tracks over half of all Earth-orbiting objects for space situational awareness. Source: Wikipedia (Cavalier Space Force Station); U.S. Space Force fact sheet.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-97.9028,48.7264,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tanegashima Space Center - Minamitane, Japan</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>JAXA&#x27;s primary spaceport, covering ~9.7 million m2 on the southeast coast of Tanegashima island, is Japan&#x27;s largest rocket launch facility and the base for H-IIA/H-IIB and H3 launches carrying satellites and ISS resupply vehicles. Source: Wikipedia (Tanegashima Space Center); JAXA.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>130.9578,30.3943,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Glencore HQ, Baar, Switzerland</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Baar-headquartered Glencore is by many estimates the world&#x27;s largest commodity trader, moving metals, minerals, coal and oil globally; in 2022 it pleaded guilty in US, UK and Brazilian courts to a multi-year bribery and market-manipulation scheme and paid roughly $1.5 billion in penalties. Its executive board and all group compliance functions sit at the Baar campus. Source: Reuters / U.S. DOJ (2022 Glencore FCPA settlement); Wikipedia: Glencore.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-01-01</begin><end>2022-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>8.5273,47.1814,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cargill HQ, Minnetonka, Minnesota</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Cargill is the largest privately held company in the United States, posting record revenue of about $177 billion and topping the Forbes private-company list nearly every year since 1985. The family-controlled agribusiness dominates global grain, meat and commodity supply chains with roughly 160,000 employees in 70 countries. Source: Forbes / Star Tribune (2023, &#x27;Cargill retains top spot on Forbes list of largest U.S. private companies&#x27;).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1985-01-01</begin><end>1985-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-93.4767,44.9522,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>ASML HQ, Veldhoven, Netherlands</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>ASML&#x27;s Veldhoven campus houses the only factory on Earth capable of building extreme-ultraviolet (EUV) lithography machines, giving it a de facto 100% monopoly on the tools required to fabricate the most advanced chips. Each EUV system costs roughly EUR 350 million, and Dutch export controls on ASML sales to China are a core front in the chip war. Source: CNBC (&#x27;Inside ASML&#x27;); Wikipedia: ASML Holding.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>5.417,51.4044,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Maersk HQ, Copenhagen, Denmark</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>A.P. Moller-Maersk, headquartered on Copenhagen&#x27;s Esplanaden, has been the world&#x27;s largest container-shipping operator since 1996, running services to 374 ports across 116 countries. Its control of global container flows makes it a systemic node in supply-chain and trade-chokepoint analysis. Source: Wikipedia: Maersk / Maersk Line; company filings.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1996-01-01</begin><end>1996-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.5977,55.6877,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rheinmetall HQ, Düsseldorf, Germany</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Rheinmetall is Germany&#x27;s largest arms manufacturer, a leading supplier of tank guns, ammunition and armored vehicles to NATO and Ukraine; its defense sales surged to EUR 7.6 billion in 2024 as European rearmament accelerated, and its stock has risen over 1,000% since 2022. Source: Fortune (2025); Wikipedia: Rheinmetall.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2024-01-01</begin><end>2024-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>6.7852,51.2536,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Samsung Digital City, Suwon, South Korea</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Samsung Electronics&#x27; principal headquarters, a roughly 390-acre &#x27;Digital City&#x27; campus 30 km south of Seoul, houses around 37,000 employees and over half of the division&#x27;s R&amp;D workforce across five office towers up to 40 stories tall. It is the birthplace of the Galaxy line and the nerve center of the Samsung chaebol. Source: YnetNews / The Business Standard (&#x27;A peek into Samsung Digital City&#x27;).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.0513,37.2581,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hikvision Headquarters - Hangzhou, China</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Hangzhou Hikvision Digital Technology, the world&#x27;s largest maker of video-surveillance gear, is partly state-owned and was placed on the U.S. Commerce Department Entity List in 2019 over its role supplying cameras used in the mass surveillance of Uyghurs in Xinjiang. Its HQ is at No.555 Qianmo Road, Binjiang District. Source: Wikipedia (Hikvision); AFSC Investigate; U.S. Commerce Dept. Entity List.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>120.2072,30.211,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Dahua Technology Headquarters - Hangzhou, China</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Zhejiang Dahua Technology, the world&#x27;s second-largest video-surveillance manufacturer, was added to the U.S. Entity List in 2019 and its equipment banned from U.S. federal networks over links to Xinjiang surveillance. HQ is at No.1199 Bin&#x27;an Road, Binjiang District. Source: Wikipedia (Dahua Technology); U.S. FCC/Commerce Dept..</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>120.2072,30.211,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Telangana Integrated Command and Control Centre - Hyderabad, India</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Opened in 2022 in Banjara Hills at a cost of about Rs 600 crore, this five-tower complex is billed as India&#x27;s largest police command center, monitoring the city through a network of hundreds of thousands of CCTV cameras with AI and social-media analytics units. Source: Wikipedia (Telangana Integrated Command and Control Centre); Gulf News; Telangana Today.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-01-01</begin><end>2022-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>78.4399,17.4177,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Canberra Deep Space Communication Complex - Tidbinbilla, Australia</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>The southern-hemisphere node of NASA&#x27;s Deep Space Network, ~20 km southwest of Canberra, is managed by CSIRO; its DSS-43 70-metre dish is the only antenna on Earth able to send commands to Voyager 2. Source: Wikipedia (Canberra Deep Space Communication Complex); CSIRO/NASA.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.9766,-35.4277,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>RAF Fylingdales - North Yorkshire, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Operational since 1963 on the North York Moors, Fylingdales is one of three Ballistic Missile Early Warning System / SSPARS radar sites (with Alaska and Greenland); its phased-array radar gives US and UK governments missile warning and tracks satellites and space debris out to ~3,000 miles. Source: Wikipedia (RAF Fylingdales); Royal Air Force.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1963-01-01</begin><end>1963-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.6902,54.3318,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Maui Space Surveillance Complex (AMOS) - Haleakalā, Hawaii</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>Atop the 10,000-ft summit of Haleakalā, this Space Force site run by the 15th Space Surveillance Squadron fields the DoD&#x27;s largest optical telescope for imaging satellites, plus GEODSS optics — one of only three ground sites globally doing deep-space optical tracking. Source: Wikipedia (Maui Space Surveillance Complex); Air Force Research Laboratory.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-156.3107,20.803,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Luigi Broglio Space Centre (Malindi Station) - Kenya</name><styleUrl>#t-satellite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; satellite</p><p>An Italian-owned equatorial spaceport near Malindi, it launched 27 satellites from the offshore San Marco platform between 1964 and 1988 and still operates a satellite-communications ground station managed by the Italian Space Agency (ASI). Source: Wikipedia (Broglio Space Center); Space in Africa; European Spaceflight.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1964-01-01</begin><end>1964-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>39.9751,-3.2296,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Saudi Aramco HQ, Dhahran, Saudi Arabia</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>State-controlled Saudi Aramco is the world&#x27;s largest oil producer and, with 2024 net income of $106 billion, the most profitable listed company on earth. It holds over 270 billion barrels of proven reserves and produces roughly 12 million barrels of crude per day from its Dhahran command center. Source: Britannica Money / Saudi Aramco 2024 results; Wikipedia: Saudi Aramco.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2024-01-01</begin><end>2024-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>50.1202,26.2967,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>TSMC HQ, Hsinchu Science Park, Taiwan</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company is the world&#x27;s largest dedicated chip foundry, controlling roughly 60-70% of the global foundry market and producing nearly all of the planet&#x27;s most advanced (5nm/3nm) processors. Its Hsinchu concentration makes the site a central chokepoint in US-China technology geopolitics. Source: TSMC corporate; CNBC / Wikipedia: TSMC.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>121.0142,24.7759,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NSO Group HQ, Herzliya, Israel</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>The Israeli cyber-intelligence firm NSO Group makes Pegasus, a zero-click smartphone spyware classified by Israel as a military export; the 2021 Pegasus Project revealed its use against journalists, activists and officials worldwide, prompting a US Commerce Department blacklisting. The company is based in Herzliya, north of Tel Aviv. Source: Amnesty International / OCCRP Pegasus Project (2021); Wikipedia: NSO Group.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2021-01-01</begin><end>2021-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>34.8308,32.1677,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vitol HQ, Geneva, Switzerland</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Vitol is the world&#x27;s largest independent oil trader, moving over 7 million barrels a day and posting revenues around $343 billion in 2025; the secretive Geneva-run firm controls some 250 tankers and has faced US and Brazilian bribery settlements over crude-trading corruption in Latin America. Source: SWI swissinfo.ch; Wikipedia: Vitol; U.S. DOJ (2020 Vitol FCPA settlement).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2025-01-01</begin><end>2025-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>6.1457,46.2078,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tencent Binhai Towers, Shenzhen, China</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Tencent&#x27;s global headquarters, the twin Binhai Towers in Shenzhen&#x27;s Nanshan tech district, opened in 2017 after a 1.8-billion-yuan build. Tencent operates WeChat, the super-app woven into Chinese payments, messaging and state-linked data governance for over a billion users. Source: Tencent corporate; Wikipedia: Tencent Binhai Mansion.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-01-01</begin><end>2017-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>113.9334,22.5258,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>IBM Corporate HQ, Armonk, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Headquarters of the company whose founding product was population registration. Herman Hollerith&#x27;s tabulating machines were built for the 1890 US census; the firm became CTR and then IBM in 1924. The through-line this map follows is not a company&#x27;s character but a capability - turning a population into a machine-readable index, sold to whoever is doing the registering. See report Section X for the full tiering, including what IBM disputes.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1890-01-01</begin><end>1890-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.72036,41.1134,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>IBM Endicott, New York - the origin plant</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Endicott is where IBM&#x27;s manufacturing began and where the punch card was industrialised - the company town, the &#x27;Homestead&#x27;, the origin of the culture. The card itself is the artefact worth noticing: a physical object encoding a person as a pattern of holes, sortable at machine speed. Every later capability in this section - the smart-city camera, the licence-plate reader, the biometric index - is the same operation performed faster and without the paper.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-76.04937,42.09841,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Dehomag works, Berlin-Lichterfelde (approx.)</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Deutsche Hollerith-Maschinen GmbH - Dehomag - IBM&#x27;s German subsidiary, whose Berlin plant supplied the tabulating machinery used in Reich census and registration work. Location approximate to the Lichterfelde district. DOCUMENTED: CTR/IBM acquired 90% of Dehomag in 1923, leaving founder Willy Heidinger 10%; Dehomag equipment was used in Nazi census and administrative operations; Thomas J. Watson Sr. accepted Hitler&#x27;s Merit Cross of the German Eagle with Star in Berlin in 1937 - the first American to receive it - and returned it in June 1940 under sustained pressure. CONTESTED: Edwin Black&#x27;s &#x27;IBM and the Holocaust&#x27; (2001) argues continuous New York knowledge and control through the war; IBM&#x27;s position is that the subsidiary was seized by the Nazi state and the parent had no control over use. A Feb 2001 Alien Tort suit was voluntarily withdrawn the following month, so the question has never been adjudicated on the merits. Sources: Black (2001); IBM statements; JTA (Mar 2001).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1940-06-01</begin><end>1940-06-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>13.31386,52.43729,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Apartheid population register administration, Pretoria</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>The administrative centre of South Africa&#x27;s racial population register - the system that assigned every person a classification and an identity document, and made the pass laws enforceable at scale. From 2002 the Khulumani/Ntsebeza Alien Tort Statute litigation alleged that IBM and Ford purposefully facilitated violations of international law by enabling denationalisation and the suppression that followed. The case ran fourteen years and ended in 2016 when the US Supreme Court declined to hear it - again without any ruling on the merits. TIER: the register and its function are documented history; the corporate-facilitation allegation was pleaded and never adjudicated, and is recorded here as an allegation. Sources: In re South African Apartheid Litigation; GroundUp / Daily Maverick (Jun 2016); Harvard IHRC statement.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2002-01-01</begin><end>2002-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>28.18693,-25.75517,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kodak Hawkeye Works, 1447 St Paul St, Rochester NY</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Kodak&#x27;s classified plant, and the reason Rochester belongs in this section. From 1954 Kodak&#x27;s role was to develop and process the special film flown in the U-2 - built in Burbank - and then in the CORONA reconnaissance satellites. CORONA was operational 1960-72: over 100 spacecraft, more than 800,000 high-resolution images, declassified in February 1995. The returned negative was cut into manageable lengths, titled frame by frame, duplicated onto black-and-white print stock and boxed; a single mission&#x27;s output shipped out of Rochester by the ton, including the special enlargements prepared to brief the president. THE END OF THE LINE: the NRO flew KH-11, the first American electro-optical satellite, in Dec 1976; the last KH-9 HEXAGON film-return vehicle was lost on launch in 1986. Kodak sold its government business to ITT in 2004, and the photographic operations centres at Hawkeye and Lincoln were gone by 2009. Sources: CIA/NRO CORONA declassification (Feb 1995); Rochester Business Journal (2012); NRO KH-11 record.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1995-02-01</begin><end>1995-02-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.62586,43.18186,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Eastman Business Park (Kodak Park), Rochester NY</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Kodak&#x27;s primary photographic manufacturing site since 1891 - the industrial base under both the consumer film business and the classified one, which ran out of the same company and the same city. SCALE, THEN AND NOW: Kodak&#x27;s Rochester employment peaked above 60,000 in 1982, roughly half the area&#x27;s economic activity; after the January 2012 bankruptcy it employs about 1,200 here. WHAT OUTLASTED THE INDUSTRY: hazardous-waste releases at the park and into the Genesee River, a $49 million cleanup trust funded under the bankruptcy settlement, and documented contamination of river sediments, wetland and floodplain soils and biota. The pattern this map keeps finding in company towns - the plume is the most durable artifact. Sources: US Attorney SDNY / EPA settlement announcement; NYSDEC Eastman Business Park record; EPA hazardous waste cleanup file.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-01-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.62816,43.20214,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Laboratory for Laser Energetics (OMEGA), University of Rochester</name><styleUrl>#t-technology</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section X</b> &middot; technology</p><p>Established 1970 and funded principally through the Department of Energy&#x27;s National Nuclear Security Administration. The OMEGA laser delivers about 30 kJ from 60 beams onto a millimetre-scale target in under a nanosecond - among the most powerful laser systems in the world - as part of the US inertial-confinement-fusion programme. It anchors a regional optics, photonics and imaging cluster of 150+ companies and roughly 19,000 employees, described in trade coverage as central to US defence readiness. TIER: the laboratory, the laser and the funding line are documented. ICF is dual-use by design - the same physics serves stewardship of the nuclear stockpile and civil fusion research - and this marker asserts nothing beyond that. The point for this map is structural: when Kodak&#x27;s consumer half collapsed, the optics competence did not leave Rochester, it stayed in the defence-facing institutions. Sources: University of Rochester LLE; NNSA programme documentation; Rochester Business Journal (2025).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1970-01-01</begin><end>1970-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.63256,43.11312,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section XI (3)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Wall Street / New Amsterdam, Manhattan</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XI</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Dutch West India Company settlement (1624-1664). Wall Street named after colony fortification wall. The financial capital sits on the extraction company&#x27;s foundation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1624-01-01</begin><end>1624-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-74.0089,40.7069,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>New Albany, Ohio</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XI</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Pop. 414 (1980) → 10,825 (2020). 2,500% growth. Wexner/Epstein designed community. Facebook data center. Google data center. Intel 926-acre fab plant.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1980-01-01</begin><end>1980-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-82.8085,40.0812,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>New Canaan, Connecticut</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XI</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Gold Coast. Median household income $141,788. Philip Johnson Glass House. Harmony Lodge No. 67 (Masonic, 1763). Waveny Park: 300-acre former Texaco founder estate.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1763-01-01</begin><end>1763-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.4951,41.1478,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section XII (53)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Indian Creek Island, Florida</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>0.47 sq mi. Single bridge with police checkpoint. 84 residents, 13-officer police force (1:6.5 ratio). Bezos ($170M), Zuckerberg, Kushner, Andreessen.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-80.159,25.851,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fisher Island, Florida</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>0.27 sq mi. Ferry/helicopter only. Wealthiest zip code in America. Nixon/Rebozo/Smathers ownership chain. ~561 residents.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-80.1425,25.7637,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Necker Island, BVI (Richard Branson)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>74 acres. Purchased 1978 for $180,000. Virgin Group operates from BVI - near-zero corporate tax. Obama vacationed here post-presidency (Feb 2017). Two fires (2011, 2017). The billionaire&#x27;s island in the tax haven.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-02-01</begin><end>2017-02-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-64.355,18.515,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Moskito Island, BVI (Branson)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>120 acres. Second BVI island owned by Branson. $25,000+/night rental. Adjacent to Necker. Multiple private territories, same jurisdiction, same owner.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-64.34,18.525,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Skorpios, Greece (Onassis → Rybolovlev)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>200 acres. Purchased 1963 by Aristotle Onassis. Jackie Kennedy married Onassis here (1968). Sold to Russian oligarch Rybolovlev for ~$150M (2013). Shipping dynasty → Russian potash billionaire.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1963-01-01</begin><end>1963-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>20.72,38.65,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tetiaroa, French Polynesia (Brando)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>12 islets, 1,325 acres. Purchased 1967 by Marlon Brando from last Tahitian royal family. Now &#x27;The Brando&#x27; resort ($3,000+/night). Obama spent a month here (2017). Former president on a private island bought from displaced royals.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1967-01-01</begin><end>1967-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-149.57,-17.02,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lanai, Hawaii (Larry Ellison)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>90,000 acres - 98% of the island. Purchased 2012 for $300M. Population ~3,200 live on Ellison&#x27;s property. Oracle founder owns an entire Hawaiian island including its residents&#x27; homes and water system.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-156.92,20.83,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Musha Cay, Bahamas (David Copperfield)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>150 acres + 10 surrounding islands (700 acres total). Purchased 2006 for $50M. Same Bahamas jurisdiction as FTX (Bankman-Fried). The illusionist who makes things disappear owns an archipelago.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2006-01-01</begin><end>2006-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-76.15,23.885,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Peter Island, BVI (Van Andel family)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>1,800 acres. Amway Corporation owned it 1978–2001; full ownership then transferred to the VAN ANDEL family, co-founders of Amway, who hold it still. Closed after Hurricane Irma (2017); resort reopened December 2024. QUALIFIED 31 Aug 2026 — an earlier ctx ran a ‘DeVos–Van Andel’ line to Betsy DeVos. Amway had TWO founding families, Van Andel and DeVos, and Betsy DeVos married into the DeVos side. The island is Van Andel property. Collapsing the two families is the same error this audit corrected on Ile d’Arros, and it is removed.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2024-12-01</begin><end>2024-12-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-64.58,18.36,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mustique, St. Vincent (The Mustique Company)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>CORRECTED 31 Aug 2026 — previously read &#x27;Tennant / British Royals&#x27;, stale by roughly fifty years and wrong about the royals. 1,400 acres. Colin Tennant developed it and gave Princess Margaret a plot as a wedding present (1960) — a PLOT, never the island. Tennant sold his controlling interest in 1976 to Venezuelan industrialist Hans Neumann and his remaining shares in the mid-1980s. Legal title is held by THE MUSTIQUE COMPANY, a homeowners’ structure. No British royal has ever owned Mustique.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1960-01-01</begin><end>1960-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-61.183,12.883,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Makepeace Island, Australia (Branson)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>25 acres. Heart-shaped island in the Noosa River. Branson&#x27;s third private island, different hemisphere. Global distribution of private territory by a single individual.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>153.06,-26.39,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Great Saint James, USVI (Epstein)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>OWNERSHIP UPDATED 31 Aug 2026. 165 acres. Purchased by Epstein in 2016 for $18M; construction documented by drone photography; USVI sued the estate in 2020. SOLD MAY 2023 with Little Saint James to STEPHEN DECKOFF for US$60M — see that marker for the purchaser&#x27;s own statement. The Epstein-era facts here are historical and are dated as such; the estate no longer holds either island.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-05-01</begin><end>2023-05-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-64.85,18.313,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Île Sainte-Marguerite, France (Man in the Iron Mask)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Fort Royal prison - Man in the Iron Mask held here 1687-1698. Historical precedent: islands as both sanctuary and prison. Same geography protects the powerful and imprisons the inconvenient.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1687-01-01</begin><end>1687-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>7.047,43.517,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Robben Island, South Africa (Mandela)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Mandela imprisoned 18 years (1964-1982). Island-as-control pattern: powerful retreat to islands, inconvenient are confined on them. Same geography, inverse purpose.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1964-01-01</begin><end>1964-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>18.366,-33.806,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Poveglia, Venice, Italy</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Plague quarantine island (1793), then psychiatric hospital (1922-1968). Closed, restricted. Islands as zones where normal rules and observation do not apply.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1793-01-01</begin><end>1793-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.333,45.383,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nauru - Mining + Detention Island</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>8.1 sq mi. Smallest republic. Phosphate mining stripped 80% of surface. Australia&#x27;s offshore detention center - asylum seekers held on a stripped-mining island. Resource extraction and human containment share coordinates.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>166.9315,-0.5228,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Norman&#x27;s Cay, Exumas, Bahamas</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Carlos Lehder (Medellín Cartel) operated drug transshipment base 1978-1982. DEA-documented cocaine runway. CIA-tolerated narco corridor. The cartel bought an entire island to move product - same Bahamas jurisdiction as FTX.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1978-01-01</begin><end>1978-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-76.82,24.595,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Four Seasons Mahé, Seychelles (Prince–Dmitriev meeting, 11 Jan 2017)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>CORRECTED 31 Aug 2026 — this marker sat on NORTH ISLAND, which is the wrong island. Per Mueller-era reporting and congressional testimony, Erik Prince met Kirill Dmitriev (RDIF) on 11 January 2017 at the Four Seasons on MAHÉ, in a bar overlooking the Indian Ocean, with an earlier meeting the same day at George Nader&#x27;s villa. Nader advised the UAE crown prince. Prince called it a chance encounter; the Mueller report records the meeting as arranged in advance. Tier: meeting DOCUMENTED; its purpose CONTESTED between Prince&#x27;s account and the report&#x27;s.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2017-01-11</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>55.4833,-4.7167,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Buck Island, BVI (The Aerial BVI) - corrected</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>CORRECTED 31 Aug 2026 — previously read &#x27;Larry Page / Google&#x27;, which was wrong on both the island and the owner. Buck Island (~45 acres) is owned and run by Britnie Turner as The Aerial BVI wellness retreat. The island reporting has linked to Larry Page is EUSTATIA ISLAND (~36 acres, North Sound, Virgin Gorda) — and Page has never publicly confirmed that, so it is ATTRIBUTED, not documented. Naming a living person as owner of property he does not own is the error class this audit exists to catch.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-64.54,18.45,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kaua&#x27;i Estate, Hawaii (Zuckerberg)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>~1,400 acres on Kaua&#x27;i. Facebook/Meta CEO bought multiple parcels including former sugar plantation land. Underground bunker with own energy and food supply reported (2023). Tech billionaire fortification on indigenous Hawaiian land.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-01-01</begin><end>2023-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-159.5261,22.0964,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>The World Islands, Dubai</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>300 artificial islands shaped as world map. $14B project. Most islands undeveloped or abandoned. Micro-nations for sale - sovereign territory as real estate product. The enclave concept perfected: build your own island.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>55.17,25.22,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Gruinard Island, Scotland</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>UK Operation Vegetarian: anthrax bioweapons tested 1942-43. Island contaminated for 48 years. Decontaminated 1986. Islands as zones where biological weapons can be tested beyond public oversight.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1986-12-01</begin><end>1986-12-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-5.459,57.849,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Devil&#x27;s Island, French Guiana</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Notorious penal colony 1852-1953. Dreyfus imprisoned here (1895-99). Estimated 70,000+ deaths over a century. Island as state-sanctioned disappearance zone.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1852-01-01</begin><end>1852-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-52.583,5.295,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Alcatraz Island, San Francisco</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Federal penitentiary 1934-63. Before that: military fortification and military prison. Native American occupation 1969-71. The island-as-prison pattern repeated across centuries and jurisdictions.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1934-01-01</begin><end>1934-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-122.4233,37.8267,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Snake Island (Zmiinyi), Ukraine</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>&#x27;Russian warship, go f**k yourself.&#x27; Feb 24, 2022 - Ukrainian border guards defied Russian Navy cruiser Moskva. The cruiser later sank. Strategic Black Sea island fought over since antiquity.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2022-02-24</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>30.204,45.2557,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Île d&#x27;Arros &amp; St Joseph Atoll, Seychelles (Save Our Seas Foundation)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>CORRECTED 31 Aug 2026 — this marker previously read &#x27;Saudi Royal Family&#x27; and that was wrong. No Saudi royal is a documented owner. Chain: Prince Shahram Pahlavi Nia of IRAN (1975) → Liliane Bettencourt, L&#x27;Oréal heiress (1998, US$18M) → sold Aug 2012 with St Joseph Atoll for US$60M, managed by the Save Our Seas Foundation; nature reserve 2014. The Saudi link is real but is a private businessman, not a royal: Abdulmohsen Abdulmalik Al-Sheikh, construction billionaire, founded SOSF in Geneva 2003 and still funds it. Al ash-Sheikh is the Saudi clerical dynasty, NOT Al Saud — the old label collapsed two different families. 1.71 km²; 975 m unpaved airstrip (ICAO FSDA) on d&#x27;Arros; St Joseph is 2.3 km east across a 1 km channel and has no strip of its own. Prior ctx also claimed proximity to the Jan 2017 Erik Prince meeting — that was on Mahé, ~250 km away, i.e. same country, not same place. Removed as an anti-map violation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-08-01</begin><end>2012-08-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>53.3017,-5.4158,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Desroches Island, Seychelles (IDC / Four Seasons)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>ADDED 31 Aug 2026. Amirantes airstrip island ~50 km ESE of d&#x27;Arros. Concrete runway ~1,380 m, ICAO FSDR — the longest strip in the group. Managed by the ISLANDS DEVELOPMENT COMPANY (IDC), a Seychelles GOVERNMENT-OWNED parastatal. Four Seasons Resort opened 1 March 2018. IDC also runs a guesthouse here for Seychellois visitors and supports the Island Conservation Society. This marker exists to carry the finding, not the glamour: the runway is state logistics, not a private strip.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2018-03-01</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>53.6542,-5.6958,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Poivre Atoll, Seychelles (IDC)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>ADDED 31 Aug 2026. Amirantes atoll ~37 km south of d&#x27;Arros. Grass strip ~1,100 m. Managed by the Islands Development Company (state-owned). Former coconut plantation. COORDINATES APPROXIMATE — atoll centroid, not a surveyed point.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>53.31,-5.75,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rémire (Eagle) Island, Seychelles (IDC)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>ADDED 31 Aug 2026. Amirantes island ~33 km north of d&#x27;Arros — the nearest airstrip to it. Concrete strip ~478 m, ICAO FSSR, the shortest in the group. IDC (state-owned) runs a guesthouse here.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>53.3117,-5.1167,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Marie Louise Island, Seychelles (IDC)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>ADDED 31 Aug 2026. Southern Amirantes, ~86 km SSW of d&#x27;Arros. Concrete strip ~730 m, ICAO FSMA. IDC (state-owned).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>53.1458,-6.1778,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Islands Development Company (IDC), Victoria, Mahé</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>ADDED 31 Aug 2026 — the entity behind most of the Outer Islands markers, and the correction to the &#x27;cluster of billionaire islands&#x27; read. A Seychelles GOVERNMENT-OWNED parastatal incorporated 29 April 1980. Manages 14 islands: Alphonse, Assomption, Astove, Coëtivy, Cosmoledo, Desnoeufs, Desroches, Farquhar, Ile Plate, Marie-Louise, Poivre, Providence, Rémire, and Silhouette. Operates its OWN AVIATION DIVISION and co-owns a supply vessel. FINDING: four of the five Amirantes airstrips are state infrastructure serving an archipelago where boats take days. Remote island runways look like a signature of private power from orbit; here they are a public logistics network. COORDINATES APPROXIMATE (Victoria, Mahé).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1980-04-29</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>55.4513,-4.6191,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Eustatia Island, BVI (linked to Larry Page - attributed, unconfirmed)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>ADDED 31 Aug 2026 to replace a false attribution elsewhere on this map. ~36 acres in North Sound near Virgin Gorda, adjacent to Branson&#x27;s Necker and Moskito. Reporting and legal filings have linked it to Google co-founder Larry Page for years, but HE HAS NEVER PUBLICLY CONFIRMED OWNERSHIP — so this is ATTRIBUTED, not documented, and is labelled that way in the marker title rather than buried in the text. The old &#x27;Buck Island (Larry Page)&#x27; marker named the wrong island entirely. COORDINATES APPROXIMATE.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-64.3333,18.5033,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Laucala Island, Fiji (Red Bull / Mateschitz)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>3,500 acres. Purchased by Dietrich Mateschitz (Red Bull co-founder, d. 2022) for $10M. $5,000+/night resort. Energy drink fortune converted to private Pacific territory.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-01-01</begin><end>2022-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-179.07,-16.85,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Guantánamo Bay, Cuba</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>U.S. naval base since 1903 on Cuban soil occupied against Cuba&#x27;s will. Detention camp since 2002. Held 780 detainees, many without charge. Territory designed to exist outside normal law.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1903-01-01</begin><end>1903-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-75.0967,19.9023,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Christmas Island, Australia</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Australian external territory. Immigration detention center since 2001. Asylum seekers held on remote island 2,600 km from mainland. Same pattern as Nauru: island as offshore human containment facility.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2001-01-01</begin><end>2001-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>105.6904,-10.4475,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Manus Island, Papua New Guinea</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Australia&#x27;s second offshore immigration detention center. Regional Processing Centre opened 2001. Detainees held in former military base. Island nation paid to confine people on behalf of a wealthier nation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2001-01-01</begin><end>2001-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>147.0594,-2.0917,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hashima Island (Gunkanjima), Japan</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Mitsubishi-operated undersea coal mine. Korean and Chinese forced laborers during WWII. Population density once highest on Earth. Abandoned 1974. UNESCO World Heritage Site - the forced labor acknowledged only after decades of denial.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1974-01-01</begin><end>1974-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>129.7385,32.6275,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Niihau, Hawaii (Robinson Family)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>&#x27;The Forbidden Island.&#x27; 69.5 sq mi. Privately owned by one family since 1864 purchase from Kingdom of Hawaii for $10,000. ~130 Native Hawaiian residents. No paved roads, no running water, no stores. Most restricted inhabited island in the United States.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1864-01-01</begin><end>1864-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-160.17,21.9,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Palmyra Atoll, Pacific (Nature Conservancy)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Unincorporated U.S. territory. Privately owned, then sold to Nature Conservancy (2000). Nuclear fallout from Pacific testing. Previously owned by Fullard-Leo family. Site of 1974 &#x27;Sea Wind&#x27; double murder. Remote territory where normal jurisdiction dissolves.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2000-01-01</begin><end>2000-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-162.0833,5.8833,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pitcairn Island, South Pacific</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Population: 50. Descendants of HMS Bounty mutineers (1790). UK overseas territory - most remote inhabited island in the world. 2004: sexual abuse trials of nearly every adult male. British jurisdiction administered by satellite phone. The smallest colony reveals the longest patterns.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1790-01-01</begin><end>1790-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-130.1005,-25.066,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>North Sentinel Island, Andaman Sea</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Home to the Sentinelese - one of the last uncontacted peoples. Population: 50-200 (estimated). Indian government protects isolation (exclusion zone). 2018: American missionary John Allen Chau killed attempting illegal contact. The last people on Earth who refuse the modern world - and the modern world keeps trying.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2018-01-01</begin><end>2018-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>92.23,11.55,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>The Cloister, Sea Island, Georgia (2004 G8 Summit)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>The private barrier-island resort hosted the 30th G8 Summit on June 8-10, 2004, gathering leaders of the U.S., UK, France, Germany, Italy, Japan, Canada and Russia at The Cloister; the G8 boardroom is still shown on resort tours. Sea Island is a gated enclave of estates that has drawn dignitaries since a 1928 visit by President Calvin Coolidge. Source: New Georgia Encyclopedia; George W. Bush White House Archives (g8/2004).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2004-01-01</begin><end>2004-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-81.3506,31.1807,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Campione d&#x27;Italia (Italian Exclave in Switzerland)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>An Italian exclave of about 1.6 square miles surrounded by Swiss territory on Lake Lugano, Campione became landlocked in 1798 and for decades built its economy almost entirely around the Casinò di Campione, opened in 1917 and one of Europe&#x27;s largest casinos. Its split Italian-Swiss legal and tax status long made it a magnet for gambling and offshore money flows. Source: Wikipedia (Campione d&#x27;Italia); Offshore Protection.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1798-01-01</begin><end>1798-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>8.9717,45.9708,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cabinda Oil Exclave, Angola</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Cabinda is an Angolan exclave separated from the rest of the country by a strip of the Democratic Republic of Congo; with only about 400,000 residents it produces roughly 60% of Angola&#x27;s oil, much of it from the Chevron-operated Malongo terminal. The Front for the Liberation of the Enclave of Cabinda (FLEC) has waged a separatist insurgency since 1975, including attacks on Chevron facilities and workers. Source: TRT World; GlobalSecurity.org (FLEC).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1975-01-01</begin><end>1975-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.1919,-5.5576,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>North Brother Island (Typhoid Mary Quarantine), New York</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>This 20-acre East River island between the Bronx and Rikers held Riverside Hospital&#x27;s quarantine station, where Mary Mallon (&#x27;Typhoid Mary&#x27;) was confined against her will for roughly 26 years until her death in 1938. Abandoned since 1963, it is now a NYC Parks bird sanctuary closed to the public, with access only by permit and Parks escort. Source: All That&#x27;s Interesting; Untapped New York.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1938-01-01</begin><end>1938-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.8985,40.8007,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cocos (Keeling) Islands - former Clunies-Ross fiefdom (ended 1978)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>TENSE CORRECTED 31 Aug 2026 — this is history, not a current arrangement, and the old text read as present. The Clunies-Ross family ruled the atoll as a private feudal domain from 1827, paying workers in a private company scrip redeemable only at the company store. AUSTRALIA BOUGHT THE FAMILY OUT IN 1978; a UN-supervised act of self-determination in 1984 chose integration with Australia. It is now an Australian external territory. The interest is precisely that it ENDED, and how: a private sovereignty dissolved by purchase and a supervised vote.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1978-01-01</begin><end>1978-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>96.8942,-12.121,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lyford Cay, New Providence, Bahamas</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>A private, invitation-only gated community of roughly 450 homes on the western tip of New Providence, founded when Canadian brewing tycoon E.P. Taylor bought the land in the 1950s-60s. Frequently ranked among the world&#x27;s wealthiest enclaves, it runs its own security force and its homes range from about USD 2 million to USD 40 million. Source: Wikipedia (Lyford Cay); Maxim.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1950-01-01</begin><end>1950-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.5287,25.0293,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ceuta (Spanish Enclave in North Africa)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Ceuta is a Spanish autonomous city and free port on Morocco&#x27;s coast at the Strait of Gibraltar, one of the European Union&#x27;s only two land borders with Africa (with Melilla). Ringed by double barbed-wire fences, it is a flashpoint for migration: in one 2021 surge some 8,000 people crossed in two days, and later mass breaches drew Spanish plans for new containment fencing. Source: Encyclopaedia Britannica (Ceuta); CBS News.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2021-01-01</begin><end>2021-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-5.3041,35.8884,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Jupiter Island, Martin County, Florida</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>A narrow barrier-island town of gated oceanfront estates in Hobe Sound, Jupiter Island had a population of 804 at the 2020 census and a per-capita income around USD 254,000, consistently ranking among the highest-income ZIP codes in the United States. It has long been a discreet retreat for industrialists, executives and political families. Source: Wikipedia (Jupiter Island, Florida); MFI-Miami.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2020-01-01</begin><end>2020-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-80.1036,27.0342,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fort Brecqhou (Barclay family), Channel Islands</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>UPDATED 31 Aug 2026 — the previous text described the twins as current &#x27;owners of the Telegraph and the Ritz&#x27;; both had already gone. David and Frederick Barclay bought Brecqhou (~160 acres, off Sark) in 1993 and built a mock-Gothic castle on it, then litigated for years against Sark&#x27;s feudal constitution. The RITZ was sold to a Qatari investor in March 2020 for about GBP 800m. SIR DAVID BARCLAY DIED 10 JANUARY 2021, aged 86. Control of the Telegraph passed out of the family in the subsequent debt fight. The island remains the family&#x27;s; the media empire attached to it in the old ctx does not.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2021-01-10</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-2.535,49.4578,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Runit Dome, Enewetak Atoll, Marshall Islands</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>A concrete cap built by the U.S. in the late 1970s over an unlined nuclear blast crater on Runit Island entombs more than 100,000 cubic yards of radioactive soil and debris from Cold War tests at Enewetak. The dome is now cracking and tidal groundwater moves beneath its unlined base roughly 30 km from the ~600 residents who still fish the lagoon, prompting UN and Marshallese warnings of leakage. Source: U.S. Department of Energy Report to Congress; CBS News.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1970-01-01</begin><end>1970-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>162.0644,11.5141,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Capella, Sentosa Island, Singapore (2018 Trump-Kim Summit)</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>The secluded Capella hotel on Sentosa, a resort island a quarter-mile off Singapore&#x27;s coast, hosted the first Trump-Kim summit on June 12, 2018 under a heavy security lockdown. The Foster + Partners-designed resort was chosen partly because the island setting could be sealed off from the public. Source: CNN Politics; TIME.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2018-06-12</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>103.8343,1.2489,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tagomago Private Island, Ibiza, Spain</name><styleUrl>#t-enclave</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XII</b> &middot; enclave</p><p>Tagomago is a roughly 600,000-square-metre privately owned islet about 900 m off Ibiza&#x27;s east coast, marketed as one of the Mediterranean&#x27;s most exclusive private-island rentals with a single luxury villa and a staff of around twelve reserved for one group at a time. It lies within the EU Natura 2000 protected network yet is held as a fully private retreat. Source: Rental Escapes; Tripadvisor (Tagomago Private Island Retreat).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2000-01-01</begin><end>2000-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>1.4743,38.9911,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section XIII (103)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Library of Alexandria, Egypt</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Destroyed in stages: 48 BC fire, 270 AD, 391 AD, 642 AD. The ancient world&#x27;s greatest library - burned four times across seven centuries.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>29.9187,31.2001,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>House of Wisdom, Baghdad, Iraq</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Destroyed 1258 during Mongol sack. 9 million manuscripts. Tigris River ran black with ink. 800 years of knowledge destroyed in one siege.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>44.4009,33.3405,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nalanda University, Bihar, India</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>800+ year Buddhist center burned 1193. 9 million manuscripts destroyed. Knowledge purge by conquest - the pattern repeats.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>85.4428,25.1357,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Great Pyramid of Giza, Egypt</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>2.3 million limestone blocks. 4,500 years old. Aligned to true north within 3/60 degree. Precision that challenges industrial explanation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>31.1342,29.9792,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Puma Punku, Tiwanaku, Bolivia</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>H-blocks with 1/50 inch precision tolerances. Interlocking modular design. 12,500 ft altitude. Technology that shouldn&#x27;t exist at the stated date.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-68.6805,-16.5617,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Baalbek, Lebanon</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Trilithon: three 800-ton stones at 20+ ft height. Stone of the Pregnant Woman: ~1,000 tons, unfinished in quarry. No modern crane can replicate the placement.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>36.211,34.0047,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Göbekli Tepe, Turkey</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Pre-12,000 years old (9500 BC). Multi-ton carved pillars. Deliberately buried by its builders. The oldest known temple - intentionally hidden.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>38.9222,37.2231,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Monte Verde, Chile</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Pre-Clovis site, 18,500 years old. Resisted by archaeological establishment for years. Proof humans were in the Americas far earlier than the accepted timeline.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-72.5812,-41.5062,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Visočica Hill (Bosnian Pyramid), Bosnia</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Proposed pyramid complex. Dismissed without investigation by establishment archaeologists. Anomalous structure - uninvestigated by design.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>18.1764,43.9767,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pine Ridge Reservation, South Dakota</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>North American pole of inaccessibility. Oglala Lakota Sioux territory. The most inaccessible point on the continent is an Indigenous reservation. Sacred Black Hills (He Sapa) - gold rush, broken treaties, Mount Rushmore carved into sacred mountain.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-102.55,43.1,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Smithsonian Institution, Washington D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Alleged sequestration of anomalous archaeological artifacts. The institution tasked with preserving knowledge accused of suppressing it. Giant skeleton reports from 19th century Bureau of Ethnology systematically disappeared. 154 million objects - what&#x27;s in the basement?</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.0259,38.8881,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kiritimati (Christmas Island), Republic of Kiribati</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Largest coral atoll on Earth (388 km²). British nuclear tests (1957-58): 3 hydrogen bombs. U.S. nuclear tests (1962): 24 atmospheric detonations. Ancient Polynesian navigation waypoint. Captain Cook arrived Christmas Eve 1777. Population exposed to fallout - compensation still unpaid. The largest atoll on Earth used as a nuclear laboratory.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1957-01-01</begin><end>1957-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-157.475,1.8721,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bouvet Island, South Atlantic</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Most remote island on Earth - 1,600 km from nearest land. Norwegian territory. 1979: &#x27;Vela Incident&#x27; - U.S. satellite detected double flash (nuclear signature) near Bouvet. Suspected Israeli/South African nuclear test. Never confirmed. The most remote place on Earth may have hosted a secret nuclear detonation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1979-01-01</begin><end>1979-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>3.4,-54.4333,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>St. Helena, South Atlantic</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Napoleon exiled here (1815-1821). Only accessible by ship until airport opened 2017. British East India Company administered until 1834. Strategic mid-Atlantic position. The island designed to imprison an emperor - so remote it didn&#x27;t need walls.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1815-01-01</begin><end>1815-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-5.7089,-15.965,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Heard Island, Australian External Territory</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Subantarctic volcanic island. Big Ben - active volcano, 2,745m. No permanent population. One of the most remote places on Earth. Used for secret nuclear monitoring (CTBTO hydroacoustic station). The volcano at the edge of the world, wired for sound.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>73.5133,-53.1,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>British Museum, London</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>8 million objects. Elgin Marbles (Parthenon). Rosetta Stone. Benin Bronzes (1897 punitive expedition looting). The largest collection of stolen cultural property on Earth, displayed as education. 22 formal repatriation requests denied. The museum as colonial warehouse.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1897-01-01</begin><end>1897-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.127,51.5194,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vatican Secret Archives (Apostolic Archive), Vatican City</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>85 linear kilometers of shelving. Documents spanning 12+ centuries. &#x27;Secret&#x27; renamed &#x27;Private&#x27; (2019). Access restricted to qualified scholars by application. Contains records of Inquisition, Galileo trial, excommunications, papal bulls authorizing colonization (Doctrine of Discovery). What the church chooses to preserve and who it allows to see it.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.4539,41.9022,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cairo Museum / Grand Egyptian Museum, Giza</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Tutankhamun collection. 120,000+ artifacts. Grand Egyptian Museum (2024, $1B+): at the foot of the Pyramids. Zahi Hawass - gatekeeper of Egyptian archaeology for decades. Access to the plateau, to the tombs, to the narrative - controlled by one man&#x27;s office. What hasn&#x27;t been excavated under the Sphinx?</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2024-01-01</begin><end>2024-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>31.1305,29.9753,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pergamon Museum, Berlin</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Ishtar Gate of Babylon. Pergamon Altar. Market Gate of Miletus. Germany disassembled entire ancient structures and shipped them to Berlin. The museum that doesn&#x27;t have artifacts - it has buildings. Entire architectural monuments extracted and reassembled in a European capital.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>13.3967,52.5212,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Göbekli Tepe Excavation Site Museum, Urfa</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Museum adjacent to world&#x27;s oldest known temple (pre-12,000 years). Klaus Schmidt excavated 1994-2014 (died 2014). Only 5% excavated. Turkish government controls access and narrative. An archaeological site that rewrites human history - 95% of it deliberately left in the ground.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1994-01-01</begin><end>1994-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>38.9222,37.2231,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Field Museum, Chicago</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Founded from 1893 World&#x27;s Columbian Exposition collections. Marshall Field (department stores) funded. 40+ million specimens. Sue the T-Rex ($8.4M, 1997). Indigenous collections: human remains and sacred objects held for decades before NAGPRA compliance. The natural history museum funded by the retail baron.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1893-01-01</begin><end>1893-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-87.617,41.8662,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Uffizi Gallery, Florence</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Built by the Medici (1581). Banking family turned art patrons turned papal dynasty. The family that invented modern banking also invented the cultural institution as power display. Medici banking network map mirrors Vatican political network. The gallery as ledger.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1581-01-01</begin><end>1581-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>11.2553,43.7678,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hermitage Museum, St. Petersburg</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>3 million items. Founded by Catherine the Great (1764). Winter Palace - seat of Romanov power. Survived revolution, Nazi siege (872 days, 1M dead in Leningrad). The museum that survived the empire that built it, the revolution that overthrew it, and the siege that tried to starve it.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1764-01-01</begin><end>1764-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>30.3146,59.9398,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Valley of the Kings, Luxor, Egypt</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>63 known tombs. Tutankhamun (KV62, 1922). Most tombs looted in antiquity. Ground-penetrating radar suggests undiscovered chambers behind Tutankhamun&#x27;s tomb (2015-2019, inconclusive). Access controlled by Supreme Council of Antiquities. What&#x27;s behind the walls?</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1922-01-01</begin><end>1922-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>32.6014,25.7402,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ellora Caves, Maharashtra, India</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>34 caves cut from basalt cliff (600-1000 CE). Kailasa Temple (Cave 16): carved TOP-DOWN from a single rock - estimated 200,000 tons of rock removed. Hindu, Buddhist, Jain temples side by side. Three religions carved into the same cliff face. The engineering required to carve downward through solid basalt is not explained by the tools available.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>75.178,20.0258,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sochi Olympic Park, Russia - 2014 Winter Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>$51B - most expensive Olympics in history. Built on coast of historical Circassia. Circassian Genocide (1864): Russian Empire killed/expelled 1-1.5M Circassians. Russia hosted its celebration games on the land of a genocide it has never acknowledged. Sochi was the port from which Circassians were expelled. The victory lap on a mass grave.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2014-01-01</begin><end>2014-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>39.9556,43.4028,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Berlin Olympic Stadium - 1936 Summer Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Nazi propaganda showcase. Jesse Owens won 4 golds - Hitler refused to shake his hand. Leni Riefenstahl&#x27;s &#x27;Olympia&#x27; - pioneered propaganda filmmaking. IBM provided tabulating machines for the regime. The Olympics as legitimization of a fascist state. Stadium still in use.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1936-01-01</begin><end>1936-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>13.2395,52.5147,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Munich Olympic Village - 1972 Summer Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Munich Massacre: 11 Israeli athletes killed by Black September. German police botched rescue at Fürstenfeldbruck airfield. Mossad launched Operation Wrath of God - targeted assassinations across Europe. The Olympics that became a war zone. Games continued after 34-hour pause. &#x27;The Games must go on.&#x27; - Avery Brundage.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1972-01-01</begin><end>1972-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>11.5518,48.1755,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Beijing National Stadium (Bird&#x27;s Nest) - 2008 Summer Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>$423M stadium. Mass displacement of Beijing hutong neighborhoods. Internet censorship tightened. Ai Weiwei co-designed the stadium, then called it &#x27;a fake smile.&#x27; Tibet protests crushed months before opening. Uyghur surveillance infrastructure expanded during Olympic security buildup. The surveillance state dressed up as a sporting event.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2008-01-01</begin><end>2008-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>116.3966,39.9929,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Athens Olympic Complex - 2004 Summer Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>$15B cost - contributed directly to Greek debt crisis (2009-2018). Most venues abandoned. Hellinikon complex: rusting, graffitied. The Olympics that bankrupted a country. Greece&#x27;s debt-to-GDP hit 180%. Troika (IMF/ECB/EU) imposed austerity. Pensions cut 40%. The party that destroyed the host.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2004-01-01</begin><end>2004-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>23.7874,38.0362,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rio Olympic Park, Barra da Tijuca - 2016 Summer Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>$13.1B cost. Favela clearances displaced thousands. Guanabara Bay: raw sewage, athletes warned not to put heads underwater. Mayor Eduardo Paes investigated for $5M bribe from Olympic construction contracts. Workers died building venues. Rio declared &#x27;state of financial emergency&#x27; months before opening. The Olympics that required a state of emergency to host.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2016-01-01</begin><end>2016-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-43.3953,-22.9714,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>London Olympic Park, Stratford - 2012 Summer Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>£8.77B cost. Massive CCTV expansion - London became most surveilled city in the Western world. East London gentrification displaced working-class communities. G4S security contract failed spectacularly - military called in. Legacy: luxury apartments where council housing stood. The regeneration that regenerated the poor out of their neighborhoods.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.0166,51.5384,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Salt Lake City - 2002 Winter Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Bribery scandal: IOC members received cash, scholarships for children, medical treatment, land deals. Tom Welch and Dave Johnson indicted. 10 IOC members expelled/resigned. First proof the IOC was for sale. The bid that proved every Olympic bid was a transaction.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2002-01-01</begin><end>2002-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-111.891,40.7608,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tokyo Olympic Stadium - 2020/2021 Summer Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>$15.4B cost. Postponed by COVID - first peacetime postponement. Empty stadiums. Original Zaha Hadid design scrapped ($2B over budget). Head of organizing committee Haruyuki Takahashi arrested for bribery (2022). Dentsu advertising agency: monopoly on Olympic sponsorship deals. The Olympics no one could attend, that still cost $15 billion.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-01-01</begin><end>2022-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>139.7134,35.6778,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>PyeongChang Olympic Complex - 2018 Winter Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>$12.9B cost. Venues in demilitarized zone proximity - nuclear tensions with DPRK months before. Kim Yo-jong attended opening ceremony - first Kim family member in South Korea since Korean War. Unified Korean team marched under single flag. The Olympics on the edge of nuclear war, used as diplomatic theater.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2018-01-01</begin><end>2018-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>128.6786,37.6319,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sarajevo Olympic Venues - 1984 Winter Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Beautiful venues built 1984. By 1992: bobsled track used as artillery position. Zetra Olympic Hall: burned, used as morgue. Athletes&#x27; Village: sniper positions. The Olympic venues that became a battlefield within 8 years. Siege of Sarajevo: 1,425 days, 11,541 killed. The fastest transformation from celebration to slaughter.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1984-01-01</begin><end>1984-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>18.4131,43.8563,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Montreal Olympic Stadium - 1976 Summer Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>$1.5B cost - &#x27;The Big Owe.&#x27; Took 30 years to pay off (2006). Mayor Jean Drapeau: &#x27;The Olympics can no more have a deficit than a man can have a baby.&#x27; Retractable roof never worked properly. The stadium whose debt outlasted a generation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1976-01-01</begin><end>1976-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.5516,45.5579,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mexico City Olympic Sites - 1968 Summer Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Tlatelolco Massacre: Oct 2, 1968 - 10 days before Opening Ceremony. Mexican army and CIA-trained Olympia Battalion fired on student protesters. 300-400 killed (government admitted 4). Bodies removed before dawn. IOC president Avery Brundage: no comment. Tommie Smith and John Carlos raised fists on podium - banned for life. The massacre before the ceremony.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1968-10-02</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-99.1042,19.3529,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Los Angeles Memorial Coliseum - 1984 Summer Olympics</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Soviet-led boycott (14 Eastern Bloc nations). Peter Ueberroth&#x27;s &#x27;private enterprise Olympics&#x27; - first to turn a profit ($250M). Created the corporate sponsorship model all future Olympics would follow. The Olympics that proved the Games were a business, not a movement.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1984-01-01</begin><end>1984-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-118.2879,34.0141,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Christie&#x27;s, King Street, London - Major Auction House</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Founded 1766. François Pinault (Kering Group: Gucci, Balenciaga) acquired Christie&#x27;s 1998. Record sales: Leonardo da Vinci &#x27;Salvator Mundi&#x27; $450.3M (2017) - buyer: Saudi Crown Prince MBS via intermediary. Art as currency for oligarchs - no provenance questions, no tax, freeport storage. The auction house as laundromat.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1766-01-01</begin><end>1766-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.137,51.5085,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sotheby&#x27;s, New Bond Street, London - Major Auction House</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Founded 1744. Patrick Drahi (Altice) acquired Sotheby&#x27;s 2019 for $3.7B. Dmitry Rybolovlev lawsuit: alleged Sotheby&#x27;s insider Yves Bouvier marked up paintings by $1B+. Bouvier Affair exposed how art dealers buy from auction houses and resell to billionaires at massive markups. The marketplace where money is the art.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1744-01-01</begin><end>1744-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.1425,51.5132,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sea Change Estate, Montauk, New York - Bacon/de Kooning Collection</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>J. Barton Riley estate &#x27;Sea Change.&#x27; Upon death, collection including Francis Bacon&#x27;s &#x27;Study after Velázquez&#x27;s Portrait of Pope Innocent X&#x27; and works by de Kooning. Bacon&#x27;s Pope paintings: screaming pontiffs, institutional power distorted. The collection named &#x27;Sea Change&#x27; - a transformation of value from paint to currency. Art as estate, estate as art, death as liquidity event.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-71.9545,41.0362,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Salvator Mundi Sale, Christie&#x27;s NYC - $450.3M</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Leonardo da Vinci &#x27;Salvator Mundi&#x27; - $450.3M (2017). Bought by Badr bin Abdullah (proxy for MBS/Saudi Arabia). Previously sold for $10,000 in 2005. Attribution disputed by scholars. Reported to be held by Saudi interests - variously placed on a yacht or in storage - but its location is ATTRIBUTED, not documented, and it has not been publicly exhibited since the sale; a planned Louvre Abu Dhabi showing was cancelled without explanation. The most expensive painting in history, bought by a prince, hidden from the world.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-01-01</begin><end>2017-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9787,40.7587,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Geneva Freeport, Switzerland - Art Storage Tax Haven</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>$100B+ in art stored in tax-free warehouses. Picassos, Warhols, Rothkos - never displayed, never taxed, never seen. Bought at auction, shipped to freeport, resold years later. Art as bearer bonds. Natural History Museum of Geneva Freeport (Hito Steyerl&#x27;s phrase): the museum no one visits, where the most valuable art on Earth sits in climate-controlled darkness.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>6.1432,46.2044,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Luxembourg Freeport - Art Tax Haven</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Le Freeport Luxembourg: opened 2014. Designed by Fernando de Mello Franco. 22,000 sq meters of vault space. Same model as Geneva freeport - art stored duty-free indefinitely. The painting enters the vault and becomes a financial instrument. No customs, no tax, no public access. Art&#x27;s final destination: a climate-controlled coffin.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2014-01-01</begin><end>2014-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>6.29,49.63,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>ARCIS Freeport, Singapore</name><styleUrl>#t-financial</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; financial</p><p>Le Freeport Singapore: opened 2010 at Changi. Sold to ARCIS 2020. High-value art, gold, wine - stored tax-free. Asia-Pacific hub for art-as-financial-instrument. When art crosses the threshold into a freeport, it stops being art and becomes collateral.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2010-01-01</begin><end>2010-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>103.988,1.356,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York - Board Patterns</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Board includes/included: David Koch (oil, donated $65M), Henry Kravis (KKR leveraged buyouts), Leonard Lauder (Estée Lauder heir, donated $1B Cubist collection), Blackstone executives. Sackler Wing (Temple of Dendur): named for the family whose company made OxyContin - 500,000 opioid deaths. Name removed 2021 after protests. The museum funded by the opioid crisis.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2021-01-01</begin><end>2021-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9632,40.7794,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Louvre Abu Dhabi - Art as Diplomacy</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>$1B paid to France for the &#x27;Louvre&#x27; name (30-year license). $747M for art loans. Designed by Jean Nouvel. Built by migrant workers (reports of labor abuses). France sold its museum&#x27;s brand to an authoritarian state. &#x27;Universal museum&#x27; - universal meaning: available to the highest bidder. Salvator Mundi reportedly destined here - never arrived.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>54.3983,24.5336,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Guggenheim Museum, New York - Solomon R. Guggenheim Foundation</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Solomon Guggenheim: mining fortune (copper, silver). Peggy Guggenheim: collected Pollock, Ernst, Kandinsky - her Venice palazzo still a museum. Guggenheim Bilbao: $89M Frank Gehry building transformed a dying industrial city into tourist destination. The &#x27;Bilbao Effect&#x27; - the idea that a museum building is worth more than the art inside it. Guggenheim Helsinki rejected by public vote.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.959,40.783,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tate Modern, London - Turbine Hall</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Unilever Series funded Turbine Hall commissions (2000-2012). BP sponsorship of Tate: protested relentlessly by Liberate Tate. BP dropped 2016 after 26 years. Tate board included oil executives while exhibiting climate-themed art. The oil company sponsoring the museum that showed art about environmental destruction.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2000-01-01</begin><end>2000-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.0994,51.5076,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Museum of Islamic Art, Doha, Qatar</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Designed by I.M. Pei. Qatar Museums (Sheikha Al-Mayassa bint Hamad Al Thani): estimated $1B/year art spending. Qatar bought Cézanne&#x27;s &#x27;The Card Players&#x27; for $250M+ (2011) - highest price ever at the time. The nation-state art collection as soft power infrastructure. Gas wealth converted to cultural capital.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2011-01-01</begin><end>2011-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>51.539,25.2959,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Broad Contemporary Art Museum, Los Angeles</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Eli Broad: SunAmerica, KB Home. Net worth $6.9B. Built own museum to house personal collection (Basquiat, Koons, Warhol, Hirst). Broad also donated $30M to LACMA. The billionaire who built a museum for himself, next to the museum he also funded. Art philanthropy as immortality project.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-118.2508,34.0544,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fondation Louis Vuitton, Paris</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Bernard Arnault (LVMH, richest person in Europe). Frank Gehry-designed, $143M. Private museum housing Arnault&#x27;s personal collection. The luxury goods magnate who built a luxury museum. When the building IS the brand. LVMH owns Christie&#x27;s competitor Phillips auction house rumors. The vertical integration of taste.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>2.2647,48.8808,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>KAWS Companion Sculptures - Various Locations</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Brian Donnelly (KAWS). XX-eyed figures: Mickey Mouse + skull = consumer death. &#x27;Companion&#x27; - 45m floating sculpture appeared Hong Kong, Taipei, worldwide. Sotheby&#x27;s: KAWS &#x27;The KAWS Album&#x27; (Simpsons parody) sold $14.8M (2019). Street art → auction house → floating corporate sculpture in Victoria Harbour. The trajectory from graffiti to global capital. Hyperstition: the cartoon that became the commodity that became the monument.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9897,40.7411,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Maman (Giant Spider) - Louise Bourgeois, Various Locations</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Louise Bourgeois, 1999. 30-foot bronze spider. Editions at Guggenheim Bilbao, Tate Modern, National Gallery of Canada, Mori Tower Tokyo, Qatar. Named for the artist&#x27;s mother (&#x27;She was my best friend&#x27;). The spider as protector - weaving, repairing, creating. Or: the spider as surveillance, the web as network. Bourgeois: &#x27;Art is a guarantee of sanity.&#x27; The mother/monster that guards the museum entrance.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1999-01-01</begin><end>1999-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>2.336,48.8612,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2001: A Space Odyssey Monolith - MGM Studios, Los Angeles</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Stanley Kubrick&#x27;s monolith: black rectangular solid (1:4:9 ratio - squares of first three integers). Appears at every evolutionary leap. The monolith is a cube stretched - a hypercube projected into 3D. Kubrick&#x27;s 2001 (1968) predicted tablets, AI assistants, video calls. The filmmaker who showed the cube as the catalyst of human evolution. Kubrick also directed &#x27;Eyes Wide Shut&#x27; - his film about elite ritual - and died 4 days after showing it to Warner Bros.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2001-01-01</begin><end>2001-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-118.4912,34.0195,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Obelisk of Luxor, Karnak Temple, Egypt</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Original source of the major Western obelisks. Thutmose I, Hatshepsut, Thutmose III - obelisks raised at Karnak over 500 years. The obelisks now in London, Paris, New York, Rome - all came from here. Luxor kept the ones the empires didn&#x27;t take. The quarry of power symbols for every subsequent empire.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>32.6573,25.7188,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Luxor Hotel Obelisk, Las Vegas</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Las Vegas Luxor: a 30-story glass pyramid with a replica obelisk, a sphinx, and the brightest beam of light on Earth shooting from its apex. Ancient Egyptian sacred architecture replicated as a casino. Pharaonic tomb → gambling hall. The sacred reduced to spectacle. The beam is visible from space. The pyramid that prints money.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-115.1761,36.0955,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>El Obelisco, Avenida 9 de Julio, Buenos Aires (Conceptual Twin)</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>The widest avenue in the world (140m, 16 lanes) with an obelisk at its center. The intersection scaled to absurdity. Buenos Aires: built by immigrants, governed by military juntas, disappeared 30,000 people (Dirty War 1976-83). The obelisk that survived the juntas, the economic collapses, the IMF restructurings. When everything else fails, the obelisk remains.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1976-01-01</begin><end>1976-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-58.3816,-34.6037,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rani ki Vav Obelisk / Pillar, Patan, Gujarat, India</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>UNESCO stepwell (11th century). Not an obelisk in Egyptian sense - but a vertical structure marking a sacred underground passage. The inversion of the obelisk: instead of reaching up, it steps downward 7 stories into the earth. 500+ sculptures descend with the water. The obelisk that goes down instead of up.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>72.1017,23.8587,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Aswan Unfinished Obelisk, Egypt</name><styleUrl>#t-obelisk</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; obelisk</p><p>Would have been the largest obelisk ever: 42m, 1,168 tons. Abandoned when a crack appeared during quarrying (15th century BC). Still lies in the quarry. The obelisk that was never finished reveals how they were made: carved directly from bedrock. The failure that explained the method. Every standing obelisk required this risk: one crack and the work of years is waste.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>32.8942,24.0772,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Black Wall Street - Greenwood District, Tulsa OK</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Greenwood District, Tulsa, Oklahoma - &#x27;Black Wall Street.&#x27; By 1921, the wealthiest Black community in America: 600+ businesses, 21 churches, 21 restaurants, 30 grocery stores, 2 movie theaters, a hospital, a bank, a post office, libraries, schools, law offices, a bus system. On May 31–June 1, 1921, white mobs - with deputized civilians and KKK involvement - burned 35+ blocks to the ground. Private aircraft dropped incendiary devices - the first aerial bombing of American civilians on U.S. soil. Oklahoma National Guard troops deployed not to protect the community but to round up and detain Black residents at gunpoint. An estimated 300+ killed, 10,000+ left homeless, over $32 million in property destroyed (1921 dollars - $500M+ today). Every insurance claim filed by Black residents was denied. The massacre was systematically erased from Oklahoma history textbooks for 75+ years. No one was ever charged. No reparations were ever paid. The land was rezoned and redeveloped. This was not a &#x27;race riot&#x27; - it was a coordinated destruction of Black economic independence.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1921-06-01</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-95.9903,36.157,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tulsa Mass Graves - Oaklawn Cemetery</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Oaklawn Cemetery and surrounding sites, Tulsa, Oklahoma. After the 1921 massacre, victims&#x27; bodies were loaded onto trucks and trains and disposed of in mass graves. Eyewitness accounts describe bodies dumped into the Arkansas River, buried in unmarked pits, and incinerated. Official death toll was suppressed to 36 for decades - actual estimates range from 100 to 300+. In 2020, forensic excavation at Oaklawn Cemetery confirmed mass graves with coffins stacked, remains showing evidence of gunshot wounds. The systematic concealment of the dead mirrors patterns at Kamloops, Pine Ridge, and other sites where the state buries evidence of its violence. Bodies still being found over 100 years later.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1921-01-01</begin><end>1921-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-95.9834,36.1485,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tulsa Convention Hall - 1921 Detention Camp</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; military</p><p>Tulsa Convention Hall and McNulty Park - used as internment camps during the 1921 massacre. The Oklahoma National Guard rounded up over 6,000 Black residents at gunpoint, marching them through the streets with hands raised, and detained them in improvised concentration camps. Black residents could only be released if a white person vouched for them - a &#x27;pass system&#x27; identical to apartheid. While residents were detained, their homes and businesses were looted and burned. The National Guard participated in the destruction, not the protection. Troops used machine guns. This was the U.S. military deployed against American citizens to facilitate the destruction of Black wealth. The same institutional infrastructure - National Guard, martial law, detention - deployed at Pine Ridge, during labor strikes, and exported via the School of the Americas.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1921-01-01</begin><end>1921-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-95.9919,36.1558,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Musée du Louvre, Paris</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>380,000 objects, 35,000 on display. Originally a royal palace. Napoleon turned it into his personal trophy case — filled it with art seized from every country he conquered. Denon Wing named for Vivant Denon, who accompanied Napoleon to Egypt and looted systematically. The Mona Lisa wasn&#x27;t bought — it was taken from Italy by François I. The museum-as-empire: if you can&#x27;t hold the territory, you hold the artifacts.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>2.3376,48.8606,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Getty Museum / Getty Villa, Los Angeles</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>J. Paul Getty — wealthiest private citizen in the world (1966). Oil fortune (Getty Oil → Texaco → Chevron). Getty Villa: 44,000 Greek/Roman/Etruscan antiquities. Marion True (curator 1986-2005) indicted in Italy for trafficking in looted antiquities. Getty returned 40 objects to Italy, 4 to Greece. The oil baron&#x27;s museum caught buying stolen ancient art. $6.4B endowment — largest of any museum on Earth.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1966-01-01</begin><end>1966-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-118.4741,34.078,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Crystal Bridges Museum of American Art, Bentonville, AR</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Alice Walton — Walmart heir, net worth $72B+. Built $500M museum in Bentonville (Walmart HQ town). Collection includes Rockwell, Warhol, Rothko. Walmart: largest private employer in the U.S., wages subsidized by billions in public assistance. The fortune built on suppressed wages converted into an art collection that becomes a tax-advantaged philanthropy vehicle. Art as wealth laundering.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-94.2028,36.3824,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>National Museum of Anthropology, Mexico City</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Aztec Sun Stone. Olmec colossal heads. Maya jade death masks. 600,000+ artifacts from Mesoamerican civilizations. Built 1964 by the same Mexican state that destroyed the civilizations whose artifacts it displays. The 1985 Christmas Eve theft: 140 objects stolen including Mixtec gold and Maya jade — recovered 1989. The museum is the state&#x27;s claim to a heritage it extinguished.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1964-01-01</begin><end>1964-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-99.1861,19.426,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Acropolis Museum, Athens</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Built 2009, €130M. Entire floor designed with empty spaces — reserved for the Parthenon Marbles currently in the British Museum. Lord Elgin removed them 1801-1812 from the Parthenon under an Ottoman permit of questionable validity. Greece has demanded return since independence (1832). The museum that was architecturally designed around its own absence — the building is a repatriation argument.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2009-01-01</begin><end>2009-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>23.7284,37.9685,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Royal Museum for Central Africa, Tervuren, Belgium</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Built by Leopold II (1897) using profits from the Congo Free State — where 10 million+ Congolese died under his forced labor rubber regime. Originally a propaganda exhibition to justify colonialism. &#x27;Civilizing mission&#x27; displays alongside severed hands. Renovated 2018 as &#x27;AfricaMuseum&#x27; — the building itself is the artifact: a monument to genocide rebranded as cultural institution. The rubber money museum.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1897-01-01</begin><end>1897-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>4.5224,50.8312,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>National Museum of Brazil, Rio de Janeiro</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Housed in former Imperial Palace. 200 years of collections. 20 million items. Luzia (11,500-year-old skeleton — oldest human remains in the Americas). September 2, 2018: fire destroyed 92.5% of the collection. Budget for fire prevention: $13,000/year. The oldest museum in the Americas burned because of a $13,000 maintenance budget. The state that couldn&#x27;t spend $13,000 to protect 20 million artifacts. What Luzia could have told us about pre-Columbian history — incinerated.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2018-09-02</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-43.2253,-22.9055,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>National Museum of China, Beijing</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Tiananmen Square — east side. 1.4 million objects. Merged from Museum of the Revolution + Museum of Chinese History (2003). Narrative controlled by CCP — permanent exhibitions frame 5,000 years of Chinese history as inevitably leading to Communist Party rule. Located on the square where the 1989 protests were crushed. The museum that tells you the state was always right, on the square where the state proved it by force.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2003-01-01</begin><end>2003-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>116.3975,39.9042,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Topkapi Palace Museum, Istanbul</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Ottoman Imperial residence 1465-1856. Houses relics: Muhammad&#x27;s sword, cloak, and tooth. Moses&#x27; staff (claimed). Joseph&#x27;s turban (claimed). 86,000 objects from three continents of empire. The Harem: 400 rooms, concubines, eunuchs, intrigue. The seat of an empire that controlled the land bridge between Europe and Asia, converted to a museum in 1924 when Atatürk abolished the sultanate. The imperial palace as tourist attraction.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1856-01-01</begin><end>1856-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>28.9834,41.0115,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Frick Collection, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Henry Clay Frick: Carnegie Steel partner, chairman of Carnegie Steel during the Homestead Strike (1892) — hired Pinkerton agents, 16 workers killed. Anarchist Alexander Berkman attempted to assassinate Frick. Frick survived, broke the union, and used his fortune to build this mansion/museum on 5th Avenue. Vermeer, Rembrandt, Bellini, Holbein. The art collection funded by the broken bodies of steelworkers. The Pinkerton budget became the Vermeer budget.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1892-01-01</begin><end>1892-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9672,40.771,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>National Palace Museum, Taipei</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>696,000+ objects — Chinese imperial collection spanning 8,000 years. Chiang Kai-shek evacuated the collection from Beijing&#x27;s Forbidden City (1948-49) during the Chinese Civil War — 2,972 crates shipped to Taiwan in three shipments. The mainland government calls it theft. Taiwan calls it preservation. The museum whose entire collection is a political argument about which China is the real one.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1948-01-01</begin><end>1948-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>121.5485,25.1024,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rijksmuseum, Amsterdam</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Dutch Golden Age collection. Rembrandt&#x27;s Night Watch. Vermeer&#x27;s Milkmaid. The &#x27;Golden Age&#x27; was funded by the VOC (Dutch East India Company) — the world&#x27;s first multinational corporation, first to issue stock, and the organization that colonized Indonesia, South Africa, and controlled the global spice trade through military force. The museum celebrates the art produced by the profits of the first corporate empire.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>4.8852,52.36,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Museo del Prado, Madrid</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>8,200+ paintings. Velázquez, Goya, El Greco, Bosch. Royal collection of the Spanish Habsburgs and Bourbons — the dynasties that extracted silver from Potosí (8 million indigenous/enslaved deaths), gold from the Americas, controlled the largest empire in history (1520s-1898). The Prado&#x27;s walls are decorated with the proceeds of colonial extraction. Las Meninas was painted while Potosí&#x27;s silver was arriving in Seville.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1520-01-01</begin><end>1520-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-3.6921,40.4138,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Natural History Museum, London</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>80 million specimens. Founded 1881 from British Museum&#x27;s natural history collection. Darwin&#x27;s specimens. Colonial-era botanical, zoological, and geological specimens collected from every continent Britain controlled. Specimen collecting was mapping for extraction — catalogue the resources, then send the companies. The museum as inventory ledger for the empire&#x27;s resource base.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1881-01-01</begin><end>1881-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-1.7682,51.4967,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Art Institute of Chicago</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Founded 1879. Impressionist collection (second only to Musée d&#x27;Orsay). Seurat&#x27;s Sunday Afternoon, Wood&#x27;s American Gothic. Board historically drawn from Chicago&#x27;s industrial aristocracy: meat-packing families (Armour), railroad barons, real estate. The same families that built the Union Stockyards, controlled grain futures, and profited from the 1893 World&#x27;s Fair — the exposition that also founded the Field Museum next door. Chicago&#x27;s museum district is its industrial fortune made permanent.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1879-01-01</begin><end>1879-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-87.6237,41.8796,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Deutsches Museum, Munich</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>World&#x27;s largest museum of science and technology. 28,000+ objects. V-2 rocket on display — the weapon built by slave labor at Mittelbau-Dora (20,000 deaths). Werner von Braun artifacts. Enigma machines. The museum that displays the technology without the slaves who built it. Science and technology museums worldwide follow this template: celebrate the invention, omit the human cost.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>11.5833,48.1299,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>International Spy Museum, Washington D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Privately owned (Malrite Company). Largest collection of espionage artifacts on public display. Opened 2002 — one year after 9/11, same year as the Iraq WMD intelligence fabrication. Advisory board includes former CIA, FBI, NSA directors. The museum that tells the public version of the story while the agencies that contributed to it continue the classified version. Entertainment as controlled disclosure.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2002-01-01</begin><end>2002-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.0231,38.8833,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sanxingdui Ruins, Guanghan, Sichuan, China</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Sacrificial pits at this Bronze Age site (c. 1700-1150 BC), first probed in 1929 and dramatically re-excavated from 2019, yielded hundreds of bronze masks, heads and trees - including a mask 1.31 m wide - from a lost Shu civilization with no written records, whose art style is unmatched anywhere else in ancient China. Source: World Archaeology, &#x27;The lost world of Sanxingdui&#x27; / China Daily.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1929-01-01</begin><end>1929-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>104.1999,30.9937,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Caral-Supe, Barranca Province, Peru</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Built around 2600 BC and home to over 3,000 people, Caral is the oldest known urban center in the Americas - roughly contemporary with the Egyptian pyramids - with six stepped platform mounds and sunken circular plazas of the Norte Chico civilization; UNESCO listed it in 2009. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Caral&#x27; / Popular Archaeology.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2009-01-01</begin><end>2009-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.5011,-10.8901,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Great Zimbabwe National Monument, Masvingo</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>The mortarless dry-stone Great Enclosure - a wall up to 9.6 m high and 250 m long - is the largest ancient structure in sub-Saharan Africa, capital of a trading empire (11th-15th c.) whose African authorship colonial authorities long tried to deny; it gives the modern nation its name. Source: Britannica, &#x27;Great Zimbabwe&#x27; / Wikipedia.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>30.9332,-20.2709,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Persepolis (Takht-e Jamshid), Fars Province, Iran</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Ceremonial capital of the Achaemenid Persian Empire, begun c. 518 BC by Darius I, with its Apadana audience hall and reliefs of tribute-bearing nations; it was looted and burned by Alexander the Great&#x27;s army in 330 BC. A UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1979. Source: UNESCO World Heritage &#x27;Persepolis&#x27; / Britannica.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1979-01-01</begin><end>1979-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>52.8904,29.9352,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Great Ziggurat of Ur, Dhi Qar, Iraq</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>A massive Sumerian stepped temple-platform to the moon god Nanna, built c. 2100 BC by King Ur-Nammu near modern Nasiriyah; its restored lower facade sits beside a former Iraqi airbase, and it anchors the ancient city of Ur, traditionally linked to the biblical Abraham. Source: Britannica, &#x27;Ziggurat of Ur&#x27; / Wikipedia.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>46.1031,30.9628,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mohenjo-daro, Larkana District, Sindh, Pakistan</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>One of the largest cities of the Indus Valley Civilization (built c. 2500 BC), notable for grid-planned streets, a covered drainage system and the &#x27;Great Bath&#x27;; its still-undeciphered script leaves a sophisticated urban society largely unreadable. UNESCO listed it in 1980 and warns of severe erosion. Source: UNESCO World Heritage &#x27;Archaeological Ruins at Moenjodaro&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1980-01-01</begin><end>1980-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>68.1349,27.3253,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nazca Lines, Nazca, Ica, Peru</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Hundreds of giant geoglyphs - animals, plants and straight lines up to kilometers long - etched into the desert plateau by the Nazca culture between roughly 500 BC and AD 500, only fully legible from the air; ongoing drone surveys keep adding newly discovered figures. UNESCO World Heritage since 1994. Source: UNESCO World Heritage &#x27;Lines and Geoglyphs of Nasca and Palpa&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1994-01-01</begin><end>1994-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-75.1853,-14.6998,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum, Boston</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>On March 18, 1990, two thieves disguised as police officers spent 81 minutes stealing 13 works — including a Vermeer and three Rembrandts — now valued at over $500 million, the largest property theft in history. The case remains unsolved with no arrests and a standing $10 million reward. Source: FBI, &#x27;Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum Heist&#x27; (fbi.gov); Smithsonian Magazine.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1990-03-18</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-71.0992,42.3382,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Museum of the Bible, Washington D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>The museum, funded by Hobby Lobby&#x27;s Green family, became a case study in illicit antiquities: Hobby Lobby paid a $3 million fine in 2017 and forfeited ~3,800 smuggled Iraqi artifacts, and the Greens agreed to return roughly 11,500 objects — including some 5,000 Egyptian papyri and 8,100 clay tablets — plus the looted Gilgamesh Dream Tablet, repatriated to Iraq in 2021. Source: OCCRP; Smithsonian Magazine; U.S. DOJ.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-01-01</begin><end>2017-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.0165,38.8845,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Humboldt Forum, Berlin</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>The Prussian Cultural Heritage Foundation agreed in 2021-22 to restitute about 530 Benin Bronzes — looted by British forces in 1897 — held in Berlin&#x27;s Ethnological Museum to Nigeria, a landmark in the global colonial-restitution debate, though roughly a third are to remain on loan in Berlin. Source: Euronews; Staatliche Museen zu Berlin (smb.museum); Artnet.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2021-01-01</begin><end>2021-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>13.4012,52.517,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Musée du quai Branly – Jacques Chirac, Paris</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>The museum holds around 70,000 sub-Saharan African objects — about two-thirds of France&#x27;s African holdings; the 2018 Sarr-Savoy report, which estimated 90-95% of Africa&#x27;s heritage sits outside the continent, prompted France to return 26 works plundered from Abomey Palace in 1892 to Benin. Source: Center for Art Law; Cultural Property News; Artnet.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2018-01-01</begin><end>2018-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>2.298,48.861,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bardo National Museum, Tunis</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>On March 18, 2015, gunmen attacked Tunisia&#x27;s national museum — home to one of the world&#x27;s greatest Roman mosaic collections — killing 22 people, mostly foreign tourists, in an assault ISIS claimed and that devastated the country&#x27;s tourism sector. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;2015 Tunisia attack&#x27;; U.S. Dept. of State; EBSCO Research Starters.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2015-03-18</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>10.1342,36.8094,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Victoria and Albert Museum, London</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>The V&amp;A holds treasures looted by British forces after the 1868 Battle of Maqdala in Ethiopia — gold crowns, crosses and royal regalia; in 2018 director Tristram Hunt publicly offered to return the Maqdala collection to Ethiopia on long-term loan rather than as outright restitution, spotlighting UK museums&#x27; colonial acquisitions. Source: Victoria and Albert Museum (vam.ac.uk); The Guardian.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1868-01-01</begin><end>1868-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.1716,51.4969,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>The Mob Museum, Las Vegas</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Officially the National Museum of Organized Crime and Law Enforcement, it opened in 2012 inside the former federal courthouse that hosted a 1950-51 Kefauver Committee hearing on organized crime, documenting the mob&#x27;s role in building Las Vegas and its casino skim operations. Source: The Mob Museum (themobmuseum.org); Las Vegas Review-Journal.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-115.1414,36.1728,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Museo Egizio, Turin</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Founded in 1824 and the oldest museum devoted solely to ancient Egypt, it holds the largest collection of Egyptian antiquities outside Cairo — over 30,000 objects — much of it amassed by French-Italian consul Bernardino Drovetti during the colonial-era scramble for Egyptian artifacts. Source: Museo Egizio (museoegizio.it); Encyclopaedia Britannica.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1824-01-01</begin><end>1824-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>7.6844,45.0684,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Karahan Tepe, Şanlıurfa Province, Turkey</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Excavated since 2019, this Pre-Pottery Neolithic ritual complex (c. 9400-8200 BCE) is the &#x27;sister site&#x27; of Göbekli Tepe, 35 km east, and part of the Taş Tepeler network of at least a dozen sites; its T-shaped stelae and carved figures push the origins of monumental religion back some 11,000 years, before agriculture. Source: Heritage Daily / Ancient Origins, &#x27;Karahan Tepe&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>39.3027,37.0917,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Machu Picchu, Cusco Region, Peru</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>A 15th-century Inca royal estate perched at ~2,430 m on a ridge above the Urubamba valley, unknown to the outside world until Hiram Bingham publicized it in 1911; its precision ashlar masonry and astronomical alignments (e.g. the Intihuatana stone) survive intact. UNESCO World Heritage since 1983. Source: UNESCO World Heritage &#x27;Historic Sanctuary of Machu Picchu&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1911-01-01</begin><end>1911-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.9658,-13.5231,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Çatalhöyük, Çumra, Konya Province, Turkey</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>A 9,000-year-old Neolithic proto-city of densely packed mudbrick houses entered through the roof, housing up to ~8,000 people with no streets, elaborate wall paintings and burials beneath the floors - a key site for understanding the origins of settled urban life. UNESCO World Heritage since 2012. Source: UNESCO World Heritage &#x27;Neolithic Site of Çatalhöyük&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>30.2569,40.6899,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mausoleum of the First Qin Emperor / Terracotta Army, Xi&#x27;an, China</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>The tomb complex of Qin Shi Huang (d. 210 BC), guarded by an estimated 8,000 life-size terracotta soldiers discovered by well-diggers in 1974; the central burial mound, described by historian Sima Qian as containing rivers of mercury, remains unexcavated. UNESCO World Heritage since 1987. Source: UNESCO World Heritage &#x27;Mausoleum of the First Qin Emperor&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1974-01-01</begin><end>1974-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>109.2093,34.3684,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>M+ Museum, West Kowloon, Hong Kong</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Asia&#x27;s largest museum of visual culture opened in November 2021 under the shadow of Hong Kong&#x27;s National Security Law; pro-Beijing figures pressured it over its collection and it withheld from display Ai Weiwei&#x27;s &#x27;Study of Perspective: Tiananmen Square,&#x27; which the artist cited as evidence the museum is &#x27;clearly under censorship.&#x27; Source: ARTnews; South China Morning Post; Al Jazeera.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2021-11-01</begin><end>2021-11-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>114.163,22.3017,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>National Museum of Afghanistan, Kabul</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>During the 1990s civil war and Taliban rule, an estimated 70% of the museum&#x27;s roughly 100,000-object collection was looted or destroyed, including some 2,500 statues smashed as idolatrous in 2001; the fabled Bactrian Gold survived, hidden in Central Bank vaults and rediscovered in 2003. Source: Britannica; Artnet News; Science (AAAS).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1990-01-01</begin><end>1990-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>69.12,34.4649,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Neue Galerie New York</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIII</b> &middot; museum</p><p>The museum&#x27;s centerpiece is Gustav Klimt&#x27;s &#x27;Portrait of Adele Bloch-Bauer I&#x27; (the &#x27;Woman in Gold&#x27;), Nazi-looted from a Jewish Viennese family and restituted to heir Maria Altmann in 2006 after a U.S. Supreme Court case, then bought by museum co-founder Ronald Lauder for a reported $135 million — a landmark in Holocaust art-restitution. Source: The New York Times; Republic of Austria v. Altmann (2004).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2006-01-01</begin><end>2006-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9454,40.8022,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section XIV (56)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Eastern Congo / DRC - Cobalt Mines</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Children as young as 6 in artisanal cobalt mining. Cobalt → batteries → surveillance cameras → smart cities. The supply chain is built on child labor.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>28.0,-3.45,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kolwezi, DRC - Cobalt Mining</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Heart of the cobalt belt. Glencore&#x27;s Mutanda and Kamoto mines. 70% of global cobalt comes from DRC. Children as young as 6 in artisanal mining. Cobalt → batteries → smartphones → surveillance cameras → smart cities. The supply chain for Section X&#x27;s surveillance cities starts in child labor mines.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>25.4667,-10.7167,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lubumbashi, DRC - Copper/Cobalt Hub</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Mining capital of southern DRC. Gécamines state mining company + Chinese-owned operations (CMOC, China Moly). $74B in Chinese mining investment. The minerals for the technology stack (Section X) are extracted by near-slave labor and purchased by Chinese state-connected firms.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>27.4794,-11.6647,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kipushi, DRC - Zinc/Copper Mine</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Historic mining complex since 1924 (Belgian colonial extraction). Ivanhoe Mines (Robert Friedland - sanctions controversies). Colonial extraction patterns continued post-independence under different names.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1924-01-01</begin><end>1924-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>27.2453,-11.7603,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Salar de Atacama, Chile - Lithium Triangle</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>World&#x27;s largest lithium reserve. Albemarle and SQM extraction. Lithium → EV batteries (Tesla/Musk, Tier 5). Chile&#x27;s Atacama Desert is being drained for the batteries that power the vehicles that the Tier 5 individual manufactures. Water table destruction for indigenous communities.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-68.25,-23.5,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Salar de Uyuni, Bolivia - Lithium Triangle</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Largest salt flat on Earth - estimated 21 million tonnes of lithium. Bolivia nationalized lithium reserves. 2019 coup against Evo Morales occurred after he cancelled a lithium deal with a German company. The coup followed the cancelled mining contract.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-67.4891,-20.1338,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Salta Province, Argentina - Lithium Triangle</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Third vertex of the lithium triangle. Livent (now Arcadium Lithium), Posco, and Chinese firms. Argentina, Bolivia, Chile together hold 58% of global lithium. The &#x27;triangle&#x27; isn&#x27;t a coincidence - it&#x27;s a single geological formation being divided by three governments.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-65.4117,-24.7859,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bayan Obo, Inner Mongolia, China - Rare Earths</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>World&#x27;s largest rare earth mine. China controls 60% of global rare earth production. Rare earths → fighter jets, guided missiles, satellites, smartphones, MRI machines. The material basis for both Section X surveillance technology and military hardware.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>109.9697,41.7808,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mount Weld, Western Australia - Rare Earths</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Lynas Corporation - largest non-Chinese rare earth mine. Australia attempting to break China&#x27;s rare earth monopoly. Strategic minerals for defense and technology sectors.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>122.55,-28.75,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Permian Basin, Texas/New Mexico - Oil &amp; Gas</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Largest oil-producing basin in the U.S. Pioneer Natural Resources, ConocoPhillips, Chevron (Rice, Tier 3). Fracking revolution transformed U.S. energy geopolitics. The energy that powers the infrastructure documented in this report.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-102.17,31.95,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ghawar Field, Saudi Arabia - World&#x27;s Largest Oil</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>World&#x27;s largest conventional oil field. Saudi Aramco (IPO 2019 - valued at $2T, world&#x27;s most valuable company). The PIF that funded Kushner&#x27;s Affinity Partners (Tier 5) derives from this oil. Energy → sovereign wealth → political influence → enclave real estate.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>49.5,25.4,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Groningen Gas Field, Netherlands</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Western Europe&#x27;s largest natural gas field. Extraction caused 1,600+ earthquakes, damaged 100,000+ homes. Production halted 2024 after decades of community destruction. The government extracted the resource until the infrastructure above it collapsed.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2024-01-01</begin><end>2024-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>6.85,53.35,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Niger Delta, Nigeria - Oil Extraction</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Shell, ExxonMobil, Chevron extraction since 1956. 13,000+ oil spills documented. Ogoni crisis: Ken Saro-Wiwa (writer, environmental activist) executed by Nigerian military government (1995) after protesting Shell&#x27;s environmental destruction. The writer killed for documenting the extraction.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1995-01-01</begin><end>1995-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>6.4457,4.8156,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Grasberg Mine, Papua, Indonesia</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Freeport-McMoRan - world&#x27;s largest gold mine and second-largest copper mine. Former Kissinger Associates client (Henry Kissinger sat on Freeport&#x27;s board). Indonesian military provides security. Indigenous Amungme and Kamoro people displaced. The Kissinger connection: advisory → mining board → indigenous displacement.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>137.1112,-4.062,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Carajás Mine, Pará, Brazil - Iron Ore</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Vale SA - world&#x27;s largest iron ore mine. Produced 300M+ tonnes/year. Brumadinho dam collapse (2019) killed 270 people - Vale knew the dam was at risk. The extraction company that knew the dam would fail and kept operating.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-50.15,-6.08,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Oyu Tolgoi, Mongolia - Copper/Gold</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Rio Tinto - underground copper-gold mine in the Gobi Desert. $16B development cost. Nomadic herder displacement. Water table depletion in a desert. Rio Tinto also destroyed Juukan Gorge (46,000-year-old Aboriginal sacred site) in Western Australia - the mining company that destroys archaeological evidence (Section XIII pattern).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>106.85,43.0,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cerrejón, Colombia - Coal Mine</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>One of world&#x27;s largest open-pit coal mines. BHP, Anglo American, Glencore (now South32). Wayuu indigenous community displacement. River diversion. The coal that powers the grid that powers the surveillance cities that monitors the populations displaced by the coal.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-72.6667,11.0833,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Escondida Mine, Chile - Copper</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>BHP - world&#x27;s largest copper mine. Produces 5% of global copper. Copper → electrical wiring, circuit boards, data centers, submarine cables. Every cable documented in this map contains copper extracted here.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-69.0667,-24.2667,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Arctic - Drilling Frontier</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Arctic drilling by Russia (Gazprom), Norway (Equinor), and others as ice melts. Same Arctic region as Svalbard seed vault and SvalSat satellite station. The vault, the satellite, and the drill - all at the same latitude, preparing for the same future.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>25.0,71.0,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Churchill, Manitoba - Northern Port</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Canada&#x27;s only Arctic deep-water port. Northern logistics corridor. Grain shipments, military positioning. Sold to private consortium (2018) after decades of federal neglect. As the Arctic melts, the port that controls the Northwest Passage becomes strategic infrastructure.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2018-01-01</begin><end>2018-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-94.165,58.7684,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Perm-36, Ural Region, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Last operating Soviet Gulag camp - closed 1988. Political prisoners until the final years of the USSR. Now a museum, though Russian government attempted to change its narrative from &#x27;political repression&#x27; to &#x27;traitors justly imprisoned.&#x27; The camp they tried to rename.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1988-01-01</begin><end>1988-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>56.73,57.62,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Norilsk, Krasnoyarsk Krai, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Most polluted city on Earth. Nornickel - world&#x27;s largest producer of palladium and refined nickel. Built by Gulag labor (Norillag: ~500,000 prisoners, estimated 17,000-18,000 deaths). Closed city until 2001. No roads connecting to outside - only air and rail. Environmental dead zone 30 km in every direction: acid rain, sulfur dioxide, soil contamination. The minerals the world needs extracted from a place the world pretends doesn&#x27;t exist.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2001-01-01</begin><end>2001-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>88.2027,69.3535,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Magadan, Russia - Gateway to the Gulag</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Transit point to Kolyma gold mines - the deadliest Gulag network. &#x27;Road of Bones&#x27; (R504 Kolyma Highway): 2,032 km road literally built on the bones of prisoners who died during construction. Dalstroy administered the Kolyma camps: estimated 1-2 million prisoners, hundreds of thousands died. Gold, tin, uranium extraction at -50°C. Mask of Sorrow monument (1996). The road paved with the dead.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1996-01-01</begin><end>1996-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>150.8083,59.568,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vorkuta, Komi Republic, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Arctic Gulag coal mining center. Vorkutlag: one of the largest Soviet forced labor camps, ~73,000 prisoners at peak. 1953 Vorkuta uprising - one of the first large-scale Gulag revolts. Coal still mined. Population collapsed from 117,000 (1991) to ~54,000 (2024). The Arctic mining city that survived the Gulag but not the free market.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1953-01-01</begin><end>1953-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>64.0602,67.4965,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nauru</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Smallest republic on Earth. Phosphate mining stripped 80% of the island (1906-2002). Richest per-capita country in 1970s, now bankrupt. Australian offshore immigration detention center. Mined to dust, then used as a prison island. The lifecycle of extraction: use it, empty it, fill it with people no one wants.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1906-01-01</begin><end>1906-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>166.9315,-0.5228,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Monsanto HQ (now Bayer), Creve Coeur, Missouri</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Agent Orange. PCBs. Glyphosate (Roundup). Acquired by Bayer (2018, $63B) - the company that made Zyklon B acquired the company that made Agent Orange. Patent ownership of seed genetics: farmers cannot replant proprietary seeds. The food supply as intellectual property.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2018-01-01</begin><end>2018-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-90.4227,38.66,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Foxconn City, Shenzhen / Zhengzhou, China</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Zhengzhou factory: 350,000 workers, 1.4 km² campus. Produces iPhone. Suicide nets installed on buildings after worker suicides (2010). 996 work culture: 9am-9pm, 6 days/week. The factory city where the world&#x27;s most profitable product is assembled under conditions that require suicide prevention infrastructure.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2010-01-01</begin><end>2010-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>113.6253,34.7466,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nestlé HQ, Vevey, Switzerland</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Largest food company on Earth. Water privatization in Michigan, Pakistan, California. Baby formula scandal: marketed formula in developing nations where clean water was unavailable (1977). CEO Peter Brabeck (2005): &#x27;Water is not a human right.&#x27; The largest food company asserting control over the most basic human need.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1977-01-01</begin><end>1977-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>6.8413,46.4603,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Potosí (Cerro Rico), Bolivia - Colonial Silver</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>&#x27;The mountain that eats men.&#x27; Spanish colonial extraction 1545-present. Estimated 8 million indigenous and enslaved African deaths over 300 years. Produced 60% of the world&#x27;s silver during colonial era. Funded the Spanish Empire, Habsburg wars, and the entire European economy. The silver in the Prado&#x27;s frames was mined here. Potosí had a larger population than London or Paris by 1600. The city built on a mountain of death that funded European civilization&#x27;s &#x27;golden age.&#x27;</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1545-01-01</begin><end>1545-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-65.7531,-19.5836,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kimberley, South Africa - De Beers &#x27;Big Hole&#x27;</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Cecil Rhodes founded De Beers here (1888). The &#x27;Big Hole&#x27; — largest hand-excavated pit on Earth. Diamonds → De Beers monopoly → &#x27;A Diamond Is Forever&#x27; marketing campaign (1947) → artificial scarcity. Rhodes&#x27; fortune funded: Rhodes Scholarships (Bill Clinton, Pete Buttigieg, Susan Rice, Rachel Maddow), Rhodesia (Zimbabwe), and the Round Table movement that influenced the Council on Foreign Relations (Section VII).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1888-01-01</begin><end>1888-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>24.7499,-28.7282,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Witwatersrand Basin, South Africa - Gold</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>World&#x27;s largest gold deposit. Anglo American Corporation (Ernest Oppenheimer) controlled both gold and diamonds. Apartheid mining labor system: migrant workers confined to hostels, separated from families, paid fraction of white wages. Gold → Bretton Woods → dollar reserve → global financial architecture. The gold standard was literally built on apartheid labor. Anglo American listed on the London Stock Exchange — apartheid profits laundered through the City of London.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>28.0456,-26.1715,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Marikana, South Africa - Lonmin Platinum Massacre</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>August 16, 2012. South African Police Service shot and killed 34 striking platinum miners (Lonmin mine). 78 wounded. Workers were demanding wages of $1,250/month. Cyril Ramaphosa (future president) was a Lonmin board member — his emails, released during inquiry, called for &#x27;concomitant action&#x27; against &#x27;dastardly criminal&#x27; strikers. The future president of post-apartheid South Africa called for action against miners, and 34 of them were killed by police. Lonmin later acquired by Sibanye-Stillwater.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2012-08-16</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>27.4893,-25.691,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bingham Canyon Mine, Utah - Kennecott/Rio Tinto</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>World&#x27;s largest man-made excavation. 1.2 km deep, 4 km wide. Visible from space. Operating since 1906. Rio Tinto (Kennecott subsidiary). Has produced more copper than any mine in history — 19 million tonnes. The copper in the electrical wiring, circuit boards, and data center cables documented across this entire map. April 2013: largest non-volcanic landslide in North American history inside the pit. They kept mining.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2013-04-01</begin><end>2013-04-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-112.1497,40.5233,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Panguna Mine, Bougainville, PNG - Rio Tinto Civil War</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Rio Tinto subsidiary (Bougainville Copper Ltd). Environmental destruction triggered the Bougainville Civil War (1988-1998). 15,000-20,000 deaths. PNG government imposed naval blockade against its own citizens to protect the mine. Australia provided military helicopters. The mine that started a war — and the foreign governments that armed both sides to protect a mining company&#x27;s asset. Mine closed 1989, island still seeking independence.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1988-01-01</begin><end>1988-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>155.4833,-6.3,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ok Tedi Mine, Papua New Guinea - BHP Environmental Disaster</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>BHP (now BHP Group). Discharged 80,000 tonnes/day of mine waste directly into the Ok Tedi and Fly River systems. Destroyed 1,500 km² of rainforest. BHP&#x27;s own environmental assessment (1999): damage &#x27;irreversible.&#x27; BHP divested in 2002 — transferred its shares to &#x27;PNG Sustainable Development Program&#x27; — a structure that allowed BHP to exit while continuing operations. The mining company that poisoned a river system, called the damage irreversible, and then left.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1999-01-01</begin><end>1999-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>141.1333,-5.2667,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Morenci Mine, Arizona - Freeport-McMoRan</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Largest copper mine in North America. Freeport-McMoRan (same company as Grasberg/Indonesia). Open-pit, 1.6 km wide. Arizona copper mining history: Phelps Dodge (now Freeport) used Arizona Rangers and National Guard against striking miners (1903 Morenci, 1917 Bisbee Deportation — 1,300 miners loaded onto cattle cars and abandoned in the desert). The mining company that deported its own workers into the desert.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1903-01-01</begin><end>1903-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-109.3331,33.0836,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Yanacocha Mine, Peru - Newmont Gold</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Largest gold mine in South America. Newmont Mining (world&#x27;s largest gold producer). Mercury contamination: Choropampa mercury spill (2000) — truck carrying mercury for the mine spilled in a village, 900+ people poisoned, children played with the &#x27;silver liquid.&#x27; Conga expansion project blocked by massive protests (2011-2012) — Maxima Acuña, a subsistence farmer, refused to sell her land. She won the Goldman Environmental Prize (2016). The farmer who beat Newmont.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2000-01-01</begin><end>2000-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-78.5333,-6.9833,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chuquicamata, Chile - World&#x27;s Largest Copper Open-Pit</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>State-owned Codelco. Operating since 1910. Salvador Allende nationalized Chilean copper (1971): &#x27;Copper is Chile&#x27;s wages.&#x27; Augusto Pinochet&#x27;s CIA-backed coup (September 11, 1973) — happened 2 years after nationalization. Anaconda Copper and Kennecott lobbied Washington. ITT Corporation offered CIA $1M to prevent Allende&#x27;s inauguration. The copper mine that triggered a coup. Cross-ref: Section VII control architecture.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1973-09-11</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-68.9014,-22.3214,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mountain Pass Mine, California - U.S. Rare Earths</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Only active rare earth mine in the United States. MP Materials (Chinese investor consortium initially). China controls 60% of rare earth mining, 90% of processing. Mountain Pass is America&#x27;s attempt to break that dependency — but the processing still largely happens in China. The mine that symbolizes U.S. strategic vulnerability: you can dig it up in California, but you can&#x27;t refine it without China.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-115.5347,35.4775,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Broken Hill, Australia - Origin of BHP</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>&#x27;The Hill&#x27; — BHP (Broken Hill Proprietary Company) was founded here (1885). Now BHP Group — world&#x27;s largest mining company by market cap. Silver, lead, zinc extraction created the company that became a global mining conglomerate operating on every continent. The Australian outback mine that grew into a $150B multinational. The company name still carries the coordinates of its first extraction site.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1885-01-01</begin><end>1885-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>141.4683,-31.9505,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Olympic Dam, South Australia - BHP Uranium</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>BHP. World&#x27;s largest known deposit of uranium. Also copper, gold, silver. Underground mine since 1988, proposed open-pit expansion would be the largest in the world (scrapped 2012 due to cost). The uranium for nuclear weapons and power plants — extracted from Aboriginal land (Kokatha people). Native title extinguished by the Roxby Downs Indenture Act (1982) — the state legislature that legislated indigenous rights out of existence for a mining company.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>136.8833,-30.45,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rössing Mine, Namibia - Rio Tinto Uranium</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Rio Tinto. One of the world&#x27;s largest open-pit uranium mines. Operated during apartheid-era South African occupation of Namibia (pre-1990 independence). Supplied uranium to apartheid South Africa&#x27;s nuclear weapons program. Iran also reportedly sourced yellowcake from Rössing through intermediaries. The uranium mine that armed apartheid — operated by the same company (Rio Tinto) that destroyed Juukan Gorge.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1990-01-01</begin><end>1990-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>15.05,-22.4833,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tenke Fungurume, DRC - CMOC Cobalt/Copper</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>China Molybdenum (CMOC) — acquired from Freeport-McMoRan for $2.65B (2016). One of the world&#x27;s largest cobalt/copper deposits. DRC suspended CMOC&#x27;s exports (2023) in a dispute over royalties — the country that controls 70% of global cobalt temporarily shut down the Chinese company extracting it. The geopolitical leverage of mineral dependency. Cross-ref: Kolwezi, Lubumbashi (same cobalt belt).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2016-01-01</begin><end>2016-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>26.1167,-10.6167,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Serra Pelada, Pará, Brazil - Open-Pit Gold Rush</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>1980s gold rush. 100,000+ garimpeiros (artisanal miners) in a single open pit. Sebastião Salgado&#x27;s photographs documented the scene: ant-like columns of mud-covered men carrying sacks up vertical ladders. No machines — pure human labor extraction. The images are indistinguishable from ancient slave mining. Mercury contamination destroyed the surrounding ecosystem. The mine is now a lake. The gold is in bank vaults; the mercury is in the water table.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1980-01-01</begin><end>1980-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-49.65,-5.9333,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Greenbushes Lithium Mine, Western Australia</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>The world&#x27;s largest hard-rock lithium mine by reserves and output, delivering about 1.48 million tonnes of spodumene concentrate a year — roughly one-third of global hard-rock lithium. It is operated by Talison Lithium, a joint venture of China&#x27;s Tianqi Lithium (51%) and Albemarle (49%), 250 km south of Perth. Source: NS Energy / Wikipedia (nsenergybusiness.com/projects/greenbushes-lithium-mine).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>116.0662,-33.8684,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Jwaneng Diamond Mine, Botswana</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Nicknamed the &#x27;Prince of Mines,&#x27; Jwaneng is the world&#x27;s richest diamond mine by value, producing 12-15 million carats a year and generating 60-70% of Debswana&#x27;s revenue. It is run by Debswana, a 50-50 joint venture between the Government of Botswana and the De Beers Group, and is moving underground to extend its life by 20 years. Source: Debswana / Mining Technology (debswana.com/jwaneng).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>24.7298,-24.5845,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Reko Diq Copper-Gold Project, Pakistan</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>One of the world&#x27;s largest undeveloped copper-gold deposits, with an estimated 5.9 billion tonnes of ore and a projected 40-year life, in the restive Chagai District of Balochistan. It is 50% owned by Barrick Gold and 50% by Pakistani federal and Balochistan governments, and is projected to generate roughly $70 billion in revenue amid a violent local insurgency. Source: The Diplomat / Mining.com (thediplomat.com/2025/09, mining.com).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>62.4333,28.9708,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mir Mine (Mirny Diamond Pipe), Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>One of the world&#x27;s largest excavated diamond pipes, an open pit about 1,200 m wide and 525 m deep in the Sakha Republic (Yakutia), so large that airspace above it was closed to helicopters. Developed by Soviet and later Alrosa operations from the 1950s, it transitioned to underground mining before a fatal 2017 flooding disaster halted work. Source: Britannica / BBC (britannica.com; bbc.com Mir mine).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1950-01-01</begin><end>1950-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>113.9925,62.5285,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sudbury Basin Nickel District, Canada</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>One of the world&#x27;s largest nickel-copper mining and smelting districts, formed by a roughly 1.85-billion-year-old meteorite impact and mined since the 1880s, now worked by Vale and Glencore. Its 380 m &#x27;Superstack&#x27; at Copper Cliff was long one of the tallest chimneys on Earth, a legacy of sulphur emissions that once denuded the surrounding landscape. Source: Britannica / Geological Survey of Canada (britannica.com/place/Sudbury-Basin).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1880-01-01</begin><end>1880-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-81.0662,46.4676,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Berkeley Pit, Butte, Montana</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>A former open-pit copper mine turned one of the largest Superfund toxic sites in the United States, now a 1.6 km-wide pit filled with roughly 900 m of acidic, metal-laden water measuring around pH 2.5. Operated by Anaconda Copper until 1982, its rising contaminated water infamously killed a flock of migrating snow geese in 2016. Source: U.S. EPA / Smithsonian (epa.gov Silver Bow Creek/Butte Area).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2016-01-01</begin><end>2016-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-112.5117,46.0172,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Muruntau Gold Mine, Uzbekistan</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>One of the world&#x27;s largest open-pit gold mines, roughly 3.5 km long and 600 m deep, producing about 1.7-2 million ounces of gold per year and ranked second globally by output. It is 100% owned and operated by Uzbekistan&#x27;s state-run Navoi Mining &amp; Metallurgy Combinat (NMMC), with reserves estimated above 170 million ounces. Source: NS Energy / Kitco (nsenergybusiness.com/projects/muruntau-gold-mine).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>64.1961,41.5719,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Simandou Iron Ore Project, Guinea</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>The largest untapped high-grade iron ore deposit in the world, holding at least 3 billion tonnes averaging 65.3% iron. At roughly $23 billion it is Africa&#x27;s biggest-ever mining project, co-developed by Rio Tinto/Chalco (Simfer) and China&#x27;s Winning Consortium Simandou, with 600+ km of new rail built to export up to 120 million tonnes per year. Source: African Business / Rio Tinto (african.business/2024/02, riotinto.com/operations/africa/simandou).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-8.3675,8.9094,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>El Teniente Copper Mine, Chile</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>The world&#x27;s largest underground copper mine, with more than 2,400 km of tunnels producing over 400,000 tonnes of refined copper a year for state-owned Codelco, 55 km east of Rancagua. Operating since 1905 under the U.S. Braden Copper Company before nationalization, it suffered a fatal shaft collapse killing five miners in August 2025. Source: Britannica / Reuters (britannica.com/place/El-Teniente).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2025-08-01</begin><end>2025-08-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-70.6512,-34.1825,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Weda Bay Nickel Mine, Indonesia</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>By some estimates the world&#x27;s largest nickel mine, holding a 45,065-hectare concession on Halmahera island and the island&#x27;s largest deforestation footprint, feeding the EV battery supply chain. Majority-owned via Strand Minerals (France&#x27;s Eramet and China&#x27;s Tsingshan), it has been linked to threats against one of Indonesia&#x27;s last uncontacted tribes. Source: Mongabay / VOA (news.mongabay.com/2024/02).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.972,0.6301,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Thacker Pass Lithium Mine, Nevada</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Home to the largest known lithium resource and reserve in the world, this Humboldt County project aims to produce about 40,000 tonnes per year of battery-grade lithium carbonate. Operated by Lithium Americas (62%) with General Motors holding 38%, it drew a $2.26 billion U.S. Department of Energy loan and sustained protests from Indigenous groups over sacred-land impacts. Source: U.S. DOE / Wikipedia (energy.gov/edf/thacker-pass).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-117.7853,41.5697,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kalgoorlie Super Pit (Fimiston Open Pit), Australia</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XIV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>One of Australia&#x27;s largest open-pit gold mines, about 3.5 km long, 1.5 km wide and over 600 m deep on the historic Golden Mile, producing hundreds of thousands of ounces of gold a year. Now owned by Northern Star Resources, it consolidated numerous 1890s underground leases into a single vast pit visible from space. Source: Northern Star / Mining Technology (mining-technology.com Super Pit).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1890-01-01</begin><end>1890-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>121.4732,-30.7464,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section XV (41)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Ukraine - Active Conflict Zone</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Russia-Ukraine war (2022-present). Largest land war in Europe since 1945. Richest agricultural land and energy infrastructure. Grain supply chains disrupted.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-01-01</begin><end>2022-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>31.1656,48.3794,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Gaza - Active Conflict Zone</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Gaza-Israel conflict (Oct 2023-present). Mass civilian casualties. Infrastructure destruction. Forced displacement. GD MK-80 bombs + Nimbus AI targeting.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-10-01</begin><end>2023-10-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>34.3088,31.3547,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sudan - Active Conflict Zone</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Civil War (April 2023-present). 10+ million displaced. Ethnic violence in Darfur. Significant gold reserves. SAF vs RSF.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-04-01</begin><end>2023-04-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>32.5599,15.5007,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Myanmar - Active Conflict Zone</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Civil War (Feb 2021-present). Military junta. Airstrikes against civilians. Millions displaced. Rare earth mineral supply chain.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2021-02-01</begin><end>2021-02-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>96.0785,19.7633,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Darfur, Sudan</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Ethnic violence region within Sudan conflict. Pattern of displacement and resource extraction beneath the violence.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>25.0,13.5,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>South China Sea - Offshore Drilling</name><styleUrl>#t-mining</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; mining</p><p>Disputed maritime territory with massive hydrocarbon reserves. China, Vietnam, Philippines, Malaysia, Brunei all claim drilling rights. Artificial islands constructed by China for military/extraction purposes. The conflict zone is the extraction zone.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>115.0,15.0,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Socotra Island, Yemen</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>&#x27;Galápagos of the Indian Ocean&#x27; - 700 species found nowhere else. UNESCO World Heritage Site. Strategic position at Gulf of Aden chokepoint. UAE military base (2018, no Yemeni consent). Ancient maritime trade route waypoint. Unique ecology militarized during Yemen conflict.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2018-01-01</begin><end>2018-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>53.8237,12.4634,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>General Dynamics HQ, Reston, Virginia</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>MK-80 series bombs used in Gaza, Yemen, and throughout the Middle East. $42.3B revenue (2023). 4th largest defense contractor. Gulfstream luxury jets AND bomb casings - the same company builds the executive jet and the weapon it drops.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-01-01</begin><end>2023-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.357,38.9586,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Iraq Museum, Baghdad</name><styleUrl>#t-museum</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; museum</p><p>Looted April 10-12, 2003 - 15,000 artifacts stolen during U.S. invasion. Cradle of civilization artifacts. Gilgamesh tablets. Ur artifacts. The museum was not on the military&#x27;s protection list. The National Library also burned. The first thing destroyed in the cradle of civilization was the record of civilization.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2003-01-01</begin><end>2003-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>44.3577,33.3386,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Palmyra, Syria</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Queen Zenobia&#x27;s capital. 2,000-year-old colonnaded streets. Temple of Bel destroyed by ISIS (Aug 2015). Arch of Triumph destroyed (Oct 2015). Syrian civil war as cover for destruction of pre-Roman archaeological evidence. What was in the Temple of Bel that warranted destruction?</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2015-08-01</begin><end>2015-08-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>38.2691,34.5504,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nimrud, Iraq</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Assyrian capital (883 BC). Northwest Palace of Ashurnasirpal II. Lamassu (winged bull) statues. ISIS bulldozed the site (March 2015), filmed the destruction. 2,900-year-old civilization erased on camera. The pattern: invade Mesopotamia, destroy the pre-existing record.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2015-03-01</begin><end>2015-03-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>43.3283,36.0954,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Aleppo, Syria - Ancient City</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Continuously inhabited for 8,000+ years. Ancient Citadel. Great Mosque minaret destroyed (2013). 60% of the Ancient City damaged or destroyed in Syrian war. UNESCO World Heritage site as battleground. One of the oldest continuously inhabited cities on Earth, systematically dismantled.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2013-01-01</begin><end>2013-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>37.1343,36.2021,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Timbuktu, Mali</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Ancient center of Islamic scholarship. 700,000+ manuscripts (astronomy, mathematics, medicine). Ansar Dine/AQIM destroyed 14 of 16 mausoleums (2012). Manuscripts smuggled out by librarians in rice sacks. French intervention (Operation Serval, 2013). The library of the desert - nearly burned by those who claim to serve the same God.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-3.0074,16.7735,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mes Aynak, Afghanistan</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>5,000-year-old Buddhist monastery complex sitting on $100B copper deposit. China Metallurgical Group Corp mining lease (2007, $3B). Archaeological race against mining deadlines. 400+ Buddha statues, stupas, manuscripts. The ancient monastery will be destroyed to extract the copper beneath it.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2007-01-01</begin><end>2007-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>69.2719,34.3972,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sanaa Old City, Yemen</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>UNESCO World Heritage site. Inhabited for 2,500+ years. Rammed earth tower houses, 6-7 stories. Saudi-led coalition airstrikes (2015-present) damaged Old City. U.S./UK manufactured bombs. Ancient Arabian city bombed with Western weapons sold to Gulf monarchies.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2015-01-01</begin><end>2015-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>44.2066,15.3539,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mosul / Nineveh, Iraq</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Ancient Nineveh - Assyrian capital, Library of Ashurbanipal (oldest known library). Mosul Museum looted - ISIS sledgehammered 3,000-year-old statues (2015). Tomb of Jonah/Nebi Yunus mosque destroyed. Pattern: every invasion of Iraq involves destruction of pre-existing civilization&#x27;s records.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2015-01-01</begin><end>2015-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>43.145,36.365,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Libyan Desert - Ancient Saharan Sites</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Saharan rock art: 12,000+ year old petroglyphs showing green Sahara - rivers, lakes, cattle, humans. Libya conflict (2011-present) left archaeological sites unprotected. Wadi Mathendous: Neolithic engravings. The Sahara was green, the evidence is carved in rock, and the country that holds it has been in civil war since NATO intervention.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2011-01-01</begin><end>2011-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>17.2283,26.3351,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Khyber Pass, Afghanistan/Pakistan</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Mountain pass connecting Central and South Asia. Every empire that invaded India came through here: Alexander, Genghis Khan, Timur, Babur, British. Every empire that invaded Afghanistan entered here. 3,500 years of invasion through a single geographic chokepoint. The most invaded corridor on Earth.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>71.0956,34.1034,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Strait of Hormuz</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>21 miles wide at narrowest. 21% of global oil passes through. Iran on one side, Oman/UAE on the other. Every oil tanker from the Persian Gulf must pass through. The most valuable chokepoint on Earth - a geographic bottleneck that makes every Gulf war a global energy crisis.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>56.25,26.5944,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bab el-Mandeb Strait, Yemen/Djibouti</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>&#x27;Gate of Tears.&#x27; 20 miles wide. Connects Red Sea to Gulf of Aden - all Suez Canal shipping must pass through. Houthi attacks (2024) disrupted global shipping. U.S./UK military response. The chokepoint that proves Yemen&#x27;s strategic value is the reason for Yemen&#x27;s destruction.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2024-01-01</begin><end>2024-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>43.3333,12.5833,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Göbekli Tepe Region, Southeastern Turkey</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Region includes world&#x27;s oldest known temple complex. Kurdish territorial claims overlap. Turkish military operations (anti-PKK). The oldest evidence of organized human civilization sits in an active conflict zone between a NATO military and a stateless people. Archaeological access controlled by military operations.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>38.85,37.15,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Angkor Wat Region, Cambodia</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Largest religious monument ever built. Khmer Empire (802-1431). Khmer Rouge (1975-79): 1.5-2M killed. U.S. carpet bombing (Operation Menu, 1969-70): 2.75M tons - more bombs than all of WWII. The temple complex survived empires but the people around it were bombed and genocided in the same century.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1975-01-01</begin><end>1975-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>103.867,13.4125,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Guatemala - 1954 CIA Coup (Operation PBSUCCESS)</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>CIA overthrew democratically elected Jacobo Árbenz (1954). Crime: land reform threatening United Fruit Company (now Chiquita). 200,000 killed in subsequent 36-year civil war. Mayan genocide in highlands. The banana company&#x27;s coup.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1954-01-01</begin><end>1954-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-90.5069,14.6349,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Iran - 1953 CIA/MI6 Coup (Operation Ajax)</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>CIA/MI6 overthrew PM Mohammad Mosaddegh (1953). Crime: nationalized Anglo-Iranian Oil Company (now BP). Installed Shah - 25 years of SAVAK secret police (trained by CIA). 1979 revolution blowback. Every Middle East crisis traces back to this oil coup.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1953-01-01</begin><end>1953-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>51.389,35.6892,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Congo - Lumumba Assassination, Lubumbashi</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Patrice Lumumba - first democratically elected PM of Congo. Assassinated 17 Jan 1961. CLAIM NARROWED 31 Aug 2026 — the previous text said &#x27;CIA and Belgian intelligence involvement confirmed&#x27;, which overstates the American half. The Church Committee (1975) documented a CIA plot to kill Lumumba with poison supplied through the technical services chief; THAT PLOT WAS NEVER CARRIED OUT and was not the means of death. He was shot by a Katangan firing squad with Belgian officers present. A Belgian parliamentary commission found in 2001 that Belgium bore moral responsibility, and Belgium apologised in 2002. So: Belgian responsibility ESTABLISHED by Belgium&#x27;s own inquiry; a CIA assassination plot DOCUMENTED but not the mechanism. Replaced by Mobutu (U.S.-backed, 32 years). Uranium from Shinkolobwe mine used in Hiroshima bomb. The country with the most strategic minerals has never been allowed self-governance.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1961-01-17</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>27.5026,-11.6876,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chile - 1973 CIA Coup, Santiago</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>CIA-backed coup against Salvador Allende (Sept 11, 1973). Pinochet installed - 3,000+ killed, 40,000 tortured. &#x27;Chicago Boys&#x27; economic experiment: Milton Friedman&#x27;s free market ideology tested on a country at gunpoint. The economic theory required a military dictatorship to implement.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1973-09-11</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-70.6693,-33.4489,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Libya - NATO Intervention, Tripoli</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>NATO bombing (2011). Gaddafi killed Oct 2011. Had proposed gold-backed African currency (Gold Dinar). Largest proven oil reserves in Africa. Country went from highest HDI in Africa to open-air slave markets. Hillary Clinton: &#x27;We came, we saw, he died.&#x27; The country that tried to create an African currency was destroyed.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2011-10-01</begin><end>2011-10-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>13.1913,32.8872,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Laos - Secret War, Plain of Jars</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Most heavily bombed country per capita in history. 270M cluster bombs dropped (1964-73). 80M unexploded. 300 casualties/year still. Plain of Jars: megalithic stone jars, 2,000+ years old - purpose unknown. The most bombed country on Earth is also home to one of the most unexplained archaeological sites. Both facts ignored.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1964-01-01</begin><end>1964-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>103.15,19.45,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vietnam - Cu Chi Tunnels, Ho Chi Minh City</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>250 km tunnel network. Underground city: hospitals, kitchens, command centers. Built over 25 years. Survived carpet bombing, chemical defoliation (Agent Orange - Monsanto/Dow Chemical). The tunnel builders defeated the largest military on Earth. 3M Vietnamese dead. 58,000 Americans dead. Monsanto has never paid damages.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>106.4625,11.1417,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Zaporizhzhia Nuclear Power Plant - Enerhodar, Ukraine</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Europe&#x27;s largest nuclear plant (six VVER-1000 reactors, 6,000 MW) has been under Russian military occupation since 4 March 2022, its reactors shut down while the site is used as a fortified base. The IAEA has repeatedly warned of shelling near the plant and loss of external power, calling the situation an unprecedented nuclear-safety risk. Source: Al Jazeera; The Conversation (nuclear-expert analysis) — aljazeera.com/news/2022/11/21/un-calls-for-end-to-madness-of-attacks-on-zaporizhzhia-plant.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2022-03-04</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>34.5867,47.5139,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>El Fasher - North Darfur, Sudan</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>The Rapid Support Forces besieged El Fasher, the Sudanese army&#x27;s last Darfur stronghold, from May 2024 until seizing it on 26 October 2025, trapping over 900,000 civilians and spreading famine. UN investigators found the 18-month siege and ensuing mass killings bore &#x27;hallmarks of genocide.&#x27; Source: UN OHCHR; Amnesty International — ohchr.org/en/documents/country-reports/report-ohchr-sudan-country-office-siege-el-fasher-north-darfur-may-2024.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2025-10-26</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>25.3556,13.6238,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mekelle - Tigray, Ethiopia</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Capital of Tigray and focal point of the 2020-2022 war between Ethiopia&#x27;s federal government and the TPLF, during which Addis Ababa imposed a de facto siege cutting food, banking, power and telecoms. Estimates put the war&#x27;s toll above 600,000 dead, including 150,000-200,000 from starvation, before the November 2022 Pretoria ceasefire. Source: International Crisis Group; GlobalSecurity.org — crisisgroup.org/stm/africa/ethiopia/turning-pretoria-deal-lasting-peace-ethiopia.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-11-01</begin><end>2022-11-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>39.4768,13.4967,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bakhmut - Donetsk Oblast, Ukraine</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Site of the longest battle of the 21st century (roughly 327 days, October 2022 to May 2023), Bakhmut became known as the &#x27;meat grinder,&#x27; with Wagner Group alone recording 19,547 dead, many recruited from Russian prisons. A city of 70,000 before the war, an estimated 500 residents remained when it fell. Source: United24 Media; Al Jazeera timeline — united24media.com/war-in-ukraine/the-longest-battle-of-the-21st-century-battle-of-bakhmut-3432.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-10-01</begin><end>2022-10-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>38.0021,48.5894,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Marib - Yemen (Oil &amp; Gas Frontline)</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Marib, the government&#x27;s last northern stronghold and home to a refinery producing about 90% of Yemen&#x27;s LPG, was the pivotal front of the 2021-2022 Houthi offensive. The UN warned the push threatened to displace at least 385,000 people sheltering in the governorate. Source: Washington Post; RUSI — washingtonpost.com/world/interactive/2021/yemen-war-marib-houthis/.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2021-01-01</begin><end>2021-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>45.323,15.4579,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mozambique LNG (Afungi site) - Palma, Cabo Delgado</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>On 24 March 2021 ISIS-linked al-Shabab militants overran the town of Palma beside TotalEnergies&#x27; Afungi LNG complex, killing more than 1,190 people in what analysts called the deadliest such attack on the African continent. TotalEnergies evacuated all staff and declared force majeure on the multi-billion-dollar project in April 2021. Source: Combating Terrorism Center at West Point — ctc.westpoint.edu/the-march-2021-palma-attack-and-the-evolving-jihadi-terror-threat-to-mozambique/.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2021-03-24</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>39.4169,-12.4255,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nord Stream Pipeline Sabotage Site - off Bornholm, Baltic Sea</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>On 26 September 2022 underwater explosions ruptured three of the four Nord Stream 1 and 2 gas pipelines on the Baltic seabed east of the Danish island of Bornholm, at depths over 100 m. Scandinavian seismographs registered the blasts and Swedish prosecutors confirmed &#x27;gross sabotage&#x27;; attribution remains internationally disputed. Source: RFE/RL; BBC — rferl.org/a/nord-stream-mystery-baltic-sea-pipeline-blasts/32315977.html.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2022-09-26</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>10.3333,55.6702,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lachin Corridor - Nagorno-Karabakh</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Azerbaijan blockaded the sole road linking Nagorno-Karabakh to Armenia from December 2022, starving Stepanakert of food, fuel and medicine for nine months. After a September 2023 military offensive the ethnic-Armenian enclave capitulated and over 100,000 Armenians fled within a week, effectively emptying the region. Source: Amnesty International; BBC — amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2023/02/azerbaijan-blockade-of-lachin-corridor-putting-thousands-of-lives-in-peril-must-be-immediately-lifted/.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-12-01</begin><end>2022-12-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>46.3142,39.7205,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Siachen Glacier - Karakoram, Ladakh</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>At roughly 18,000-22,000 ft, the Siachen Glacier is the world&#x27;s highest battlefield, contested by India and Pakistan since India&#x27;s 1984 Operation Meghdoot. With temperatures reaching -50°C, more soldiers on both sides have died from avalanches and cold than from combat. Source: GlobalSecurity.org; WorldAtlas — globalsecurity.org/military/world/war/siachen.htm.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1984-01-01</begin><end>1984-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>77.6569,33.9456,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Crimean (Kerch Strait) Bridge - Kerch, Crimea</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>The 19 km road-and-rail bridge Russia built across the Kerch Strait after its 2014 annexation of Crimea is the main military supply artery to the peninsula. A truck-bomb blast on 8 October 2022 collapsed two road spans and killed five people, and the span has been struck repeatedly since. Source: CNN; Wikipedia &#x27;2022 Crimean Bridge explosion&#x27; — cnn.com/2022/10/08/europe/crimea-bridge-explosion-intl-hnk.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2022-10-08</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>36.4671,45.3563,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Guerguerat Crossing / Moroccan Berm - Western Sahara</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Guerguerat sits on the roughly 2,700 km Moroccan sand berm, the world&#x27;s longest operational military barrier and longest continuous minefield, dividing Morocco-controlled Western Sahara from the Polisario-held Free Zone. A November 2020 flare-up at the crossing ended a near-30-year UN ceasefire, reigniting armed conflict. Source: Wikipedia &#x27;Moroccan Western Sahara Wall&#x27;; Georgetown Security Studies Review — en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moroccan_Western_Sahara_Wall.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2020-11-01</begin><end>2020-11-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-16.9599,21.427,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Second Thomas Shoal (BRP Sierra Madre) - Spratly Islands</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XV</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>In 1999 the Philippines deliberately grounded the WWII-era warship BRP Sierra Madre on the shoal to assert its claim; rotating marines still garrison the rusting hull. China has maintained a coast-guard blockade since 2013, in 2014 cutting off resupply for three weeks and repeatedly ramming and water-cannoning Philippine boats. Source: CSIS Asia Maritime Transparency Initiative — amti.csis.org/tracking-tensions-at-second-thomas-shoal/.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1999-01-01</begin><end>1999-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>115.86,9.72,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section XVI (50)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Pentagon, Washington D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; military</p><p>Operation Northwoods (1962): Joint Chiefs proposed false flag attacks on U.S. soil to justify Cuba invasion. Kennedy rejected it.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1962-01-01</begin><end>1962-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.0562,38.8711,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Gulf of Tonkin, Vietnam - DESOTO patrol area</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; military</p><p>2-4 Aug 1964. FOIA-SOURCED UPGRADE (read directly from NSA&#x27;s reading room, 18 Aug 2026). NSA released its Tonkin holdings in two tranches - 30 Nov 2005 and 30 May 2006 - and states on the release page that it was &#x27;not NSA&#x27;s intention to prove or disprove any one set of conclusions,&#x27; only to publish the material. The substantive finding is NSA historian Robert J. Hanyok&#x27;s Cryptologic Quarterly study &#x27;Skunks, Bogies, Silent Hounds, and the Flying Fish: The Gulf of Tonkin Mystery, 2-4 August 1964&#x27; (classified 2001, declassified Nov 2005): the 2 Aug attack happened; the 4 Aug attack did not; and the SIGINT product that appeared to confirm it was built from 4 Aug intercepts about recovery of the P-4s damaged on 2 Aug - re-dated, re-translated and selectively excerpted. PRECISION: that is Hanyok&#x27;s conclusion, not an institutional NSA finding, and he describes a mix of analytic error and deliberate misrepresentation rather than a single fabrication order. Collection also holds CAPT J.J. Herrick, Col Ralph Steakley (DESOTO) and Lt Col Delmar C. Lang reports. Sources: nsa.gov Gulf of Tonkin release; rel1_skunks_bogies.pdf.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1964-08-04</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>107.5,20.5,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hanslope Park - Operation Legacy / Migrated Archive, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>MI5/MI6/FCO facility housing the &#x27;Migrated Archive&#x27; - 1.2 million classified colonial files moved here from 37 colonies before independence handovers. Documents detailing torture, massacres, forced labor systematically removed from colonial territories. Existence denied for 50+ years until Mau Mau veterans&#x27; lawsuit (Mutua v. FCO, 2011). Operation Legacy: systematic destruction/concealment of the British Empire&#x27;s operational record.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2011-01-01</begin><end>2011-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.8301,52.0847,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Porton Down - MoD Chemical/Biological Testing, Wiltshire, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>UK Ministry of Defence CBW research facility. 20,000+ servicemen exposed to nerve agents (sarin, VX), LSD, CS gas without informed consent (1939-1989). Leading Aircraftman Ronald Maddison killed by sarin nerve agent 1953 - inquest returned &#x27;unlawful killing&#x27; verdict in 2004, 51 years later. Direct parallel to MKUltra: same era, same methods, Five Eyes partner.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1939-01-01</begin><end>1939-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-1.71,51.1311,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mururoa Atoll - French Nuclear Testing, French Polynesia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; military</p><p>193 French nuclear tests (1966-1996) - atmospheric and underground. Irradiated soldiers, sailors, and Polynesian civilians. French government denied health effects for decades. INSERM study (2020) confirmed thyroid cancer rates 3-5x higher in exposed populations. Loi Morin (2010) created compensation mechanism - 50 years after first tests. &#x27;Moruroa e Tatou&#x27; (veterans&#x27; association) documented contamination the state denied.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1966-01-01</begin><end>1966-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-138.9108,-21.8301,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Reggane - French Nuclear Tests in Algeria (Sahara)</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; military</p><p>First French nuclear test &#x27;Gerboise Bleue&#x27; (February 13, 1960) - 4x Hiroshima yield. 17 tests in the Algerian Sahara (1960-66) including 4 atmospheric. Local populations (including French soldiers) exposed without warning. Saharan communities still report elevated cancer rates. Files partially declassified 2013 - 53 years after first detonation. France conducted nuclear tests in its colony, then left.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1960-02-13</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>0.1714,26.7143,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Allan Memorial Institute, McGill University, Montreal</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Dr. Donald Ewen Cameron&#x27;s MKUltra subproject (1957-1964). CIA-funded experiments on Canadian psychiatric patients: &#x27;psychic driving&#x27; (continuous playback of recorded messages for weeks), massive electroshock (30-40x normal), drug-induced coma for months, sensory deprivation. Patients&#x27; personalities erased. Canadian government settled in 1992, denied residual liability until 2017. Same program as U.S. MKUltra - Five Eyes jurisdiction.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1957-01-01</begin><end>1957-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.5913,45.5086,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Maralinga Nuclear Test Site, South Australia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; military</p><p>British nuclear tests on Aboriginal Pitjantjatjara/Yankunytjatjara land (1956-1963). Indigenous communities not evacuated - &#x27;black mist&#x27; reports of immediate radiation sickness and burns. McClelland Royal Commission (1984-85) confirmed contamination. &#x27;Cleanup&#x27; involved burying 20+ kg of plutonium in shallow pits. Aboriginal elders report ongoing health effects across generations. UK government denied severity for 40 years.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1956-01-01</begin><end>1956-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>131.6136,-30.1594,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Katyn Forest, Russia (site of NKVD massacre)</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>NKVD executed 22,000 Polish officers, intellectuals, clergy, police (April-May 1940). Mass graves discovered by Nazi Germany (1943) - USSR blamed Nazis for 50 years. Nuremberg prosecutors attempted to include Katyn as a Nazi crime. Soviet responsibility finally acknowledged by Gorbachev (1990). Putin partially opened archives, then re-sealed key documents. 50 years of state denial of a documented massacre.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1940-05-01</begin><end>1940-05-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>31.7858,54.7723,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>ESMA (Navy Mechanics School) - Argentine Dirty War, Buenos Aires</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Primary clandestine detention/torture center during Argentina&#x27;s Dirty War (1976-1983). Estimated 5,000 prisoners passed through - most &#x27;disappeared.&#x27; Death flights: prisoners drugged, loaded onto naval aircraft, dropped alive into the Río de la Plata and Atlantic. Officers admitted to burning records. Now a museum and memory site. 30,000 disappeared across Argentina. CONADEP &#x27;Nunca Más&#x27; report (1984).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1976-01-01</begin><end>1976-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-58.4627,-34.5431,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Colonia Dignidad, Chile</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>German enclave in Chile (1961-2005) operated by Paul Schäfer, ex-Nazi. Served simultaneously as: agricultural commune, Pinochet-era torture/detention center (DINA collaboration), child sexual abuse site, weapons cache, and alleged chemical weapons facility. German and Chilean intelligence knew for decades. Schäfer fled to Argentina (1997), extradited (2005), died in Chilean prison (2010). German BND connection confirmed. Operation Condor node.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1961-01-01</begin><end>1961-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.748,-36.4518,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sverdlovsk (Yekaterinburg) - Biopreparat Anthrax Leak Site</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Compound 19 (Military Facility 19) - Soviet biological weapons facility. Accidental anthrax spore release (April 2, 1979) killed 66+ people downwind. USSR blamed contaminated meat for 12 years. Yeltsin admitted it was a weapons facility leak (1992). Ken Alibek (Biopreparat deputy director, defected 1992) confirmed: USSR operated world&#x27;s largest offensive bioweapons program (60+ facilities, 60,000 employees) while signatory to the 1972 Biological Weapons Convention. Signed the ban, then expanded the program.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1979-04-02</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>60.6057,56.8389,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Stasi Headquarters (Normannenstraße), Berlin</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>Ministry for State Security (MfS) headquarters. 91,000 employees, 173,000 informants - 1 informant per 63 citizens. The most comprehensive pre-digital domestic surveillance system ever built. 111 km of files. When the Wall fell (1989), Stasi officers shredded documents 24/7 - citizens stormed the building January 15, 1990, stopping the destruction. 16,000 bags of shredded documents still being reconstructed by computer. The surveillance state that almost erased its own record.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1990-01-15</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>13.4872,52.5147,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kamloops Indian Residential School, British Columbia</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Ground-penetrating radar (2021) detected remains of 215 children in unmarked graves. Part of Canada&#x27;s residential school system (1831-1996): 150,000+ Indigenous children forcibly removed from families. TRC (2008-2015) documented 4,100+ deaths - actual number estimated far higher. Churches burned records. Government burned records. Multiple subsequent sites found: Marieval (751), Cowessess (751), Williams Lake, Kuper Island. 100+ years of systematic evidence destruction.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2021-01-01</begin><end>2021-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-120.325,50.7116,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Unit 731 Site, Pingfang District, Harbin, China</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Imperial Japanese Army biological warfare unit (1937-1945). Vivisection of live prisoners without anesthesia, plague bomb tests, frostbite experiments. 3,000+ killed directly, 300,000+ estimated killed via biological weapon deployments in China. U.S. granted full immunity to all Unit 731 personnel - including commander Shirō Ishii - in exchange for research data. Data folded into Fort Detrick program. Same immunity-for-data pattern as Operation Paperclip. Japan has never officially acknowledged the program.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1937-01-01</begin><end>1937-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>126.644,45.6127,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Riebeeck Park - Project Coast / Roodeplaat Research Lab, South Africa</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Apartheid-era CBW program (1981-1993) led by Dr. Wouter Basson (&#x27;Dr. Death&#x27;). Developed: anthrax-laced cigarettes, botulinum-tipped umbrellas, cholera for water supplies, fertility-reducing agents targeting Black populations. Basson traveled to Libya, Iraq, Taiwan for CBW exchange. Most documents destroyed before TRC hearings. Basson acquitted on 67 charges (2002). Evidence destruction pattern: same as MKUltra, same as COINTELPRO.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1981-01-01</begin><end>1981-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>28.35,-25.5906,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>In Ekker Nuclear Test Site, Algeria (French underground tests)</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; military</p><p>13 underground French nuclear tests (1961-1966). &#x27;Béryl&#x27; test (May 1, 1962) - containment failure caused radioactive cloud to irradiate soldiers and officials including ministers. Footage suppressed for decades. French military personnel ordered to walk through contaminated zone. Algerian independence (1962) did not stop French testing - they continued for 4 more years under treaty provision. The colony that gained independence but not sovereignty over its own soil.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1962-05-01</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>5.05,24.05,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tiananmen Square, Beijing - June Fourth Suppression</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Declassified UK cables (released 2017) estimated 10,000+ killed - contradicting China&#x27;s long-suppressed official figures. 36+ years of domestic censorship: &#x27;June Fourth Incident&#x27; blocked from Chinese internet, social media, textbooks, search engines. No Chinese FOIA mechanism exists to request records. Mothers of Tiananmen (Tiānānmén Mǔqīn) advocacy group systematically suppressed. The massacre that a billion people are forbidden to search for.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-01-01</begin><end>2017-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>116.3976,39.9054,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Spring Grove State Hospital, Catonsville, MD</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>MKUltra Subproject 69. LSD experiments on psychiatric patients (1963-1976) conducted by Dr. Stanislav Grof and Dr. Walter Pahnke, funded through CIA cutouts. Spring Grove was Maryland&#x27;s oldest psychiatric hospital (founded 1797). Patients with terminal illness given LSD without meaningful consent. The research continued 3 years AFTER MKUltra was &#x27;officially terminated&#x27; in 1973. The program that ended didn&#x27;t end.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1963-01-01</begin><end>1963-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-76.7358,39.2724,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ionia State Hospital, Michigan</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>MKUltra Subproject 53. Dr. James Hamilton conducted experiments on prisoners at the adjacent Ionia State Reformatory - and psychiatric patients at the hospital. LSD, mescaline, scopolamine administered to incarcerated populations who could not leave. Ionia closed 1968. Records largely destroyed. The hospital that experimented on prisoners and called it psychiatry.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1968-01-01</begin><end>1968-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-85.071,42.987,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>St. Elizabeths Hospital, Washington D.C.</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Federal psychiatric hospital (founded 1855). Held John Hinckley Jr. (Reagan shooter) for 35 years. Held Ezra Pound for 12 years (1946-1958) - the poet who broadcast fascist propaganda from Rome, declared &#x27;insane&#x27; to avoid treason trial. St. Elizabeths: where the government puts people it can&#x27;t convict. Walter Freeman performed ice-pick lobotomies here. DHS/USCG headquarters now occupying the campus. The psychiatric hospital became the homeland security headquarters. Same buildings. Same function: containment.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1855-01-01</begin><end>1855-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-76.974,38.849,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Creedmoor Psychiatric Center, Queens, NY</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>MKUltra Subproject 26. Dr. Paul Hoch administered mescaline and LSD to patients. Harold Blauer - tennis professional, admitted for depression - died December 1952 after injection of a mescaline derivative (EA-1298) in Army-funded experiments conducted at New York State Psychiatric Institute (Creedmoor network). Army contract W-18-064-CML-2397. Blauer&#x27;s family didn&#x27;t learn the truth for 23 years. The depressed tennis player killed by the Army in a hospital.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1952-12-01</begin><end>1952-12-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.731,40.745,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>New York State Psychiatric Institute, Manhattan</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Columbia University affiliate. MKUltra subprojects under Dr. Paul Hoch and Dr. James Cattell. Harold Blauer died here (1952) - Army mescaline injection. Hoch also injected patients with LSD and then performed lobotomies to compare &#x27;pre- and post-LSD&#x27; brain tissue. The psychiatrist who drugged and then lobotomized patients to study the interaction. Connected to Columbia University&#x27;s Department of Psychiatry - the Ivy League seal on black-budget human experimentation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1952-01-01</begin><end>1952-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.942,40.8405,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Riverview Hospital (Essondale), Coquitlam, BC, Canada</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>British Columbia&#x27;s psychiatric hospital. LSD experiments on patients (1950s-1960s) parallel to Allan Memorial. Dr. Hollywood (actual name: Dr. J.G. Chicken worked under pseudonym), BC government-funded. Canada&#x27;s MKUltra participation extended beyond Cameron&#x27;s Montreal - multiple provincial facilities participated. The Canadian government acknowledged these experiments in 2017. The apology came 60 years after the injury.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1950-01-01</begin><end>1950-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-122.8467,49.255,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Oak Ridge - Penetanguishene Mental Health Centre, Ontario</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Maximum security psychiatric facility. Dr. Elliott Barker&#x27;s &#x27;total encounter capsule&#x27; program (1960s-1970s): patients locked naked in a room together for weeks under LSD, forced to undergo &#x27;psychic driving&#x27; (borrowed from Cameron at Allan Memorial). Defense Research Board funded. Barker believed he could &#x27;cure&#x27; psychopathy through forced intimacy under hallucinogens. The experiment that used one MKUltra technique to treat the damage caused by another.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1960-01-01</begin><end>1960-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-79.9383,44.7583,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bethlem Royal Hospital (Bedlam), London, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>World&#x27;s oldest psychiatric institution (founded 1247). The word &#x27;bedlam&#x27; - meaning chaos, madness - comes from this hospital&#x27;s name. 777 years of continuous operation. Public could pay to watch inmates as entertainment (17th-18th century). Deep brain stimulation experiments (1950s-60s). William Sargant - MI5/MI6-connected psychiatrist - practiced narcosis (&#x27;deep sleep therapy&#x27;), electroshock, and insulin shock at St. Thomas&#x27; and Belmont (Royal Earlswood) in the same network. The original architecture of institutional madness.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1950-01-01</begin><end>1950-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.0625,51.3807,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chelmsford Private Hospital, Sydney, Australia</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Dr. Harry Bailey&#x27;s &#x27;deep sleep therapy&#x27; program (1963-1979): patients sedated into comas for weeks using barbiturates + ECT. 85 patients died. Bailey trained under William Sargant at St. Thomas&#x27; Hospital London - Sargant was MI5/MI6 connected. Bailey visited Allan Memorial and met Ewen Cameron. The techniques traveled: CIA (MKUltra) → Cameron (Montreal) → Sargant (London) → Bailey (Sydney). Five Eyes intelligence sharing included psychiatric torture methods. Bailey suicided 1985 before commission findings.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1963-01-01</begin><end>1963-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>151.138,-33.771,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vipeholm Experiments - Lund, Sweden</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Vipeholm Hospital for the intellectually disabled (1945-1955). Swedish government-funded dental experiments: patients force-fed extreme quantities of sticky candy to deliberately cause tooth decay - to study cavity formation. Not MKUltra. Not CIA. A neutral nation&#x27;s public health authority using institutionalized disabled people as dental test subjects. The Swedish Dental Board sponsored it. The results established modern dental science. The foundation of your dentist&#x27;s advice was built on mentally disabled people being used as experimental cavities. Neutral countries have their own architecture.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1945-01-01</begin><end>1945-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>13.1915,55.7045,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pavlov Institute of Physiology, St. Petersburg, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Ivan Pavlov&#x27;s conditioning laboratory - the foundational research that the entire behavioral modification architecture rests on. Pavlov → behaviorism → Skinner → programmatic behavior control → CIA behavioral research → MKUltra. The Soviet Union continued Pavlov&#x27;s work through the Serbsky Center (Moscow) - diagnosing political dissidents with &#x27;sluggish schizophrenia&#x27; to justify indefinite psychiatric commitment. Different state, same principle: define the behavior you want to eliminate, classify it as illness, treat it with force.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>30.3218,59.9718,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Serbsky State Scientific Center, Moscow, Russia</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Soviet &#x27;punitive psychiatry&#x27; headquarters. Political dissidents diagnosed with &#x27;sluggish schizophrenia&#x27; (вялотекущая шизофрения) - a diagnosis that existed only in Soviet psychiatry. Symptoms: &#x27;reform delusions,&#x27; &#x27;litigation mania,&#x27; &#x27;truth-seeking.&#x27; The diagnosis that made political opposition a mental illness. Gen. Pyotr Grigorenko - decorated WWII hero - committed here for criticizing Khrushchev. Estimated 2,000-5,000 political prisoners psychiatrically committed (1960s-1980s). The hospital that cured dissent.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1960-01-01</begin><end>1960-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>37.5997,55.7256,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kasr El Aini Hospital, Cairo, Egypt</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Egypt&#x27;s oldest hospital (founded 1837). Under Mubarak regime (1981-2011) and el-Sisi (2014-present): psychiatric commitment as political tool. Human Rights Watch documented forced psychiatric evaluations of activists, bloggers, LGBTQ individuals. The pattern: dissident → arrested → &#x27;psychiatric evaluation&#x27; → commitment → disappeared from legal system. Same architecture as Soviet punitive psychiatry, different flag. The Cairo version has never been formally investigated.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1837-01-01</begin><end>1837-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>31.2271,30.0287,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ankang Institutions - Beijing, China</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Ankang (安康, &#x27;Peace and Health&#x27;): China&#x27;s network of forensic psychiatric facilities administered by the Ministry of Public Security - not the Ministry of Health. Police-run psychiatric hospitals. Robin Munro (Human Rights Watch) documented: Falun Gong practitioners, political petitioners, labor activists committed to Ankang facilities. Forcible medication with antipsychotics. The psychiatric hospital run by the police, not doctors. At least 20 Ankang facilities across China. The name means &#x27;peace and health.&#x27;</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>116.4,39.93,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Topeka State Hospital, Kansas</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>MKUltra Subproject 43 - Dr. Robert Hyde. Connected to Boston Psychopathic Hospital network. Menninger Foundation in Topeka was CIA&#x27;s preferred psychiatric training ground - Dr. William Menninger served as Army&#x27;s chief psychiatrist (WWII). Karl Menninger Foundation trained CIA-affiliated psychiatrists who later conducted behavioral experiments across the MKUltra network. The hospital that trained the psychiatrists who ran the other hospitals.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-95.698,39.043,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vacaville - California Medical Facility</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>California state prison/medical facility. CIA behavior modification programs (1960s-1970s) under Dr. James Hamilton (also Ionia State). Bureau of Prisons/CIA collaboration: recidivist prisoners used for behavioral experiments. Anectine (succinylcholine) - a paralytic that simulates drowning/suffocation while conscious - used as &#x27;aversion therapy.&#x27; The prison medical facility that paralyzed inmates as treatment. Also connected to Vacaville&#x27;s START program (Special Treatment and Rehabilitative Training) - behavior control through isolation and drug protocols.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1960-01-01</begin><end>1960-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-121.971,38.3575,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tuol Sleng (S-21) Prison, Phnom Penh, Cambodia</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>A former high school converted by the Khmer Rouge into Security Office 21, the regime&#x27;s central interrogation and extermination site; the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia record roughly 18,000 people killed, with only a handful of known survivors. During early 1977 it claimed about 100 victims a day. Source: United States Holocaust Memorial Museum, &#x27;S-21, Tuol Sleng&#x27;; Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia records.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1977-01-01</begin><end>1977-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>104.9176,11.5495,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Automotores Orletti, Buenos Aires, Argentina</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>A former auto-repair garage in the Floresta neighbourhood used in 1976 by Argentina&#x27;s SIDE intelligence service as the main operational base of Operation Condor, the transnational plan to disappear dissidents; more than 300 people, many of them foreign nationals, were held there. Declared a national historic site in 2014. Source: Centro de Estudios Legales y Sociales (CELS), cels.org.ar; Plan Cóndor archive.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1976-01-01</begin><end>1976-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-58.4778,-34.631,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Holmesburg Prison, Philadelphia, USA</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Between 1951 and 1974, University of Pennsylvania dermatologist Albert Kligman ran hundreds of non-therapeutic experiments on nearly 1,000 mostly Black inmates, exposing them to dioxin, viruses, asbestos, and Army-commissioned psychotropic and hallucinogenic drugs. Philadelphia issued a formal apology in 2022. Source: Alliance for Human Research Protection, ahrp.org; Philadelphia Inquirer (Oct. 6, 2022).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1951-01-01</begin><end>1951-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-75.0188,40.0371,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Evin Prison, Tehran, Iran</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>Iran&#x27;s most notorious prison, at the foot of the Alborz Mountains in northwestern Tehran, holding activists, journalists and dual nationals; its Ward 209 is controlled directly by the Ministry of Intelligence and documented by Human Rights Watch for prolonged solitary confinement and &#x27;white torture.&#x27; Source: Human Rights Watch, &#x27;Like the Dead in Their Coffins&#x27; (2004); Wikipedia / Evin Prison.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>51.3841,35.7961,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bagram Theater Internment Facility / &#x27;Black Jail&#x27;, Afghanistan</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>The main U.S. detention site in Afghanistan, alongside a separate DIA/special-operations &#x27;Black Jail&#x27;; a 2005 Army report obtained by the New York Times documented the 2002 homicides of detainees Habibullah and Dilawar, who were chained and beaten to death, with autopsies describing leg trauma comparable to being run over by a bus. Source: New York Times / Army CID report (2005); Wikipedia, &#x27;Bagram torture and prisoner abuse&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2005-01-01</begin><end>2005-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>69.2765,34.9391,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Saydnaya Military Prison, Syria</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>A military prison ~30 km north of Damascus where Amnesty International estimated 5,000-13,000 detainees were extrajudicially hanged between September 2011 and December 2015, calling it a &#x27;human slaughterhouse.&#x27; Weekly night-time mass hangings of 20-100 people were documented as crimes against humanity. Source: Amnesty International, &#x27;Human Slaughterhouse: Mass Hangings and Extermination at Saydnaya Prison&#x27; (2017), amnesty.org/en/documents/mde24/5415/2017/en/.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2011-09-01</begin><end>2011-09-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>36.3727,33.6989,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Villa Grimaldi (Cuartel Terranova), Santiago, Chile</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>A former estate in Peñalolén that Pinochet&#x27;s secret police (DINA) ran as its most important Santiago torture center from 1974 to 1978; about 4,500 detainees passed through and at least 240 were killed or &#x27;disappeared.&#x27; It is now the Parque por la Paz memorial. Source: Wikipedia / Villa Grimaldi Peace Park; Plan Cóndor archive, plancondor.org.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1974-01-01</begin><end>1974-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-70.5423,-33.463,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Willowbrook State School, Staten Island, USA</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>At this state institution for intellectually disabled children, an NYU team led by Saul Krugman deliberately infected institutionalized children with hepatitis from 1956 to 1972, sometimes via a virus-laced milkshake, with parental enrollment often conditioned on consenting to the study. A 1972 Geraldo Rivera exposé forced its closure. Source: C. Elliott, New York Review of Books (Nov. 21, 2024); Bioethics Research Center case study.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1956-01-01</begin><end>1956-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-74.1509,40.5965,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kaechon Internment Camp (Camp 14), North Korea</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>A roughly 155-square-kilometre &#x27;total control zone&#x27; political prison on the Taedong River (approx. 39.571 N, 126.055 E) holding an estimated 15,000 prisoners serving life sentences; a UN Commission of Inquiry found extermination, enslavement and torture there. It is tracked via satellite imagery by HRNK. Source: Committee for Human Rights in North Korea (HRNK), &#x27;North Korea Imagery Analysis of Camp 14&#x27;; U.S. State Department, &#x27;Prisons of North Korea&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>125.8747,39.2413,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tazmamart Secret Prison, Morocco</name><styleUrl>#t-blacksite</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; blacksite</p><p>A secret desert prison in the High Atlas, built after the 1971-72 coup attempts against King Hassan II, where 58 soldiers and officials were disappeared into windowless concrete cells for 18 years (1973-1991). A 2014 field visit found only two razed blocks and 33 unmarked graves. Source: ICRC Missing Persons Platform, &#x27;Descending into Hell: Tazmamart&#x27;; Wikipedia / Tazmamart.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1971-01-01</begin><end>1971-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-4.7257,32.4861,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Arlington Hall Station, Arlington, Virginia</name><styleUrl>#t-surveillance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; surveillance</p><p>FOIA-SOURCED (NSA reading room, read 18 Aug 2026). Arlington Hall - a former girls&#x27; school seized under wartime powers in 1942 - was the headquarters of NSA&#x27;s predecessors, the Army Security Agency and the Armed Forces Security Agency, until the move to Fort Meade in the 1950s. It is where the VENONA decryption effort against Soviet cable traffic was run. NSA has declassified over 800 photographs of the site covering the mid-1940s to mid-1950s, with a downloadable photo index, and solicits public help identifying people in them. The campus now houses the State Department&#x27;s Foreign Service Institute and an Army National Guard facility. Source: NSA Historical Releases - Arlington Hall collection.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1942-01-01</begin><end>1942-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.10367,38.86762,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>USS Liberty (AGTR-5) attack position, off Sinai</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; military</p><p>8 June 1967 (position approximate). FOIA-SOURCED (NSA reading room, read 18 Aug 2026). The USS Liberty, a US Navy signals-intelligence ship, was attacked by Israeli aircraft and torpedo boats in international waters during the Six-Day War; 34 Americans were killed and about 171 wounded. NSA&#x27;s declassified collection runs to 17 pages of material - attack reports, situation summaries, operational orders and authorisation memos, an &#x27;Aftermath of Israeli Attack on USS Liberty, 22 June 1967&#x27; report, and contemporaneous press coverage from 11 and 17 June. TIER: the attack, the casualties and the documents are documented; whether the attack was deliberate or a misidentification remains disputed between the US and Israeli official accounts and this map does not settle it. Source: NSA Historical Releases - USS Liberty collection.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1967-06-08</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>33.383,31.383,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>USS Pueblo (AGER-2) seizure position, off Wonsan</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; military</p><p>23 January 1968 (position approximate). FOIA-SOURCED (NSA reading room, read 18 Aug 2026). North Korean forces seized the US signals-intelligence ship USS Pueblo off the east coast of Korea; one crewman was killed and 82 were held for eleven months. NSA released 19 pages of material in July 2021, including &#x27;Lessons Learned&#x27; reports comparing the Pueblo and EC-121 incidents, NSA response and action reports, cryptologic-impact assessments, SIGINT reflections covering 23-26 January 1968, and documentation of attempts to recover the material lost with the ship. The Pueblo is still held by North Korea and is moored in Pyongyang as a museum - the only commissioned US Navy vessel in foreign captivity. Source: NSA Historical Releases - USS Pueblo collection.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1968-01-23</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>127.9,39.42,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>C-130 60528 shootdown site, Sasnashen, Soviet Armenia</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; military</p><p>2 September 1958. FOIA-SOURCED (NSA reading room, read 18 Aug 2026). Soviet MiG-17 pilots shot down a US Air Force reconnaissance-configured C-130 over Soviet Armenia; all 17 crew were lost. NSA released roughly 13 documents in July 2021 - incident reports, Russian-language intercept transcripts with translations of the fighter pilots&#x27; own radio traffic during the engagement, audio files, crew and casualty records, and a survey of reconnaissance incidents 1949-1960. The intercepted cockpit traffic is the reason this case is unusual: the shootdown is documented from inside the attacking formation&#x27;s own communications. Source: NSA Historical Releases - C130 Shootdown collection.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1958-09-02</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>43.9921,40.35703,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bigelow Aerospace / BAASS, North Las Vegas, Nevada</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>FOIA-SOURCED (DIA reading room; contract-status PDF text extracted directly, 18 Aug 2026). Bigelow Aerospace Advanced Space Studies (BAASS) held DIA aerospace contract HHM402-08-C-0072 under the Advanced Aerospace Weapon System Applications Program (AAWSAP/AATIP). DIA&#x27;s own status brief records: performance &#x27;has been excellent and they are in full compliance&#x27;; 12 project management plans and 26 detailed research reports delivered by 30 June 2009 - &#x27;twice minimum requirement&#x27;; &#x27;$12 million for the continuation of this contract by DIA/DI has been submitted in the FY10 defense budget&#x27;; the contracting officer extended the contract to 30 September at no additional cost, and BAASS indicated willingness to operate &#x27;at risk&#x27; in option year 1 until FY10 funds arrived. Deliverable titles include Warp Drives, Wormholes in Space Time, Antigravity Studies, Metamaterials and Invisibility, Brain-Machine Interfaces, and Field Effects on Biological Tissues; one author organisation survives redaction as Sandia. Redactions are marked (b)(3):10 USC 424, the statute shielding DIA organisational detail. TIER: the contract, the money and the report titles are documented in DIA&#x27;s own release; the existence of recovered craft is NOT documented by any of it. Source: DIA FOIA reading room, AAWSAP/AATIP collection, Aerospace_Contract_Status_Bigelow_Aerospace_Advanced_Space_Studies.pdf.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2009-06-30</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-115.16721,36.2119,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Defense Intelligence Agency HQ, Joint Base Anacostia-Bolling, DC</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVI</b> &middot; military</p><p>FOIA-SOURCED (DIA reading room, read 18 Aug 2026). DIA headquarters, and the agency whose electronic reading room holds the AAWSAP/AATIP collection: 53 released items covering the Bigelow contract chain and 37 Defense Intelligence Reference Documents on subjects from inertial electrostatic confinement fusion to traversable wormholes. The collection also holds the paper trail of Senator Harry Reid&#x27;s interest - memos on his visit to DIA, and his letter to the Deputy Secretary of Defense seeking Special Access Program status for the effort, which was reviewed and, per the same file series, not granted in the form requested. Other DIA reading-room collections indexed the same day: Unidentified Anomalous Phenomena, POWs/MIA/Detainees, Weapons Development and Proliferation, China Mission Group, and annual FOIA request logs 2001-2023. Source: DIA FOIA Electronic Reading Room.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVI">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2001-01-01</begin><end>2001-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-77.01588,38.84268,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section XVII (35)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Mena, Arkansas - CIA Cocaine Transshipment</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Barry Seal&#x27;s base of operations. CIA-linked cocaine flights from Central America through Mena&#x27;s Intermountain Municipal Airport. Seal ran an estimated $3-5B in cocaine. Assassinated Feb 19, 1986 in Baton Rouge. State Police investigator Russell Welch shot with military-grade anthrax after documenting flights.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1986-02-19</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-94.2394,34.5862,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ilopango Air Base, El Salvador</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>CIA cocaine logistics hub. Contra supply flights returned loaded with cocaine. Oliver North&#x27;s notebooks reference the operation. Kerry Committee (1989) confirmed Contra drug trafficking as state-facilitated policy.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1989-01-01</begin><end>1989-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-89.1199,13.6995,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Culiacán, Sinaloa, Mexico - Cartel HQ</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Sinaloa Cartel headquarters. Jesús Vicente Zambada-Niebla testified (2013) the cartel had an agreement with DEA and DOJ - immunity in exchange for intelligence on rival cartels. U.S. government provided cartel leadership with protection while publicly fighting the drug war. El Chapo was captured and escaped repeatedly - the 2015 Altiplano escape ran through a mile-long tunnel with a motorcycle on rails, GPS-tracked to within inches of his cell. The tunnels reach into maximum-security prisons, not just across the border.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2013-01-01</begin><end>2013-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-107.394,24.8094,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Otay Mesa, California - Cartel Tunnel</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Major tunnel corridor between Tijuana and San Diego. Sinaloa Cartel operated sophisticated drug tunnels with rail systems, ventilation, and electricity. Distribution hub connecting Mexican production to U.S. market.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-116.9386,32.5547,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chicago, Illinois - Sinaloa Distribution Hub</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>DEA identified Chicago as the primary Sinaloa Cartel distribution hub in the United States. The cartel used Chicago as a central node to supply cocaine, heroin, and methamphetamine to the entire eastern seaboard and Midwest.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.6298,41.8781,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Arezzo, Italy - P2 Lodge / Villa Wanda</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Licio Gelli&#x27;s Villa Wanda - headquarters of Propaganda Due (P2) Masonic lodge. 962 members including 44 parliamentarians, military commanders, intelligence chiefs, financiers, media editors. Gelli&#x27;s &#x27;Plan of Democratic Rebirth&#x27; - a 53-point manifesto for authoritarian capture of Italian democracy through media control, judicial infiltration, and constitutional amendment.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>11.8781,43.4633,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Milan, Italy - Banco Ambrosiano</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Banco Ambrosiano headquarters. Italy&#x27;s largest private bank collapsed in 1982 with a $1.287 billion hole. Chairman Roberto Calvi found hanged under Blackfriars Bridge, London. Vatican Bank (IOR) was the principal shareholder. P2 Lodge controlled the bank through Gelli and Calvi.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1982-01-01</begin><end>1982-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>9.19,45.4642,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Blackfriars Bridge, London - Calvi Murder</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Roberto Calvi - &#x27;God&#x27;s Banker&#x27; - found hanging under Blackfriars Bridge, June 18, 1982. Pockets filled with bricks and cash. Initially ruled suicide, reclassified as murder (2002). Calvi was fleeing with evidence connecting Vatican Bank, P2 Lodge, Mafia, and CIA funding of Solidarity and the Contras through Ambrosiano.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1982-06-18</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-0.1036,51.5106,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Reggio Calabria, Italy - &#x27;Ndrangheta HQ</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>&#x27;Ndrangheta homeland. Estimated revenue €44-53 billion/year - 3% of Italian GDP. Controls 80% of European cocaine trade. Decentralized &#x27;ndrine (family clans) make it nearly impossible to dismantle. Global operations in 30+ countries.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>15.6501,38.1147,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Gioia Tauro, Italy - &#x27;Ndrangheta Port</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Calabrian port controlled by &#x27;Ndrangheta. Primary cocaine entry point for European distribution. Largest transshipment port in the Mediterranean used as a logistics hub for narcotics trafficking.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>15.8983,38.4262,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>San Luca, Italy - &#x27;Ndrangheta Origin</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Spiritual and organizational homeland of the &#x27;Ndrangheta. Annual pilgrimage to the Sanctuary of Our Lady of Polsi serves as the organization&#x27;s annual meeting for strategic decisions. Duisburg massacre (2007) - six &#x27;Ndrangheta members killed in Germany - originated from a San Luca clan feud.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2007-01-01</begin><end>2007-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>16.0719,38.1475,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Duisburg, Germany - &#x27;Ndrangheta Massacre</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>August 15, 2007: six men from San Luca &#x27;Ndrangheta clans shot dead outside Da Bruno restaurant. The massacre exposed &#x27;Ndrangheta&#x27;s deep presence in Germany and broader European operations. Led to increased European law enforcement focus on Calabrian organized crime.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2007-08-15</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>6.7623,51.4344,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rotterdam, Netherlands - Cocaine Port</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Europe&#x27;s largest port. Primary &#x27;Ndrangheta cocaine entry point for Northern Europe. Record seizures of 60+ tons annually, with authorities estimating they intercept only 10-20% of total flow.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>4.4777,51.9244,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Antwerp, Belgium - Cocaine Port</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Europe&#x27;s second-largest port. Massive cocaine transshipment hub, often exceeding Rotterdam in seizure volumes. &#x27;Ndrangheta and Albanian organized crime networks coordinate distribution through the port.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>4.4025,51.2194,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>HSBC HQ, London - Cartel Laundering</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>HSBC fined $1.9 billion (2012) for laundering $881 million for Sinaloa and Norte del Valle cartels. Bank processed $660 billion in wire transfers from Mexico. No criminal charges against any individual. The fine represented approximately five weeks of profit.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.0194,51.5047,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Luxembourg - BCCI</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>BCCI (Bank of Credit and Commerce International) - the most corrupt bank in history. $13 billion in fraud. CIA&#x27;s primary off-book banking channel. Laundered for Medellín Cartel, Noriega, Abu Nidal, and nuclear proliferation networks. Founded 1972, collapsed 1991.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1972-01-01</begin><end>1972-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>6.13,49.6117,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>São Paulo, Brazil - PCC-&#x27;Ndrangheta Nexus</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Primeiro Comando da Capital (PCC) alliance with &#x27;Ndrangheta - cocaine flows from Andean production through Brazilian ports to Calabrian distribution networks in Europe. São Paulo serves as the logistics and financial coordination hub.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-46.6333,-23.5505,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bologna, Italy - Strategy of Tension</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>August 2, 1980: Bologna train station bombing - 85 dead, 200+ wounded. Carried out by neo-fascist NAR with P2 Lodge and Gladio involvement. Vincenzo Vinciguerra (convicted Gladio operative) testified that NATO stay-behind networks organized false flag attacks to blame the left and justify authoritarian state responses.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1980-08-02</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>11.3426,44.4949,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Managua, Nicaragua - Dual-Funding</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Banco Ambrosiano funds flowed to both the Contras and Sandinista government - the same bank funded both sides. CIA cocaine flights from Ilopango supplied the Contras while Argentina trained them with Exocet missile profits from the Falklands War. Vatican Bank, P2, CIA, and Mafia financial streams converged here.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-86.2362,12.115,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Medellín, Colombia - CENTRA SPIKE / ISA</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>ISA (Intelligence Support Activity) operation CENTRA SPIKE tracked Pablo Escobar using signals intelligence. The same U.S. intelligence apparatus that facilitated drug trafficking through the Contra pipeline simultaneously hunted Escobar - the competitor to CIA-allied cartels.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-75.5658,6.2476,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nogales, Arizona-Sonora - Tunnel Corridor</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Major narco-tunnel corridor. 130+ tunnels discovered since 1990. Storm drain system exploited for smuggling. Sinaloa and CJNG cartels. The tunnels they find and the tunnels they don&#x27;t - border infrastructure as smuggling infrastructure.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1990-01-01</begin><end>1990-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-110.94,31.34,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>San Luis, Arizona - Tunnel Zone</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Cross-border tunnel terminus. December 2019: 4,309-ft tunnel - longest drug tunnel in U.S. history (at discovery). Rail system, ventilation, electricity, elevator entrance. The underground railroad that moves product, not people.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-12-01</begin><end>2019-12-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-114.7822,32.4869,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Narco-Submarines - Pacific Coast, Colombia</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Semi-submersible and fully submersible vessels built in jungle workshops. Carry 5-10 tonnes of cocaine per trip. Estimated 30% of Colombian cocaine now moves by submarine. The cartels reverse-engineered submarine technology in the jungle.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-78.76,2.44,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Toncontin Airport, Tegucigalpa, Honduras</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; airport</p><p>One of world&#x27;s most dangerous airports - mountain approach, short runway. Honduras: highest murder rate in the world post-2009 coup (U.S.-backed). Drug trafficking corridor. The dangerous airport in the dangerous country at the center of the narco-state pipeline.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2009-01-01</begin><end>2009-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-87.2173,14.0611,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mena Intermountain Airport, Arkansas</name><styleUrl>#t-airport</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; airport</p><p>Barry Seal&#x27;s base for CIA-linked cocaine flights from Central America. $3-5B in cocaine through a small-town airport. Governor at the time: Bill Clinton. DEA, CIA, and state politics intersecting on a rural Arkansas runway.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-94.2025,34.545,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Le Vele di Scampia - Camorra Drug Market, Naples</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>The sail-shaped &#x27;Vele&#x27; housing blocks in Scampia, built 1962–1975, became one of Europe&#x27;s largest open-air drug markets under the Camorra and the setting for Roberto Saviano&#x27;s 2006 book and the series &#x27;Gomorrah.&#x27; The 2004–2005 Scampia feud between the Di Lauro clan and breakaway &#x27;Scissionisti&#x27; killed dozens; authorities have estimated the Scampia–Secondigliano narcotics trade at around 100 million euros a year. Source: BBC News (bbc.co.uk), &#x27;Naples beefs up anti-mafia forces&#x27;; France 24 (france24.com), &#x27;After Gomorrah,&#x27; 2020.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1962-01-01</begin><end>1962-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>14.2397,40.8984,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sun Yee On Triad Ground - Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Sun Yee On, founded 1919 and traced to the earlier &#x27;Yee On&#x27; Chiu Chow trade association, is regarded as the largest triad society in the world, with estimates exceeding 55,000 members. Its influence has long been concentrated in the entertainment and nightlife districts of Tsim Sha Tsui in Kowloon, spanning extortion, loan-sharking, counterfeiting and narcotics. Source: Grey Dynamics (greydynamics.com), &#x27;Organised Crime: The Sun Yee On Triad&#x27;; Wikipedia, &#x27;Sun Yee On&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1919-01-01</begin><end>1919-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>114.1741,22.2989,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cali - Cali Cartel Stronghold, Colombia</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>The Cali Cartel, run 1975–1995 by brothers Gilberto and Miguel Rodríguez Orejuela with José Santacruz Londoño and Hélmer Herrera, was headquartered in Cali in the Valle del Cauca and at its peak controlled an estimated 80% of the U.S. cocaine market. It laundered profits through legitimate fronts such as the Drogas La Rebaja pharmacy chain before its leadership was dismantled in the mid-1990s. Source: InSight Crime (insightcrime.org), &#x27;Gilberto Rodríguez Orejuela, alias The Chess Player&#x27;; TIME (time.com), &#x27;The Cali Cartel: New Kings of Coke&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1975-01-01</begin><end>1975-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-76.5812,3.4108,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Guadalajara - CJNG Base of Operations, Mexico</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Guadalajara, capital of Jalisco, is the operational base of the Cartel Jalisco Nueva Generación (CJNG), founded in 2009 and one of Mexico&#x27;s most powerful and fastest-growing syndicates, known for trafficking fentanyl and methamphetamine to the United States. It was led by Nemesio &#x27;El Mencho&#x27; Oseguera Cervantes, who carried a 10-million-dollar U.S. bounty until Mexican forces killed him in Tapalpa, Jalisco, in February 2026. Source: InSight Crime (insightcrime.org), &#x27;Jalisco Cartel New Generation (CJNG)&#x27;; NPR (npr.org), &#x27;Mexican army kills leader of Jalisco New Generation Cartel,&#x27; 2026.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2026-02-01</begin><end>2026-02-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-103.3384,20.672,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Yamaguchi-gumi Headquarters - Kobe, Japan</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Fortress-like headquarters of the Yamaguchi-gumi, Japan&#x27;s largest yakuza syndicate, founded in Kobe in 1915; its address is publicly listed on the National Police Agency&#x27;s designated-crime-group registry. At the end of 2017 it counted roughly 4,700 full members and about 10,300 total, then roughly 30% of all yakuza in Japan, and it and top leaders were placed under U.S. Treasury OFAC sanctions in 2012. Source: U.S. Treasury OFAC; Japan National Police Agency; Asia Times (asiatimes.com), &#x27;Japan&#x27;s leading yakuza gangs in US Treasury&#x27;s cross-hairs,&#x27; 2018.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1915-01-01</begin><end>1915-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>135.2396,34.7124,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tocorón Prison (Tren de Aragua Cradle) - Aragua, Venezuela</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Tren de Aragua, Venezuela&#x27;s most powerful transnational gang, was founded inside Tocorón prison around 2014 by Héctor &#x27;Niño&#x27; Guerrero, who ran the compound as a fiefdom complete with a zoo, swimming pool, nightclub and restaurant. Venezuelan security forces retook the prison in September 2023, by which point the gang had projected criminal cells into at least three other South American countries; the U.S. later designated it a foreign terrorist organization. Source: InSight Crime (insightcrime.org), &#x27;Tren de Aragua Explained&#x27;; Encyclopaedia Britannica, &#x27;Tren de Aragua&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-09-01</begin><end>2023-09-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-67.5866,10.0923,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Corleone - Cradle of Cosa Nostra, Sicily</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Corleone is the historic stronghold of the Corleonesi, the most violent faction of the Sicilian Mafia, and birthplace of bosses Luciano Liggio, Salvatore &#x27;Totò&#x27; Riina (Cosa Nostra chief 1974–1993) and Bernardo Provenzano, who was arrested in a farmhouse just outside the town in 2006 after nearly 40 years as a fugitive. The Corleonesi seized control of Cosa Nostra through the 1981–1983 Second Mafia War, which left hundreds dead. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Corleonesi Mafia clan&#x27;; Fox News (foxnews.com), &#x27;Sicilian town had long bloody past before Godfather fame&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1974-01-01</begin><end>1974-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>14.155,37.5878,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Solntsevo - Solntsevskaya Bratva Base, Moscow</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>The Solntsevskaya Bratva, one of the world&#x27;s richest crime syndicates, took its name from the Solntsevo district of southwest Moscow where it coalesced in the late 1980s under Sergei Mikhailov and Viktor Averin. Its position near the MKAD ring road, the M3 highway and Vnukovo Airport let it dominate the post-Soviet car-import racket; a 2014 Fortune/Guinness estimate put its annual revenue at roughly 8.5 billion dollars. Source: Wikipedia, &#x27;Solntsevskaya Bratva&#x27;; Guinness World Records, &#x27;Largest criminal organization (profits)&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1980-01-01</begin><end>1980-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>37.4729,55.696,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>UWSA Headquarters, Pangkham - Golden Triangle, Myanmar</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Pangkham is the capital of the autonomous Wa State and headquarters of the roughly 30,000-strong United Wa State Army, which the U.S. State Department has called the world&#x27;s largest drug-trafficking army. From this Golden Triangle base the UWSA is tied to industrial-scale methamphetamine and heroin production, with casino revenue from Chinese visitors bolstering the group; leaders including Wei Hsueh-kang carry U.S. narcotics indictments and sanctions. Source: VOA News (voanews.com), &#x27;Myanmar&#x27;s largest rebel group quietly gains strength&#x27;; GIJN, &#x27;Guide to Investigating Organized Crime in the Golden Triangle&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>98.0098,21.5122,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Regency Hotel - Kinahan-Hutch Feud Attack, Dublin</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XVII</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>The February 2016 gun attack at the Regency Hotel (now the Bonnington), which killed Kinahan associate David Byrne during a boxing weigh-in, ignited the Kinahan-Hutch feud that left more than a dozen dead. The U.S. Treasury sanctioned the Kinahan Organised Crime Group in 2022 with a 5-million-dollar reward for its leaders; alleged boss Daniel Kinahan was extradited from the UAE to Dublin in August 2026. Source: BBC News (bbc.co.uk), &#x27;Kinahan crime gang: UAE freezes assets after US sanctions&#x27;; Al Jazeera (aljazeera.com), &#x27;UAE extradites alleged crime boss Daniel Kinahan,&#x27; 2026.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XVII">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2016-02-01</begin><end>2016-02-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-6.2454,53.3809,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section XX (36)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Microsoft Project Natick - off Orkney, Scotland</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Project Natick — Microsoft&#x27;s underwater data center, deployed on the seabed at the European Marine Energy Centre off Orkney, Scotland (2018), retrieved 2020. First proof-of-concept subsea DC; Microsoft concluded the program in 2024. Offshore point (approx). Source: Microsoft; Data Center Frontier.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2018-01-01</begin><end>2018-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-3.322,58.937,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Highlander Hainan Underwater Data Center, China</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>World&#x27;s first commercially scaled subsea data center cluster, off Lingshui/Sanya, Hainan, China (Highlander, 2023). ~1,433 tons of underwater hardware; capacity ~60,000 traditional computers. Backed by four Chinese authorities. Offshore point (approx). Source: DCD; E&amp;T; Data Center Frontier.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-01-01</begin><end>2023-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>110.03,18.3,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shanghai Offshore Underwater Data Center, China</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>World&#x27;s first offshore wind-powered underwater data center (announced 2025), ~24 MW, off the Shanghai coast — integrates green energy with subsea compute. Offshore point (approx). Source: Data Center Frontier (2025).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2025-01-01</begin><end>2025-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>122.2,30.9,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nautilus Data Technologies (floating) - Stockton, CA</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Barge-mounted floating data center at the Port of Stockton, California — river-water cooled. Investors include Keppel Data Centres (Singapore). Source: Data Center Knowledge; Nautilus.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.3266,37.951,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Keppel Floating Data Center Park - Singapore</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Keppel&#x27;s nearshore floating data center park concept, Singapore — offshore siting to bypass land/power constraints. Offshore point (approx). Source: Keppel; industry reports.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>103.85,1.2644,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NSA Utah Data Center - Bluffdale, UT</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Intelligence Community Comprehensive National Cybersecurity Initiative Data Center — the NSA&#x27;s mass-data storage/processing facility at Camp Williams, Bluffdale, Utah (~1M+ sq ft, online 2014). Central to the post-Snowden bulk-surveillance debate. Source: public reporting.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2014-01-01</begin><end>2014-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-111.9358,40.4278,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ashburn &#x27;Data Center Alley&#x27; - Loudoun County, VA</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Ashburn/Loudoun County, Virginia — the world&#x27;s densest data-center cluster (&#x27;Data Center Alley&#x27;); a large share of global internet traffic transits here. Northern Virginia + Greater Beijing ≈ 20% of world hyperscale capacity. Source: Synergy Research; Data Center Frontier.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.4744,39.0298,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Switch Citadel Campus - Tahoe Reno, NV</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Switch &#x27;Citadel&#x27; campus, Tahoe Reno Industrial Center, Storey County, NV — largest operational data center by floor area (~7.2M sq ft, 650 MW). Source: Data Center Frontier.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-119.4903,39.556,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Stargate AI Campus - Abilene, TX</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>&#x27;Stargate&#x27; (OpenAI / Oracle / Microsoft-linked) AI supercomputer campus, Abilene, Texas — targeting ~1.2 GW at Phase 1, set to exceed Switch Citadel. Source: Data Center Frontier (2025).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-99.7476,32.4465,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Google Data Center - The Dalles, OR</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Google&#x27;s flagship Columbia River data center, The Dalles, Oregon (since 2006) — hydro-powered. Source: Google; Synergy Research.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2006-01-01</begin><end>2006-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-121.1842,45.6015,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Meta Data Center - Prineville, OR</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Meta (Facebook) Prineville, Oregon campus — one of its first owned hyperscale data centers; Apple also operates in Prineville. Source: Meta; industry reports.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-120.8464,44.3035,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Google Data Center - Council Bluffs, IA</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Google Council Bluffs, Iowa — among Google&#x27;s largest U.S. campuses. Iowa is a top-5 global hyperscale market. Source: Synergy Research.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-95.8519,41.2588,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Meta Data Center - Luleå, Sweden</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Meta&#x27;s Luleå, Sweden data center near the Arctic Circle — free-air cooling, hydro power. Europe&#x27;s flagship hyperscale node. Source: Meta.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>22.146,65.5831,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Google Data Center - Hamina, Finland</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Google Hamina, Finland — built in a former paper mill; seawater-cooled from the Gulf of Finland. Source: Google.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>27.1926,60.5683,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ulanqab / Hohhot Hyperscale Corridor, Inner Mongolia</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Ulanqab–Hohhot corridor, Inner Mongolia — the single largest concentration of hyperscale capacity on Earth (&gt;3,000 MW: China Mobile, Alibaba, ByteDance, Baidu, Tencent, China Telecom) under Beijing&#x27;s &#x27;East Data, West Computing&#x27; plan. Source: Data Center Frontier; Synergy Research.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>113.1316,40.9903,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lefdal Mine Datacenter - Nordfjord, Norway</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Data center inside the former Lefdal olivine mine, Nordfjord, Norway — fjord-water cooled, hydro-powered, deep underground. Source: Lefdal Mine; industry reports. Pin approximate.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>5.77,61.79,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>xAI Colossus - Memphis, TN</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>xAI &#x27;Colossus&#x27; AI supercomputer, south Memphis, Tennessee. Expanded to ~2 GW / 555,000 NVIDIA GPUs (Jan 2026) — reported as the largest single AI training site. Drew scrutiny over gas-turbine emissions in the Boxtown neighborhood. Pin at city level. Source: Introl; Sherwood; Epoch AI (2026).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2026-01-01</begin><end>2026-01-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-90.0518,35.146,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Meta Hyperion AI Campus - Richland Parish, LA</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Meta &#x27;Hyperion&#x27; — a city-sized AI data center in Richland Parish, Louisiana; Zuckerberg says it will scale to ~5 GW over several years. Source: Meta; Data Center Frontier (2025-26).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-91.8106,32.4197,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Meta Prometheus AI Campus - New Albany, OH</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Meta &#x27;Prometheus&#x27; AI campus, New Albany, Ohio — GW-scale, ~562 MW IT power projected. Source: Epoch AI; Data Center Frontier (2026).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-82.8088,40.0812,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Amazon / Anthropic AI Campus - New Carlisle, IN</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Amazon Web Services campus at New Carlisle, Indiana (Project Rainier) — ~1+ GW, built to train Anthropic&#x27;s models. Source: Epoch AI; AWS (2026).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-86.5098,41.7057,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Microsoft Fairwater AI DC - Lithia Springs, GA</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Microsoft &#x27;Fairwater&#x27; AI data center, Atlanta area (Lithia Springs), Georgia — ~636 MW. Source: Epoch AI; Microsoft (2025-26).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-84.6506,33.7798,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Microsoft Data Center - Boydton, VA</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Microsoft hyperscale cloud campus, Boydton, Virginia — a town of ~400 people hosting one of Azure&#x27;s largest East-Coast footprints. Source: Data Center Frontier.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-78.3882,36.6673,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Microsoft Data Center - Quincy, WA</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Microsoft Columbia Basin campus, Quincy, Washington — cool climate + cheap hydro; one of the original hyperscale clusters (also Yahoo, Sabey, Dell). Source: Data Center Frontier.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-119.8535,47.2344,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Apple / Google Data Centers - Maiden / Catawba, NC</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Apple&#x27;s first purpose-built data center (iCloud), Maiden, NC (2012, ~500,000 sq ft), alongside a major Google campus — one of the densest hyperscale clusters on the U.S. East Coast. Source: Data Center Frontier.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-81.2139,35.5766,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pionen &#x27;White Mountains&#x27; Bunker DC - Stockholm</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Bahnhof&#x27;s &#x27;Pionen&#x27; data center inside a Cold War nuclear bunker under Vita Bergen park, Södermalm, Stockholm — 30m below granite; once hosted WikiLeaks servers. Source: Bahnhof; public reporting.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>18.087,59.3133,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Alibaba Zhangbei Cloud Campus - Hebei, China</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Alibaba Cloud&#x27;s Zhangbei (Cloud Valley) hyperscale campus, Hebei, China — cold-climate northern-China node serving Beijing. Source: Alibaba; industry reports.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>114.7693,41.2878,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Gui&#x27;an Big Data Valley - Guizhou, China</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Gui&#x27;an New Area, Guizhou — China&#x27;s flagship &#x27;big data valley&#x27;: Apple&#x27;s China iCloud (via GCBD), Tencent, Huawei, and China Telecom operate mountain/cave-cooled data centers here. Apple&#x27;s China user data is stored on GCBD-operated servers. Source: public reporting.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>106.4831,26.4688,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>GDS Hyperscale Campus - Langfang, Hebei, China</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>GDS Holdings hyperscale data-center campus, Langfang, Hebei — a core node in the Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei cloud cluster. Source: GDS filings; industry reports.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>116.6926,39.5302,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Green Mountain DC1 - Rennesøy (Stavanger), Norway</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Green Mountain DC1-Stavanger — a Tier III data center built inside a former high-security NATO ammunition store dug into a mountain on Rennesøy, Norway; fjord-water cooled, hydro-powered, ~22,600 m². Source: Green Mountain; Data Centre Magazine.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>5.6492,59.1148,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Iron Mountain WPA-1 - Boyers, PA</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Iron Mountain&#x27;s underground data center in a former limestone mine ~220 ft below Boyers, Pennsylvania — also stores U.S. federal records (OPM retirement archive) and film masters. Source: Iron Mountain; Data Center Knowledge.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-79.8989,41.1084,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Swiss Fort Knox - Saanen, Switzerland</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Swiss Fort Knox — a high-security data center inside a former military bunker in the Swiss Alps near Saanen; blast doors, groundwater cooling, redundant hidden entrances. Source: Data Centre Magazine; industry reports.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>7.2616,46.4898,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Google AI Campus - West Memphis, AR</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Alphabet/Google broke ground on a data-center campus in West Memphis, Arkansas — directly across the Mississippi from xAI&#x27;s Colossus in Memphis. Two rival AI megacampuses facing each other across the river. Source: Data Center Frontier (2025).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-90.1845,35.1465,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>G42 / Stargate UAE - Masdar City, Abu Dhabi</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>G42-anchored &#x27;Stargate UAE&#x27; AI compute cluster near Masdar City, Abu Dhabi — a sovereign-scale AI data center (OpenAI/Oracle/Nvidia-linked), part of a planned 5 GW campus. Source: Data Center Frontier; company announcements (2025).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>54.6235,24.4275,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Google Data Center - St. Ghislain, Belgium</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Google&#x27;s St. Ghislain, Belgium data center — one of its largest European sites; among the first to run without chillers (free-air/water cooling). Source: Google.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>3.8195,50.4477,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Meta Data Center - Clonee, Ireland</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Meta&#x27;s Clonee, County Meath, Ireland campus — a flagship European hyperscale site; part of Ireland&#x27;s dense data-center cluster around Dublin. Source: Meta.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-6.4404,53.4104,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Subsea Cloud pods - Port Angeles, WA</name><styleUrl>#t-datacenter</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XX</b> &middot; datacenter</p><p>Subsea Cloud — commercial subsea data-center pods (&#x27;Jules Verne&#x27; etc.) designed for seabed deployment; U.S. Pacific Northwest / Gulf of Mexico siting. Offshore point (approx). Source: Subsea Cloud; Data Center Frontier.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XX">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-123.4307,48.1181,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Section XXIV (4)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Mount Waterman, Angeles National Forest, CA - Reza LKP</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XXIV</b> &middot; military</p><p>Monica Jacinto Reza - Mondaloy alloy co-inventor (US Patent 2010/0266442 A1), Columbia PhD, UCLA postdoc, Aerojet Rocketdyne Technical Fellow, then JPL. Last known position June 22 2025. FLIR-negative (no thermal signature). Scent trail terminated. Find a Grave memorial created 4 days later - &#x27;green burial&#x27; designation while SAR still active.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XXIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2025-06-22</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-117.9628,34.3496,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sandia Mountains, Albuquerque, NM - McCasland Disappearance</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XXIV</b> &middot; military</p><p>Maj. Gen. William Neil McCasland - AFRL Commander 2011-2013, oversaw $4.4B R&amp;D portfolio that funded Reza&#x27;s Mondaloy work. Vanished hiking February 27 2026. Left all electronics behind. Named in DeLonge-Podesta email (Wikileaks ID 2125) re: UFO/UAP phenomenon. Second vertex of the Mondaloy triangle to disappear.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XXIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2026-02-27</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-106.451,35.2107,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Wright-Patterson AFB, Dayton, OH - AFRL HQ</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XXIV</b> &middot; military</p><p>Air Force Research Laboratory headquarters. Dallis Hardwick - first Mondaloy co-inventor - served at AFRL Materials and Manufacturing Directorate. Died 2014 (cancer). First vertex of the Mondaloy chain of custody to be eliminated. Every person in the alloy&#x27;s chain - Hardwick, Reza, McCasland - dead or missing by 2026.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XXIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2014-01-01</begin><end>2014-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-84.0483,39.8261,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>JPL / La Cañada Flintridge, CA - Reza&#x27;s Employer</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Section XXIV</b> &middot; military</p><p>Jet Propulsion Laboratory - Reza&#x27;s employer at time of disappearance. JPL issued no public statement. NASA headquarters silent. Aerojet Rocketdyne (former employer) silent. AIAA silent. SpaceNews silent. The institutional perimeter holds.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XXIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-118.1714,34.2014,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Animal research (36)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Marshall BioResources - North Rose, NY (HQ)</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Marshall BioResources / Marshall Farms — 5800 Lake Bluff Road, Town of Huron, Wayne County, NY. Global breeder of purpose-bred research animals: the &#x27;Marshall Beagle&#x27; line since 1962, plus ferrets, cats and Göttingen minipigs. Reported ~66,000 animals incl. 20,000+ beagles. Advocates cite 20+ Animal Welfare Act citations over the years; 3-day protest May 2026 (Beagle Lovers &amp; Rescuers; Against All Oddz). Company states its May 2026 unannounced USDA inspection returned no citations. FOLLOW THE MONEY: privately held / family-owned (Marshall Farms Group Ltd, founded 1939) — no public shareholders; revenue is customer sales (pharma/CRO) plus U.S. federal contracts. Direct federal awards total 2.36M across 193 transactions (USAspending, all years): DoD 1.84M, HHS/NIH 415K, VA 77K, USDA 23K — the DoD military-medical share is the largest. The far bigger flow is indirect: NIH grant money funds the university/pharma research that then buys Marshall animals. Sources: 13WHAM; Wikipedia; USAspending.gov (UEI DVGAR51JKM99).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2026-05-01</begin><end>2026-05-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-76.9049,43.2139,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Marshall BioResources - MBR Acres, Wyton, UK</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>MBR Acres, Wyton, Cambridgeshire, England. Marshall beagle-breeding facility supplying UK research labs; up to ~2,000 beagles bred per year. Long-running site of the &#x27;Camp Beagle&#x27; protest. Part of Marshall&#x27;s global network.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.1366,52.3618,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Marshall BioResources - Gannat, France</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Marshall BioResources facility at Gannat, Allier, France (acquired 2017). Part of Marshall&#x27;s European breeding network.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-01-01</begin><end>2017-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>3.1995,46.0996,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Marshall BioResources - Mézilles, France</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Centre d&#x27;Élevage du Domaine des Souches, Mézilles, Yonne, France — acquired by Marshall BioResources. Breeds beagles and golden retrievers for laboratories. Part of Marshall&#x27;s European breeding network.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>3.172,47.7009,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Charles River Laboratories - HQ, Wilmington, MA</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Charles River Laboratories — 251 Ballardvale St, Wilmington, MA. Global contract research organization and breeder of research models incl. beagles. A 2014 CBS News investigation documented dog use at its Massachusetts labs. FOLLOW THE MONEY: publicly traded (NYSE: CRL). Disclosed largest holders are the big asset managers — Vanguard (7.38%), BlackRock, State Street, Fidelity/FMR, Wellington — much of it passive index ownership. Source: Wikipedia; CBS News (2014); SEC 13G/13F.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2014-01-01</begin><end>2014-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.1579,42.5955,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Charles River - Stone Ridge, NY (breeding, approx.)</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Charles River breeding facility, Stone Ridge (Town of Marbletown), Ulster County, NY (RR 209). Long-documented dog/beagle breeding site. Pin at town level — exact parcel pending. Source: SourceWatch.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-74.1544,41.8448,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Inotiv - HQ, West Lafayette, IN</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Inotiv, Inc. (formerly BASi) — 2701 Kent Ave, West Lafayette, IN. Parent company of Envigo RMS. Source: Inotiv (Wikipedia).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-86.9297,40.4588,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Envigo / Inotiv - Cumberland, VA (approx.)</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Envigo RMS beagle-breeding facility, Cumberland County, VA. ~4,000 beagles relinquished to the Humane Society (2022). Inotiv pleaded guilty to Animal Welfare Act violations and agreed to pay 35M+ — the largest AWA penalty in U.S. history (2024). FOLLOW THE MONEY: Inotiv (Nasdaq: NOTV) filed prepackaged Chapter 11 on June 3, 2026 with a 65.5M debtor-in-possession loan, cutting funded debt from ~488.7M to ~163.3M; existing shareholders wiped out. WHO ENDS UP OWNING IT: under the restructuring support agreement (June 2, 2026; U.S. Bankruptcy Court, S.D. Texas), the prepetition FIRST-LIEN LENDERS take ~93% of the reorganized company&#x27;s new equity; the Ad Hoc Group of Noteholders (holders of the 15% second-lien PIK notes due 2027 and 3.25% convertible notes due 2027) provide the $65.4M DIP and receive minority equity + warrants. The filings name creditor classes, not individual funds (counsel: Davis Polk; claims agent: Kroll) — the fund identities live in the RSA exhibit / court docket. Pin at county level — exact parcel pending. Sources: U.S. DOJ; SEC 8-K &amp; RSA; Davis Polk; Kroll (2026).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2026-06-03</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-78.2469,37.5004,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>The Jackson Laboratory (JAX) - Bar Harbor, ME</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>The Jackson Laboratory — 600 Main St, Bar Harbor, Maine. Nonprofit; the world&#x27;s largest supplier of laboratory mice (11,000+ genetic strains, &#x27;JAX Mice&#x27;). Additional sites: Sacramento CA, Farmington CT, and Shanghai, China. Source: JAX; MarketsandMarkets.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-68.1963,44.3653,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Taconic Biosciences - HQ, Rensselaer, NY</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Taconic Biosciences HQ, 1 Discovery Drive, Rensselaer, NY 12144 (Albany Health Sciences Campus). Major rodent-model breeder: 3 service labs + 6 breeding facilities across the U.S. and Europe (incl. Germany, Denmark); primary U.S. breeding operations ~45 mi south in Germantown, NY. Source: Taconic; Discover Rensselaer.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.7342,42.627,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Janvier Labs - Le Genest-Saint-Isle, France</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Janvier Labs — Le Genest-Saint-Isle, Mayenne, France. Leading European breeder of research rodents (mice/rats). Source: industry market reports.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.8869,48.099,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>GemPharmatech - Nanjing, China</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>GemPharmatech — Nanjing, Jiangsu, China. Large-scale Chinese mouse-model breeder (knockout/humanized strains); expanded to San Diego, CA (2025). Source: GemPharmatech; market reports.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2025-01-01</begin><end>2025-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>118.7789,32.0438,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Charles River - Vital River, Beijing, China</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Beijing Vital River Laboratory Animal Technology — Charles River&#x27;s China joint venture / rodent-breeding arm. Part of CRL&#x27;s Asia-Pacific production network. Source: Charles River; market reports.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>116.3913,39.9057,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Charles River - Hylasco Bio-Technology, Hyderabad, India</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Hylasco Bio-Technology, Hyderabad — Charles River&#x27;s India rodent-breeding subsidiary. Source: Charles River.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>78.4741,17.3606,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Charles River - Kuopio, Finland</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Charles River facility, Kuopio, Finland (imaging-equipped preclinical site, 2025). CRL European production/discovery network. Source: Charles River (2025).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2025-01-01</begin><end>2025-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>27.6784,62.8925,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vanny Bio-Research - Pursat Province, Cambodia (approx.)</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Vanny Bio-Research macaque farm, Pursat Province, Cambodia. Center of the U.S. DOJ/USFWS long-tailed-macaque smuggling case (2022–2023): wild-caught, internationally protected macaques laundered with false &#x27;captive-bred&#x27; labels. Cambodian wildlife officials indicted; CITES recommended a global ban on Cambodian macaque trade. Pin at province level. Sources: U.S. DOJ; Pulitzer Center; Bloomberg (2024).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-01-01</begin><end>2022-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>103.9197,12.542,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Noveprim - Mauritius (Charles River 90%)</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Noveprim Ltd, Mauritius — nonhuman-primate (long-tailed macaque) supplier. Charles River acquired a 90% controlling interest (Nov 2023). Undercover footage alleged wild capture of macaques before export. Source: PETA; Species Unite; CRL filings (2023).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-11-01</begin><end>2023-11-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>57.7061,-20.4111,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bioculture - Rivière des Anguilles, Mauritius</name><styleUrl>#t-animal-research</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; animal-research</p><p>Bioculture (Mauritius) — long-tailed macaque breeder/exporter to U.S./European research. Part of the Mauritius primate-export node in the global lab-monkey supply chain. Source: Bloomberg &#x27;Monkey Laundering&#x27; (2024).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>57.5556,-20.4621,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Vanguard Group - Malvern, PA</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>The Vanguard Group, Malvern, PA. Disclosed largest shareholder of Charles River Laboratories: 7.38% (~3.63M shares) as of 03/31/2026 (SEC Schedule 13G). Predominantly passive index funds. Source: SEC 13G; Fintel.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-75.5069,40.0521,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>BlackRock - 50 Hudson Yards, NYC</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>BlackRock, Inc., New York. Among the top institutional holders of Charles River Laboratories (index + active funds). World&#x27;s largest asset manager. Source: SEC 13G/13F; Fintel.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-74.0001,40.7545,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>State Street - 1 Congress St, Boston</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>State Street Corp, Boston. Top-tier institutional holder of Charles River Laboratories (the third of the &#x27;Big Three&#x27; index managers). Source: Fintel/13F.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-71.058,42.3604,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>FMR / Fidelity - 245 Summer St, Boston</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>FMR LLC (Fidelity), Boston. Disclosed institutional holder of Charles River Laboratories. Source: Fintel/13F.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-71.0537,42.3513,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Wellington Management - Boston</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>Wellington Management Group, Boston. Active institutional holder of Charles River Laboratories. Source: Fintel/13F.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-71.0572,42.3545,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>U.S. Dept of Defense / DHA - Falls Church, VA</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>U.S. Department of Defense — Marshall BioResources&#x27; largest federal buyer: ~1.84M in direct awards (USAspending, all years), largely DoD military-medical research (e.g. USUHS). Node at Defense Health Agency HQ. Source: USAspending.gov.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.2103,38.8676,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NIH / HHS - Bethesda, MD</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>National Institutes of Health / Dept of Health &amp; Human Services, Bethesda, MD. ~415K in direct federal awards to Marshall; far larger indirect role as the primary public funder of the university/pharma animal research that buys from these breeders. Source: USAspending.gov; NIH RePORTER.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.104,39.0,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Blackstone HQ, 345 Park Avenue, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>Blackstone is the world&#x27;s largest alternative-asset manager, with about US$1.27 trillion under management in private equity, real estate and credit, and is one of the largest corporate landlords and commercial-property owners globally. It occupies most of 345 Park Avenue. Source: Wikipedia, Blackstone Inc.; SEC Form 10-K FY2025.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.9725,40.7577,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Berkshire Hathaway HQ, Omaha</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>From a modest office at Kiewit Plaza in Omaha, Warren Buffett built Berkshire Hathaway into a conglomerate with over US$1 trillion market capitalization (2024), wholly owning firms like GEICO and BNSF Railway and holding vast equity stakes including Apple and American Express. Source: Wikipedia, Berkshire Hathaway; Berkshire Hathaway (berkshirehathaway.com).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2024-01-01</begin><end>2024-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-95.9659,41.2575,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Renaissance Technologies, East Setauket, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>Founded by mathematician Jim Simons, Renaissance runs the legendary Medallion Fund, which generated roughly 66% annualized returns before fees from 1988-2021 and over US$100 billion in trading profits — widely regarded as the most successful quantitative fund in history. It operates from a campus on Long Island. Source: Institutional Investor; Wikipedia, Renaissance Technologies.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1988-01-01</begin><end>1988-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.1106,40.9307,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Norges Bank Investment Management (GPFG), Oslo</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>NBIM manages Norway&#x27;s Government Pension Fund Global — the world&#x27;s largest sovereign wealth fund, exceeding US$2 trillion in assets as of 2026 and owning roughly 1.4% of all listed shares worldwide across nearly 9,000 companies. Its holdings equal about 1.5% of the value of the world&#x27;s listed firms. Source: Norges Bank Investment Management (nbim.no); CNBC (2025).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>10.7424,59.9086,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Abu Dhabi Investment Authority (ADIA), Abu Dhabi</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>Founded in 1976 to invest Abu Dhabi&#x27;s oil surpluses, ADIA manages an estimated US$1.1 trillion across public equities, fixed income, private equity, real estate and infrastructure in over 50 countries from its landmark Corniche tower. It is among the largest and most secretive sovereign wealth funds. Source: Wikipedia, Abu Dhabi Investment Authority; ADIA (adia.ae).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1976-01-01</begin><end>1976-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>54.3516,24.4898,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Public Investment Fund (PIF), Riyadh</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>Saudi Arabia&#x27;s PIF, chaired by Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman, holds over US$930 billion and is the primary vehicle of Vision 2030, funding NEOM, LIV Golf, and stakes in firms worldwide. It targets US$2 trillion in assets by 2030. Source: Wikipedia, Public Investment Fund; PIF (pif.gov.sa).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>46.6407,24.7657,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Government Pension Investment Fund (GPIF), Tokyo</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>Japan&#x27;s GPIF is the world&#x27;s largest public pension fund, managing about 293.6 trillion yen (roughly US$1.9 trillion) as of March 2026 for the national pension system. Its portfolio is split roughly evenly among domestic and foreign bonds and equities. Source: Private Equity International / PERE institution profile; GPIF (gpif.go.jp).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7515,35.658,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>China Investment Corporation (CIC), Beijing</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>Established in 2007 with US$200 billion to diversify China&#x27;s foreign-exchange reserves, CIC managed roughly US$1.57 trillion by 2026 from New Poly Plaza. It invests globally in equities, private equity and infrastructure and is a key vehicle of Chinese overseas capital. Source: Wikipedia, China Investment Corporation; china-inv.cn.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2007-01-01</begin><end>2007-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>116.41,39.9269,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bridgewater Associates, Westport, Connecticut</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>Founded by Ray Dalio in 1975, Bridgewater is the world&#x27;s largest hedge fund, managing roughly US$90-124 billion at its wooded Nyala Farms campus. Its &#x27;Pure Alpha&#x27; macro strategy and &#x27;radical transparency&#x27; culture made it one of the most influential and studied investment firms. Source: Wikipedia, Bridgewater Associates.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1975-01-01</begin><end>1975-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.3301,41.1257,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Temasek Holdings, Singapore</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>Temasek is a Singapore state-owned investment company with a net portfolio around US$521 billion (2026), holding controlling or major stakes in Singapore Airlines, DBS Bank, Singtel and global firms. Unlike a reserve fund, it operates as an active commercial investor. Source: Wikipedia, Temasek Holdings; Temasek (temasek.com.sg).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2026-01-01</begin><end>2026-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>103.8456,1.3,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>GIC Private Limited, Capital Tower, Singapore</name><styleUrl>#t-capital</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Animal research</b> &middot; capital</p><p>GIC manages Singapore&#x27;s foreign reserves — estimated at over US$770 billion — across more than 40 countries, and is one of the world&#x27;s largest and most active sovereign investors in real estate and private markets. It was established in 1981 and is famously secretive about its exact size. Source: Wikipedia, GIC (sovereign wealth fund); GIC (gic.com.sg).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#XIV">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1981-01-01</begin><end>1981-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>103.8476,1.2776,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Mass shootings (161)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Welding shop shooting - Miami, Florida</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>8/20/1982. Venue type: other. Killed: 8. Injured: 3. Total victims: 11. Junior high school teacher Carl Robert Brown, 51, opened fire inside a welding shop and was later shot dead by a witness as he fled the scene. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.nytimes.com/1982/08/21/us/gunman-in-miami-kills-8-in-rampage.html; http://www.nytimes.com/1982/08/24/us/no-ch....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1982-08-20</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-80.22668,25.79649,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Dallas nightclub shooting - Dallas, Texas</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>6/29/1984. Venue type: other. Killed: 6. Injured: 1. Total victims: 7. Abdelkrim Belachheb, 39, opened fire at an upscale nightclub after a woman rejected his advances. He was later arrested. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://books.google.com/books?id=Hr3OBwP-lbUC&amp;pg=PA38&amp;lpg=PA38&amp;dq=Abdelkrim+Belachheb+mental&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=D56pgdNnnl&amp;si....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1984-06-29</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-96.83868,32.92517,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>San Ysidro McDonald&#x27;s massacre - San Ysidro, California</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>7/18/1984. Venue type: other. Killed: 22. Injured: 19. Total victims: 41. James Oliver Huberty, 41, opened fire in a McDonald&#x27;s restaurant before he was shot dead by a police officer. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.utsandiego.com/san-ysidro-massacre/; http://www.vpc.org/studies/wgun840718.htm.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1984-07-18</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-117.04308,32.552,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>United States Postal Service shooting - Edmond, Oklahoma</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>8/20/1986. Venue type: workplace. Killed: 15. Injured: 6. Total victims: 21. Postal worker Patrick Sherrill, 44, opened fire at a post office before committing suicide. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://news.google.com/newspapers?id=dm8aAAAAIBAJ&amp;sjid=pyoEAAAAIBAJ&amp;pg=2297,4870051&amp;dq=patrick+sherrill&amp;hl=en.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1986-08-20</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-97.42937,35.6672,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shopping centers spree killings - Palm Bay, Florida</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>4/23/1987. Venue type: other. Killed: 6. Injured: 14. Total victims: 20. Retired librarian William Cruse, 59, was paranoid neighbors gossiped that he was gay. He drove to a Publix supermarket, killing two Florida Tech students en route before opening fire outside and killing a woman. He then drove to a Winn-Dixie supermarket and killed three more, including two police officers. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://articles.latimes.com/1987-04-25/news/mn-990_1_palm-bay-police.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1987-04-23</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-80.64297,28.03319,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>ESL shooting - Sunnyvale, California</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>2/16/1988. Venue type: workplace. Killed: 7. Injured: 4. Total victims: 11. Former ESL Incorporated employee Richard Farley, 39, gunned down seven people at his former workplace, after stalking and harassing a coworker he was romantically interested in. He was later arrested and now sits on death row at San Quentin. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://articles.latimes.com/1988-02-18/news/mn-43514_1_mr-farley-richard-farley-sunnyvale-public-safety-department; http....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1988-02-16</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-122.03635,37.36883,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Stockton schoolyard shooting - Stockton, California</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>1/17/1989. Venue type: school. Killed: 6. Injured: 29. Total victims: 35. Patrick Purdy, 26, an alcoholic with a police record, launched an assault at Cleveland Elementary School, where many young Southeast Asian immigrants were enrolled. Purdy killed himself with a shot to the head. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.recordnet.com/apps/pbcs.dll/article?AID=/20090118/A_NEWS/901170304; http://news.google.com/newspapers?id=N8Iz....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1989-01-17</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-121.29078,37.9577,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Standard Gravure shooting - Louisville, Kentucky</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>9/14/1989. Venue type: workplace. Killed: 9. Injured: 12. Total victims: 21. Joseph T. Wesbecker, 47, gunned down eight people at his former workplace before committing suicide. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://nl.newsbank.com/nl-search/we/Archives?p_product=LH&amp;s_site=kentucky&amp;p_multi=LH&amp;p_theme=realcities&amp;p_action=search&amp;....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1989-09-14</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-85.75941,38.25424,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>GMAC massacre - Jacksonville, Florida</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>6/18/1990. Venue type: other. Killed: 10. Injured: 4. Total victims: 14. James Edward Pough, 42, opened fire at a General Motors Acceptance Corporation office before committing suicide. (The day prior, Pough killed a pimp and prostitute and injured two others. Those victims are not included in the mass murder count.) Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.nytimes.com/1990/06/19/us/florida-gunman-kills-8-and-wounds-6-in-office.html; http://www.nytimes.com/1990/06/....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1990-06-18</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-81.65565,30.33218,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Luby&#x27;s massacre - Killeen, Texas</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>10/16/1991. Venue type: other. Killed: 24. Injured: 20. Total victims: 44. George Hennard, 35, drove his pickup truck into a Luby&#x27;s cafeteria and opened fire before committing suicide. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.nytimes.com/1991/10/18/us/portrait-of-texas-killer-impatient-and-troubled.html?pagewanted=all&amp;src=pm; http://....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1991-10-16</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-97.7278,31.11712,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>University of Iowa shooting - Iowa City, Iowa</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>11/1/1991. Venue type: school. Killed: 6. Injured: 1. Total victims: 7. Former graduate student Gang Lu, 28, went on a rampage on campus and then committed suicide at the scene. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.nytimes.com/1991/11/03/us/gunman-in-iowa-wrote-of-plans-in-five-letters.html?pagewanted=all&amp;src=pm; http://th....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1991-11-01</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-91.53022,41.66069,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Royal Oak postal shootings - Royal Oak, Michigan</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>11/14/1991. Venue type: workplace. Killed: 5. Injured: 5. Total victims: 10. Laid-off postal worker Thomas McIlvane, 31, opened fire at his former workplace before committing suicide. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.nytimes.com/1991/11/15/us/ex-postal-worker-kills-3-and-wounds-6-in-michigan.html; http://www.mlive.com/news/d....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1991-11-14</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-83.14465,42.48948,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lindhurst High School shooting - Olivehurst, California</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>5/1/1992. Venue type: school. Killed: 4. Injured: 10. Total victims: 14. Former Lindhurst High School student Eric Houston, 20, angry about various personal failings, killed three students and a teacher at the school before surrendering to police after an eight-hour standoff. He was later sentenced to death. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.schoolshooters.info/PL/Subject-Houston_files/Nine%20Brief%20Sketches.pdf; http://www.appeal-democrat.com/news....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1992-05-01</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-121.54758,39.07869,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Watkins Glen killings - Watkins Glen, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>10/15/1992. Venue type: other. Killed: 5. Injured: 0. Total victims: 5. John T. Miller, 50, killed four child-support workers in a county office building before turning the gun on himself. Miller was upset about a court order garnishing his paycheck to cover overdue child-support payments. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.nytimes.com/1992/10/17/nyregion/shooting-followed-tougher-efforts-to-collect-child-support.html?pagewanted=2&amp;....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1992-10-15</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-76.87058,42.38106,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>101 California Street shootings - San Francisco, California</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>7/1/1993. Venue type: other. Killed: 9. Injured: 6. Total victims: 15. Failed businessman Gian Luigi Ferri, 55, opened fire throughout an office building before he committed suicide inside as police pursued him. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://articles.latimes.com/1993-07-03/news/mn-10731_1_mortgage-business/2; http://www.motherjones.com/print/16316; http....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1993-07-01</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-122.39797,37.79297,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Luigi&#x27;s shooting - Fayetteville, North Carolina</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>8/6/1993. Venue type: other. Killed: 4. Injured: 8. Total victims: 12. Army Sgt. Kenneth Junior French, 22, opened fire inside Luigi&#x27;s Italian restaurant while ranting about gays in the military before he was shot and arrested by police. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://articles.latimes.com/1993-08-08/news/mn-21847_1_kills-army-french; http://news.google.com/newspapers?id=0AhPAAAAI....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1993-08-06</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-78.87871,35.05299,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Long Island Rail Road massacre - Garden City, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>12/7/1993. Venue type: other. Killed: 6. Injured: 19. Total victims: 25. Colin Ferguson, 35, opened fire on an eastbound Long Island Rail Road train as it approached a Garden City station. He was later arrested. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.nytimes.com/1993/12/12/nyregion/tormented-life-special-report-long-slide-privilege-ends-slaughter-train.html;....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1993-12-07</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-73.6343,40.72677,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chuck E. Cheese&#x27;s killings - Aurora, Colorado</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>12/14/1993. Venue type: workplace. Killed: 4. Injured: 1. Total victims: 5. Nathan Dunlap, 19, a recently fired Chuck E. Cheese&#x27;s employee, went on a rampage through his former workplace and was arrested the following day. He now awaits execution on death row. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.denverpost.com/news/ci_20218952/aurora-chuck-e-cheese-killers-appeal-cites-mental; http://abcnews.go.com/US/a....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1993-12-14</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-104.84485,39.6756,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Air Force base shooting - Fairchild Air Force Base, Washington</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>6/20/1994. Venue type: military. Killed: 5. Injured: 23. Total victims: 28. Former airman Dean Allen Mellberg, 20, opened fire inside a hospital at the Fairchild Air Force Base before he was shot dead by a military police officer outside. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://articles.latimes.com/1994-06-22/news/mn-7137_1_air-force; http://www.nytimes.com/1994/06/22/us/an-airman-s-reveng....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1994-06-20</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-117.64836,47.61864,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Walter Rossler Company massacre - Corpus Christi, Texas</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>4/3/1995. Venue type: workplace. Killed: 6. Injured: 0. Total victims: 6. Disgruntled former metallurgist James Daniel Simpson, 28, opened fire throughout the Walter Rossler Company where he had worked before exiting the building and committing suicide. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://web.caller.com/2000/april/03/today/local_ne/4127.html.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1995-04-03</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-97.5482,27.82803,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fort Lauderdale revenge shooting - Fort Lauderdale, Florida</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>2/9/1996. Venue type: workplace. Killed: 6. Injured: 1. Total victims: 7. Fired city park employee Clifton McCree, 41, opened fire on former coworkers he called &quot;racist devils&quot; inside their municipal trailer in an act of revenge after failing a drug test. He then committed suicide. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.nytimes.com/1996/02/11/us/florida-killer-said-victims-were-racists-police-say.html; http://articles.sun-senti....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1996-02-09</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-80.10412,26.11927,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>R.E. Phelon Company shooting - Aiken, South Carolina</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>9/15/1997. Venue type: workplace. Killed: 4. Injured: 3. Total victims: 7. Ex-con Hastings Arthur Wise, 43, opened fire at the R.E. Phelon Company in retaliation for being fired after an argument with a supervisor. He attempted suicide by ingesting insecticide, failed, and was executed by the state of South Carolina eight years later. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.vpc.org/studies/wgun970915.htm; http://chronicle.augusta.com/stories/1997/09/18/met_214833.shtml.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1997-09-15</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-81.72195,33.55986,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Caltrans maintenance yard shooting - Orange, California</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>12/18/1997. Venue type: workplace. Killed: 5. Injured: 2. Total victims: 7. Former Caltrans employee Arturo Reyes Torres, 41, opened fire at a maintenance yard after he was fired for allegedly selling government materials he&#x27;d stolen from work. He was shot dead by police. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://articles.latimes.com/1997/dec/20/news/mn-431; http://articles.latimes.com/1997/dec/22/local/me-1156; http://www.v....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1997-12-18</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-117.85311,33.78779,0</coordinates></Point></Pl