s</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>2/14/2008. Venue type: school. Killed: 5. Injured: 21. Total victims: 26. Steven Kazmierczak, 27, opened fire in a lecture hall, then shot and killed himself before police arrived. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.huffingtonpost.com/jonathan-fast/steve-kazmierczak-the-sec_b_87031.html; http://www.msnbc.msn.com/id/23171567....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2008-02-14</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-88.75036,41.92947,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Atlantis Plastics shooting - Henderson, Kentucky</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>6/25/2008. Venue type: workplace. Killed: 6. Injured: 1. Total victims: 7. Disgruntled employee Wesley Neal Higdon, 25, shot up an Atlantis Plastics factory after he was escorted out of his workplace for an argument with a supervisor. Higdon shot the supervisor outside the factory before opening fire on coworkers inside. He then committed suicide. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: http://www.foxnews.com/story/0,2933,371242,00.html; http://www.msnbc.msn.com/id/25393695/ns/us_news-crime_and_courts/t/w....</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2008-06-25</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-87.55737,37.76721,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Carthage nursing home shooting - Carthage, North Carolina</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>3/29/2009. Venue type: other. Killed: 8. Injured: 3. Total victims: 11. Robert Stewart, 45, opened fire at a nursing home where his estranged wife worked before he was shot and arrested by a police officer. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-