 Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: https://www.nytimes.com/2025/12/19/us/mit-professor-shooting-suspect-portugal-lisbon-physics.html; https://www.nytimes.c.... Coordinates city-level (geocoded from the dataset place name).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2025-12-13</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-71.41283,41.82399,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Austin bar shooting - Austin, Texas</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>3/1/2026. Venue type: other. Killed: 3. Injured: 13. Total victims: 16. Ndiaga Diagne, 53, opened fire in a popular entertainment district along Sixth Street, and was quickly killed in a gun battle with police. Diagne had emigrated to the US in 2000 and became a naturalized citizen in 2013. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: https://www.cnn.com/2026/03/02/us/austin-mass-shooting-ndiaga-diagne-wwk-hnk. Coordinates city-level (geocoded from the dataset place name).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2026-03-01</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-97.7437,30.27113,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>San Diego mosque shooting - San Diego, CA</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>5/18/2026. Venue type: religious. Killed: 3. Injured: 0. Total victims: 3. Cain Clark, 17, and Caleb Vasquez, 18, attacked a mosque and then died by self-inflicted gunshots as police responded. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2026-05-18/san-diego-islamic-center-shooting-suspects-what-we-know; https://www.... Coordinates city-level (geocoded from the dataset place name).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2026-05-18</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-117.16277,32.71742,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>In-N-Out Burger shooting - Twin Falls, Idaho</name><styleUrl>#t-mass-shooting</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Mass shootings</b> &middot; mass-shooting</p><p>8/1/2026. Venue type: other. Killed: 3. Injured: 7. Total victims: 10. Chad Williams, 24, opened fire outside the restaurant, faced return fire from an armed citizen and an off-duty police officer, and shot himself to death. Source: Mother Jones mass-shootings dataset (1982-2026); row sources: https://abcnews.com/US/burger-shooting-suspect/story?id=135337720; https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/02/us/gunman-acted-al.... Coordinates city-level (geocoded from the dataset place name).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#X">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2026-08-01</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-114.47007,42.55585,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Sport and gambling (73)</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>Flamingo Hotel - Bugsy Siegel / Meyer Lansky</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Opened Dec 26, 1946. Bugsy Siegel (Murder Inc.) financed by Meyer Lansky&#x27;s syndicate. The prototype for the modern Las Vegas Strip. Siegel was murdered June 20, 1947 — shot through the eye at his Beverly Hills home. The mob didn&#x27;t leave Vegas after Siegel — it professionalized. Lansky&#x27;s financial architecture became the model for legal casino corporations. The infrastructure didn&#x27;t change; the business cards did.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1946-12-26</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-115.1745,36.1162,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Stardust Casino - Frank Rosenthal / Chicago Outfit</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Frank &#x27;Lefty&#x27; Rosenthal ran the Stardust, Fremont, Hacienda, and Marina casinos for the Chicago Outfit (1970s-80s). Tony Spilotro was the Outfit&#x27;s enforcer. FBI documented systematic &#x27;skimming&#x27; — cash siphoned before it reached the count room, sent to mob bosses in Kansas City, Milwaukee, and Chicago. Rosenthal survived a car bomb (Oct 4, 1982). Depicted in &#x27;Casino&#x27; (1995). The Stardust was imploded Feb 13, 2007 — the physical evidence demolished, but the financial architecture it pioneered is now called &#x27;the gaming industry.&#x27;</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1982-10-04</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-115.1631,36.1367,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Caesars Palace - Jay Sarno / Teamsters Loans</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Opened Aug 5, 1966. Built with $10.6M Teamsters Central States Pension Fund loan — the Teamsters pension fund was the primary financial vehicle for mob-connected Vegas construction. Jimmy Hoffa controlled the fund, Allen Dorfman administered it. Dorfman was murdered Jan 20, 1983 — shot in the head in a parking lot, one month before he was scheduled to be sentenced for bribery. The pension fund that built the Strip was run by a man who disappeared and a man who was executed.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1966-08-05</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-115.1745,36.1162,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Havana Casinos - Lansky/Trafficante Pre-Revolution</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Meyer Lansky operated the Hotel Nacional and Hotel Riviera casinos in Havana. Santo Trafficante Jr. controlled the Sans Souci and other operations. The mob&#x27;s Caribbean gambling infrastructure generated hundreds of millions annually. Castro&#x27;s revolution (Jan 1, 1959) shut it down overnight. Pattern question: where did that capital, expertise, and operational infrastructure go? Answer: Las Vegas expansion accelerated dramatically in 1959-1960. The mob didn&#x27;t lose its gambling operations — it relocated them to U.S. soil with state licensing.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1959-01-01</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-82.3666,23.1136,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>T-Mobile Arena / Las Vegas Strip - Sports Capital</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Opened Apr 6, 2016. Vegas Golden Knights (NHL, 2017), Las Vegas Raiders (NFL, 2020), Las Vegas Aces (WNBA), UNLV Rebels. Las Vegas went from &#x27;no major sports leagues will touch us&#x27; to hosting NFL, NHL, WNBA, NBA Summer League, F1 Grand Prix, Super Bowl LVIII (2024), and the planned A&#x27;s (MLB) relocation. The city the mob built is now the center of American professional sports. The leagues that banned gambling now partner with the casinos.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2016-04-06</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-115.1784,36.1029,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Allegiant Stadium - Las Vegas Raiders</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>$1.9 billion, publicly financed with $750M in hotel room tax. Oakland Raiders relocated 2020. Mark Davis (owner) — son of Al Davis, franchise value $6.2B. The NFL — which suspended players for gambling — moved a franchise to the city built by the mob. $750M in public money subsidized a private billionaire&#x27;s stadium in the gambling capital of the world. The taxpayers funded the house; the owner keeps the revenue. Las Vegas Sands CEO Sheldon Adelson (d. 2021) was instrumental in bringing the Raiders to Vegas with the $750M subsidy, and was the largest Republican donor in U.S. history ($218M in the 2020 cycle alone): casino magnate → political funding → stadium subsidy → franchise relocation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2020-01-01</begin><end>2020-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-115.1833,36.0909,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NBA HQ - 645 Fifth Ave, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>National Basketball Association headquarters. Commissioner Adam Silver wrote a 2014 New York Times op-ed publicly advocating for legal sports betting — the first major sports commissioner to do so. The league that had a referee convicted of working with the Gambino crime family (Tim Donaghy, 2007) now has official gambling partnerships with MGM, FanDuel, DraftKings. Silver&#x27;s position: the gambling was happening anyway, better to regulate and profit from it. The shift from prohibition to partnership happened within 10 years of the Donaghy scandal.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2014-01-01</begin><end>2014-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9747,40.761,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tim Donaghy - West Chester, Pennsylvania</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>FBI investigation (2007): NBA referee Tim Donaghy bet on games he officiated and made calls affecting point spreads. Handler: James &#x27;Baa Baa&#x27; Battista, connected to the Gambino crime family. Thomas Martino was the middleman. Donaghy pleaded guilty, sentenced to 15 months federal prison. He alleged other referees were also compromised and that the NBA office influenced playoff outcomes — allegations the league denied and Congress did not fully investigate. The structural question: if one referee did it for years undetected, what is the actual detection rate?</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2007-01-01</begin><end>2007-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-75.6057,39.9607,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Boston College - 1978-79 Point Shaving</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Henry Hill (Lucchese crime family) organized the scheme with Rick Kuhn and Jim Sweeney. Gamblers bet against BC when the fix was in — the team still won most fixed games, just failed to cover the spread. Hill&#x27;s testimony established that point shaving was a systematic revenue operation for organized crime, not a one-off. Documented in &#x27;Goodfellas.&#x27; The Lucchese family treated college basketball as a financial instrument.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1978-01-01</begin><end>1978-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.1685,42.3355,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tulane University - 1985 Point Shaving</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Players accepted cocaine and $18,500 in cash from gambler Gary Kranz to shave points in two games (Feb 1985). University president Eamon Kelly shut down the basketball program for four years. The scandal demonstrated that gambling corruption had penetrated Southern universities — the same pipeline that feeds the NBA and NFL. Drugs as payment currency — the sports gambling/narcotics infrastructure overlap.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1985-02-01</begin><end>1985-02-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-90.1208,29.9401,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Arizona State - 1994 Point Shaving</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Benny Silman recruited ASU guard Stevin &#x27;Hedake&#x27; Smith and Isaac Burton to fix four games during the 1993-94 season. Silman was connected to a gambling ring with ties to organized crime figures in the Midwest. Smith and Burton shaved points — the team won but failed to cover. Silman sentenced to 46 months. Pattern: every decade has a documented point-shaving case, suggesting these are detection events, not the total universe of incidents.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1994-01-01</begin><end>1994-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-111.9281,33.4242,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NFL HQ - 345 Park Ave, New York</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>National Football League headquarters. Commissioner Roger Goodell repeatedly opposed sports betting until the revenue opportunity became clear. The NFL suspended players for gambling (Paul Hornung 1963, Alex Karras 1963, Art Schlichter, Josh Shaw, Calvin Ridley, etc.) while simultaneously accepting $1B+ annually in gambling advertising revenue. FanDuel, DraftKings, Caesars are all &#x27;official partners.&#x27; The league that suspends players for betting profits from the betting industry. $20.2B league revenue (2023).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1963-01-01</begin><end>1963-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.968,40.7589,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>1958 NFL Championship - &#x27;Greatest Game Ever Played&#x27;</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Yankee Stadium, Dec 28, 1958. Baltimore Colts 23, New York Giants 17 (OT). The game that made the NFL a television product. Carroll Rosenbloom (Colts owner) was a known gambler with documented mob connections. Rosenbloom later admitted to betting on the 1958 championship game. He drowned under suspicious circumstances in 1979 — ruled accidental, widely suspected otherwise. The single most important game in NFL history was owned by a man who bet on it and later died under unexplained circumstances.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1958-12-28</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-73.9262,40.8296,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Art Schlichter - Gambling / Organized Crime</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Ohio State quarterback, 4th overall pick (1982, Baltimore Colts). Lost millions gambling, suspended by the NFL, caught in a bookmaking operation connected to organized crime in Indiana and Ohio. Eventually convicted on 18 federal charges (2012). Sentenced to 10 years. Schlichter was the warning: a #4 pick destroyed by the same gambling infrastructure the NFL now officially partners with. The pipeline from organized crime bookmaking to &#x27;legal sportsbook&#x27; is a rebranding.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1982-01-01</begin><end>1982-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-82.9988,39.9612,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Calvin Ridley - NFL Gambling Suspension</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Atlanta Falcons WR suspended entire 2022 season for placing $1,500 in parlay bets on NFL games (including Falcons games) through a legal sportsbook. He was not accused of fixing anything — just betting. Suspended one year, lost $11.1M salary. The NFL made $1B+ from gambling partnerships the same year it suspended a player for $1,500 in legal bets. The player is punished for doing what the league profits from.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-01-01</begin><end>2022-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-84.388,33.749,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Jerry Jones - Dallas Cowboys / Comstock Resources</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>AT&amp;T Stadium, Arlington TX. Jones purchased the Cowboys for $140M (1989), now valued at $10.32B — most valuable franchise in global sports. Jones is also CEO of Comstock Resources (oil/gas). Pattern: NFL ownership is a secondary holding for individuals whose primary wealth derives from energy, real estate, finance, and media — the same sectors documented in Sections VII and XVII. The franchise is a prestige asset that provides access to other networks.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1989-01-01</begin><end>1989-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-97.0945,32.7473,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Robert Kraft - New England Patriots / Kraft Group</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Gillette Stadium, Foxborough MA. Kraft purchased Patriots for $172M (1994), now valued $7B+. Kraft Group: paper, packaging, real estate, private equity. Kraft was charged in a prostitution sting at Orchids of Asia Day Spa, Jupiter FL (Feb 2019) — charges later dropped. The spa was connected to a human trafficking investigation. An NFL owner caught in a human trafficking-connected operation — charges disappeared. Pattern: charges that should stick evaporate for franchise-level individuals.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-02-01</begin><end>2019-02-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.2643,42.0909,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Stan Kroenke - LA Rams / Arsenal / Walmart Heir</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>SoFi Stadium, Inglewood CA. Kroenke owns LA Rams, Denver Nuggets, Colorado Avalanche, Colorado Rapids, Arsenal FC (English Premier League). Married to Ann Walton (Walmart heiress). A single family network controls NFL, NBA, NHL, MLS, and Premier League franchises — plus the world&#x27;s largest retailer. Cross-border sports ownership as financial network mapping.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-118.339,33.9535,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Comiskey Park - 1919 Black Sox Scandal</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>1919 World Series: Eight Chicago White Sox players conspired with gamblers (Arnold Rothstein&#x27;s network) to intentionally lose to the Cincinnati Reds. Rothstein — the original &#x27;Big Bankroll&#x27; — was the financial architect of organized crime&#x27;s penetration of professional sports. He financed the fix through intermediaries. Rothstein was murdered Nov 4, 1928 at the Park Central Hotel, NYC. Players acquitted in court (1921) but banned for life by Commissioner Landis. The Black Sox established the template: organized crime → gambling → sports corruption. Every subsequent scandal follows this architecture.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1928-11-04</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-87.6338,41.8299,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Arnold Rothstein - Park Central Hotel, NYC</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>The man who fixed the 1919 World Series was shot at the Park Central Hotel on Nov 4, 1928 and died Nov 6. Rothstein was the organizational genius who professionalized American organized crime — he taught Meyer Lansky, Lucky Luciano, Dutch Schultz, and Frank Costello. He pioneered the integration of gambling, narcotics, and labor racketeering into a unified financial operation. The man who corrupted baseball invented the business model that built Las Vegas and funded the Cosa Nostra for 50 years.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1928-11-04</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-73.9794,40.7648,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pete Rose - Gambling Ban / Hit King</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Riverfront Stadium / Great American Ball Park, Cincinnati. Rose — MLB&#x27;s all-time hits leader (4,256) — banned for life by Commissioner Giamatti (Aug 24, 1989) for betting on baseball, including games he managed. Rose denied it for 15 years, admitted it in 2004. Giamatti died of a heart attack Sept 1, 1989 — 8 days after banning Rose. The commissioner who enforced the gambling ban died within a week. Rose died Sept 30, 2024. He was never reinstated. MLB now has official gambling partnerships with the same sportsbooks Rose would have used.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1989-08-24</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-84.5069,39.0976,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>BALCO Labs - Burlingame, California</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Bay Area Laboratory Co-Operative. Victor Conte supplied undetectable steroids (THG/&#x27;The Clear&#x27;) to Barry Bonds, Marion Jones, Tim Montgomery, and dozens of professional athletes. Federal investigation (2003) exposed systematic performance enhancement across MLB, NFL, and Olympic sports. The steroids era inflated offensive statistics → which drove television ratings → which drove gambling volume → which drove franchise valuations. The performance enhancement pipeline was a financial instrument for everyone except the players who took the drugs.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2003-01-01</begin><end>2003-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-122.3661,37.5841,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>MLB HQ - 1271 Ave of the Americas, NYC</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Major League Baseball headquarters. MLB signed exclusive deals with DraftKings, FanDuel, BetMGM, Caesars. Commissioner Rob Manfred — the same league that banned Pete Rose for life for gambling now generates hundreds of millions annually from gambling partnerships. The &#x27;integrity of the game&#x27; argument was used to destroy Pete Rose and is now used to justify official gambling revenue. The principle didn&#x27;t change; the revenue model did.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.979,40.7614,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Houston Astros - Sign Stealing Scandal</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Minute Maid Park, Houston. 2017-2018: Astros used cameras and a monitor near the dugout to steal opposing catchers&#x27; signs, relaying them to batters by banging on a trash can. Team won the 2017 World Series. Manager AJ Hinch and GM Jeff Luhnow suspended one year then fired. No players were punished. Pattern: institutional corruption at the team level — electronic surveillance used to manipulate outcomes. The team kept the World Series title. If the outcome was manipulated and the result stands, what exactly does &#x27;integrity of the game&#x27; mean?</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-01-01</begin><end>2017-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-95.3555,29.7572,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NCAA HQ - Indianapolis, Indiana</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; governance</p><p>National Collegiate Athletic Association headquarters. Revenue: $1.28B (2023). The NCAA governed a $20B/year industry while classifying the athletes generating the revenue as &#x27;student-athletes&#x27; — a term invented by Walter Byers (first NCAA executive director) specifically to avoid workers&#x27; compensation claims. The Supreme Court ruled unanimously (NCAA v. Alston, 2021) that NCAA compensation limits violated antitrust law. Justice Kavanaugh&#x27;s concurrence: &#x27;The NCAA&#x27;s business model would be flatly illegal in almost any other industry in America.&#x27; The largest unpaid labor operation in American sports history, operated from Indianapolis.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-01-01</begin><end>2023-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-86.149,39.8105,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CCNY - 1950-51 Point Shaving Scandal</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>City College of New York. 1950-51 investigation revealed point shaving across seven universities: CCNY, LIU, NYU, Manhattan, Kentucky, Bradley, Toledo. 32 players arrested. Gamblers Salvatore Sollazzo and Eli Kaye ran the operation. CCNY had won both the NIT and NCAA tournament in 1950 — the only team ever to win both in the same year — and the fixers were already embedded. Kentucky&#x27;s program suspended for entire 1952-53 season. The scandal proved organized gambling had systematically penetrated college basketball nationwide. The pipeline from college to NBA was already compromised at the source.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1950-01-01</begin><end>1950-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.95,40.8198,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>University of Kentucky - Rupp Arena</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>UK basketball — the most storied program in college basketball history — was implicated in the 1951 point-shaving scandal. Coach Adolph Rupp initially claimed the fixers &#x27;couldn&#x27;t touch my boys with a ten-foot pole.&#x27; Three players were arrested. The NCAA suspended the program for the entire 1952-53 season. Judge Saul Streit called UK&#x27;s program &#x27;the acme of commercialism and overemphasis&#x27; — in 1951. 75 years later, UK basketball generates $50M+ in annual revenue. The commercialism the judge identified has been formalized, not reformed.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1951-01-01</begin><end>1951-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-84.4953,38.0434,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Northwestern University - 1994 Gambling Scandal</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Evanston, IL. Two Northwestern basketball players (Dion Lee, Dewey Williams) shaved points in three games during the 1994-95 season. A former player, Kevin Pendergast, was the fixer. Connected to a gambling ring operating through the Chicago suburbs — same Chicago corridor as the Outfit&#x27;s historical gambling operations. An Ivy-adjacent Big Ten school in the same metropolitan area as the mob&#x27;s historical gambling infrastructure. The geographic overlap is not coincidental.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1994-01-01</begin><end>1994-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-87.6753,42.0565,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>University of San Diego - Gambling Ring (2011)</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>USD basketball assistant coach Thaddeus Brown was connected to a point-shaving scheme involving a San Diego-based gambling ring. Brown pleaded guilty (2013). The case demonstrated that point shaving continued at the college level well into the 21st century — it didn&#x27;t stop after each decade&#x27;s scandal, it just moved to different programs. Detection events, not total events.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2011-01-01</begin><end>2011-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-117.188,32.772,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>FIFA HQ - Zurich, Switzerland</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; governance</p><p>Fédération Internationale de Football Association. Revenue: $7.5B (2018 cycle). May 27, 2015: DOJ indicted 14 FIFA officials and associates on 47 counts including racketeering, wire fraud, and money laundering. Swiss police arrested seven FIFA officials at the Baur au Lac hotel in Zurich. The indictment described &#x27;rampant, systemic, and deep-rooted&#x27; corruption spanning 24 years. FIFA — which governs the world&#x27;s most popular sport (3.5 billion fans) — was prosecuted under RICO, the same statute designed for the Mafia. Same Swiss soil as BIS. Same sovereign immunity claims. Same institutional opacity.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2015-05-27</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>8.5749,47.3815,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Baur au Lac Hotel - FIFA Arrests, Zurich</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>May 27, 2015: Swiss police entered before dawn, arrested seven FIFA officials on U.S. corruption charges. They used bed sheets to shield the officials from cameras. $150M+ in bribes documented. The hotel where FIFA officials stayed during World Cup bidding votes is where they were arrested. The luxury venue and the crime scene share coordinates.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2015-05-27</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>8.54,47.3658,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CONMEBOL HQ - Luque, Paraguay</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>South American football confederation. Multiple presidents convicted of corruption: Nicolás Leoz (charged 2015), Juan Ángel Napout (convicted 2017, sentenced to 9 years — racketeering, wire fraud, money laundering), José Luis Meiszner (charged). The continental body that governs South American football operated as a corruption enterprise. Copa América and Copa Libertadores rights sold through bribe-mediated deals for decades.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2015-01-01</begin><end>2015-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-57.487,-25.2752,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CONCACAF HQ - Miami, Florida</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>North/Central American football confederation. Jack Warner (president 1990-2011, Trinidad) and Chuck Blazer (general secretary 1990-2011, USA) ran the organization as a personal enrichment vehicle. Warner convicted — fled to Trinidad. Blazer became an FBI cooperating witness, wore a wire at FIFA meetings, recorded fellow officials. Blazer lived in Trump Tower NYC, rented a separate apartment there for his cats. CONCACAF&#x27;s top two officials for 21 years: one fled prosecution, the other became a federal informant living in Trump Tower.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1990-01-01</begin><end>1990-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-80.1918,25.7617,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Trump Tower - Chuck Blazer&#x27;s Apartment</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>721 Fifth Avenue, NYC. Chuck Blazer (CONCACAF general secretary, FIFA executive committee) maintained a $6,000/month apartment here — plus a separate $6,000/month apartment in the same building for his cats. Blazer failed to pay taxes on $11.7M in income. He became an FBI cooperating witness, wore a wire at FIFA meetings in London (2011-2012). The man who brought down FIFA leadership lived in Trump Tower and didn&#x27;t pay taxes for years. The FBI ran its FIFA corruption operation through a witness who lived in the President&#x27;s building.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2011-01-01</begin><end>2011-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9742,40.7625,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Qatar - 2022 FIFA World Cup</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>FIFA awarded Qatar the 2022 World Cup (Dec 2, 2010). DOJ investigation documented $5M+ in bribes to FIFA voters. 6,500+ migrant workers died during construction (Guardian investigation, Feb 2021) — primarily from Nepal, India, Bangladesh, Sri Lanka, Pakistan. Workers operated under the kafala system — a form of bonded labor where employers control workers&#x27; legal status. A country with no football infrastructure, summer temperatures exceeding 120°F, a population of 2.8 million, and a bonded labor system was awarded the world&#x27;s largest sporting event. The deaths were categorized as &#x27;natural causes&#x27; or &#x27;cardiac arrest.&#x27;</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2010-12-02</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>51.1839,25.3548,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Russia - 2018 FIFA World Cup</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>FIFA awarded Russia the 2018 World Cup (Dec 2, 2010 — same vote as Qatar 2022). DOJ investigation documented corruption in the bidding process. Garcia Report (2014) — FIFA&#x27;s own internal investigation into bidding corruption — was kept secret, then summarized in a way Garcia himself called &#x27;materially incomplete.&#x27; Russia hosted the tournament while actively conducting military operations in Crimea/Ukraine (annexed 2014). The world&#x27;s most popular sport awarded its premier event to a country engaged in territorial annexation.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2010-12-02</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>37.6173,55.7558,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bochum, Germany - Match Fixing Hub</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>2009 Bochum investigation: Europol and German police uncovered a massive international match-fixing network. 200+ games fixed across 15 countries. €16M+ in bets placed through Asian gambling syndicates. Ante Sapina, a Croatian-German, was the central fixer. Connected to Singaporean betting syndicates (Dan Tan Seet Eng). The network fixed matches in European leagues, Champions League qualifying, friendlies, and lower-division games. The corruption was structural, cross-border, and connected organized crime in Europe to gambling syndicates in Asia.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2009-01-01</begin><end>2009-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>7.2162,51.4818,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Singapore - Dan Tan / Global Match Fixing</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>Dan Tan Seet Eng — the alleged mastermind behind the world&#x27;s largest match-fixing syndicate. Interpol operation (2013) identified his network as responsible for fixing hundreds of matches globally. Singapore declined to extradite him despite international pressure. The global match-fixing network operates from Singapore — one of the world&#x27;s most important financial centers, same jurisdiction that handles massive capital flows. The match-fixing hub and the banking hub share coordinates.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2013-01-01</begin><end>2013-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>103.8198,1.3521,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Calciopoli - Rome / Italian Football Fixing</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>2006 Italian football scandal: Wiretaps revealed Juventus GM Luciano Moggi systematically selected favorable referees through Italian Football Federation contacts. Juventus stripped of two Serie A titles, relegated to Serie B. AC Milan, Fiorentina, Lazio, Reggina all penalized. The scandal exposed that Italy&#x27;s top football league was being managed through a network of executive-to-referee influence. Moggi&#x27;s contact book was a map of institutional corruption. &#x27;Ndrangheta involvement in Italian football (match fixing, money laundering through player transfers) is extensively documented by Italian prosecutors.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2006-01-01</begin><end>2006-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>12.4964,41.9028,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>IOC HQ - Lausanne, Switzerland</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; governance</p><p>International Olympic Committee headquarters. The IOC operates from Swiss soil with special legal status — same jurisdiction pattern as BIS and FIFA. Revenue: $7.6B (2017-2021 cycle). IOC members serve in a self-electing body with no democratic accountability. The same organizational structure documented across Sections VII and XVII: sovereign immunity, Swiss jurisdiction, self-governance, opacity. The IOC decides which cities spend $10-50B hosting events and which corporations become &#x27;official partners.&#x27;</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-01-01</begin><end>2017-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>6.6323,46.5197,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Salt Lake City - 2002 Olympic Bribery Scandal</name><styleUrl>#t-organized-crime</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; organized-crime</p><p>1998 investigation revealed Salt Lake Organizing Committee paid $1.3M+ in direct payments to IOC members and their relatives to secure the 2002 Winter Olympics bid. Tom Welch and Dave Johnson (bid leaders) indicted on bribery charges — later acquitted after judge ruled the IOC&#x27;s practices made the bribes &#x27;business as usual.&#x27; The defense that worked: everyone does it, so it&#x27;s not corruption. The ruling established that systematic bribery was the IOC&#x27;s standard operating procedure.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2002-01-01</begin><end>2002-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-111.891,40.7608,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rio de Janeiro - 2016 Olympics / Corruption</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>2016 Summer Olympics. Total cost: $13.1B. Brazilian federal police subsequently arrested Carlos Nuzman (Brazilian Olympic Committee president) for his role in a $2M bribery scheme to secure IOC votes. Nuzman convicted (2021). Rio&#x27;s Olympic venues are largely abandoned or deteriorating — the $13.1B was extracted from Brazilian taxpayers, the infrastructure was temporary, and the organizing committee&#x27;s president went to prison. The host city pattern: public cost, private profit, criminal prosecution after the event.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2016-01-01</begin><end>2016-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-43.1729,-22.9068,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sochi - 2014 Winter Olympics / $51 Billion</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Most expensive Olympics in history: $51 billion — widely reported as the most corrupt, with estimates that $25-30B was lost to corruption and embezzlement. Putin&#x27;s personal allies received construction contracts. Boris Nemtsov documented the corruption in detail — Nemtsov was murdered on Feb 27, 2015, shot four times on a bridge within sight of the Kremlin. Russia also ran a state-sponsored doping program exposed by Grigory Rodchenkov (Moscow Anti-Doping Centre director turned whistleblower). Rodchenkov is in U.S. witness protection. The Olympics cost $51B, half was stolen, the corruption documenter was murdered, and the doping whistleblower is in hiding.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2015-02-27</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>39.7342,43.6028,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Beijing - 2008/2022 Olympics / Dual Host</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Beijing is the only city to host both Summer (2008) and Winter (2022) Olympics. The 2008 Games cost $44B — the most expensive Summer Olympics at that time. Human rights organizations documented mass evictions, surveillance expansion, and press suppression during both events. The IOC awarded the world&#x27;s premier sporting events to a government operating mass internment (Uyghur camps documented by satellite imagery, UN reports) and systematic surveillance (social credit system). The IOC&#x27;s response to human rights concerns: &#x27;We are not a world government.&#x27;</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2008-01-01</begin><end>2008-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>116.4074,39.9042,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Berlin - 1936 Olympics / Nazi Propaganda</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Olympiastadion. Hitler&#x27;s Olympics — the template for using international sporting events as state propaganda. Leni Riefenstahl&#x27;s &#x27;Olympia&#x27; (1938) invented modern sports broadcasting aesthetics. Jesse Owens won four gold medals — and returned to an America that wouldn&#x27;t let him eat in the same restaurants as white people. IBM provided the tabulation equipment. Coca-Cola was an official sponsor. The IOC awarded the Games to Nazi Germany, American corporations sponsored them, and the U.S. government participated while enforcing racial segregation at home. The blueprint for every subsequent &#x27;politics-free&#x27; Olympics.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1936-01-01</begin><end>1936-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>13.2395,52.5147,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Munich - 1972 Olympics / Black September</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Olympiapark. Sept 5, 1972: Black September (Palestinian militant group) took 11 Israeli athletes hostage. German rescue operation (Operation Sunshine) failed catastrophically — all 11 hostages, 5 attackers, and 1 police officer killed. Israel launched Operation Wrath of God — Mossad assassination campaign targeting Black September members across Europe. The Olympics as a stage for geopolitical violence. The &#x27;apolitical&#x27; games became the site of the deadliest political operation in sports history. IOC President Avery Brundage — who had praised the 1936 Berlin Olympics — refused to cancel the Games.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1972-09-05</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>11.5461,48.1735,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Atlanta - 1996 Olympics / Centennial Park Bombing</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Centennial Olympic Park bombing, July 27, 1996. Pipe bomb killed Alice Hawthorne, injured 111. Eric Robert Rudolph was the bomber — domestic terrorist who also bombed abortion clinics and a lesbian nightclub. Security guard Richard Jewell, who discovered the bomb and saved lives, was falsely accused by the FBI and destroyed by media coverage. The FBI&#x27;s incorrect investigation ruined an innocent man while the actual bomber evaded capture for 5 years. The Olympics as a target, the investigation as a pattern of institutional failure.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>1996-07-27</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-84.393,33.7604,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tilman Fertitta - Toyota Center, Houston</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Owns Houston Rockets (NBA, purchased $2.2B, 2017), Landry&#x27;s Inc. (Golden Nugget Casinos, Bubba Gump, Rainforest Cafe, 600+ properties). Net worth $8.8B. A single individual simultaneously owns an NBA franchise AND casinos. The NBA&#x27;s &#x27;integrity&#x27; policies prohibit players from gambling while the team is literally owned by a casino operator. The structural conflict of interest is not hidden — it&#x27;s the business model.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-01-01</begin><end>2017-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-95.3621,29.7508,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>MGM Resorts HQ - Las Vegas</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Official gaming partner of NBA, NHL, MLB, MLS. BetMGM is a joint venture with Entain (formerly GVC Holdings, UK gambling conglomerate). Annual gaming revenue: $14.4B (2023). MGM operates the same casinos that were built by the mob (Bellagio, Mirage, MGM Grand — all formerly mob-connected properties). The &#x27;official partner&#x27; of American professional sports is the corporate inheritor of organized crime&#x27;s casino infrastructure. The buildings are the same. The revenue flows the same way. The business cards changed.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-01-01</begin><end>2023-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-115.1684,36.1024,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>FanDuel HQ - New York</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Parent company: Flutter Entertainment (Irish gambling conglomerate, market cap $35B+). Flutter also owns Paddy Power, Betfair, PokerStars, Sky Betting, Sportsbet, FOX Bet. Official partner of NFL, NBA, MLB, NHL. An Irish-domiciled gambling conglomerate controls significant betting market share across all four major American sports leagues through a single subsidiary. The corporate structure is designed for regulatory arbitrage — Irish holding company, American-facing brand.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.9897,40.741,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>DraftKings HQ - Boston</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Founded 2012 as daily fantasy sports — a legal loophole exploiting the Unlawful Internet Gambling Enforcement Act&#x27;s fantasy sports exemption. Transitioned to full sportsbook after Murphy v. NCAA (2018). Official partner of NFL, NBA, MLB, NHL, UFC, PGA. Market cap $18B+. Same Boston metropolitan area as the 1978-79 BC point-shaving scandal. The geographic corridor that produced mob-run bookmaking now hosts the corporate headquarters of legal bookmaking. The activity is identical; the licensing changed.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2012-01-01</begin><end>2012-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-71.0405,42.3482,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kroenke Sports &amp; Entertainment - Denver</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Ball Arena, Denver. Stan Kroenke (married Ann Walton, Walmart heiress) owns: LA Rams (NFL), Denver Nuggets (NBA), Colorado Avalanche (NHL), Colorado Rapids (MLS), Arsenal FC (English Premier League), Los Angeles Gladiators (Overwatch League). A single family controls franchises across five sports and two countries, connected to the world&#x27;s largest retailer. Cross-border ownership portfolio maps the same financial network topology documented in Section VII.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-105.0077,39.7487,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Madison Square Garden - Dolan / MSG Networks</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Owns NY Knicks (NBA, valued $6.6B), NY Rangers (NHL), MSG Networks (regional sports broadcasting). James Dolan — Cablevision heir. MSG Networks broadcasts the games, MSG Entertainment operates the venue, and the Dolan family captures revenue at every point in the chain: venue, broadcast rights, advertising, ticket sales, concessions. Vertical integration of the sports-media pipeline. Same model as Murdoch&#x27;s Fox Sports / Sky / Premier League ownership overlap.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-73.9934,40.7505,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Crypto.com Arena - AEG / Philip Anschutz</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Formerly Staples Center. Philip Anschutz (AEG — Anschutz Entertainment Group) owns LA Kings (NHL), LA Galaxy (MLS), and operates 300+ venues globally. Anschutz also owns: The Examiner newspaper chain, The Weekly Standard (conservative media, now defunct), Regal Cinemas (prior), Qwest Communications (prior), oil/gas operations, railroad investments. Conservative media + entertainment infrastructure + sports ownership under a single private individual. Net worth $12B+. The patron-model: sports, media, and political narrative under unified control.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-118.2673,34.043,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chase Center - San Francisco / Lacob-Guber</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Golden State Warriors arena. Joe Lacob (ownership group lead) — former partner at Kleiner Perkins Caufield &amp; Byers (Silicon Valley&#x27;s most famous VC firm). Peter Guber (co-owner) — former chairman of Sony Pictures, Mandalay Entertainment. VC + Hollywood + NBA ownership. The same venture capital firms documented in tech surveillance (Section X) own professional sports teams. The capital that funds surveillance technology also owns the spectacle.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-122.3877,37.768,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Barclays Center - Brooklyn / Joe Tsai</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Brooklyn Nets arena. Joe Tsai — co-founder and executive vice chairman of Alibaba Group. Purchased Nets for $3.4B (2019), most expensive NBA sale ever. Also owns New York Liberty (WNBA), San Diego Seals (NLL). Alibaba operates in a jurisdiction (China) where the government can access corporate data at will. A co-founder of China&#x27;s largest tech company owns a professional sports franchise in Brooklyn, New York. Cross-border capital flow, cross-border information access, cross-border influence.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2019-01-01</begin><end>2019-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.9754,40.6826,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>U.S. Supreme Court - Murphy v. NCAA (2018)</name><styleUrl>#t-governance</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; governance</p><p>May 14, 2018: SCOTUS ruled 7-2 that the Professional and Amateur Sports Protection Act (PASPA, 1992) was unconstitutional — it violated the anti-commandeering doctrine by forbidding states from authorizing sports betting. Justice Samuel Alito wrote the majority opinion. Within 5 years, 38 states legalized sports betting, generating $10B+ in annual revenue. The same court that decided Citizens United (unlimited political spending) opened the floodgates on sports gambling. Both decisions transferred enormous revenue streams to private entities through constitutional reasoning.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2018-05-14</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-77.0044,38.8907,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Calabasas Crash Site - N72EX / Kobe Bryant</name><styleUrl>#t-conflict</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; conflict</p><p>Jan 26, 2020. Sikorsky S-76B (N72EX), 9 fatalities. Aircraft with Illinois government provenance (N761LL, 2007-2015), unknown pre-2007 ownership, CVR removed by Island Express after acquisition, no FDR installed, no TAWS despite NTSB recommendation. Pilot Ara Zobayan: 8,577 total hours, ~75 IFR, cited 2015 for VFR-into-IMC. ATC controller rotated at 9:43 — one minute before critical final transmissions. Island Express not certified for IFR. Net effect: zero recording devices, zero ground proximity warning, on an aircraft manufactured by the DARPA ALIAS autonomous flight contractor. Cross-ref: ai-attack-vector-analysis.html Section 5.10. Bryant occupied an observational position across NBA, venture capital ($2B AUM Bryant Stibel), entertainment (Academy Award, Granity Studios), and technology. 20-year NBA career spanning the pre- and post-Donaghy eras.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeStamp><when>2020-01-26</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>-118.6917,34.1369,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Island Express Helicopters - Long Beach, CA</name><styleUrl>#t-corporate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; corporate</p><p>Operator of N72EX. Acquired from initial post-Illinois owner. Removed the cockpit voice recorder after acquisition (March 2016). Not certified to fly in Instrument Flight Rules conditions. Filed &#x27;act of God&#x27; defense and cross-complaint against FAA controllers after the crash. The operator removed the one recording device, lacked the certification to fly in the conditions of the crash, then blamed God and the government. The liability defense is also a forensic defense: no recording = no evidence = &#x27;act of God.&#x27;</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2016-03-01</begin><end>2016-03-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-118.1513,33.8178,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sikorsky / Lockheed Martin - Stratford, CT</name><styleUrl>#t-military</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; military</p><p>Manufacturer of S-76 (crash aircraft) and UH-60 Black Hawk. Lockheed Martin subsidiary since 2015. DARPA ALIAS program → Sikorsky MATRIX autonomous flight technology → H-60Mx optionally piloted Black Hawk. The S-76 shares architecture heritage with the H-60. &#x27;Optionally piloted&#x27; = the aircraft can fly without a human pilot providing inputs. This capability exists on the platform family. N72EX was built in 1991 — spanning three corporate ownership eras of its manufacturer (pre-UTC, UTC, Lockheed Martin). Cross-ref: Section VII military-industrial markers.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1991-01-01</begin><end>1991-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-73.1332,41.1865,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Colosseum - Rome (The Original &#x27;Baal Game&#x27;)</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Opened 80 AD under Emperor Titus. Capacity 50,000-80,000. Gladiatorial combat, animal hunts, executions, naval battles. Free admission — funded by the state (et circenses). The operational template: spectacle as social control. The population is fed and entertained; the rulers govern without resistance. The Colosseum was not entertainment — it was governance infrastructure. Bread and circuses is not a metaphor. It is an engineering specification. Every modern stadium is an iteration of this design: public subsidy, private profit, mass distraction, political utility.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>12.4922,41.8902,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Circus Maximus - Rome</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Chariot racing venue, capacity 250,000. Operational for over 600 years. Gambling on chariot races was systematic and organized — racing factions (Blues, Greens, Reds, Whites) functioned as early sports franchises with wealthy patrons, professional athletes, and betting markets. The Nika Riots (532 AD, Constantinople) — racing faction violence nearly overthrew Emperor Justinian. 30,000 killed. Sports fandom as political mobilization vehicle — documented since antiquity. The stadium as a site of both spectacle and political crisis.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>12.4853,41.8862,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Olympia, Greece - Ancient Olympic Games</name><styleUrl>#t-archaeological</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; archaeological</p><p>Olympic Games originated here, 776 BC. Sacred truce (ekecheiria) between warring city-states during the games. Athletes competed nude, women were banned from attendance (penalty: death). The games were religious festivals dedicated to Zeus — not &#x27;secular sports.&#x27; When the user says &#x27;Baal games&#x27; the ancient parallel is exact: athletic competition as religious ritual under divine authority. Emperor Theodosius I abolished the games in 393 AD. The IOC &#x27;revived&#x27; them in 1896 — stripping the religious content and replacing it with nationalism and corporate sponsorship. The sacred truce became the &#x27;Olympic ideal&#x27;; the temple became the sponsor village.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>1896-01-01</begin><end>1896-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>21.63,37.6388,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>The Venetian Macao / Cotai Strip, Macau</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>The anchor of Macau&#x27;s Cotai Strip, the gambling capital of the world, whose revenues long dwarfed Las Vegas; the VIP junket system that fed it collapsed when Suncity chief Alvin Chau — whose firm held ~40% of the junket market and handled bets prosecutors valued at HK$824 billion — was jailed 18 years in 2023 for running an illegal gambling and criminal syndicate. Source: TIME; South China Morning Post; Al Jazeera.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-01-01</begin><end>2023-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>113.5605,22.1482,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Crown Melbourne</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>A 2021 royal commission found James Packer&#x27;s Crown facilitated money laundering — cash brought into the casino in cooler and shopping bags for chips — and let its junket business be infiltrated by organised crime; former judge Ray Finkelstein declared Crown &#x27;unsuitable&#x27; to hold Victoria&#x27;s only casino licence. Source: BBC; The Conversation; The Guardian Australia.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2021-01-01</begin><end>2021-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>144.9583,-37.8233,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>The Star Sydney</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Two NSW inquiries (2022 and the 2024 Bell review) found The Star unsuitable to hold a Sydney casino licence, exposing anti-money-laundering failures — including &#x27;Salon 95,&#x27; a secret VIP room with a hidden cash cage — and cash disguised as hotel expenses; the operator was fined AU$100 million and placed under a government manager. Source: NSW Independent Casino Commission (nicc.nsw.gov.au); iGaming Business; Yogonet.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2022-01-01</begin><end>2022-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>151.1956,-33.8687,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Wynn Las Vegas - $130M Money-Laundering Forfeiture</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>In September 2024 Wynn Las Vegas forfeited $130.1 million — the largest such forfeiture by a casino admitting criminal wrongdoing — for conspiring with unlicensed money-transmitting businesses that used &#x27;Flying Money&#x27; and &#x27;Human Head&#x27; schemes to move funds for foreign gamblers, especially from China, evading U.S. reporting laws. Source: U.S. DOJ / IRS Criminal Investigation (irs.gov); Washington Times.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2024-09-01</begin><end>2024-09-28</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-115.1658,36.1264,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>bet365 Headquarters, Stoke-on-Trent</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Founded in 2000 by Denise Coates from a portable building in a Stoke-on-Trent car park, bet365 grew into one of the world&#x27;s largest online gambling firms, serving over 90 million customers; Coates has drawn scrutiny for pay packages exceeding £250 million in a single year. Source: CNN; BBC; Wikipedia, &#x27;bet365&#x27;.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2000-01-01</begin><end>2000-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-2.1995,53.0248,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Flutter Entertainment HQ, Dublin</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Flutter is the world&#x27;s largest online betting company, owner of FanDuel, PokerStars, Paddy Power, Betfair and Sky Bet; formed by the 2020 merger of Paddy Power Betfair and The Stars Group, it dominates the U.S. sports-betting market via FanDuel while keeping its registered base in Dublin. Source: Flutter Entertainment (flutter.com); Wikipedia; CNN Business.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2020-01-01</begin><end>2020-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-6.241,53.2938,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hong Kong Jockey Club - Happy Valley Racecourse</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>The Jockey Club holds a legal monopoly on Hong Kong betting and is the city&#x27;s single largest taxpayer, contributing a record HK$35.9 billion to the community in 2022/23; its 2025/26 racing turnover reached HK$143.3 billion, and its charities trust ranks among the world&#x27;s largest donors. Source: South China Morning Post; Hong Kong Jockey Club (corporate.hkjc.com).</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>114.187,22.2672,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Malta Gaming Authority, Kalkara</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>The EU licensing hub for much of online betting, the MGA was described by investigators as an &#x27;ATM for the Italian Mafia&#x27;: the &#x27;Ndrangheta used Maltese licences (e.g. Betuniq) to grow profits to €16 million a month, and it suspended CenturionBet in 2017 after an anti-mafia raid arrested 68 people over cross-border laundering. Source: OCCRP (Daphne Project); The Shift News; MaltaToday.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2017-01-01</begin><end>2017-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>14.5275,35.8969,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Illegal Sports-Betting Ring - U.S. Courthouse, Santa Ana</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>At this federal courthouse in 2025, Orange County bookmaker Mathew Bowyer was sentenced to a year and a day for running an illegal sports-gambling business used by Shohei Ohtani&#x27;s interpreter Ippei Mizuhara, who placed at least 19,000 bets and stole nearly $17 million from the MLB star to cover his losses. Source: U.S. Department of Justice (justice.gov); ESPN; Sportico.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2025-01-01</begin><end>2025-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-117.8711,33.7481,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Entain plc HQ, London</name><styleUrl>#t-sports-gambling</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Sport and gambling</b> &middot; sports-gambling</p><p>Entain — owner of Ladbrokes, Coral, bwin, partypoker and co-owner of BetMGM — agreed in 2023 to a £585 million penalty (£615 million total) under the UK&#x27;s first CPS deferred prosecution agreement, over bribery tied to its former Turkish-facing operations in breach of the Bribery Act 2010. Source: Crown Prosecution Service (cps.gov.uk); Racing Post; Poker.org.</p><p><a href="https://www.b0b.dev/report#SPORTS">View in report</a></p>]]></description><TimeSpan><begin>2023-01-01</begin><end>2023-12-31</end></TimeSpan><Point><coordinates>-0.0835,51.5113,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder></Document></kml>
